msgstr "<bat>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:spriggan baker"
msgid ""
"“Blood, sweat, and tea, sister! That's what it takes to achieve all great and\n"
" terrible things.”\n"
"    -Emory R. Frie, _Wonderland_. 2016.\n"
msgstr ""
"“鲜血、汗水，还有茶，姐妹！要成就一切伟大而可怕之事，就得靠这些。”\n"
"    -Emory R. Frie, _Wonderland_. 2016.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:witch"
msgid ""
"“Thou shalt not suffer a witch to live.”\n"
"    -KJV Bible, Exodus 22:18.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"“不可容女巫存活。”\n"
"    -KJV Bible, Exodus 22:18.\n"
"\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:__c_suffix"
msgid ""
"“When Peleus, some distance away, saw him torn apart by the frightful wound he\n"
" shouted: ‘Accept this tribute to the dead, at least, Crantor, dearest of\n"
" youths’, and with his powerful arm, he hurled his ash spear, at full strength,\n"
" at Demoleon. It ruptured the ribcage, and stuck quivering in the bone. The\n"
" centaur pulled out the shaft minus its head (he tried with difficulty to reach\n"
" that also) but the head was caught in his lung. The pain itself strengthened\n"
" his will: wounded, he reared up at his enemy and beat the hero down with his\n"
" hooves. Peleus received the resounding blows on helmet and shield, and\n"
" defending his upper arms, and controlling the weapon he held out, with one\n"
" blow through the arm he pierced the bi-formed breast.”\n"
"    -Ovid, _Metamorphoses_, XII, 330. 8 AD.\n"
msgstr ""
"“佩琉斯从远处看见他被可怕伤口撕裂，喊道：亲爱的克兰托尔，年轻人中最亲爱的，至少接受这份祭死贡礼。他奋力把白蜡木矛掷向德摩勒翁，刺裂肋笼，颤抖着钉入骨中。半人马拔出矛杆，却没拔出矛头，后者卡在肺里。痛苦反而增强斗志，他负伤立起，以蹄击倒英雄。佩琉斯用盔盾接住轰击，护住双臂，稳住武器，一击穿过对方手臂，刺入那双形的胸膛。”\n"
"    -Ovid, _Metamorphoses_, XII, 330. 8 AD.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:__d_suffix"
msgid ""
"“Trogdor was a man!\n"
" I mean, he was a dragon-man!\n"
" Or... maybe he was just a dragon.\n"
" ...\n"
" And the Trogdor comes in the night!”\n"
"    -The Brothers Chaps, “Trogdor”. 2003.\n"
msgstr ""
"“特罗格多是个人！\n"
"我是说，他是个龙人！\n"
"或者……也许只是条龙。\n"
"……\n"
"特罗格多在夜间来临！”\n"
"    -The Brothers Chaps, “Trogdor”. 2003.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:__q_suffix"
msgid "<__d_suffix>\n"
msgstr "<__d_suffix>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:__r_suffix"
msgid ""
"HAMLET [Drawing his sword.]: How now! a rat? Dead, for a ducat, dead\n"
"       [Stabs through the arras.]\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _The Tragedy of Hamlet, Prince of Denmark_, III, 4.\n"
"1603.\n"
msgstr ""
"哈姆雷特［拔剑］：怎么！老鼠？赌一枚金币，它死定了！\n"
"［隔着帷幔刺去。］\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _The Tragedy of Hamlet, Prince of Denmark_, III, 4.\n"
"1603.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:__cap-k_suffix"
msgid ""
"“The Parts Septentrionall are with these Sp'ryts Much haunted.. About the\n"
" places where they dig for Oare. The Greekes and Germans call them Cobali.”\n"
"    -Thomas Heywood, _The Hierarchy of the Blessed Angels_, Book IX, l. 568.\n"
"1635.\n"
msgstr ""
"“北方地区常被这些精灵出没，尤其采矿之处。希腊人与德意志人称它们为 Cobali。”\n"
"    -Thomas Heywood, _The Hierarchy of the Blessed Angels_, Book IX, l. 568.\n"
"1635.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:__cap-s_suffix"
msgid ""
"“The latter lived in the country, and before his house there was an oak, in\n"
" which there was a lair of snakes. His servants killed the snakes, but Melampus\n"
" gathered wood and burnt the reptiles, and reared the young ones. And when the\n"
" young were full grown, they stood beside him at each of his shoulders as he\n"
" slept, and they purged his ears with their tongues. He started up in a great\n"
" fright, but understood the voices of the birds flying overhead, and from what\n"
" he learned from them he foretold to men what should come to pass.”\n"
"    -Pseudo-Apollodorus , _Library and Epitome_, 1.9.11. circa 150 BC.\n"
"    trans. Sir James George Frazer, 1913.\n"
"\n"
"“A snake, with mottles rare,\n"
" Surveyed my chamber floor,\n"
" In feature as the worm before,\n"
" But ringed with power.”\n"
"    -Emily Dickinson, “In Winter In My Room”. circa 1860.\n"
msgstr ""
"“他住在乡间，屋前橡树中有蛇窝。仆人杀了蛇，墨兰波斯却捡柴焚葬蛇身，养育幼蛇。幼蛇长大后，在他睡眠时各守一肩，以舌舔净双耳。他惊醒，却能听懂头上飞鸟的声音，并据所闻向人预言未来。”\n"
"    -Pseudo-Apollodorus , _Library and Epitome_, 1.9.11. circa 150 BC.\n"
"    trans. Sir James George Frazer, 1913.\n"
"\n"
"“一条斑纹罕见的蛇，\n"
"打量着我屋子的地板；\n"
"外貌似从前的蠕虫，\n"
"却环绕着力量。”\n"
"    -Emily Dickinson, “In Winter In My Room”. circa 1860.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:__cap-t_suffix"
msgid ""
"“Buckshank bold and Elfinstone,\n"
" And more than I can mention here,\n"
" They caused to be built so stout a ship,\n"
" And unto Iceland they would steer.\n"
"\n"
" They launched the ship upon the main,\n"
" Which bellowed like a wrathful bear;\n"
" Down to the bottom the vessel sank,\n"
" A laidly Trold has dragged it there.”\n"
"    -George Borrow, _Lavengro: The Scholar, the Gypsy, the Priest_. 1851.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"“勇敢的巴克尚克与埃尔芬斯通，\n"
"还有许多难以尽数的人，\n"
"造了一艘坚固大船，\n"
"打算驶向冰岛。\n"
"\n"
"船入大海，海如怒熊咆哮；\n"
"船却沉向海底，\n"
"一只可憎的巨魔，\n"
"将它拖到那里。”\n"
"    -George Borrow, _Lavengro: The Scholar, the Gypsy, the Priest_. 1851.\n"
"\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:adder"
msgid ""
"ADDER, n. A species of snake. So called from its habit of adding funeral outlays\n"
"to the other expenses of living.\n"
"    -Ambrose Bierce, _The Devil's Dictionary_, 1906.\n"
msgstr ""
"蝰蛇，名词。一种蛇。其英文名 adder 源于它习惯在生活的其他开支上，再“加”一笔丧葬费。\n"
"    -Ambrose Bierce, _The Devil's Dictionary_, 1906.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:alderking"
msgid ""
"““My father, my father, he seizes me fast,\n"
" Full sorely the Erl-King has hurt me at last.”\n"
"\n"
" The father now gallops, with terror half wild,\n"
" He grasps in his arms the poor shuddering child;\n"
" He reaches his courtyard with toil and with dread,\n"
" The child in his arms finds he motionless, dead.”\n"
"    -Johann Wolfgang von Goethe, _Erlkönig_, 1782.\n"
"    trans. Edgar Alfred Bowring, 1853.\n"
msgstr ""
"“父亲，父亲，他紧紧抓我，\n"
"桤木之王终于把我重伤！\n"
"\n"
"父亲恐惧得近乎疯狂，策马狂奔，\n"
"紧抱可怜颤抖的孩子；\n"
"费尽力气、满怀惊惧抵达庭院，\n"
"才发现怀中孩子一动不动，死了。”\n"
"    -Johann Wolfgang von Goethe, _Erlkönig_, 1782.\n"
"    trans. Edgar Alfred Bowring, 1853.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:alligator"
msgid ""
"“Alligators commit errors of diet.”\n"
"    -Bennet Bowler, M.D., _Contributions to the Natural History of the\n"
"     Alligator, (Crocodilus Mississipiensis), with a Microscopic Addendum_,\n"
"     p. 17. 1846.\n"
msgstr ""
"“短吻鳄会犯饮食错误。”\n"
"    -Bennet Bowler, M.D., _Contributions to the Natural History of the\n"
"     Alligator, (Crocodilus Mississipiensis), with a Microscopic Addendum_,\n"
"     p. 17. 1846.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:apocalypse crab"
msgid ""
"“I should have been a pair of ragged claws\n"
" scuttling across the floors of silent seas.”\n"
"    -T.S. Eliot, _The Love Song of J. Alfred Prufrock_. 1915.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我本该是一双参差的蟹爪，\n"
"爬过寂静海洋的底部。”\n"
"    -T.S. Eliot, _The Love Song of J. Alfred Prufrock_. 1915.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:arcanist"
msgid "<occultist>\n"
msgstr "<occultist>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:basilisk"
msgid ""
"“Be thou like the imperial Basilisk\n"
" Killing thy foe with unapparent wounds!\n"
" Gaze on Oppression, till at that dread risk\n"
" Aghast she pass from the Earth's disk:\n"
" Fear not, but gaze—for freemen mightier grow,\n"
" And slaves more feeble, gazing on their foe:—\n"
" If Hope, and Truth, and Justice may avail,\n"
" Thou shalt be great—All hail!”\n"
"    -Percy Bysshe Shelley, “Posthumous Poems”. 1824.\n"
msgstr ""
"“愿你如帝王般的蛇怪，\n"
"以看不见的伤口杀敌！\n"
"凝视压迫，直到她惊惶\n"
"从大地上消失。\n"
"别怕，只管凝视；自由人因凝视敌人更强，\n"
"奴隶却更弱。\n"
"若希望、真理与正义有用，\n"
"你必伟大——向你致敬！”\n"
"    -Percy Bysshe Shelley, “Posthumous Poems”. 1824.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:bat"
msgid ""
"“The sun was set; the night came on apace,\n"
" And falling dews bewet around the place;\n"
" The bat takes airy rounds on leathern wings,\n"
" And the hoarse owl his woeful dirges sings.”\n"
"    -John Gay, Shepherd's Week, Wednesday; or, The Dumps.\n"
"\n"
"“Ere the bat hath flown\n"
" His cloister'd flight.”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _Macbeth_, III, 2, line 40. 1605.\n"
msgstr ""
"“太阳已落，夜色迅速来临，\n"
"露水落下，打湿四周；\n"
"蝙蝠以皮翼在空中盘旋，\n"
"沙哑猫头鹰唱起悲伤挽歌。”\n"
"    -John Gay, Shepherd's Week, Wednesday; or, The Dumps.\n"
"\n"
"“在蝙蝠完成\n"
"幽闭的飞行之前。”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _Macbeth_, III, 2, line 40. 1605.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:battlesphere"
msgid ""
"“I'm your only friend\n"
" I'm not your only friend\n"
" But I'm a little glowing friend\n"
" But really I'm not actually your friend\n"
" But I am”\n"
"    -They Might Be Giants, “Birdhouse in Your Soul”. 1989.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我是你唯一的朋友，\n"
"我不是你唯一的朋友，\n"
"但我是个发光的小朋友，\n"
"可实际上我并非你的朋友，\n"
"但我又是。”\n"
"    -They Might Be Giants, “Birdhouse in Your Soul”. 1989.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:bes kemwar"
msgid ""
"“The Bès Kěmwar, “maggot spirit”, is one of the many _bès_ or disease spirits\n"
" known to the Jah Hut of Malaysia. A polyvalent spirit, it is depicted as a\n"
" maggot or caterpillar, with variants distinguished by hair, thorns, wings, and\n"
" other details. It eats rice, vegetables, and other crops. It is responsible for\n"
" aches in bones, joints, and muscles. If its caterpillar hair falls into water\n"
" and that water is drunk, it causes coughing and bleeding in the throat. Maggot\n"
" spirits are also known to live in rotten tree trunks and feed in them. Anyone\n"
" who approaches the fallen tree will be bitten in the leg by the spirit, causing\n"
" redness, swelling, and itching. All the toenails fall off but the swelling will\n"
" be gone by two or three months.”\n"
"    - _A Book of Creatures_, 2020.\n"
msgstr ""
"“Bès Kěmwar，即‘蛆虫精灵’，是马来西亚 Jah Hut 人所知的众多 bès 疾病精灵之一。它形象多变，呈蛆或毛虫状，以毛、刺、翅膀等区别变体。它吃稻米、蔬菜及其他作物，引发骨、关节与肌肉疼痛。毛虫的毛落进水里，人喝了会咳嗽、喉咙出血。蛆虫精灵也住在腐树干中，以其为食。接近倒树者会被咬腿，发红、肿胀、发痒；脚趾甲全掉，肿胀则在两三个月后消退。”\n"
"    - _A Book of Creatures_, 2020.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:boggart"
msgid ""
"“He thinks every bush a boggart.”\n"
"    -John Ray, _A Compleat Collection of English Proverbs_. 1768.\n"
"\n"
"“A BOGGART intruded himself, upon what pretext or by what authority is unknown,\n"
" into the house of a quiet, inoffensive, and laborious farmer; and, when once\n"
" it had taken possession it disputed the right of domicile with the legal\n"
" mortal tenant, in a very unneighbourly and arbitrary manner. In particular, it\n"
" seemed to have a great aversion to children. As there is no point on which a\n"
" parent feels more acutely than that of the maltreatment of his offspring, the\n"
" feelings of the father and more particularly of his good dame, were daily, ay,\n"
" and nightly, harrowed up by the malice of this malignant and invisible\n"
" boggart.”\n"
"    -C.J.T., _Folk-lore and Legends: English_  1890.\n"
msgstr ""
"“他把每丛灌木都当成妖怪。”\n"
"    -John Ray, _A Compleat Collection of English Proverbs_. 1768.\n"
"\n"
"“一只妖怪不知借何理由、凭何权力，闯入安分、无害、勤劳农夫的屋子。占据以后，它便蛮横无理地与合法凡人住客争夺居住权，尤其厌恶孩子。父母最无法忍受的，莫过于子女受虐；因此，父亲尤其善良妻子的心，日日夜夜都被这邪恶隐形妖怪的恶意折磨。”\n"
"    -C.J.T., _Folk-lore and Legends: English_  1890.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:bullfrog"
msgid ""
"“Hello, my baby\n"
" Hello, my honey\n"
" Hello, my ragtime gal\n"
"\n"
" Send me a kiss by wire\n"
" Baby, my hearts on fire\n"
"\n"
" If you refuse me\n"
" Honey, you'll lose me\n"
" Then you'll be left alone\n"
"\n"
" Oh baby, telephone\n"
" And tell me I'm your own.”\n"
"    -Ida Emerson and Joseph E. Howard, “Hello My Baby!”\n"
msgstr ""
"“你好，宝贝，\n"
"你好，甜心，\n"
"你好，我的拉格泰姆姑娘。\n"
"\n"
"用电线送我一个吻，\n"
"宝贝，我的心在燃烧。\n"
"\n"
"若拒绝我，\n"
"亲爱的，你会失去我，\n"
"只剩自己孤单。\n"
"\n"
"宝贝，打电话来，\n"
"告诉我，我属于你。”\n"
"    -Ida Emerson and Joseph E. Howard, “Hello My Baby!”\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:bush"
msgid ""
"“And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the\n"
" midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and\n"
" the bush was not consumed.”\n"
"    -KJV Bible, Exodus 3:2.\n"
msgstr ""
"“耶和华的使者从荆棘中火焰里向他显现。他观看，见荆棘被火烧着，却没有烧毁。”\n"
"    -KJV Bible, Exodus 3:2.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:butterfly"
msgid ""
"“Happiness is a butterfly, which when pursued, is always just beyond your\n"
" grasp, but which, if you will sit down quietly, may alight upon you.”\n"
"    -Nathaniel Hawthorne\n"
msgstr ""
"“幸福是蝴蝶，追逐时总在手边之外；若你安静坐下，它却可能落到你身上。”\n"
"    -Nathaniel Hawthorne\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:cacodemon"
msgid ""
"“We'll call him Cacodemon, with his black Gib there, his Succuba, his Devil's\n"
" Seed, his Spawn of Phlegethon, that o’ my Consience was bred o’ the Spume of\n"
" Cocytus.”\n"
"    -John Fletcher, _The Knight of Malta_. 1647.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我们叫他邪魔，还有那只黑公猫、他的魅魔、魔鬼之种、弗勒革通之嗣；凭良心说，那肯定生自悲叹河的泡沫。”\n"
"    -John Fletcher, _The Knight of Malta_. 1647.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:catoblepas"
msgid ""
"“So passed he over into the island, taking with him the two brothers of\n"
" Anaxius; where he found the forsaken knight attired in his own livery, as\n"
" black as sorrow itself could see itself in the blackest glass: his ornaments\n"
" of the same hue, but formd into the figures of ravens which seemed to gape for\n"
" carrion: only his reins were snakes, which finely wrapping themselves one\n"
" within the other, their heads came together to the cheeks and bosses of the\n"
" bit, where they might seem to bite at the horse, and the horse, as he champed\n"
" the bit, to bite at them, and that the white foam was engendered by the\n"
" poisonous fury of the combat. His impresa was a Catoblepta, which so long lies\n"
" dead as the moon (whereto it hath so natural a sympathy) wants her light. The\n"
" word signified, that the moon wanted not the light, but the poor beast wanted\n"
" the moon's light.”\n"
"    -Sir Philip Sidney\n"
msgstr ""
"“他带着阿纳克修斯两兄弟渡到岛上，发现那被遗弃的骑士穿着自己的号衣，黑得如悲伤在最黑镜中所见自身。装饰同样黑，却铸成张口等腐肉的乌鸦；缰绳则是相互盘绕的蛇，蛇头聚在嚼口两旁，仿佛咬马，马嚼衔时也像咬蛇，白沫仿佛来自这场战斗的毒怒。徽记是一只卡托布莱帕：它与月亮天然相感，月失光时便如死去。题辞意为，缺的并非月自身之光，而是可怜野兽所需的月光。”\n"
"    -Sir Philip Sidney\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:cherub"
msgid ""
"“The glory of Yahweh mounted up from the cherub, and stood over the threshold\n"
" of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was full\n"
" of the brightness of Yahweh's glory.\n"
"\n"
" The sound of the wings of the cherubim was heard even to the outer court, as\n"
" the voice of God Almighty when he speaks.”\n"
"    -WEB Bible, Ezekiel 10:4-5\n"
msgstr ""
"“耶和华的荣耀从基路伯升起，停在殿门槛上，殿内充满云，院中满是荣耀的光。\n"
"\n"
"基路伯的翅声传到外院，如全能神说话的声音。”\n"
"    -WEB Bible, Ezekiel 10:4-5\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:chonchon"
msgid ""
"“In its simplest form it is a bird of the night, an owl (_Strix rufipes_) that\n"
" flies on silent wings during the night to announce illness, death, or some\n"
" other unwelcome event. When its croaking is heard it is advised to throw ash\n"
" into the air and utter a few prayers in the hopes of turning away its evil.\n"
"\n"
" The chonchón is also said to be a _calcu_ or evil sorcerer in disguise. It\n"
" resemble a human head, with oversized wing-like ears that allow it to fly.\n"
" During the night, these sorcerers’ heads detach themselves from their bodies\n"
" and fly around to cause mischief, invisible to most, their ominous _tué, tué,\n"
" tué_ call announcing misfortune. They have the same powers as sorcerers do,\n"
" and have been known to suck the blood of sleepers.”\n"
"    - _A Book of Creatures_, 2015.\n"
msgstr ""
"“最简单的形态，是一只夜鸟、棕林鸮（Strix rufipes），夜间无声飞翔，宣告疾病、死亡或其他不幸。听见沙哑叫声时，宜向空中撒灰并祈祷，希望驱走邪恶。\n"
"\n"
"据说琼琼也是伪装的 calcu 邪术师，形如人头，巨大的翼状耳朵使其飞行。夜晚，术士的头脱离身体，四处作祟，多数人看不见，只有不祥的 tué、tué、tué 声预示厄运。它们拥有术士之力，也会吸饮熟睡者的血。”\n"
"    - _A Book of Creatures_, 2015.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:crimson imp"
msgid ""
"“The Devil, too, sometimes steals human children; it is not infrequent for him\n"
" to carry away infants within the first six weeks after birth, and to\n"
" substitute in their place imps.”\n"
"    -Martin Luther\n"
msgstr ""
"“魔鬼有时也偷人类孩子；出生六周内的婴儿常被带走，换上小恶魔。”\n"
"    -Martin Luther\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:crocodile"
msgid ""
"“How doth the little crocodile\n"
"  Improve his shining tail,\n"
" And pour the waters of the Nile\n"
"  On every golden scale!\n"
"\n"
" How cheerfully he seems to grin,\n"
"  How neatly spreads his claws,\n"
" And welcomes little fishes in\n"
"  With gently smiling jaws!”\n"
"    -Lewis Carroll, _Alice's Adventures in Wonderland_, 1865.\n"
msgstr ""
"“小鳄鱼多会打理\n"
"自己闪亮的尾巴，\n"
"把尼罗河水浇在\n"
"每片金色鳞上！\n"
"\n"
"它笑得多快活，\n"
"爪张得多漂亮，\n"
"用温柔微笑的双颚，\n"
"欢迎小鱼进来！”\n"
"    -Lewis Carroll, _Alice's Adventures in Wonderland_, 1865.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:curse skull"
msgid ""
"“Good friend for Jesus’ sake forbear,\n"
" To dig the dust enclosed here.\n"
" Blessed be the man that spares these stones,\n"
" And cursed be he that moves my bones.”\n"
"    -Epitaph on William Shakespeare's grave\n"
msgstr ""
"“好朋友，看在耶稣分上，\n"
"别挖这里封存的尘土。\n"
"留下这些石头者有福，\n"
"挪动我骨头者受诅。”\n"
"    -Epitaph on William Shakespeare's grave\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:daeva"
msgid ""
"“Between these twain the Daevas also chose not aright, for infatuation came\n"
" upon them as they took counsel together, so that they chose the Worst Thought.\n"
" Then they rushed together to Violence, that they might enfeeble the world of\n"
" men.”\n"
"    -the Avesta, Yasna XXX, 6, Ahunavaiti Gatha.\n"
"    trans. Christian Bartholomae, 1951.\n"
msgstr ""
"“在两者之间，诸魔也未作正确选择；它们商议时受到迷妄，于是选择最恶之念。随后一同投向暴力，企图削弱人间世界。”\n"
"    -the Avesta, Yasna XXX, 6, Ahunavaiti Gatha.\n"
"    trans. Christian Bartholomae, 1951.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:demonspawn soul scholar"
msgid ""
"“Xinchub: At least you're conceding that I've got a soul.\n"
"   Petey: Yes, but it is battered, twisted, and drenched in the blood of the\n"
"          innocent.\n"
" Xinchub: Mmm... yeah.\n"
"   Petey: When you stop being pleased by that we'll know you're making\n"
"          progress.”\n"
"    -Howard Tayler, _Schlock Mercenary_. February 8, 2008.\n"
msgstr ""
"“辛丘布：至少你承认我有灵魂。\n"
"皮蒂：是，但它破损、扭曲，浸满无辜者的血。\n"
"辛丘布：嗯……没错。\n"
"皮蒂：等你不再为此高兴，我们就知道你进步了。”\n"
"    -Howard Tayler, _Schlock Mercenary_. February 8, 2008.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:diamond obelisk"
msgid ""
"“As one example of the meanings inherent in a form, let us examine a particular\n"
" form of vertical stone marker, variously called stele, obelisk, standing-stone,\n"
" and memorial column. These have been historically and commonly used to\n"
" commemorate honored phenomena. So, when a people wish to remember an important\n"
" relationship, event or personage, a location is dedicated to it and often\n"
" marked with an enduring and aspiring vertical form or sets of them. In natural\n"
" language, a vertical stone means: an aspiring connector between us (on earth)\n"
" and an ideal (up there); that we ‘stand up’ with pride about this honored\n"
" phenomenon. The marker is a symbolic inhabitation of the place it occupies. Its\n"
" size and workmanship is a sacrifice of much work and resources to a memory. It\n"
" is a strong suggestion (because we left it to them and it is of durable\n"
" material) that future people also give honor to the memorialized phenomenon.\n"
" When we use this particular physical form of the vertical marker, both its\n"
" historic use as an honorific and its meanings in natural language may well send\n"
" a message that this is an honored place, a place about a ‘good’ both in our\n"
" culture and in the culture of future observers.”\n"
"    -“Expert Judgment on Markers to Deter Inadvertent Human Intrusion into the\n"
"      Waste Isolation Pilot Plant”, Sandia National Laboratories report. 1993\n"
msgstr ""
"“以形态内含的意义为例，考察称作石碑、方尖碑、立石或纪念柱的竖直石标。历史上，它们通常用来纪念受尊崇之事。人们想记住重要关系、事件或人物时，会指定地点，常竖起耐久、向上的形体。自然语言中，立石意味着我们在地上与上方理想之间的奋起连接，也意味着为受敬重之事骄傲地站立。标志象征性占据其所在地点；大小与工艺，是为记忆献出大量劳力和资源。耐久材料和留给后人的事实，还强烈暗示未来人也应尊崇所纪念之物。因此，使用这种竖直标记，其历史上的尊荣用途及自然语言意义，很可能传达：此地值得敬重；无论对我们的文化还是未来观察者，这里都关乎一种‘善’。”\n"
"    -“Expert Judgment on Markers to Deter Inadvertent Human Intrusion into the\n"
"      Waste Isolation Pilot Plant”, Sandia National Laboratories report. 1993\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:oblivion hound"
msgid ""
"“Standing over Hugo, and plucking at his throat, there stood a foul thing, a\n"
" great, black beast, shaped like a hound, yet larger than any hound that ever\n"
" mortal eye has rested upon. And even as they looked the thing tore the throat\n"
" out of Hugo Baskerville...”\n"
"    -Arthur Conan Doyle, _The Hound of the Baskervilles_. 1902.\n"
msgstr ""
"“俯在雨果身上、撕扯其喉咙的是一个污秽怪物，一只巨大的黑兽，形似猎犬，却比凡人眼睛见过的任何猎犬都大。他们眼睁睁看着它扯出雨果·巴斯克维尔的喉咙……”\n"
"    -Arthur Conan Doyle, _The Hound of the Baskervilles_. 1902.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:dream sheep"
msgid ""
"“How undisturbed, the sleep of the foolish.”\n"
"    -Philip K. Dick\n"
msgstr ""
"“愚人睡得多安稳。”\n"
"    -Philip K. Dick\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:dryad"
msgid ""
" • Roy Quixote: Wait, what's my beef with clean energy again?\n"
" — Durkon Pansa: Dunno, but if'n ye prefer, I know a grove o'peach trees tha've\n"
"   been gettin' fresh wit tha locals.\n"
"    -Rich Burlew, “Haleo and Julean”\n"
msgstr ""
"• Roy Quixote：等等，我为什么又要跟清洁能源过不去？\n"
"— Durkon Pansa：不知道，不过你愿意的话，我知道有片桃树林，老对本地人动手动脚。\n"
"    -Rich Burlew, “Haleo and Julean”\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:efreet"
msgid ""
"“When the hoopoe returned to Solomon (he told him the news), and he responded\n"
" (to Sheba's people): “Are you giving me money? What GOD has given me is far\n"
" better than what He has given you. You are the ones to rejoice in such gifts.”\n"
" (To the hoopoe, he said), “Go back to them (and let them know that) we will\n"
" come to them with forces they cannot imagine. We will evict them, humiliated\n"
" and debased.” He said, “O you elders, which of you can bring me her mansion,\n"
" before they arrive here as submitters?” One afrit from the jinns said, “I can\n"
" bring it to you before you stand up. I am powerful enough to do this.”\n"
"    -The Quran, Sura 27 Al-Naml\n"
msgstr ""
"“戴胜鸟回到所罗门那里报告消息，他答复示巴人：你们用钱财赠我？真主给我的，远胜给你们的，你们才为这种礼物欢喜。他又吩咐戴胜鸟：回去告诉他们，我们将带来他们无法想象的军队，屈辱地将他们驱逐。他问长老：他们归顺到来前，你们谁能把她的宫殿带来？精灵中的一位强者说：我能在你起身前带来，我有足够力量。”\n"
"    -The Quran, Sura 27 Al-Naml\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:eidolon"
msgid ""
"“No sooner had sleep caught him, dissolving all his grief\n"
" as mists of refreshing slumber poured around him there—\n"
" his powerful frame was bone-weary from charging Hector\n"
" straight and hard to the walls of windswept Troy—\n"
" than the ghost of stricken Patroclus drifted up...\n"
" He was like the man to the life, every feature,\n"
" the same tall build and the fine eyes and voice\n"
" and the very robes that used to clothe his body.\n"
" Hovering at his head the phantom rose and spoke:\n"
" ‘Sleeping, Achilles? You’ve forgotten me, my friend.\n"
" You never neglected me in life, only now in death.\n"
" Bury me, quickly—let me pass the Gates of Hades.\n"
" They hold me off at a distance, all the souls,\n"
" the shades of the burnt-out, breathless dead,\n"
" never to let me cross the river, mingle with them...\n"
" They leave me to wander up and down, abandoned, lost\n"
" at the House of Death with the all-embracing gates.’”\n"
"    -Homer, _The Iliad_, XXIII, 72-88.\n"
"     trans. Robert Fagles, 1990.\n"
msgstr ""
"“睡眠刚攫住他，清新睡雾消去悲伤——\n"
"他曾猛烈追赶赫克托耳至风扫特洛伊城墙，\n"
"强健躯体已疲惫入骨——\n"
"死去帕特罗克洛斯的鬼魂便飘来。\n"
"容貌、身高、俊眼、声音，\n"
"乃至衣袍，都与生前无异。\n"
"幻影悬在头边，说：\n"
"‘睡着吗，阿喀琉斯？朋友，你忘了我。\n"
"生前从未冷落我，死后却如此。\n"
"快埋葬我，让我越过冥府之门。\n"
"死去、烧尽、失去呼吸的魂灵把我远远挡住，\n"
"不许渡河，不许与它们相聚。\n"
"我只能被遗弃、迷失地游荡，\n"
"在容纳一切的死亡宫门外。’”\n"
"    -Homer, _The Iliad_, XXIII, 72-88.\n"
"     trans. Robert Fagles, 1990.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:electric golem"
msgid ""
"“I sing the Body electric”\n"
"    -Walt Whitman, “I Sing the Body Electric”, _Leaves of Grass_. 1867.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我歌唱带电的身体。”\n"
"    -Walt Whitman, “I Sing the Body Electric”, _Leaves of Grass_. 1867.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:elephant"
msgid ""
"“And the King went to where the blind men were, and drawing near said to them:\n"
" ‘Do you now know what an elephant is like?’\n"
" ‘Assuredly, Lord: we now know what an elephant is like.’\n"
" ‘Tell me then, O blind men, what an elephant is like.’\n"
" And those blind men, O Bhikkhus, who had felt the head of the elephant, said:\n"
" ‘An elephant, Sir, is like a large round jar.\n"
" Those who had felt its ears, said: 'it is like a winnowing basket.’\n"
" Those who had felt its tusks, said: ‘it is like a plough-share.’\n"
" Those who had felt its trunk, said: ‘it is like a plough.’\n"
" Those who had felt its body, said: ‘it is like a granary.’\n"
" Those who had felt its feet, said: ‘it is like a pillar.’\n"
" Those who had felt its back, said: ‘it is like a mortar.’\n"
" Those who had felt its tail, said: ‘it is a like a pestle.’\n"
" Those who had felt the tuft of its tail, said: ‘it is like a broom.’\n"
" And they all fought amongst themselves with their fists, declaring, ‘such is\n"
" an elephant, such is not elephant, an elephant is not like that, it is like\n"
" this.’”\n"
" And the King, O Bhikkhus, was highly delighted.\n"
"    -_Udāna_, VI “Jaccandhavagga”. ca. 5th cent. B.C.\n"
"     trans. Dawsonne Melanchthon Strong, 1902.\n"
msgstr ""
"“王走到盲人面前问：如今知道大象像什么了吗？\n"
"他们回答：当然，主啊。\n"
"王又问：那说来听听。\n"
"摸头的说像大圆罐；摸耳的说像簸箕；摸牙的说像犁铧；摸鼻的说像犁；摸身的说像粮仓；摸脚的说像柱；摸背的说像臼；摸尾的说像杵；摸尾毛的说像扫帚。\n"
"他们挥拳互斗，喊道：大象就是这样，不是那样！\n"
"比丘们，王看得十分欢喜。”\n"
"    -_Udāna_, VI “Jaccandhavagga”. ca. 5th cent. B.C.\n"
"     trans. Dawsonne Melanchthon Strong, 1902.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:emperor scorpion"
msgid ""
"“Portents had occurred indicating [Titus Flavius Vespasianus'] approaching end,\n"
" such as the comet which was visible for a long time and the opening of the\n"
" mausoleum of Augustus of its own accord. When his physicians chided him for\n"
" continuing his usual course of living during his illness and attending to all\n"
" the duties that belonged to his office, he answered: ‘The emperor ought to die\n"
" on his feet.’”\n"
"    -Cassius Dio, _Roman History_, LXVI, xvii, 2. 222 A.D.\n"
"     trans. Earnest Cary, 1925.\n"
msgstr ""
"“预示韦斯帕芗末日将近的征兆已经出现：长久可见的彗星，以及奥古斯都陵墓自行打开。医生责备他患病仍维持日常起居、处理全部政务，他却答：皇帝应站着死。”\n"
"    -Cassius Dio, _Roman History_, LXVI, xvii, 2. 222 A.D.\n"
"     trans. Earnest Cary, 1925.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:endoplasm"
msgid ""
"“Sea horses floundering in the slimy mud,\n"
" Tossed up their heads, and dashed the ooze about them.”\n"
"    -John Dryden. _All For Love_, I, i, 15-17. 1678.\n"
msgstr ""
"“海马在黏滑泥浆里挣扎，\n"
"扬起头，将软泥甩向四周。”\n"
"    -John Dryden. _All For Love_, I, i, 15-17. 1678.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:entropy weaver"
msgid ""
"“SEE! warp is stretched\n"
" For warrior’s fall;\n"
" Lo, weft in loom,\n"
" ’Tis wet with blood;\n"
" Now, fight foreboding,\n"
" ’Neath friends’ swift fingers\n"
" Our gray woof waxeth\n"
" With war’s alarms,\n"
" Our warp blood-red,\n"
" Our weft corse-blue.\n"
"\n"
" This woof is y-woven\n"
" With entrails of men;\n"
" This warp is hard weighted\n"
" With heads of the slain;\n"
" Spears blood-besprinkled\n"
" For spindles we use,\n"
" Our loom iron-bound,\n"
" And arrows our reels;\n"
" With swords for our shuttles\n"
" This war-woof we work;\n"
" So weave we, weird sisters,\n"
" Our war-winning woof.\n"
"\n"
" Now war-winner walketh\n"
" To weave in her turn,\n"
" Now Sword-swinger steppeth,\n"
" Now Swift-stroke, now Storm;\n"
" When they speed the shuttle\n"
" How spear-heads shall flash!\n"
" Shields crash, and helm-gnawer\n"
" On harness bite hard!”\n"
"    -_The Story of Burnt Njal_, trans. George Dasent. 1861\n"
msgstr ""
"“看！经线已张，为战士倒下而织；\n"
"织机纬线湿透鲜血。\n"
"朋友快指下，灰布随战警而长，\n"
"经线血红，纬线尸青。\n"
"\n"
"这布以人的肠子织成，\n"
"经线坠着死者头颅；\n"
"血溅长矛作纺锤，\n"
"铁箍织机，箭作卷轴，\n"
"剑作梭子，织这战争之布。\n"
"我们，命运姐妹，织出制胜的布。\n"
"\n"
"赢战者前来轮织，\n"
"挥剑者、迅击者、风暴相继迈步。\n"
"梭子疾飞时，矛尖将闪耀，\n"
"盾牌碎裂，啃盔之刃\n"
"狠狠咬入甲胄！”\n"
"    -_The Story of Burnt Njal_, trans. George Dasent. 1861\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ettin"
msgid ""
"“But he had not been long in his hiding-hole, before the awful Ettin came in;\n"
" and no sooner was he in, than he was heard crying:\n"
" ‘Snouk but and snouk ben,\n"
"  I find the smell of an earthly man,\n"
"  Be he living, or be he dead,\n"
"  His heart this night shall kitchen my bread.’”\n"
"    -Joseph Jacobs, _The Red Ettin_\n"
msgstr ""
"“他躲进去不久，可怕的双头巨人便回来了，一进门就喊：\n"
"里里外外嗅一嗅，\n"
"我闻到凡人的味。\n"
"不论是生还是死，\n"
"今晚拿他的心下饭。”\n"
"    -Joseph Jacobs, _The Red Ettin_\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:executioner"
msgid ""
"“Behold the Lord High Executioner\n"
" A personage of noble rank and title —\n"
" A dignified and potent officer\n"
" Whose functions are particularly vital!\n"
" Defer, defer\n"
" To the Lord High Executioner!\n"
" Defer, defer\n"
" To the noble Lord, to the noble Lord\n"
" To the Lord High Executioner!”\n"
"    -Gilbert and Sullivan, “Behold the Lord High Executioner”,\n"
"      _The Mikado_. 1885\n"
msgstr ""
"“看，那位最高刽子手大人，\n"
"头衔与品级高贵；\n"
"威严而强大的官员，\n"
"职责尤其关乎性命！\n"
"尊敬，尊敬，\n"
"最高刽子手大人！\n"
"向高贵大人，向高贵大人，\n"
"向最高刽子手大人致敬！”\n"
"    -Gilbert and Sullivan, “Behold the Lord High Executioner”,\n"
"      _The Mikado_. 1885\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:fenstrider witch"
msgid ""
"“All the infections that sun sucks up\n"
" From bogs, fens, flats, on Prosper fall and make him\n"
" By inch-meal a disease! His spirits hear me\n"
" And yet I needs must curse.”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _The Tempest_, II, 2. 1611.\n"
msgstr ""
"“愿太阳从沼泽、湿地与滩涂\n"
"吸起的一切瘟病，都落到普罗斯佩罗身上，\n"
"一寸寸使他成为疾病！\n"
"他的精灵听见我，我却仍非诅咒不可。”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _The Tempest_, II, 2. 1611.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:fire crab"
msgid ""
"“The planet brought forth scintillating jewelled scuttling crabs, which the\n"
" Vogons ate, smashing their shells with iron mallets; tall aspiring trees with\n"
" breathtaking slenderness and colour which the Vogons cut down and burned the\n"
" crab meat with; elegant gazellelike creatures with silken coats and dewy eyes\n"
" which the Vogons would catch and sit on.”\n"
"    -Douglas Adams, _The Hitch-hiker's Guide to the Galaxy_. 1979.\n"
msgstr ""
"“这星球生出闪耀宝石的爬行螃蟹，沃贡人用铁锤砸壳吃掉；又生出高耸、细长而色彩惊人的树，沃贡人砍下烧烤蟹肉；还有丝绸皮毛、湿润眼睛、优雅如羚羊的生物，沃贡人捉来坐在屁股下。”\n"
"    -Douglas Adams, _The Hitch-hiker's Guide to the Galaxy_. 1979.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:flayed ghost"
msgid ""
"“Solamen miseris socios habuisse doloris.”\n"
"    -Christopher Marlowe, _Doctor Faustus_. 1604\n"
msgstr ""
"“苦难者的慰藉，是有同伴分担悲痛。”\n"
"    -Christopher Marlowe, _Doctor Faustus_. 1604\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:formless jellyfish"
msgid ""
"“From this story it is evident that in former times the jellyfish once had a\n"
"shell and bones something like a tortoise, but, ever since the Dragon King's\n"
"sentence was carried out on the ancestor of the jelly fishes, his descendants\n"
"have all been soft and boneless just as you see them to-day thrown up by the\n"
"waves high upon the shores of Japan.”\n"
"    -“The Jellyfish and the Monkey”, adapted by Yei Theodora Ozaki, _Young\n"
"     Folk's Treasury_, vol. II. 1909.\n"
msgstr ""
"“故事清楚表明，水母从前也像龟，有壳有骨。但自龙王判决在水母祖先身上执行后，它的后代便都柔软无骨，正如如今被海浪冲上日本岸边的模样。”\n"
"    -“The Jellyfish and the Monkey”, adapted by Yei Theodora Ozaki, _Young\n"
"     Folk's Treasury_, vol. II. 1909.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ghost moth"
msgid ""
"“Always in focus\n"
" You can't feel my stare.\n"
" I zoom into you\n"
" You don't know I'm there.”\n"
"    -Judas Priest, “Electric Eye”. 1982.\n"
msgstr ""
"“始终对准焦点，\n"
"你感觉不到我的凝视。\n"
"我拉近你的影像，\n"
"你却不知我在那里。”\n"
"    -Judas Priest, “Electric Eye”. 1982.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ghoul"
msgid ""
"“In the desert\n"
" I saw a creature, naked, bestial,\n"
" Who, squatting upon the ground,\n"
" Held his heart in his hands,\n"
" And ate of it.\n"
" I said, ‘Is it good, friend?’\n"
" ‘It is bitter — bitter’, he answered,\n"
" ‘But I like it\n"
" Because it is bitter,\n"
" And because it is my heart.’”\n"
"    -Stephen Crane, _The Black Riders and Other Lines_. 1895.\n"
msgstr ""
"“在沙漠里，我见一生物，赤裸、野蛮，\n"
"蹲在地上，双手捧心，吃着它。\n"
"我问：朋友，好吃吗？\n"
"它答：苦，苦。\n"
"但我喜欢，\n"
"因为它苦，\n"
"因为它是我的心。”\n"
"    -Stephen Crane, _The Black Riders and Other Lines_. 1895.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:glass eye"
msgid ""
"“El ojo que ves\n"
" no es ojo porque tú lo veas,\n"
" es ojo porque te ve.”\n"
"    -Antonio Machado, Campos de Castilla. 1912-1917.\n"
msgstr ""
"“你看见的眼睛，\n"
"不是因为被你看见才是眼睛，\n"
"而是因为它看着你。”\n"
"    -Antonio Machado, Campos de Castilla. 1912-1917.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:gnoll"
msgid ""
"“Then he descended softly and beckoned to Nuth. But the gnoles had watched him\n"
" through knavish holes that they bore in trunks of the trees, and the unearthly\n"
" silence gave way, as it were with a grace, to the rapid screams of Tonker as\n"
" they picked him up from behind — screams that came faster and faster until\n"
" they were incoherent. And where they took him it is not good to ask, and what\n"
" they did with him I shall not say.”\n"
"    -Lord Dunsany, “How Nuth Would Have Practised His Art Upon the Gnoles”.\n"
"1912.\n"
msgstr ""
"“他轻轻下去，向纳思示意。但豺狼人已透过树干上狡猾的窥孔注视他。诡异寂静仿佛优雅退场，换成它们从背后抓起汤克时急促的惨叫，越来越快，最终不成声音。它们把他带去哪里，最好别问；对他做了什么，我不说。”\n"
"    -Lord Dunsany, “How Nuth Would Have Practised His Art Upon the Gnoles”.\n"
"1912.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:goblin"
msgid ""
"“Swish, smack! Whip crack!\n"
" Batter and beat! Yammer and bleat!\n"
" Work, work! Nor dare to shirk,\n"
" While Goblins quaff, and Goblins laugh,\n"
" Round and round far underground\n"
" Below, my lad!”\n"
"    -J.R.R. Tolkien, _The Hobbit_\n"
msgstr ""
"“唰，啪！鞭子抽！\n"
"敲打，殴打！哀叫，嘶嚎！\n"
"干活，干活！谁敢偷懒，\n"
"地精痛饮，地精大笑，\n"
"在遥远地下转啊转，\n"
"下面，小子！”\n"
"    -J.R.R. Tolkien, _The Hobbit_\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:golden dragon"
msgid ""
"“You do not come dramatically, with dragons\n"
" That rear up with my life between their paws\n"
" And dash me butchered down beside the wagons”\n"
"    -Philip Larkin, “To Failure”. 1949.\n"
msgstr ""
"“你并非戏剧般带着巨龙而来，\n"
"巨龙昂起，把我的生命夹在爪间，\n"
"屠碎后摔在车旁。”\n"
"    -Philip Larkin, “To Failure”. 1949.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:golden eye"
msgid ""
"“No coveting nor envy burns\n"
"   In thy bright golden eye,\n"
" That calm and innocently turns\n"
"   On all below the sky.”\n"
"    -Hannah Flagg Gould, _The Youth's Coronal_\n"
msgstr ""
"“你明亮的金色眼里，\n"
"没有贪欲，也无嫉妒燃烧；\n"
"它平静、天真地，\n"
"望向天空下的一切。”\n"
"    -Hannah Flagg Gould, _The Youth's Coronal_\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:guardian golem"
msgid ""
"“‘Listen Reb _Golem_,’ the old man said, wagging his finger. ‘Pay attention to\n"
"  what I say—you understand?’\n"
" ‘Understand...’\n"
" ‘If you want to stay here, you got to do like Mr. Gumbeiner says.’\n"
" ‘Do-like-Mr.-Gumbeiner-says...’\n"
" ‘_That's_ the way I like to hear a golem talk. Malka, give here the mirror\n"
"  from the pocketbook. Look, you see your face? You see on the forehead, what's\n"
"  written? If you don't do like Mr. Gumbeiner says, he'll wipe out what's\n"
"  written and you'll be no more alive.’\n"
" ‘No-more-alive...’\n"
" ‘_That's_ right. Now, listen. Under the porch you'll find a lawnmower. Take\n"
"  it. And cut the lawn. Then come back. Go.’”\n"
"    -Avram Davidson, “The Golem”, 1955.\n"
msgstr ""
"“老人摇指说：听着，魔像先生，认真听，懂吗？\n"
"‘懂……’\n"
"‘想住这里，就照贡拜纳先生的话做。’\n"
"‘照贡拜纳先生的话做……’\n"
"‘这才像魔像说的话。玛尔卡，把包里的镜子拿来。看见自己的脸吗？额上写着什么？不听话，他就擦掉字，你便不再活。’\n"
"‘不再活……’\n"
"‘没错。门廊下有割草机，拿去割草，再回来。去。’”\n"
"    -Avram Davidson, “The Golem”, 1955.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:guardian sphinx"
msgid ""
"“The Second Coming! Hardly are those words out\n"
" When a vast image out of Spiritus Mundi\n"
" Troubles my sight: somewhere in sands of the desert\n"
" A shape with lion body and the head of a man,\n"
" A gaze blank and pitiless as the sun,\n"
" Is moving its slow thighs, while all about it\n"
" Reel shadows of the indignant desert birds.”\n"
"    -W. B. Yeats, \"The Second Coming\". 1920.\n"
msgstr ""
"“再临！话刚出口，\n"
"世界之灵中一个巨大影像便困扰视线：\n"
"沙漠某处，狮身人首的形体，\n"
"目光如太阳般空洞无情，\n"
"缓慢移动大腿；四周，\n"
"愤怒沙漠鸟的影子盘旋。”\n"
"    -W. B. Yeats, \"The Second Coming\". 1920.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:harpy"
msgid ""
"“Bird-bodied, girl-faced things they are; abominable their droppings, their\n"
" hands are talons, their faces haggard with hunger insatiable.”\n"
"    -Virgil, Aeneid 3\n"
"\n"
"“And Phineus had scarcely taken the first morsel up when, with as little\n"
" warning as a whirlwind or a lightning flash, they dropped from the clouds\n"
" proclaiming their desire for food with raucous cries. The young lords saw them\n"
" coming and raised the alarm. Yet they had hardly done so before the Harpyiai\n"
" had devoured the whole meal and were on the wing once more, far out at sea.\n"
" All they left was an intolerable stench.”\n"
"    -Apollonius Rhodius, Argonautica 2. 179 — 434\n"
msgstr ""
"“它们鸟身少女面，粪便恶臭，双手是利爪，脸因永不满足的饥饿而憔悴。”\n"
"    -Virgil, Aeneid 3\n"
"\n"
"“菲纽斯才举起第一口食物，它们便如旋风闪电般毫无预警地从云中降下，以嘶哑叫声宣告饥饿。年轻领主看见，急忙报警，却几乎尚未出声，鸟妖就已吃光整餐，再次飞向远海。只留下无法忍受的恶臭。”\n"
"    -Apollonius Rhodius, Argonautica 2. 179 — 434\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:hell hound"
msgid ""
"“About her middle round\n"
" A cry of Hell-hounds never-ceasing barked\n"
" With wide Cerberean mouths full loud, and rung\n"
" A hideous peal; yet, when they list, would creep,\n"
" If aught disturbed their noise, into her womb,\n"
" And kennel there; yet there still barked and howled\n"
" Within unseen.”\n"
"    -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_, Book II, 1667.\n"
msgstr ""
"“她腰间一圈地狱犬，\n"
"以刻耳柏洛斯般的巨口不停狂吠，\n"
"响成可怕钟声。有时，\n"
"若有什么打断吠叫，它们便爬回子宫，\n"
"在里面筑窝，却仍在看不见处\n"
"狂吠、嚎叫。”\n"
"    -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_, Book II, 1667.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:hell knight"
msgid ""
"“Ok, let's review. It's up to the fair young maiden to rescue the dragon from\n"
" the fire breathing knights in shining armour.”\n"
"    -Exiern\n"
msgstr ""
"“好，复习一下：这回该由美丽少女，把龙从喷火的闪甲骑士手中救出来。”\n"
"    -Exiern\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:hobgoblin"
msgid ""
"“A foolish consistency is the hobgoblin of little minds, adored by little\n"
" statesmen and philosophers and divines.”\n"
"    -Ralph Waldo Emerson, _Essays: First Series_, Essay II: Self-Reliance.\n"
"     1841.\n"
msgstr ""
"“愚蠢的一致性，是小心灵的妖怪，受渺小政客、哲人和神学家崇拜。”\n"
"    -Ralph Waldo Emerson, _Essays: First Series_, Essay II: Self-Reliance.\n"
"     1841.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:hog"
msgid ""
"“Fern came slowly down the stairs. Her eyes were red from crying. As she\n"
" approached her chair, the carton wobbled, and there was a scratching noise.\n"
" Fern looked at her father. Then she lifted the lid of the carton. There,\n"
" inside, looking up at her, was the newborn pig. It was a white one. The\n"
" morning light shone through its ears, turning them pink. “He's yours,” said\n"
" Mr. Arable.  “Saved from an untimely death. And may the good Lord forgive me\n"
" for this foolishness.”\n"
"    -E.B. White, _Charlotte's Web_\n"
msgstr ""
"“芬慢慢走下楼，眼睛哭红了。走近椅子时，纸箱晃动，传来抓挠声。她看父亲，再揭开箱盖。里面，一只新生小猪抬头看她，白白的，晨光透过耳朵，染成粉红。阿拉布尔先生说：它归你了，从夭折中救回来。愿主原谅我这愚行。”\n"
"    -E.B. White, _Charlotte's Web_\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:hound"
msgid ""
"“A traveller, by the faithful hound, Half-buried in the snow was found, Still\n"
" grasping in his hand of ice That banner with the strange device, Excelsior!”\n"
"    -Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, “Excelsior”\n"
msgstr ""
"“忠犬找到旅人，半埋雪中；\n"
"冰冷手里仍紧握着\n"
"那面写有奇异铭文的旗：\n"
"更高！”\n"
"    -Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, “Excelsior”\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:human"
msgid ""
"“Do you know\n"
" Do I know\n"
" What's this thing called ‘man’?\n"
" God only knows what a man is!\n"
" I only know his price.”\n"
"    -Bertolt Brecht, “The Measures Taken”. 1930.\n"
msgstr ""
"“你知道吗？\n"
"我知道吗？\n"
"所谓‘人’是什么？\n"
"只有神知道人是什么！\n"
"我只知道他的价钱。”\n"
"    -Bertolt Brecht, “The Measures Taken”. 1930.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:iguana"
msgid ""
"“Once on a time when Brahmadatta was reigning in Benares, the Bodhisatta was\n"
" born an iguana. When he grew up he dwelt in a big burrow in the river bank\n"
" with a following of many hundreds of other iguanas. Now the Bodhisatta had a\n"
" son, a young iguana, who was great friends with a chameleon, whom he used to\n"
" clip and embrace. This intimacy being reported to the iguana king, he sent for\n"
" his young son and said that such friendship was misplaced, for chameleons were\n"
" low creatures, and that if the intimacy was persisted in, calamity would\n"
" befall the whole of the tribe of iguanas. And he enjoined his son to have no\n"
" more to do with the chameleon. But the son continued in his intimacy.”\n"
"    -_Khuddaka Nikāya_, Jātaka 141 “Godha-jātaka”. ca. 4th cent. B.C.\n"
"     trans. Robert Chalmers, 1895.\n"
msgstr ""
"“从前梵授王统治波罗奈时，菩萨生为鬣蜥，长大后带着数百同类住在河岸大洞中。其子与一只变色龙亲密，常相拥。鬣蜥王听说后，召儿子告诫：这友谊不当，变色龙是低等生物，若继续亲近，灾难将临整个族群，令其不再来往。但儿子依然如故。”\n"
"    -_Khuddaka Nikāya_, Jātaka 141 “Godha-jātaka”. ca. 4th cent. B.C.\n"
"     trans. Robert Chalmers, 1895.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:jackal"
msgid ""
"“Always ready to take advantage of every favourable opportunity, the Jackal is\n"
" a sad parasite, and hangs on the skirts of the larger carnivora as they roam\n"
" the country for prey, in the hope of securing some share of the creatures\n"
" which they destroy or wound.”\n"
"    -John George Wood, _The Illustrated Natural History: Mammalia_. 1865.\n"
msgstr ""
"“豺狼随时准备利用有利机会，是个可悲寄生者，尾随大型食肉兽在乡野觅食，盼着分到被它们杀死或咬伤的猎物。”\n"
"    -John George Wood, _The Illustrated Natural History: Mammalia_. 1865.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:jelly"
msgid ""
"“Beware of the Blob!\n"
" It creeps\n"
" And leaps\n"
" and glides and slides\n"
" Across the floor\n"
" Right through the door\n"
" And all around the wall,\n"
" A splotch, a blotch...”\n"
"    -Burt Bacharach and Mack David, “Beware of the Blob”. 1958.\n"
msgstr ""
"“当心胶怪！\n"
"它爬，它跳，\n"
"滑来又滑去，\n"
"越过地板，穿过门，\n"
"绕着墙，\n"
"一团斑迹，一块污痕……”\n"
"    -Burt Bacharach and Mack David, “Beware of the Blob”. 1958.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:killer klown"
msgid ""
"“All the world loves a clown.”\n"
"    -Cole Porter, “Be a Clown”. 1948.\n"
msgstr ""
"“全世界都爱小丑。”\n"
"    -Cole Porter, “Be a Clown”. 1948.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:kobold"
msgid ""
"“Kobolds are harmless.”\n"
"    -Bearand the Bold, epitaph (Magic: the Gathering)\n"
msgstr ""
"“狗头人无害。”\n"
"    -Bearand the Bold, epitaph (Magic: the Gathering)\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:komodo dragon"
msgid ""
"“The three of us were sitting ashen faced as if we had just witnessed a foul\n"
" and malignant murder. At least if we had been watching a murder the murderer\n"
" wouldn't have been looking us impassively in the eye as he did it. Maybe it\n"
" was the feeling of cold unflinching arrogance that so disturbed us. But\n"
" whatever malign emotions we tried to pin on to the lizard, we knew that they\n"
" weren't the lizard's emotions at all, only ours. The lizard was simply going\n"
" about its lizardly business in a simple, straightforward lizardly way. It\n"
" didn't know anything about the horror, the guilt, the shame, the ugliness that\n"
" we, uniquely guilty and ashamed animals, were trying to foist on it. So we got\n"
" it all straight back at us, as if reflected in the mirror of its single\n"
" unwavering and disinterested eye.”\n"
"    -Douglas Adams, “Last Chance to See”. 1990.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我们三人脸色惨白，像刚目睹邪恶凶杀。但若真是凶杀，凶手至少不会一边杀，一边毫无感情地直视我们。也许是冷漠而不动摇的傲慢使我们不安。不过，无论试图给蜥蜴附上何种恶意感情，我们知道那都不是它的感情，只是我们的。蜥蜴只以简单直接、蜥蜴式的方法做蜥蜴的事，不懂我们这些独有负罪与羞耻感的动物，想强加给它的恐怖、罪恶、羞耻与丑陋。因此一切反射回来，仿佛映在那只毫不动摇、漠不关心的眼睛里。”\n"
"    -Douglas Adams, “Last Chance to See”. 1990.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:kraken"
msgid ""
"“... Kraken, also called the Crab-fish, which [according to the pilots of\n"
" Norway] is not that huge, for heads and tails counted, he is no larger than\n"
" our Öland is wide [i.e. less than 16 km] ... He stays at the sea floor,\n"
" constantly surrounded by innumerable small fishes, who serve as his food and\n"
" are fed by him in return: for his meal, if I remember correctly what E.\n"
" Pontoppidan writes, lasts no longer than three months, and another three are\n"
" then needed to digest it. His excrements nurture in the following an army of\n"
" lesser fish, and for this reason, fishermen plumb after his resting place ...\n"
" Gradually, Kraken ascends to the surface, and when he is at ten to twelve\n"
" fathoms, the boats had better move out of his vicinity, as he will shortly\n"
" thereafter burst up, like a floating island, spurting water from his dreadful\n"
" nostrils and making ring waves around him, which can reach many miles. Could\n"
" one doubt that this is the Leviathan of Job?”\n"
"    -Jacob Wallenberg, “Min son på galejan”. 1781.\n"
msgstr ""
"“克拉肯，又称蟹鱼，据挪威领航员说并不算大：连头带尾，也不过厄兰岛那么宽，不到十六公里。它卧在海底，被无数小鱼包围，吃鱼，也反过来养鱼。据我记得蓬托皮丹所写，一餐不超过三个月，再用三个月消化；排泄物滋养小鱼大军，因此渔人测深寻找其栖处。它渐渐上浮，到水深十至十二噚时，船最好远离，因为它很快会像浮岛冲出水面，从可怕鼻孔喷水，激起延伸数英里的环浪。谁还能怀疑，这就是约伯的利维坦？”\n"
"    -Jacob Wallenberg, “Min son på galejan”. 1781.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:large abomination"
msgid "<small abomination>\n"
msgstr "<small abomination>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:lindwurm"
msgid ""
"“Freilich verbürgt uns keine Silbe die Existenz von solcherlei Thieren, wenn\n"
" wir uns den Drachen oder Lindwurm als ein Ungeheuer vorstellen, dessen langer\n"
" Hals in einen Adler-, Löwen- oder Delphinenkopf endigt; das auf dem breiten\n"
" Rücken Greifs- oder Nachisittige trägt; und am vielfach\n"
" gerollten Schweif einen Stachel mit Widerhaken hat; Feuer speit; sich in\n"
" Mädchen verliebt und diese entführt; bald diese bald jene Gestalt annimmt; auf\n"
" sauer erworbenen Schatzen ruht — kurz, als ein Ungeheuer, das alle\n"
" Eigenschaften besitzt, welche die Fabel ihm andichtet; dann wäre es Wahnsinn,\n"
" an Drachen und Lindwürmer glauben zu wollen. Nehmen wir aber dafür bloß ein\n"
" furchtbares Ungeheuer überhaupt, welches nun aus unserem Welttheile vertilgt\n"
" ist, so hat der Glaube daran nichts Lächerliches.”\n"
"    -Leopold Ziegelhauſer, _Schattenbilder der Vorzeit: Ein Kranz von\n"
"     Geschichten, Sagen, Legenden, Märchen, Skizzen und Heldenmahlen, Aus allen\n"
"     Gegenden Deutschlands und des österreichischen Kaiserstaates_. 1844.\n"
msgstr ""
"“若把龙想成长颈尽头接鹰、狮或海豚头，阔背生狮鹫或其他翅膀，盘尾带倒钩，喷火，爱上并掳走少女，随意变形，趴在辛苦积来的宝藏上，总之拥有传说赋予的一切特征的怪物，那么没有一个字能保证它存在，相信它便是疯狂。但若只指一种可怕、如今已从我们这片世界灭绝的巨兽，相信它便没有什么可笑。”\n"
"    -Leopold Ziegelhauſer, _Schattenbilder der Vorzeit: Ein Kranz von\n"
"     Geschichten, Sagen, Legenden, Märchen, Skizzen und Heldenmahlen, Aus allen\n"
"     Gegenden Deutschlands und des österreichischen Kaiserstaates_. 1844.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:lost soul"
msgid ""
"“She walks in the twilight, her steps make no sound,\n"
"  Her feet leave no tracks on the dew-covered ground.\n"
" Her hand gently beckons, she whispers your name—\n"
"  But those who go with her are never the same.”\n"
"    -Magic: the Gathering\n"
msgstr ""
"“她走在暮色里，脚步无声，\n"
"露地上不留足迹。\n"
"她轻轻招手，低唤你的名字，\n"
"但随她去的人，再也不会相同。”\n"
"    -Magic: the Gathering\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:manticore"
msgid ""
"“Ctesias writeth, that in Aethiopia likewise there is a beast which he calleth\n"
" Mantichora, having three rankes of teeth, which when they meet togither are\n"
" let in one within another like the teeth of combes: with the face and eares of\n"
" a man, with red eyes; of colour sanguine, bodied like a lyon, and having a\n"
" taile armed with a sting like a scorpion: his voice resembleth the noise of a\n"
" flute and trumpet sounded together: very swift he is, and mans flesh of all\n"
" others hee most desireth.”\n"
"    -Pliny the Elder, _Natural History_, Book 8, Chapter XXI\n"
msgstr ""
"“克忒西亚斯说，埃塞俄比亚有兽名蝎尾狮，牙有三排，合起时像梳齿彼此嵌入；人面人耳，红眼，血色，狮身，尾带蝎刺；声音如笛与号同响，行动极快，所有肉中最爱人肉。”\n"
"    -Pliny the Elder, _Natural History_, Book 8, Chapter XXI\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:meliai"
msgid ""
"“And Heaven came, bringing on night and longing for love, and he lay about Earth\n"
" spreading himself full upon her. Then the son from his ambush stretched forth\n"
" his left hand and in his right took the great long sickle with jagged teeth,\n"
" and swiftly lopped off his own father's members and cast them away to fall\n"
" behind him. And not vainly did they fall from his hand; for all the bloody\n"
" drops that gushed forth Earth received, and as the seasons moved round she bare\n"
" the strong Erinyes and the great Giants with gleaming armour, holding long\n"
" spears in their hands, and the Nymphs whom they call Meliae all over the\n"
" boundless earth.”\n"
"    -Hesiod, _Theogony_, 182-187, trans. H.G. Evelyn-White. 1920\n"
msgstr ""
"“天带着夜与爱欲到来，覆在地上。儿子从埋伏中伸左手，右手持巨大长锯齿镰，迅速割下父亲生殖器，抛到身后。它们并未徒然坠落：喷出的血滴全由大地承接。时序流转，大地生出强大的复仇女神、披亮甲持长枪的巨人，以及遍布无边大地、名为墨利埃的宁芙。”\n"
"    -Hesiod, _Theogony_, 182-187, trans. H.G. Evelyn-White. 1920\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:merfolk"
msgid ""
"“Again at length my thought reviving came,\n"
" When I no longer found my self the same;\n"
" Then first this sea-green beard I felt to grow,\n"
" And these large honours on my spreading brow;\n"
" My long-descending locks the billows sweep,\n"
" And my broad shoulders cleave the yielding deep;\n"
" My fishy tail, my arms of azure hue,\n"
" And ev'ry part divinely chang'd, I view.”\n"
"    -Ovid, _Metamorphoses_, XIII, 546-7. 8 A.D.\n"
"     trans. Garth, Dryden, et al.\n"
msgstr ""
"“心思终于再度苏醒，\n"
"却发现我已不是原来的自己。\n"
"海绿胡须开始生长，\n"
"额头宽展，添了华饰；\n"
"长发扫过波浪，\n"
"阔肩劈开柔顺深水。\n"
"我看见鱼尾、碧蓝双臂，\n"
"每个部位都被神奇地改变。”\n"
"    -Ovid, _Metamorphoses_, XIII, 546-7. 8 A.D.\n"
"     trans. Garth, Dryden, et al.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:merfolk aquamancer"
msgid ""
"“Lord, Lord! methought, what pain it was to drown!\n"
" What dreadful noise of waters in mine ears!\n"
" What ugly sights of death within mine eyes!\n"
" Methought I saw a thousand fearful wrecks,\n"
" Ten thousand men that fishes gnawed upon,\n"
" Wedges of gold, great anchors, heaps of pearl,\n"
" Inestimable stones, unvalued jewels,\n"
" All scattered in the bottom of the sea:\n"
" Some lay in dead men’s skulls; and in those holes\n"
" Where eyes did once inhabit, there were crept,\n"
" As ’t were in scorn of eyes, reflecting gems.”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _King Richard III_, I, iv. 1597\n"
msgstr ""
"“主啊，溺水何等痛苦！\n"
"耳中可怕的水声，眼里丑恶的死亡！\n"
"我仿佛看见千艘骇人沉船，\n"
"万具被鱼啃食的人，\n"
"金锭、巨锚、珍珠堆，\n"
"无价石与宝玉散落海底。\n"
"有的躺在死人头骨中，\n"
"曾容双眼的孔穴里爬入反光宝石，\n"
"仿佛嘲笑眼睛。”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _King Richard III_, I, iv. 1597\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:merfolk avatar"
msgid ""
"“Then up it raise the mermaiden,\n"
" Wi the comb an glass in her hand:\n"
" ‘Here's a health to you, my merrie young men,\n"
" For you never will see dry land.’”\n"
"    -“Sir Patrick Spens”, Scottish folk song, version 58J in Francis James\n"
"     Child, _The English and Scottish Popular Ballads_. 1898.\n"
msgstr ""
"“美人鱼浮上来，\n"
"手拿梳子与镜子：\n"
"敬你们一杯，快活年轻人，\n"
"你们再也见不到陆地。”\n"
"    -“Sir Patrick Spens”, Scottish folk song, version 58J in Francis James\n"
"     Child, _The English and Scottish Popular Ballads_. 1898.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:merfolk impaler"
msgid ""
"“Damn ye! Let Neptune strike ye dead, Winslow! HAAARK! Hark Triton, hark!\n"
" Bellow, bid our father the Sea King rise from the depths full foul in his fury!\n"
" Black waves teeming with salt-foam to smother this young mouth with pungent\n"
" slime, to choke ye, engorging your organs ‘til ye turn blue and bloated with\n"
" bilge and brine and can scream no more -- only when he, crowned in cockle\n"
" shells with slitherin’ tentacled tail and steaming beard take up his fell\n"
" be-finnéd arm, his coral-tine trident screeches banshee-like in the tempest and\n"
" plunges right through yer gullet, bursting ye -- a bulging bladder no more, but\n"
" a blasted bloody film now -- a nothing for the harpies and the souls of dead\n"
" sailors to peck and claw and feed upon, only to be lapped up and swallowed by\n"
" the infinite waters of the dread emperor himself -- forgotten to any man, to\n"
" any time, forgotten to any god or devil, forgotten even to the sea, for any\n"
" stuff or part of Winslow, even any scantling of your soul is Winslow no more,\n"
" but is now itself the sea!”\n"
"    -Thomas Wake, _The Lighthouse_. 2019\n"
msgstr ""
"“该死的温斯洛！愿海神将你击毙！听啊，特里同，听！咆哮，唤我们的海王父亲从深处愤怒而起！黑浪满载盐沫，以刺鼻黏液堵住你的年轻嘴巴，呛死你，灌满内脏，让你因舱底污水与盐水变得青紫肿胀，再也无法叫喊。直到祂头戴贝壳冠，拖着滑溜触须尾、蒸腾胡须，举起带鳍恶臂，珊瑚尖三叉戟在风暴中如女妖尖叫，贯穿你的咽喉，将你刺爆！不再是鼓胀皮囊，只剩破碎血膜，任鸟妖和亡水手之魂啄抓吞吃，最后被可怕帝王无尽的海水舔食咽下。被所有人、所有时代遗忘，被神和魔遗忘，甚至被海遗忘，因为温斯洛的任何一部分，哪怕一丝灵魂，都不再是温斯洛，而是海本身！”\n"
"    -Thomas Wake, _The Lighthouse_. 2019\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:merfolk javelineer"
msgid "<merfolk>\n"
msgstr "<merfolk>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:merfolk siren"
msgid ""
"“Row'd on, in reach of an erected voice,\n"
" The Sirens soon took note, without our noise,\n"
" Tuned those sweet accents that made charms so strong,\n"
" And these learn'd numbers made the Sirens' song:\n"
" ‘Come here, thou worthy of a world of praise,\n"
" That dost so high the Grecian glory raise,\n"
" Ulysses! stay thy ship, and that song hear\n"
" That none past ever but it bent his ear,\n"
" But left him ravish'd, and instructed more\n"
" By us, than any ever heard before.\n"
" For we know all things whatsoever were\n"
" In wide Troy labour'd; whatsoever there\n"
" The Grecians and the Trojans both sustain'd\n"
" By those high issues that the Gods ordain'd.\n"
" And whatsoever all the earth can show\n"
" T' inform a knowledge of desert, we know.’”\n"
"    -Homer, _The Odyssey_, XII, 268-82.\n"
"     trans. George Chapman, 1857.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我们划进歌声可及之处，\n"
"塞壬无需我们的声音便已察觉，\n"
"调起迷人的甜美歌调：\n"
"来吧，值得世人赞颂、\n"
"让希腊荣光升高的奥德修斯！\n"
"停船，听这无过客能不侧耳的歌，\n"
"人人离去都陶醉，并比从前更博学。\n"
"因为我们知道广阔特洛伊的一切，\n"
"希腊人与特洛伊人承受的，\n"
"诸神安排的重大命运，\n"
"以及整片大地能展示给知识的所有事物。”\n"
"    -Homer, _The Odyssey_, XII, 268-82.\n"
"     trans. George Chapman, 1857.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:molten gargoyle"
msgid "<war gargoyle>\n"
msgstr "<war gargoyle>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:moth of wrath"
msgid ""
"“When within sight of their foe Berserks wrought themselves into such a state\n"
" of frenzy, that they bit their shields and rushed forward to the attack,\n"
" throwing away their arms of defence, reckless of every danger, sometimes\n"
" having nothing but a club, which carried with it death and destruction.”\n"
"    -Paul Belloni Du Chaillu,_The Viking Age: the Early History, Manners, and\n"
"     Customs of the Ancestors of the English Speaking Nations_. 1889.\n"
msgstr ""
"“狂战士一看见敌人，便使自己陷入狂乱，咬盾冲锋，丢掉防具，不顾一切危险。有时仅持一根木棒，却随之带来死亡与毁灭。”\n"
"    -Paul Belloni Du Chaillu,_The Viking Age: the Early History, Manners, and\n"
"     Customs of the Ancestors of the English Speaking Nations_. 1889.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:mummy"
msgid ""
"“I see Egypt and the Egyptians — I see the pyramids and obelisks;\n"
" I look on chisel'd histories, songs, philosophies, cut in slabs\n"
"     of sand-stone, or on granite-blocks;\n"
" I see at Memphis mummy-pits, containing mummies, embalm'd, swathed\n"
"     in linen cloth, lying there many centuries;\n"
" I look on the fall'n Theban, the large-ball'd eyes, the side-drooping\n"
"     neck, the hands folded across the breast.”\n"
"    -Walt Whitman, “Salut au Monde”\n"
msgstr ""
"“我看见埃及与埃及人，金字塔与方尖碑；\n"
"看见刻在砂岩板或花岗岩块上的历史、歌与哲学；\n"
"在孟菲斯看见木乃伊坑，防腐裹麻的死者已躺了许多世纪；\n"
"看见倒下的底比斯人，圆大的眼，\n"
"歪垂的颈，交叠胸前的手。”\n"
"    -Walt Whitman, “Salut au Monde”\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:naga"
msgid ""
"“Amongst the deities and Asuras and celestial Rishis, O amiable lady, the Nagas\n"
" are endued with great energy. Possessed of great speed, they are endued again\n"
" with excellent fragrance. They deserve to be worshipped. They are capable of\n"
" granting boons. Indeed, we too deserve to be followed by others in our train.\n"
" I tell thee, O lady, that we are incapable of being seen by human beings.”\n"
"    -Mahābhārata, Santi Parva, Mokshadharma Parva, section CCCLX. ca. 500 B.C.\n"
"     trans. Kisari Mohan Ganguli, 1883.\n"
msgstr ""
"“温雅的女士，在诸神、阿修罗与天仙之中，纳迦充满巨大能量，速度极快，又有美妙芳香。它们值得崇拜，能够赐福。我们也值得别人随侍。我告诉你，女士，人类无法看见我们。”\n"
"    -Mahābhārata, Santi Parva, Mokshadharma Parva, section CCCLX. ca. 500 B.C.\n"
"     trans. Kisari Mohan Ganguli, 1883.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:naga mage"
msgid "<naga>\n"
msgstr "<naga>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:nagaraja"
msgid ""
"“Then there have also come\n"
" nagas from Lake Nabhasa,\n"
" Vesali, and Tacchaka.\n"
" Kambalas, Assataras,\n"
" Payagas, and their kin.\n"
" And from the River Yamuna\n"
" comes the prestigious naga, Dhatarattha.\n"
" The great naga Eravanna:\n"
" He, too, has come\n"
" to the forest meeting.”\n"
"    -Mahasamaya Sutta, _Dīgha Nikāya_, 20. ca. 500 B.C.\n"
"     trans. Thanissaro Bhikkhu\n"
msgstr ""
"“来自纳巴萨湖、毗舍离与怛叉迦的纳迦也来了，\n"
"还有甘婆罗、阿湿波多罗、波耶迦及其亲属。\n"
"从阎牟那河，来的是尊贵纳迦持国。\n"
"伟大的伊罗婆那龙王，\n"
"也来到森林集会。”\n"
"    -Mahasamaya Sutta, _Dīgha Nikāya_, 20. ca. 500 B.C.\n"
"     trans. Thanissaro Bhikkhu\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:naga warrior"
msgid "<naga>\n"
msgstr "<naga>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:nameless horror"
msgid ""
"“Then the sallow oval between Ged's arms grew bright. It widened and spread, a\n"
" rent in the darkness of the earth and night, a ripping open of the fabric of\n"
" the world. Through it blazed a terrible brightness. And through that bright\n"
" misshapen breach clambered something like a clot of black shadow, quick and\n"
" hideous, and it leaped straight out at Ged's face.”\n"
"    -Ursula K. Le Guin, _A Wizard Of Earthsea_. 1968.\n"
msgstr ""
"“于是，格得双臂之间那苍白的椭圆亮了起来。它不断扩大，在大地与黑夜的幽暗中裂开一道口子，撕开了世界的织物。可怕的光芒从中迸射。一个如同凝结黑影的东西从那明亮而扭曲的裂口爬出，迅疾而狰狞，径直扑向格得的脸。”\n"
"    -Ursula K. Le Guin, _A Wizard Of Earthsea_. 1968.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:necromancer"
msgid ""
"“Even now the intensity of his dread power can be felt\n"
" Weakening the body and saddening the heart\n"
" Ultimately they will become empty, mindless spectres\n"
" Stripped of will and soul\n"
" Only their thirst for freedom\n"
" Gives them hunger for vengeance...”\n"
"    -Rush, “The Necromancer”. 1975.\n"
msgstr ""
"“直到此刻，仍能感到他那可怕力量的强烈威势，\n"
"使身体衰弱，使心灵悲伤。\n"
"他们终将成为空洞、无知觉的幽魂，\n"
"意志与灵魂被剥夺殆尽。\n"
"唯有对自由的渴望，\n"
"使他们饥渴地寻求复仇……”\n"
"    -Rush, “The Necromancer”. 1975.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:nekomata"
msgid ""
"“Humans, eh? Think they’re lords of creation. Not like us cats. We _know_ we\n"
" are. Ever see a cat feed a human? Case proven.”\n"
"    -Terry Pratchett, “The Amazing Maurice and His Educated Rodents”. 2001.\n"
msgstr ""
"“人类，是吧？他们自以为是万物之主。我们猫可不同。我们_知道_自己就是。你见过猫喂养人吗？证明完毕。”\n"
"    -Terry Pratchett, “The Amazing Maurice and His Educated Rodents”. 2001.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:neqoxec"
msgid ""
"“If thus mutation is influenced by natural selection, it implies, that any\n"
" particular mutation must advance in a direction advantageous for the\n"
" respective species, and, indeed, many examples of mutation known among fossil\n"
" animals are apparently due to the advantage produced by the change. I must add\n"
" here, however that probably not all mutations (in a palaeontological meaning)\n"
" are due to natural selection, but that many do not imply an actual\n"
" improvement.”\n"
"    -_Proceedings of the American Philosophical Society_, Volume XXV, no. 150.\n"
"     1896.\n"
msgstr ""
"“倘若变异确实如此受到自然选择的影响，那就意味着，任何一种特定变异都必定朝着有利于相应物种的方向发展；事实上，化石动物中许多已知的变异实例，显然都源于这种改变所带来的益处。但我必须在此补充：大概并非所有古生物学意义上的变异都由自然选择造成，其中许多并不意味着实际的改善。”\n"
"    -_Proceedings of the American Philosophical Society_, Volume XXV, no. 150.\n"
"     1896.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:occultist"
msgid ""
"“Each family or tribe has a wizard or conjuring doctor, whose office we could\n"
" never clearly ascertain.”\n"
"    -Charles Darwin, _The Voyage of the Beagle_, ch. X. 1839.\n"
msgstr ""
"“每个家族或部落都有一名巫师或施法的医生，我们始终未能确切弄清他们的职责。”\n"
"    -Charles Darwin, _The Voyage of the Beagle_, ch. X. 1839.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:octopode"
msgid ""
"“In their brief time together Slothrop forms the impression that this octopus\n"
" is not in good mental health, though where's his basis for comparing? But\n"
" there is a mad exhuberance, as with inanimate objects which fall off of tables\n"
" when we are sensitive to noise and our own clumsiness and don't want them to\n"
" fall, a sort of wham! ha-ha you hear that? here it is again, WHAM! in the\n"
" cephalopod's every movement, which Slothrop is glad to get away from as he\n"
" finally scales the crab like a discus, with all his strength, out to sea, and\n"
" the octopus, with an eager splash and gurgle, strikes out in pursuit, and is\n"
" presently gone.”\n"
"    -Thomas Pynchon, _Gravity's Rainbow_. 1973.\n"
msgstr ""
"“在短暂的相处中，斯洛思罗普觉得这只章鱼的精神不太正常，虽说他又有什么比较的依据呢？然而它的每个动作都透着疯狂的兴奋，仿佛那些无生命的东西，总在人对噪声和自己的笨拙格外敏感、极不愿它们掉下时，从桌上摔下来：砰！哈哈，听见了吗？再来一次，砰！他终于用尽全力，像掷铁饼那样把螃蟹甩向海里；章鱼迫不及待地扑水追去，哗啦咕噜一阵，很快便消失了，斯洛思罗普也乐得摆脱它。”\n"
"    -Thomas Pynchon, _Gravity's Rainbow_. 1973.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ogre"
msgid ""
"“The little princess, asleep in her cradle, floated on the water, and at last\n"
" she was cast up on the shore of a beautiful country, where, however, very few\n"
" people dwelt since the ogre Ravagio and his wife Tourmentine had gone to live\n"
" there-for they ate up everybody. Ogres are terrible people. When once they\n"
" have tasted raw human flesh they will hardly eat anything else, and\n"
" Tourmentine always knew how to make some body come their way, for she was half\n"
" a fairy.”\n"
"    -Marie-Catherine Le Jumel de Barneville, Baronne d'Aulnoy, “'Orangier et\n"
"l'Abeille”. 1697.\n"
"\n"
"“NO. Layers. Onions have layers. Ogres have layers. Onions have layers. You get\n"
" it? We both have layers.”\n"
"    -Shrek. 2001.\n"
msgstr ""
"“小公主睡在摇篮里，漂在水上，最终被冲上一片美丽国土的海岸。可是自从食人魔拉瓦焦和妻子图尔芒蒂娜搬来，这里就几乎没了居民——因为他们把大家都吃了。食人魔是可怕的家伙，一旦尝过生人肉，就几乎不肯再吃别的；而图尔芒蒂娜总有办法引人送上门，因为她有一半仙女血统。”\n"
"    -Marie-Catherine Le Jumel de Barneville, Baronne d'Aulnoy, “'Orangier et\n"
"l'Abeille”. 1697.\n"
"\n"
"“不。层次。洋葱有层次，食人魔也有层次。洋葱有层次。明白了吗？我们都有层次。”\n"
"    -Shrek. 2001.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ogre mage"
msgid "<ogre>\n"
msgstr "<ogre>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:oklob plant"
msgid ""
"“Carbonic acid is one of the three materials which together form the starting\n"
" point of vegetable growth; the others being water and nitric acid. This acid is\n"
" formed of carbon and oxygen in the proportion of one part of the former to\n"
" two of the latter chemically combined. It is a colorless gas, having an acid\n"
" taste and smell; is soluble in water; weighs one-half more than air and can be\n"
" poured from one vessel to another, as a liquid may be; 100 parts of water\n"
" dissolve 106 parts of this gas, and it is from this source that the roots of\n"
" plants derive the needed supplies of it.”\n"
"    -Henry Stuart, _The Culture of Farm Crops: A Manual of the Science of\n"
"    Agriculture, and a Hand-book of Practice for American Farmers_, ch X. 1887.\n"
msgstr ""
"“碳酸是构成植物生长起点的三种物质之一，另外两种是水和硝酸。这种酸由一份碳与两份氧按化学比例结合而成。它是一种无色气体，气味和滋味都带酸性，能溶于水，比空气重一半，也能像液体那样从一个容器倾倒至另一个容器。一百份水能溶解一百零六份这种气体，而植物的根正是从这一来源取得所需的供应。”\n"
"    -Henry Stuart, _The Culture of Farm Crops: A Manual of the Science of\n"
"    Agriculture, and a Hand-book of Practice for American Farmers_, ch X. 1887.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:oklob sapling"
msgid "<oklob plant>\n"
msgstr "<oklob plant>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:oni incarcerator"
msgid ""
"“The popularity and longevity of the oni myth is no doubt partially based on\n"
" the beings’ conventional demonic accoutrements, which have remained\n"
" relatively constant through the ages: they are dreadful super-natural\n"
" beings emerging from the abyss of Buddhist hell to terrify wicked mortals;\n"
" their grotesque and savage demeanor and form instill instant fear; and the\n"
" oni’s omnipresence in the socio-historical and cultural archive of Japan is\n"
" directly attributable to the moral, social, and religious edification that\n"
" stories about oni engender.”\n"
"    -Noriko T. Reider, _Japanese Demon Lore: Oni from Ancient Times to the\n"
"     Present_, ch. 1, 2010.\n"
msgstr ""
"“鬼的传说如此流行而长寿，无疑部分缘于这类存在历代以来相对稳定的典型恶魔特征：它们是从佛教地狱深渊中现身、恐吓作恶凡人的可怕超自然存在；它们怪诞凶蛮的形貌和举止会立即激起恐惧；而鬼在日本社会历史与文化记载中的无所不在，则直接源于鬼故事所产生的道德、社会与宗教教化作用。”\n"
"    -Noriko T. Reider, _Japanese Demon Lore: Oni from Ancient Times to the\n"
"     Present_, ch. 1, 2010.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ophan"
msgid ""
"“As I looked at the living creatures, I saw a wheel on the ground beside\n"
" each creature with its four faces. This was the appearance and structure\n"
" of the wheels: They sparkled like chrysolite, and all four looked alike.\n"
" Each appeared to be made like a wheel intersecting a wheel. As they\n"
" moved, they would go in any one of the four directions the creatures faced;\n"
" the wheels did not turn about as the creatures went. Their rims were\n"
" high and awesome, and all four rims were full of eyes all around.”\n"
"    -Ezekiel 1:15-18 (New International Version)\n"
msgstr ""
"“我观看活物的时候，见四脸的活物旁边，地上各有一个轮子。轮子的形状和构造是这样：闪耀如贵橄榄石，四个轮子形状相同，仿佛轮中套轮。它们行走时，能向着活物面对的四方任意前进，并不随活物转弯。轮辋高大可畏，四个轮辋周围都布满了眼睛。”\n"
"    -Ezekiel 1:15-18 (New International Version)\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:orange demon"
msgid ""
"“In Sparkill buried lies that man of mark\n"
" Who brought the Obelisk to Central Park,\n"
" Redoubtable Commander H.H. Gorringe,\n"
" Whose name supplies the long-sought rhyme for ‘orange.’”\n"
"    -Arthur Guiterman, “Local Note”. 1934.\n"
msgstr ""
"“斯帕基尔葬着那位名人，\n"
"他把方尖碑送进中央公园，\n"
"威风凛凛的 H. H. Gorringe 指挥官，\n"
"他的姓终于让‘orange’找到苦寻的韵脚。”\n"
"    -Arthur Guiterman, “Local Note”. 1934.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:orb guardian"
msgid ""
"“X gon' give it to ya (what)\n"
" Fuck waitin' for you to get it on your own, X gon' deliver to ya\n"
" Knock knock, open up the door, it's real\n"
" With the non-stop pop-pop from stainless steel\n"
" [...]\n"
" First we gonna rock, then we gonna roll\n"
" Then we let it pop, go, let it go\n"
" X gon' give it to ya, he gon' give it to ya\n"
" X gon' give it to ya, he gon' give it to ya\n"
"    -DMX, “X Gon' Give It To Ya”. 2002\n"
msgstr ""
"“X 会给你送上门（什么）\n"
"去他的等你自己来拿，X 会亲自送到。\n"
"咚咚，开门，真家伙来了，\n"
"不锈钢枪管不停砰砰响。\n"
"[…]\n"
"先让我们震起来，再让我们滚起来，\n"
"然后让它炸响，来吧，放开来。\n"
"X 会给你送上门，他会给你送上门。\n"
"X 会给你送上门，他会给你送上门。”\n"
"    -DMX, “X Gon' Give It To Ya”. 2002\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:orb of fire"
msgid ""
"“There 's not the smallest orb which thou behold'st\n"
" But in his motion like an angel sings,\n"
" Still quiring to the young-eyed cherubins.”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _The Merchant of Venice_, V, i. 1597.\n"
msgstr ""
"“你所看见的星球，无论多么渺小，\n"
"都在运行中如天使般歌唱，\n"
"永远向着目光清澈的智天使齐声高歌。”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _The Merchant of Venice_, V, i. 1597.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:pandemonium lord"
msgid ""
"“Mean while the winged heralds by command\n"
" Of Sovran power, with awful Ceremony\n"
" And Trumpets sound throughout the Host proclaim\n"
" A solemn Councel forthwith to be held\n"
" At Pandaemonium, the high Capital\n"
" Of Satan and his Peers...”\n"
"    -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_, Book I, 1667.\n"
msgstr ""
"“与此同时，生翼的使者奉至高权威之命，\n"
"以庄严仪式和号角之声向全军宣布：\n"
"即刻在万魔殿——\n"
"撒旦与其同僚的巍峨都城——\n"
"召开肃穆的议会……”\n"
"    -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_, Book I, 1667.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:phantom"
msgid ""
"“Who wondrous things concerning our welfare, And straunge phantomes doth lett\n"
" us ofte foresee.”\n"
"    -Spenser, _The Faerie Queene_ II. xii. 47\n"
msgstr ""
"“它常使我们预见关乎自身福祉的奇事，以及种种诡异的幻影。”\n"
"    -Spenser, _The Faerie Queene_ II. xii. 47\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:pillar of salt"
msgid ""
"“Then the LORD rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from the\n"
" LORD out of heaven; And he overthrew those cities, and all the plain, and all\n"
" the inhabitants of the cities, and that which grew upon the ground. But\n"
" [Lot's] wife looked back from behind him, and she became a pillar of salt.”\n"
"    -KJV Bible, Genesis 19:24-26.\n"
msgstr ""
"“当时，耶和华将硫磺与火从天上降在所多玛和蛾摩拉，倾覆了那些城、全平原、城中一切居民，以及地上生长的万物。罗得的妻子从他后面回头一看，便变成了一根盐柱。”\n"
"    -KJV Bible, Genesis 19:24-26.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:player ghost"
msgid ""
"“Know thyself.”\n"
"    -Inscription in the pronaos of the Temple of Apollo at Delphi\n"
msgstr ""
"“认识你自己。”\n"
"    -Inscription in the pronaos of the Temple of Apollo at Delphi\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:polar bear"
msgid ""
"“The Polar Bear is an animal of tremendous strength and fierceness. Barentz, in\n"
" his voyage in search of a north-east passage to China, had proofs of the\n"
" ferocity of these animals, in the island of Nova Zembla, where they attacked\n"
" his seamen, seizing them in their mouths; carrying them off with the utmost\n"
" ease, and devouring them in the sight of their comrades. It is said that they\n"
" will attack and attempt to board armed vessels, at a great distance from\n"
" shore, and have sometimes been with much difficulty repelled.”\n"
"    -George Shaw, _General Zoology, or, Systematic Natural History_, vol. I,\n"
"     p. 2. 1800.\n"
msgstr ""
"“北极熊是力量惊人、性情凶猛的动物。巴伦支在寻找通往中国的东北航道时，就在新地岛见识了它们的凶残：它们袭击水手，将人叼在嘴里，轻而易举地拖走，当着同伴的面吞食。据说，它们甚至会在远离海岸的地方攻击武装船只，试图爬上甲板，有时人们费尽力气才将其击退。”\n"
"    -George Shaw, _General Zoology, or, Systematic Natural History_, vol. I,\n"
"     p. 2. 1800.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:profane servitor"
msgid ""
"“A spell was cast and the sky turned red\n"
" The angel's heart froze to ice\n"
" In the gloomy sky black clouds were gathering\n"
" The silence was broken by cries\n"
" A spell was cast and the sky turned red\n"
" The angel's heart froze to ice\n"
" In the gloomy sky — The silence where dead angels lie\n"
"\n"
" Touch the snow... Caress the lifeless sculptures\n"
" Die!!!”\n"
"    -Dissection, “Where Dead Angels Lie”. 1996.\n"
msgstr ""
"“咒语施下，天空转红，\n"
"天使的心冻成了冰。\n"
"阴沉的天际聚起乌云，\n"
"尖叫打破了寂静。\n"
"咒语施下，天空转红，\n"
"天使的心冻成了冰。\n"
"阴沉的天空里——死去天使躺卧的寂静之地。\n"
"\n"
"触摸积雪……抚慰无生命的雕像。\n"
"死吧！！！”\n"
"    -Dissection, “Where Dead Angels Lie”. 1996.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:program bug"
msgid ""
"“If builders built buildings the way programmers wrote programs, then the first\n"
" woodpecker that came along would destroy civilization.”\n"
"    -Gerald Weinberg, Weinberg's Second Law\n"
msgstr ""
"“如果建筑师盖房子的方式和程序员写程序一样，那么第一只飞来的啄木鸟就能摧毁文明。”\n"
"    -Gerald Weinberg, Weinberg's Second Law\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:protean progenitor"
msgid ""
"“I call upon Proteus,\n"
" key-holding master of the sea,\n"
" first-born, who showed\n"
" the beginnings of all nature,\n"
" changing matter\n"
" into a great variety of forms.\n"
" Honored by all, he is wise,\n"
" and he knows what is now,\n"
" what was before,\n"
" and what will be in the future.\n"
" He has all at his disposal,\n"
" transformed far beyond\n"
" all other immortals\n"
" who dwell on snowy Olympos\n"
" and fly through the air\n"
" and over land and sea,\n"
" for Physis was the first to place\n"
" everything in Proteus.\n"
" Father, attended by holy providence,\n"
" visit the mystic initiates,\n"
" and bring a good end to a life\n"
" of industry and prosperity.”\n"
"    -_The Orphic Hymns_, XXV.\n"
"     trans. Apostolos N. Athanassakis and Benjamin M. Wolkow, 2013.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我呼唤普罗透斯，\n"
"执掌钥匙的海洋之主，\n"
"最初诞生者，曾展现万物自然的起源，\n"
"将物质变成千姿百态。\n"
"他受万众尊崇，充满智慧，\n"
"知晓当下、过去与未来。\n"
"万物尽在他的支配之下，\n"
"他的变化远胜其他不朽者——\n"
"那些居于白雪覆盖的奥林波斯，\n"
"飞越天空、大地与海洋的神明。\n"
"因为自然女神最先将一切置于普罗透斯之中。\n"
"父亲啊，在神圣天意的陪伴下，\n"
"请探访参加秘仪的人们，\n"
"让勤劳而富足的一生得到美好的归宿。”\n"
"    -_The Orphic Hymns_, XXV.\n"
"     trans. Apostolos N. Athanassakis and Benjamin M. Wolkow, 2013.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:rakshasa"
msgid ""
"“Vaisampayana said, 'Not far from the place where the Pandavas were asleep, a\n"
" Rakshasa by name Hidimva dwelt on the Sala tree. Possessed of great energy and\n"
" prowess, he was a cruel cannibal of visage that was grim in consequence of his\n"
" sharp and long teeth. He was now hungry and longing for human flesh. Of long\n"
" shanks and a large belly, his locks and beard were both red in hue. His\n"
" shoulders were broad like the neck of a tree; his ears were like unto arrows,\n"
" and his features were frightful.”\n"
"    -_Mahābhārata_, Adi Parva, Hidimva-vadha Parva, section CLIV. ca. 500 B.C.\n"
"     trans. Kisari Mohan Ganguli, 1883.\n"
msgstr ""
"“毗舍耶那说：离般度诸子熟睡之处不远，一棵娑罗树上住着名叫希丁婆的罗刹。他精力充沛，勇猛过人，是个残忍的食人者；尖长的牙齿让面容格外狰狞。他此刻饥肠辘辘，渴望人肉。他双腿修长，肚腹硕大，头发与胡须都是红色，肩膀宽阔如树干，耳朵如箭，面目可怖。”\n"
"    -_Mahābhārata_, Adi Parva, Hidimva-vadha Parva, section CLIV. ca. 500 B.C.\n"
"     trans. Kisari Mohan Ganguli, 1883.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:reaper"
msgid ""
"“All our times have come.\n"
" Here but now they're gone.\n"
" Seasons don't fear the reaper,\n"
" Nor do the wind, the sun or the rain.\n"
" We can be like they are.\n"
" Come on baby, don't fear the reaper.”\n"
"\n"
"    -Buck Dharma, Blue Öyster Cult, “(Don't Fear) The Reaper”. 1976.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我们的时刻都已到来，\n"
"方才还在，转眼消逝。\n"
"四季不惧死神，\n"
"风、太阳和雨也不惧怕。\n"
"我们也能像它们一样。\n"
"来吧，宝贝，别怕死神。”\n"
"    -Buck Dharma, Blue Öyster Cult, “(Don't Fear) The Reaper”. 1976.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ribbon worm"
msgid ""
"“While the angels, all pallid and wan,\n"
"   Uprising, unveiling, affirm\n"
" That the play is the tragedy, ‘Man’,\n"
"   And its hero, the Conqueror Worm.”\n"
"    -Edgar Allan Poe\n"
msgstr ""
"“而天使们苍白憔悴，\n"
"起身揭幕，齐声宣告：\n"
"这出戏就是悲剧‘人’，\n"
"它的主角，便是征服者蠕虫。”\n"
"    -Edgar Allan Poe\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:royal mummy"
msgid "<mummy>\n"
msgstr "<mummy>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:salamander"
msgid ""
"“As for example: the Salamander made in fashion of a Lizard, marked with spots\n"
" like to stars, never comes abroad and sheweth it selfe but in great showers;\n"
" for in faire weather he is not seene. He is of so cold a complexion, that if\n"
" hee do but touch the fire, hee wil quench it as presently, as if yce were put\n"
" into it. The Salamander casteth up at the mouth a certaine venomous matter\n"
" like unto milke, let it but once touch any bare part of a man or womans bodie,\n"
" all the haire will fall off: and the part so touched will change the colour of\n"
" the skin to the white morphew.”\n"
"    -Gaius Plinius Secundus, _Naturalis Historia_, Book X, ch. LXVII. 79 A.D.\n"
"     trans. Philemon Holland, 1601.\n"
msgstr ""
"“譬如蝾螈，其形如蜥蜴，遍身星点，只在大雨倾盆时出来现身，晴天则不见踪迹。它体质极寒，只需碰触火焰，就能如冰投入其中一般立刻将火熄灭。蝾螈口中吐出一种乳汁般的毒物，只要碰到男女身上任何裸露之处，毛发便会尽落，接触处的皮肤也会变成白斑病的颜色。”\n"
"    -Gaius Plinius Secundus, _Naturalis Historia_, Book X, ch. LXVII. 79 A.D.\n"
"     trans. Philemon Holland, 1601.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:scorpion"
msgid ""
"“Those poisonous fields, with rank luxuriance crown'd,\n"
" Where the dark scorpion gathers death around”\n"
"    -Oliver Goldsmith, “The Deserted Village”, l. 351-2. 1770.\n"
msgstr ""
"“那毒野上，茂草蓊郁，\n"
"黝黑的蝎子在其间聚集死亡。”\n"
"    -Oliver Goldsmith, “The Deserted Village”, l. 351-2. 1770.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:seraph"
msgid ""
"“In the year that king Uzziah died I saw also the LORD sitting upon a throne,\n"
" high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple.\n"
"\n"
" Above it stood the seraphims: each one had six wings; with twain he covered\n"
" his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly.\n"
"\n"
" And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts:\n"
" the whole earth is full of his glory.”\n"
"    -KJV Bible, Isaiah 6:1-3.\n"
msgstr ""
"“乌西雅王崩的那年，我看见主坐在高高的宝座上，他的衣裳垂下，遮满圣殿。\n"
"\n"
"其上有撒拉弗侍立，各有六个翅膀：两个遮脸，两个遮脚，两个飞翔。\n"
"\n"
"彼此呼喊说：圣哉！圣哉！圣哉！万军之耶和华，他的荣光充满全地。”\n"
"    -KJV Bible, Isaiah 6:1-3.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:shadowghast"
msgid ""
"“Between the idea\n"
" And the reality\n"
" Between the motion\n"
" And the act\n"
" Falls the Shadow\n"
"     For thine is the Kingdom\n"
"\n"
" Between the conception\n"
" And the creation\n"
" Between the emotion\n"
" And the response\n"
" Falls the Shadow\n"
"     Life is very long”\n"
"    -T.S. Eliot, “The Hollow Men”. 1925.\n"
msgstr ""
"“在理念\n"
"与现实之间，\n"
"在动势\n"
"与行动之间，\n"
"阴影落下。\n"
"    因为国度是你的。\n"
"\n"
"在构思\n"
"与创造之间，\n"
"在情感\n"
"与回应之间，\n"
"阴影落下。\n"
"    生命很漫长。”\n"
"    -T.S. Eliot, “The Hollow Men”. 1925.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:shadow demon"
msgid ""
"“As we grow old, we become aware that death is drawing near; his shadow falls\n"
" across our path...”\n"
"    -Stefan Zweig, _Twenty-Four Hours in the Life of a Woman_. 1927.\n"
msgstr ""
"“随着年岁增长，我们开始意识到死亡正在逼近；他的阴影横落在我们的路上……”\n"
"    -Stefan Zweig, _Twenty-Four Hours in the Life of a Woman_. 1927.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:shadow dragon"
msgid ""
"“Crux sacra sit mihi lux / Non draco sit mihi dux\n"
" Vade retro satana / Numquam suade mihi vana\n"
" Sunt mala quae libas / Ipse venena bibas\n"
"\n"
" [Let the Holy Cross be my light / Let not the dragon be my guide\n"
"  Step back Satan / Never tempt me with vain things\n"
"  What you offer me is evil / You drink the poison yourself.]”\n"
"    -Full text of initials on the Saint Benedict Medal, worn to ward off evil\n"
"     spirits. Inscription from 11-15th century, formally approved by Pope\n"
"     Benedict XIV in 18th century.\n"
msgstr ""
"“Crux sacra sit mihi lux / Non draco sit mihi dux\n"
"Vade retro satana / Numquam suade mihi vana\n"
"Sunt mala quae libas / Ipse venena bibas\n"
"\n"
"[愿圣十字为我光明，莫让恶龙引我前行。\n"
"撒旦退去，莫以虚妄诱我。\n"
"你所献的皆是邪恶，那毒你自己喝下。]”\n"
"    -Full text of initials on the Saint Benedict Medal, worn to ward off evil\n"
"     spirits. Inscription from 11-15th century, formally approved by Pope\n"
"     Benedict XIV in 18th century.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:shadow wraith"
msgid ""
"“Yesterday, upon the stair,\n"
" I met a man who wasn't there\n"
" He wasn't there again today\n"
" I wish, I wish he'd go away...”\n"
"    -Hughes Mearns ,_Antigonish_, 1-4. 1899.\n"
msgstr ""
"“昨天在楼梯上，\n"
"我遇到一个并不存在的人。\n"
"今天他又不在那里，\n"
"但愿，但愿他快走开……”\n"
"    -Hughes Mearns ,_Antigonish_, 1-4. 1899.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:shambling mangrove"
msgid ""
"“There is unrest in the forest\n"
" There is trouble with the trees\n"
" For the maples want more sunlight\n"
" And the oaks ignore their pleas”\n"
"    -Rush, \"The Trees\". 1978.\n"
msgstr ""
"“森林里起了骚动，\n"
"树木之间出了纷争。\n"
"枫树想要更多阳光，\n"
"橡树却不理它们的恳求。”\n"
"    -Rush, \"The Trees\". 1978.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:shapeshifter"
msgid ""
"“And then th' old Sea-God crept\n"
" From forth the deeps, and found his fat calves there,\n"
" Survey'd, and number'd, and came never near\n"
" The craft we used, but told us five for calves.\n"
" His temples then dis-eased with sleep he salves;\n"
" And in rush'd we, with an abhorred cry,\n"
" Cast all our hands about him manfully;\n"
" And then th' old Forger all his forms began:\n"
" First was a lion with a mighty mane,\n"
" Then next a dragon, a pied panther then,\n"
" A vast boar next, and suddenly did strain\n"
" All into water. Last he was a tree,\n"
" Curl'd all at top, and shot up to the sky.”\n"
"    -Homer, _The Odyssey_, IV, 602-14.\n"
"     trans. George Chapman, 1857.\n"
msgstr ""
"“于是老海神从深处爬出，\n"
"找到肥美的海豹，巡视点数，\n"
"丝毫未察觉我们的计谋，\n"
"把我们五人也当成了海豹。\n"
"他以睡眠抚慰疲惫的额头，\n"
"我们却大喊一声，猛扑上去，\n"
"奋力伸手将他紧紧抱住。\n"
"老变化师随即开始变幻：\n"
"先是鬃毛浓密的狮子，\n"
"接着是龙，再是斑斓的豹，\n"
"然后是巨大的野猪，又忽然尽化流水。\n"
"最后他变成一棵树，\n"
"树冠蜷曲，直冲云天。”\n"
"    -Homer, _The Odyssey_, IV, 602-14.\n"
"     trans. George Chapman, 1857.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:silent spectre"
msgid ""
"“There is a silence where hath been no sound,\n"
" There is a silence where no sound may be,—\n"
" In the cold grave, under the deep, deep sea,\n"
" Or in the wide desert where no life is found.”\n"
"    -Thomas Hood, “Silence”. Early 19th cent.\n"
msgstr ""
"“有一种寂静，在从无声音之处；\n"
"有一种寂静，在声音无法存在之地——\n"
"冰冷的坟墓里，深深的海底，\n"
"或是没有生命的辽阔荒漠。”\n"
"    -Thomas Hood, “Silence”. Early 19th cent.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:simulacrum"
msgid ""
"“The simulacrum now hides, not the truth, but the fact that there is none, that\n"
" is to say, the continuation of Nothingness.”\n"
"    -Jean Baudrillard, “Radical Thought”. 1994.\n"
"     trans. François Debrix, 1995.\n"
msgstr ""
"“如今拟像所掩盖的，并非真相，而是真相根本不存在这一事实，也就是说，虚无的延续。”\n"
"    -Jean Baudrillard, “Radical Thought”. 1994.\n"
"     trans. François Debrix, 1995.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:sixfirhy"
msgid ""
"“I saw a mouth jeering. A smile of melted red iron ran over it. Its laugh was\n"
" full of nails rattling. It was a child's dream of a mouth.\n"
" A fist hit the mouth: knuckles of gun-metal driven by an electric wrist and\n"
" shoulder. It was a child's dream of an arm.\n"
" The fist hit the mouth over and over, again and again. The mouth bled melted\n"
" iron, and laughed its laughter of nails rattling.\n"
" And I saw the more the fist pounded the more the mouth laughed. The fist is\n"
" pounding and pounding, and the mouth answering.”\n"
"    -Carl Sandburg, “Gargoyle”, _Cornhusker_. 1918.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我看见一张嘲弄的嘴，熔化红铁般的笑容从上面掠过，笑声满是铁钉的碰撞。那是孩子梦中的一张嘴。\n"
"一只拳头打在嘴上：炮铜般的指节，由电动的手腕和肩膀驱使。那是孩子梦中的一条胳膊。\n"
"拳头一遍又一遍地击打那张嘴。嘴里流出熔铁般的血，仍发出铁钉碰撞般的笑声。\n"
"我看见拳头打得越狠，那张嘴就笑得越响。拳头不停地打，那张嘴不停地回应。”\n"
"    -Carl Sandburg, “Gargoyle”, _Cornhusker_. 1918.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:skeletal warrior"
msgid ""
"“Speak! speak! thou fearful guest!\n"
" Who, with thy hollow breast\n"
" Still in rude armor drest,\n"
" Comest to daunt me!\n"
" Wrapt not in Eastern balms,\n"
" But with thy fleshless palms\n"
" Stretched, as if asking alms,\n"
" Why dost thou haunt me?”\n"
"    -Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, “The Skeleton in Armor”. 1841.\n"
msgstr ""
"“说话！说话！可怕的来客！\n"
"你胸膛空洞，\n"
"仍披粗陋甲胄，\n"
"前来使我惊惧！\n"
"你不裹东方香膏，\n"
"却伸着没有血肉的双掌，\n"
"仿佛乞讨施舍，\n"
"为何要来纠缠我？”\n"
"    -Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, “The Skeleton in Armor”. 1841.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:skeleton"
msgid ""
"“God save us from the skeleton\n"
" Who sitteth at the feast!”\n"
"    -James Jeffrey Roche, _The Skeleton at the Feast_. 1890.\n"
msgstr ""
"“愿上帝救我们脱离\n"
"那坐在宴席上的骷髅！”\n"
"    -James Jeffrey Roche, _The Skeleton at the Feast_. 1890.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:sky beast"
msgid ""
"“Her own mother lived the latter years of her life in the horrible suspicion\n"
" that electricity was dripping invisibly all over the house.”\n"
"    -James Thurber, _My Life and Hard Times_. 1934.\n"
msgstr ""
"“她母亲晚年一直活在可怕的疑虑中，总怀疑看不见的电流正在屋内到处滴落。”\n"
"    -James Thurber, _My Life and Hard Times_. 1934.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:slime creature"
msgid ""
"“The very deep did rot: O Christ!\n"
" That ever this should be!\n"
" Yea, slimy things did crawl with legs\n"
" Upon the slimy sea.”\n"
"    -Samuel Tayor Coleridge, “The Rime of the Ancient Mariner”. 1798.\n"
msgstr ""
"“深海竟也腐烂：基督啊！\n"
"怎么会有这样的事！\n"
"是的，黏滑的东西生出腿脚，\n"
"在黏滑的海上爬行。”\n"
"    -Samuel Tayor Coleridge, “The Rime of the Ancient Mariner”. 1798.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:small abomination"
msgid ""
"“No — it wasn't that way at all. It was everywhere — a gelatin — a slime yet it\n"
" had shapes, a thousand shapes of horror beyond all memory. There were eyes —\n"
" and a blemish. It was the pit — the maelstrom — the ultimate abomination.\n"
" Carter, it was the unnamable!”\n"
"    -H.P. Lovecraft, _The Unnamable_. 1925.\n"
msgstr ""
"“不——根本不是那样。它无处不在——一团胶质——一滩黏液，却又有形状，有一千种超出一切记忆的恐怖形状。有眼睛——还有污斑。那是深渊——是大漩涡——是终极的憎恶。卡特，那是不可名状之物！”\n"
"    -H.P. Lovecraft, _The Unnamable_. 1925.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:smoke demon"
msgid ""
"“Why does the thin grey strand\n"
" Floating up from the forgotten\n"
" Cigarette between my fingers,\n"
" Why does it trouble me?”\n"
"    -D.H. Lawrence, “Sorrow”. 1916.\n"
msgstr ""
"“为什么从指间那支\n"
"被遗忘的香烟上，\n"
"轻轻浮起的灰色细缕，\n"
"为什么它令我不安？”\n"
"    -D.H. Lawrence, “Sorrow”. 1916.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:snapping turtle"
msgid ""
"“After a while they came to a village. ”Now then,“ said Snapping Turtle, ”in\n"
" the morning at daylight, my friends, we will make on attack. I myself will\n"
" first go to the place,“ the leader of the war party said to them.\n"
"\n"
" ”Good,“ said the other little one, ”thou art the one who sees to it what we\n"
" shall do,“ they said to that Snapping Turtle. ”Now then,“ said Snapping\n"
" Turtle, ”verily I am now going to tell you what I shall do.“ Thus he spoke.\n"
" ”Now is the time I shall begin to walk toward this village. Verily at the time\n"
" I shall kill the daughter of the chief will be when the light of day is\n"
" breaking, and at the same instant the sky will glow with red in the direction\n"
" whence the morrow comes. ‘Ho, there, our comrade has killed her!’ will thus be\n"
" the thought in your hearts. Then is the time when you want to make a great\n"
" noise, when you shall whoop all keep it up. Now is the time that you go to\n"
" attack this village.“ Thus he spoke to those his young men.\n"
"\n"
" ”All right!“ said the other little fellows.”\n"
"    -“When Snapping Turtle went to War”, _Publications of the American\n"
"     Ethnological Society, Volume IX: Kickapoo Tales_. 1915.\n"
"     trans. Truman Michelson\n"
msgstr ""
"“过了一会儿，他们来到一个村庄。鳄龟说：‘朋友们，明天天一亮，我们就进攻。我会先去那里。’这位战队首领这样告诉他们。\n"
"\n"
"‘好，’其他小家伙说，‘该怎么做，都由你决定。’鳄龟说：‘那么，现在我要告诉你们，我将怎样行动。现在我就向村庄走去。等我杀死酋长的女儿时，恰好就是天亮之际，明日升起的方向也会同时映红天空。你们心里便会想：啊，我们的同伴杀死她了！到那时候，你们就大声喧哗，持续呐喊，然后进攻这个村庄。’他这样对手下的年轻人说。\n"
"\n"
"‘好！’其他小家伙回答。”\n"
"    -“When Snapping Turtle went to War”, _Publications of the American\n"
"     Ethnological Society, Volume IX: Kickapoo Tales_. 1915.\n"
"     trans. Truman Michelson\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:soul eater"
msgid ""
"“Negation is the mind's first freedom.”\n"
"    -E.M. Cioran, _The Temptation to Exist_. 1956.\n"
msgstr ""
"“否定是心灵的第一种自由。”\n"
"    -E.M. Cioran, _The Temptation to Exist_. 1956.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:spatial vortex"
msgid ""
"“It was just a colour out of space—a frightful messenger from unformed realms\n"
" of infinity beyond all Nature as we know it; from realms whose mere existence\n"
" stuns the brain and numbs us with the black extra-cosmic gulfs it throws open\n"
" before our frenzied eyes.”\n"
"    -H.P. Lovecraft, “The Colour out of Space”. 1927.\n"
msgstr ""
"“那不过是来自太空的色彩——一位恐怖的使者，来自我们所知的一切自然之外、无垠而尚未成形的领域。那些领域的存在本身，就足以震慑头脑；它们在我们狂乱的眼前敞开宇宙之外漆黑的深渊，使我们麻木。”\n"
"    -H.P. Lovecraft, “The Colour out of Space”. 1927.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:spatial maelstrom"
msgid ""
"“In any composition, the solid narrates the anomalies generated by the void, or\n"
" the infection of the void through the solid (where the void comes to the solid,\n"
" it works as a convoluting plague, a coiling swirling epidemic rather than a\n"
" nullifying process or a solid-annihilating agent); in a composition there is no\n"
" pure solid but a defiled one, a diseased and deflowered solid.\n"
" [...]\n"
" The only way that the solid can initialize its architectonic and compositional\n"
" activities (processes for survival, development, etc.) is by letting the void\n"
" in. The dynamic traits of solid can only be actuated when solid is eaten,\n"
" convoluted and messed up by the void. There is no other option for solid.”\n"
"    -Reza Negarestani, _Cyclonopedia: Complicity with Anonymous Materials_. 2008\n"
msgstr ""
"“在任何构成之中，实体都在讲述虚空造成的异常，或虚空穿过实体所引发的感染。虚空进入实体时，作用如盘曲缠绕的瘟疫、一场回旋翻涌的流行病，而非使事物归零的过程或消灭实体的媒介。在构成中，没有纯粹的实体，只有被玷污、患病而遭到摧残的实体。\n"
"[…]\n"
"实体若想启动其建筑与构成活动——生存、发展等过程——唯一的办法就是让虚空进入。只有当实体被虚空吞噬、扭曲并搅乱时，它的动态特征才能启动。实体别无选择。”\n"
"    -Reza Negarestani, _Cyclonopedia: Complicity with Anonymous Materials_. 2008\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:spectral thing"
msgid ""
"“On the hungry craving wind\n"
" My Spectre follows thee behind.”\n"
"    -William Blake, “Broken Love”. ca. 1800.\n"
msgstr ""
"“乘着饥渴的风，\n"
"我的幽魂在你身后追随。”\n"
"    -William Blake, “Broken Love”. ca. 1800.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:spellspark servitor"
msgid ""
"“When you think\n"
" Your toys have gone berserk\n"
" It's an illusion\n"
" You cannot shirk”\n"
"    -Siouxsie and the Banshees, “Spellbound”\n"
msgstr ""
"“当你以为\n"
"玩具已经发狂，\n"
"那是一个幻象，\n"
"你却无从逃避。”\n"
"    -Siouxsie and the Banshees, “Spellbound”\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:sphinx marauder"
msgid ""
"“Oedipus speaks: 'Far from me is the crime and shame of cowardice, and my\n"
" valour knows not dastard fears[...] The Sphinx, weaving her words in darkling\n"
" measures, I fled not; I faced the bloody jaws of the fell prophetess and the\n"
" ground white with scattered bones. And when from a lofty cliff, already\n"
" hovering over her prey, she prepared her pinions and, lashing her tail like\n"
" a savage lion, stirred up her threatening wrath, I asked her riddle.\n"
" Thereupon came a sound of dread; her jaws crashed, and her talons, brooking\n"
" no delay, eager for my vitals, tore at the rocks. The lot's intricate,\n"
" guile-entangled words, the grim riddle of the winged beast, I solved.'”\n"
"    -Seneca, _Oedipus_, 1st cent. A.D.\n"
"     trans. Frank Justus Miller, 1917.\n"
msgstr ""
"“俄狄浦斯说：怯懦的罪名与耻辱离我很远，我的勇气不知卑怯的恐惧为何物……斯芬克斯以晦暗的韵律编织话语，我并未逃跑；我直面那凶恶女预言者的血口，以及遍地散骨的苍白。当她从高崖俯临猎物，张开羽翼，像猛狮般抽打尾巴，激起凶险的怒意时，我向她讨问谜题。随即一声可怕的响动传来：她双颚撞响，利爪急不可耐地渴求我的内脏，撕扯着岩石。我解开了那签辞般复杂、诡计纠缠的语句，解开了有翼野兽的恐怖谜题。”\n"
"    -Seneca, _Oedipus_, 1st cent. A.D.\n"
"     trans. Frank Justus Miller, 1917.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:star jelly"
msgid ""
"\"My colleagues may have dismissed the sightings as blink frog egg casings, but\n"
"today I shall prove that these creatures came from beyond the firmament. Let's\n"
"begin the dissection.\"\n"
"        -Ardun Idrick, cryptozoologist, last words\n"
msgstr "“同事们或许把那些目击当成了闪烁蛙的卵壳，但今天我要证明，这些生物来自苍穹之外。让我们开始解剖吧。”\n        -Ardun Idrick, cryptozoologist, last words\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:starcursed mass"
msgid ""
"“Did you see that star go out?\n"
" I seen it burn.\n"
"\n"
" That little star went out,\n"
" your little eyes went out.\n"
"\n"
" Our burnt little dreams are hid\n"
" up where the stars get lit.”\n"
"    -Thee Silver Mt. Zion, “I Built Myself a Metal Bird”. 2010.\n"
msgstr ""
"“你看见那颗星熄灭了吗？\n"
"我看见它燃烧。\n"
"\n"
"那颗小星熄灭了，\n"
"你的小眼睛熄灭了。\n"
"\n"
"我们烧焦的小小梦想，\n"
"藏在星辰点亮的地方。”\n"
"    -Thee Silver Mt. Zion, “I Built Myself a Metal Bird”. 2010.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:stone giant"
msgid ""
"“I really believe what you say, answered the knight; for, I have been engaged\n"
" with the giant, in the most obstinate and outrageous combat that I believe I\n"
" shall ever fight in all the days of my life: with one backstroke, slam went\n"
" his head to the ground; and discharged such a quantity of blood, that it ran\n"
" like rills of water, along the field.”\n"
"    -Miguel de Cervantes Saavedra, _The Ingenious Gentleman Don Quixote of La\n"
"     Mancha_, IV, 10. 1605.\n"
"     trans. Carlos Fuentes, 1997.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我完全相信你说的话，骑士回答，因为我刚刚与巨人展开一场顽强而狂暴的搏斗，我想此生再不会有这样的战斗了：我反手一击，砰的一声，他的脑袋便落到地上，涌出大量鲜血，像一道道细流淌过田野。”\n"
"    -Miguel de Cervantes Saavedra, _The Ingenious Gentleman Don Quixote of La\n"
"     Mancha_, IV, 10. 1605.\n"
"     trans. Carlos Fuentes, 1997.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:sun demon"
msgid ""
"“Behold him setting in his western skies,\n"
" The shadows lengthening as the vapours rise.”\n"
"    -John Dryden, “Absalom and Achitophel”, I, 268. 1681.\n"
"\n"
"“The sky is sad and beautiful, like a vast altar.\n"
" The sun has drowned in its congealing blood.”\n"
"    -Charles Baudelaire, _Flowers of Evil_, 43: Evening Harmony. 1857.\n"
"     trans. Ruth White, 1969.\n"
msgstr ""
"“看他沉入西方的天空，\n"
"雾气升起，影子渐渐拉长。”\n"
"    -John Dryden, “Absalom and Achitophel”, I, 268. 1681.\n"
"\n"
"“天空忧伤而美丽，像一座辽阔的祭坛。\n"
"太阳淹没在自身渐渐凝结的血中。”\n"
"    -Charles Baudelaire, _Flowers of Evil_, 43: Evening Harmony. 1857.\n"
"     trans. Ruth White, 1969.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:swamp drake"
msgid ""
"“Sweet is the swamp with its secrets,\n"
" Until we meet a snake;\n"
" 'T is then we sigh for houses,\n"
" And our departure take\n"
"\n"
" At that enthralling gallop\n"
" That only childhood knows.\n"
" A snake is summer's treason,\n"
" And guile is where it goes.”\n"
"    -Emily Dickinson, “A Snake”. ca. 1865.\n"
msgstr ""
"“沼泽与它的秘密何等甜美，\n"
"直到我们遇见一条蛇；\n"
"那时我们叹着气想念房屋，\n"
"转身就走，\n"
"\n"
"以只有童年才懂的\n"
"那种令人着迷的狂奔。\n"
"蛇是夏日的背叛，\n"
"它所到之处便有狡诈。”\n"
"    -Emily Dickinson, “A Snake”. ca. 1865.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:swamp worm"
msgid ""
"“The fool, as I think, at the chasm's brink,\n"
" Prone by the swamp or the marsh's side,\n"
" Did, even as I, in the end rejoice,\n"
" Since the voice of death must be His true voice.”\n"
"    -Arthur Edward Waite, “At The End of Things”. 1906.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我想，那悬崖边的愚人，\n"
"俯伏在沼泽或湿地旁，\n"
"最后也像我一样欢欣，\n"
"因为死亡之声必是祂真正的声音。”\n"
"    -Arthur Edward Waite, “At The End of Things”. 1906.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:tengu"
msgid ""
"“A Bird came down the Walk —\n"
" He did not know I saw —\n"
" He bit an Angleworm in halves\n"
" And ate the fellow, raw”\n"
"    -Emily Dickinson, “A Bird came down the Walk”. ca. 1865.\n"
msgstr ""
"“一只鸟沿小径走来——\n"
"它不知道我正看着——\n"
"它把蚯蚓咬成两半，\n"
"生吞了那家伙。”\n"
"    -Emily Dickinson, “A Bird came down the Walk”. ca. 1865.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:tengu warrior"
msgid ""
"“I can puff up my feathers, look real mean\n"
" Be the old man that this here's scene\n"
" I'm a struttin' preenin' bantam rooster looking for a fight.”\n"
"    -Andrew Bird's Bowl of Fire, “Cock o' the Walk”. 1998.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我能竖起羽毛，摆出真正凶狠的样子，\n"
"做这片地盘的老大；\n"
"我是一只昂首阔步、梳羽抖擞、四处找架打的矮脚公鸡。”\n"
"    -Andrew Bird's Bowl of Fire, “Cock o' the Walk”. 1998.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:tentacled monstrosity"
msgid ""
"“Oozing and surging up out of that yawning trap-door in the Cyclopean crypt I\n"
" had glimpsed such an unbelievable behemothic monstrosity that I could not\n"
" doubt the power of its original to kill with its mere sight. Even now I cannot\n"
" begin to suggest it with any words at my command. I might call it gigantic —\n"
" tentacled — proboscidian — octopus-eyed — semi-amorphous — plastic — partly\n"
" squamous and partly rugose — ugh!”\n"
"    -H.P. Lovecraft and Hazel Heald, “Out of the Aeons”, _Weird Tales_, 25, No.\n"
"     4, pp. 478-96. April 1935.\n"
msgstr ""
"“从那座巨石地穴张开的活板门里涌出的，是一头令人难以置信的巨大怪物；我只瞥了一眼，就毫不怀疑它的本体单凭外貌便足以杀人。直到现在，我也无法用自己掌握的任何词语稍加描绘。我或许能说它巨大——长着触手——有象鼻——有章鱼的眼睛——半无定形——柔软可塑——一部分覆鳞，一部分皱褶重重——呕！”\n"
"    -H.P. Lovecraft and Hazel Heald, “Out of the Aeons”, _Weird Tales_, 25, No.\n"
"     4, pp. 478-96. April 1935.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:titan"
msgid ""
"“And on the other part the Titans eagerly strengthened their ranks, and both\n"
" sides at one time showed the work of their hands and their might. The\n"
" boundless sea rang terribly around, and the earth crashed loudly: wide Heaven\n"
" was shaken and groaned, and high Olympus reeled from its foundation under the\n"
" charge of the undying gods, and a heavy quaking reached dim Tartarus and the\n"
" deep sound of their feet in the fearful onset and of their hard missiles. So,\n"
" then, they launched their grievous shafts upon one another, and the cry of\n"
" both armies as they shouted reached to starry heaven; and they met together\n"
" with a great battle-cry.”\n"
"    -Hesiod, _Theogony_, 8th cent. B.C.\n"
"     trans. H.G. Evelyn-White, 1914.\n"
msgstr ""
"“另一边，泰坦们急切地加固阵列，双方同时展现双手的作为与力量。无边的大海发出可怕的轰鸣，大地轰然作响；辽阔的天空震颤呻吟，不朽诸神的冲锋使巍峨的奥林波斯从根基摇晃，剧烈的震动传到幽暗的塔耳塔洛斯。恐怖的进攻中，脚步与坚硬的投射物发出沉重巨响。他们彼此射出惨痛的箭矢，两军的呐喊直达繁星满天的天穹，在震天战吼中撞在一起。”\n"
"    -Hesiod, _Theogony_, 8th cent. B.C.\n"
"     trans. H.G. Evelyn-White, 1914.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:toadstool"
msgid ""
"“But the Seneschal gathered the toadstool fly-bane.”\n"
"    -Adam Mickiewicz, _Pan Tadeusz_, III. 1834.\n"
"     trans. G.R. Noyes, 1917.\n"
msgstr ""
"“而总管采集的是毒蝇伞。”\n"
"    -Adam Mickiewicz, _Pan Tadeusz_, III. 1834.\n"
"     trans. G.R. Noyes, 1917.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:toenail golem"
msgid ""
"“Gentle socks pamper them by day, and shoes cobbled of leather fortify them,\n"
" but my toes hardly notice. All they're interested in is turning out\n"
" toenails—semitransparent, flexible sheets of a hornlike material, as defence\n"
" against—whom?”\n"
"    -Jorge Luis Borges, “Toenails”. 1960.\n"
"    trans. Andrew Hurley, 1998.\n"
msgstr ""
"“白天，柔软的袜子娇宠着它们，皮革缝制的鞋子护卫着它们，我的脚趾却几乎毫不在意。它们唯一感兴趣的，就是不断制造脚趾甲——半透明、柔韧的角质薄片，用来抵御——谁呢？”\n"
"    -Jorge Luis Borges, “Toenails”. 1960.\n"
"    trans. Andrew Hurley, 1998.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:tormentor"
msgid ""
"“Thou art to me a delicious torment.”\n"
"    -Ralph Waldo Emerson, _Essays: First Series_, Essay VI: Friendship. 1841.\n"
msgstr ""
"“你于我是一种甜美的折磨。”\n"
"    -Ralph Waldo Emerson, _Essays: First Series_, Essay VI: Friendship. 1841.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:torpor snail"
msgid ""
"“Snail, snail, slug-slow,\n"
" To me thy four horns show;\n"
" If thou dost not show me thy four,\n"
" I will throw thee out of the door,\n"
" For the crow in the gutter,\n"
" To eat for bread and butter.”\n"
"    -Silesian rhyme. Quoted by S.W. Singer in _Notes and Queries_, no. 69.\n"
"     1851.\n"
msgstr ""
"“蜗牛，蜗牛，慢吞吞，\n"
"四只角儿伸给我；\n"
"若不伸出四只角，\n"
"我就把你扔出门，\n"
"让沟里的乌鸦，\n"
"拿你当黄油面包吃。”\n"
"    -Silesian rhyme. Quoted by S.W. Singer in _Notes and Queries_, no. 69.\n"
"     1851.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:training dummy"
msgid ""
"“Things are only mannequins and even the great world-historical events are only\n"
" costumes beneath which they exchange glances with nothingness, with the base\n"
" and the banal.”\n"
"    -Walter Benjamin, _Protocols to the Experiments on Hashish, Opium and\n"
"     Mescaline 1927-1934_, “Protocol II: Highlights of the Second Hashish\n"
"     Impression”. 15 January 1928.\n"
"     trans. Scott J. Thompson, 1997.\n"
msgstr ""
"“事物不过是人体模型，甚至宏大的世界历史事件也不过是戏服；在衣装之下，它们与虚无、卑下和平庸彼此交换眼色。”\n"
"    -Walter Benjamin, _Protocols to the Experiments on Hashish, Opium and\n"
"     Mescaline 1927-1934_, “Protocol II: Highlights of the Second Hashish\n"
"     Impression”. 15 January 1928.\n"
"     trans. Scott J. Thompson, 1997.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:two-headed ogre"
msgid "<ogre>\n"
msgstr "<ogre>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:tyrant leech"
msgid ""
" Scully: “Where the hell did it come from?”\n"
" Mulder: “I don’t know, but it looks like I’m going to have to tell Skinner\n"
"          that his suspect is a giant bloodsucking worm after all.”\n"
"    -_The X-Files_, “The Host”. 1994\n"
msgstr ""
"斯卡莉：“它到底是从哪儿来的？”\n"
"穆德：“我不知道，不过看来我还是得告诉斯金纳，他的嫌疑犯真是一条巨大的吸血蠕虫。”\n"
"    -_The X-Files_, “The Host”. 1994\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ufetubus"
msgid ""
"“We were permitted to shriek in the tongue of dwarfs and demons”\n"
"    -Czesław Miłosz, “A Task”.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我们获准以矮人与恶魔的语言尖叫。”\n"
"    -Czesław Miłosz, “A Task”.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ugly thing"
msgid ""
"“Beauty is no quality in things themselves: It exists merely in the mind which\n"
" contemplates them; and each mind perceives a different beauty. One person may\n"
" even perceive deformity, where another is sensible of beauty; and every\n"
" individual ought to acquiesce in his own sentiment, without pretending to\n"
" regulate those of others.”\n"
"    -David Hume\n"
msgstr ""
"“美并非事物自身的性质：它只存在于凝视事物的心灵中，而每个心灵感受到的美都不相同。在一人眼中美丽的东西，另一人甚至可能觉得畸形；每个人都应安于自己的感受，不要妄图支配别人的感受。”\n"
"    -David Hume\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:unseen horror"
msgid ""
"“The awful shadow of some unseen Power\n"
" Floats, tho’ unseen, amongst us.”\n"
"    -Percy Bysshe Shelley, “Hymn to Intellectual Beauty”, I, 1-2. 1816.\n"
msgstr ""
"“某种不可见力量的可怖阴影，\n"
"虽不可见，仍漂浮在我们之间。”\n"
"    -Percy Bysshe Shelley, “Hymn to Intellectual Beauty”, I, 1-2. 1816.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ushabti"
msgid ""
"“Spell for causing a shabti to do work for a man in the realm of the dead:\n"
" O shabti, allotted to me, if I be summoned or if I be detailed to do any work\n"
" which has to be done in the realm of the dead, if indeed any obstacles are\n"
" implanted for you therewith as a man at his duties, you shall detail yourself\n"
" for me on every occasion of making arable the fields, of flooding the banks or\n"
" of conveying sand from east to west; ‘Here I am’, you shall say.\n"
"\n"
"    -Spell 6, _Book of the Dead_, from _Ancient Egyptian Book of the Dead:\n"
"     Journey through the afterlife_, edited by John H. Taylor. 2010\n"
msgstr ""
"“使沙布提在死者国度代人劳作的咒文：\n"
"分配给我的沙布提啊，若我被传唤，或被指派去完成死者国度中必须做的任何工作，若那里确实如履职者一般给你设下障碍，那么，每逢耕种田地、灌溉河岸或将沙子从东运往西，你都要代我应役；你应当说：‘我在这里。’”\n"
"    -Spell 6, _Book of the Dead_, from _Ancient Egyptian Book of the Dead:\n"
"     Journey through the afterlife_, edited by John H. Taylor. 2010\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:vampire"
msgid ""
" • Scuze me. My friend Burt says you're a vampire hunter. 'zat so?\n"
" — Uh yes. Yes it is.\n"
" • Well you n'ain't gonna find one round here, mate. They ain't no vampires.\n"
" — You don't believe in vampires?\n"
" • 'course not!\n"
" • But I do believe in con artists. And charletans who like to stir up trouble!\n"
" • Dead people who get up at night and suck blood. How stupid do you think we\n"
"   are?\n"
" • My place is haunted with 16 ghosts and they all say there n'ain't no\n"
"   vampires!\n"
"    -Rich Morris, Yet Another Fantasy Gamer Comic\n"
msgstr ""
"• 打扰一下，我朋友伯特说你是猎杀吸血鬼的，是吗？\n"
"— 呃，对，是的。\n"
"• 那你在这儿可找不到，伙计。根本没有吸血鬼。\n"
"— 你不信吸血鬼？\n"
"• 当然不信！\n"
"• 可我相信有骗子，有那些爱惹麻烦的江湖术士！\n"
"• 死人半夜爬起来吸血？你当我们有多蠢？\n"
"• 我家闹着十六个鬼，它们全都说根本没有吸血鬼！\n"
"    -Rich Morris, Yet Another Fantasy Gamer Comic\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:vampire bat"
msgid ""
"“For something is amiss and out of place\n"
" When mice with wings can wear a human face.”\n"
"    -Theodore Roethke, “The Bat”. 1938.\n"
msgstr ""
"“总有什么不对劲，哪里出了差错，\n"
"当长翅膀的老鼠竟能戴上人的面孔。”\n"
"    -Theodore Roethke, “The Bat”. 1938.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:very ugly thing"
msgid ""
"“I'm ugly, I'm ugly as sin,\n"
" But beautiful's out, ugly's in.\n"
" If you're ugly like me, you're in good company.\n"
" There are millions of us who are ugly.”\n"
"    -_The Muppet Show_, “Ugly Song”. 1977\n"
msgstr ""
"“我丑，我丑得像罪孽，\n"
"可漂亮已过时，丑陋才流行。\n"
"要是你和我一样丑，你可不孤单，\n"
"我们有几百万人，全都这么丑。”\n"
"    -_The Muppet Show_, “Ugly Song”. 1977\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:vine stalker"
msgid ""
"“The monstrous plant bud . . . had grown again with preternatural rapidity,\n"
" from Falmer's head. A loathsome pale-green stem was mounting thickly, and had\n"
" started to branch like antlers after attaining a height of six or seven\n"
" inches.\n"
"\n"
" More dreadful than this, if possible, similar growths had issued from the\n"
" eyes; and their stems, climbing vertically across the forehead, had entirely\n"
" displaced the eyeballs.”\n"
"    -Clark Ashton Smith, “The Seed from the Sepulcher”. 1933.\n"
msgstr ""
"“那怪异的植物嫩芽……又以超自然的速度从法尔默的头上长了出来。一根恶心的浅绿色粗茎不断攀升，长到六七英寸高时，便开始像鹿角一样分杈。\n"
"\n"
"如果还有更可怕的事，那就是眼睛里也长出了同样的东西；那些茎秆竖直地爬过额头，已经完全挤掉了眼球。”\n"
"    -Clark Ashton Smith, “The Seed from the Sepulcher”. 1933.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:wandering mushroom"
msgid ""
"“Telimena, wearied with the prolonged wrangling, wanted to go out into the\n"
" fresh air, but sought a partner. She took a little basket from the peg.\n"
" “Gentlemen, I see that you wish to remain within doors,” she said, wrapping\n"
" around her head a red cashmere shawl, “but I am going for mushrooms: follow me\n"
" who will!” Under one arm she took the little daughter of the Chamberlain, with\n"
" the other she raised her skirt up to her ankles. Thaddeus silently hastened\n"
" after her—to seek mushrooms!”\n"
"    -Adam Mickiewicz, _Pan Tadeusz_, II. 1834.\n"
"     trans. G.R. Noyes, 1917.\n"
msgstr ""
"“特莉梅娜厌倦了长久的争吵，想出去呼吸新鲜空气，却又想找个伴。她从挂钩上取下一只小篮子，一边用红色开司米披巾裹住头，一边说：‘先生们，看来你们想留在屋里，可我要去采蘑菇了，愿意的就跟来吧！’她一只胳膊牵着内侍的小女儿，另一只手把裙摆提到脚踝。塔德乌什默默地赶紧跟上她——去找蘑菇！”\n"
"    -Adam Mickiewicz, _Pan Tadeusz_, II. 1834.\n"
"     trans. G.R. Noyes, 1917.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:war gargoyle"
msgid ""
"“Their innumerable sculptures of demons and dragons assumed a lugubrious\n"
" aspect. The restless light of the flame made them move to the eye. There were\n"
" griffins which had the air of laughing, gargoyles which one fancied one heard\n"
" yelping, salamanders which puffed at the fire, tarasques which sneezed in the\n"
" smoke. And among the monsters thus roused from their sleep of stone by this\n"
" flame, by this noise, there was one who walked about, and who was seen, from\n"
" time to time, to pass across the glowing face of the pile, like a bat in front\n"
" of a candle.”\n"
"    -Victor Hugo, _The Hunchback of Notre-Dame_, 10, ch. IV. 1831.\n"
"     trans. Isabel F. Hapgood\n"
msgstr ""
"“那些数不清的恶魔与龙的雕塑显出阴森的神情，摇曳的火光让它们仿佛动了起来。有些狮鹫似乎在笑，有些滴水兽仿佛在叫，有些蝾螈向火堆喷气，有些塔拉斯克在烟里打喷嚏。而在这些被火焰与喧声从石头睡眠中唤醒的怪物之间，有一个来回行走的身影，时不时掠过火堆灼亮的表面，像烛火前的一只蝙蝠。”\n"
"    -Victor Hugo, _The Hunchback of Notre-Dame_, 10, ch. IV. 1831.\n"
"     trans. Isabel F. Hapgood\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:weeping skull"
msgid ""
"“Alas, poor Yorick! I knew him, Horatio, a fellow of infinite jest, of most\n"
" excellent fancy. He hath bore me on his back a thousand times, and now how\n"
" abhorr'd in my imagination it is! My gorge rises at it.”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _The Tragedy of Hamlet, Prince of Denmark_, V, 1. 1603\n"
msgstr ""
"“唉，可怜的约里克！我认识他，霍拉旭，一个有着无穷笑话、绝妙奇想的家伙。他背过我一千次，如今想来却多么令人厌恶！我的胃都要翻起来了。”\n"
"    -William Shakespeare, _The Tragedy of Hamlet, Prince of Denmark_, V, 1. 1603\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:wolf"
msgid ""
"“Teacher: How does a dog smell?\n"
" Student: I don't know.\n"
" Teacher: Correct!”\n"
"    -Traditional Spanish joke.\n"
msgstr ""
"“老师：狗怎么嗅东西？\n"
"学生：不知道。（西班牙语中与‘用鼻子’谐音。）\n"
"老师：答对了！”\n"
"    -Traditional Spanish joke.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:water nymph"
msgid ""
"“Oh, but you can't expect to wield supreme executive power just because some\n"
" watery tart threw a sword at you.”\n"
"    -Monty Python and the Holy Grail, 1975.\n"
msgstr ""
"“喂，你可不能因为哪个水里的荡妇朝你扔了一把剑，就指望掌握至高无上的行政权。”\n"
"    -Monty Python and the Holy Grail, 1975.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:wight"
msgid ""
"“Unhappie wight, borne to desastrous end,\n"
" That doth his life in so long tendance spend!”\n"
"    -Edmund Spenser, “Mother Hubberds Tale”, _Complaints_. 1591.\n"
msgstr ""
"“不幸的人啊，生来注定惨淡收场，\n"
"竟把一生耗在如此漫长的侍候之中！”\n"
"    -Edmund Spenser, “Mother Hubberds Tale”, _Complaints_. 1591.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:worm"
msgid "<ribbon worm>\n"
msgstr "<ribbon worm>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:wraith"
msgid ""
"“God, though this life is but a wraith,\n"
" Although we know not what we use,\n"
" Although we grope with little faith,\n"
" Give me the heart to fight—and lose.”\n"
"    -Louis Untermeyer, “Prayer”. 1919.\n"
msgstr ""
"“上帝啊，纵使此生不过幽影，\n"
"纵使我们不懂手中所用，\n"
"纵使我们以微弱信念摸索，\n"
"请赐我一颗敢于战斗——也敢于失败的心。”\n"
"    -Louis Untermeyer, “Prayer”. 1919.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:wretched star"
msgid ""
"“Stare into the sun\n"
" Wherever you may roam\n"
" Feel it calling you home\n"
" Despite the mounting danger\n"
" Stare into the sun\n"
" Let its fire fill you\n"
" Whatever doesn’t kill you\n"
" Only makes you stranger”\n"
"    -The Sunbeams, “The Tug”. 2020\n"
msgstr ""
"“凝望太阳，\n"
"无论你流浪何方，\n"
"感受它唤你归乡，\n"
"哪怕危险日渐增长。\n"
"凝望太阳，\n"
"让它的火焰充满你；\n"
"凡不能杀死你的，\n"
"只会使你更加古怪。”\n"
"    -The Sunbeams, “The Tug”. 2020\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:wyrmhole"
msgid ""
"“My complete answer to the late 19th century question 'what is electrodynamics\n"
" trying to tell us' would simply be this:\n"
"\n"
" Fields in empty space have physical reality; the medium that supports them does\n"
" not.\n"
"\n"
" Having thus removed the mystery from electrodynamics, let me immediately do the\n"
" same for quantum mechanics:\n"
"\n"
" Correlations have physical reality; that which they correlate does not.”\n"
"    -N. David Mermin, _What is quantum mechanics trying to tell us?_, 1998.\n"
msgstr ""
"“对于十九世纪末的那个问题——‘电动力学想告诉我们什么’——我的完整回答很简单：\n"
"\n"
"空旷空间中的场具有物理实在性，承载它们的介质却没有。\n"
"\n"
"既然如此消除了电动力学的神秘，让我立刻为量子力学做同样的事：\n"
"\n"
"关联具有物理实在性，被关联的事物却没有。”\n"
"    -N. David Mermin, _What is quantum mechanics trying to tell us?_, 1998.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:ynoxinul"
msgid ""
"“He fixed his eyes upon the door, which, slowly opening, disclosed a stranger\n"
" of majestic form, but scowling features, who demanded sternly, why he was\n"
" summoned? ‘I did not summon you,’ said the trembling student. ‘You did!’ said\n"
" the stranger, advancing, angrily; ‘and the demons are not to be invoked in\n"
" vain.’ The student could make no reply; and the demon, enraged that one of the\n"
" uninitiated should have summoned him out of mere presumption, seized him by\n"
" the throat and strangled him.\n"
"\n"
" When Agrippa returned, a few days afterwards, he found his house beset with\n"
" devils. Some of them were sitting on the chimneypots, kicking up their legs in\n"
" the air; while others were playing at leapfrog, on the very edge of the\n"
" parapet. His study was so filled with them that he found it difficult to make\n"
" his way to his desk.”\n"
"    -Charles Mackay, _Memoirs of Extraordinary Popular Delusions_, Vol. III,\n"
"     Part I. 1841.\n"
msgstr ""
"“他盯着门，门缓缓打开，现出一个身形威严、面容阴沉的陌生人，严厉地问为何召唤他。颤抖的学生说：‘我没有召唤你。’陌生人怒气冲冲地上前说：‘你召唤了！恶魔可不能白白被召来。’学生无言以对。恶魔恼怒于一个未经传授的人竟敢仅凭狂妄就召唤自己，便扼住他的喉咙，将他掐死。\n"
"\n"
"几天后阿格里帕回来时，发现房子已被魔鬼包围。有些坐在烟囱顶上，朝空中踢腿；另一些就在矮墙边缘玩跳背游戏。他的书房挤满了魔鬼，以至于他很难走到自己的书桌旁。”\n"
"    -Charles Mackay, _Memoirs of Extraordinary Popular Delusions_, Vol. III,\n"
"     Part I. 1841.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/quotes.txt:zombie"
msgid ""
"“It seemed that while the zombie came from the grave, it was neither a ghost,\n"
" nor yet a person who had been raised like Lazarus from the dead. The zombie,\n"
" they say, is a soulless human corpse, still dead, but taken from the grave and\n"
" endowed by sorcery with a mechanical semblance of life—it is a dead body which\n"
" is made to walk and act and move as if it were alive. People who have the\n"
" power to do this go to a fresh grave, dig up the body before it has had time\n"
" to rot, galvanize it into movement, and then make of it a servant or slave,\n"
" occasionally for the commission of some crime, more often simply as a drudge\n"
" around the habitation or the farm, setting it dull heavy tasks, and beating it\n"
" like a dumb beast if it slackens.”\n"
"    -William Seabrook, _The Magic Island_. 1929.\n"
"\n"
"“They’re not afraid! No matter what we do, no matter how many we kill, they will\n"
" never, ever be afraid!”\n"
"    -Max Brooks, _World War Z: An Oral History of the Zombie War_. 2006.\n"
msgstr ""
"“看来，僵尸虽然来自坟墓，却既不是幽灵，也不是像拉撒路那样死而复生的人。据说，僵尸是失去灵魂的人类尸体，仍然死着，却被从坟墓中取出，再由巫术赋予一种机械的生命假象——一具被迫像活物那样行走、行动、活动的尸体。拥有这种能力的人会去新坟，在尸体腐烂前将其挖出，驱使它动起来，然后把它变成仆役或奴隶。偶尔是为了犯罪，更多时候只是让它在住所或农场干苦活，给它安排枯燥繁重的工作；一旦懈怠，就像殴打不会说话的牲畜那样打它。”\n"
"    -William Seabrook, _The Magic Island_. 1929.\n"
"\n"
"“它们不会害怕！不管我们做什么，不管杀死多少，它们永远、永远都不会害怕！”\n"
"    -Max Brooks, _World War Z: An Oral History of the Zombie War_. 2006.\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of sloth"
msgid "A lazily written book.\n"
msgstr "一本懒懒散散写成的书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of conjurations"
msgid ""
"A book containing an introduction to the destructive magical arts of\n"
"Conjurations.\n"
msgstr "一本介绍破坏性魔法技艺——塑能系魔法的入门书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of hexes"
msgid ""
"A spellbook containing an assortment of powerful Hexes, which sparkles and\n"
"shimmers as the pages are flipped.\n"
msgstr "一本收录多种强大妖术的魔法书，翻页时闪烁着微光。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:decaying skeleton"
msgid "A decaying skeleton.\n"
msgstr "一具正在腐朽的骸骨。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of fixed level"
msgid "A book of magic spells.\n"
msgstr "一本魔法咒语书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of fixed theme"
msgid "A book of magic spells.\n"
msgstr "一本魔法咒语书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:corpse"
msgid "A corpse. Useless and dead.\n"
msgstr "一具尸体。死了，而且毫无用处。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:giant club"
msgid "A giant lump of wood.\n"
msgstr "一大块木头。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:gold piece"
msgid "A pile of glittering gold coins.\n"
msgstr "一堆闪闪发光的金币。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:baked corpse"
msgid "A baked corpse. Warm, useless, and dead.\n"
msgstr "一具烤熟的尸体。温热、无用，而且已经死了。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:longbow"
msgid "A long, strong bow made of yew.\n"
msgstr "一把以紫杉木制成的强劲长弓。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of lightning"
msgid "A book that fairly crackles with arcane power.\n"
msgstr "一本几乎因奥术力量而噼啪作响的书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:great mace"
msgid "An enormous metal war club, of great cumbrousness.\n"
msgstr "一根巨大而极其笨重的金属战棒。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scimitar"
msgid "A long sword with a wide, curved blade.\n"
msgstr "一把刀身宽阔弯曲的长刀。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:demon blade"
msgid "A terrible weapon, forged in the fires of Hell.\n"
msgstr "一把在地狱烈焰中锻成的可怕武器。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:dire flail"
msgid "A flail with long spikes and a heavy head.\n"
msgstr "一把锤头沉重、长满尖刺的连枷。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:falchion"
msgid "A long single-edged sword with a slightly curved blade.\n"
msgstr "一把刀刃微弯的长单刃刀。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:hammer"
msgid "A blunt striking weapon, essentially equivalent to a mace.\n"
msgstr "一件钝击武器，实质上与钉头锤相当。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:demon whip"
msgid "A terrible weapon, woven in the depths of the inferno.\n"
msgstr "一件在地狱深处编成的可怕武器。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:glaive"
msgid "A pole with a large, heavy blade on one end.\n"
msgstr "一端装有沉重大刀刃的长杆。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:rune of zot"
msgid "A charm which allows entry into the Realm of Zot.\n"
msgstr "一枚能让人进入佐特领域的符印。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:deck of punishment"
msgid "A deck of magical cards which wreak havoc on the user.\n"
msgstr "一副会给使用者招致灾祸的魔法卡牌。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:fen folio"
msgid "A collection of spells once used by the great swamp civilisations.\n"
msgstr "一本法术集，收录着伟大沼泽文明曾经使用的法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:giant spiked club"
msgid "A giant lump of wood with sharp spikes at one end.\n"
msgstr "一大块木头，一端带有锋利的尖刺。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:deck of escape"
msgid "A deck of magical cards, mainly dealing with various forms of escape.\n"
msgstr "一副主要提供各种逃生手段的魔法卡牌。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:great sword"
msgid "A sword with a very long, heavy blade and a long handle.\n"
msgstr "一把剑身又长又重、剑柄也很长的剑。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:handbook of applied construction"
msgid ""
"A practical introduction to Forgecraft, covering basic principles and their\n"
"common applications.\n"
msgstr "一本实用的锻造术入门书，介绍基本原理及其常见应用。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:manual"
msgid "A valuable book which allows one to learn a certain skill faster.\n"
msgstr "一本能让人更快学习某项技能的珍贵手册。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:partisan"
msgid "A long polearm with sharp protrusions on either side of the spearhead.\n"
msgstr "一件长柄武器，矛头两侧各有尖锐的突起。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:deck of summoning"
msgid "A deck of magical cards, depicting a range of weird and wonderful creatures.\n"
msgstr "一副魔法卡牌，描绘着各种奇异而神妙的生物。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of burglary"
msgid ""
"A book containing spells useful for theft, breaking and entering, and other\n"
"miscellaneous larceny.\n"
msgstr "一本收录适用于盗窃、破门而入及其他偷盗行为的法术的书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of callings"
msgid ""
"An introductory text on the magical summoning of beasts and beings from other\n"
"realms.\n"
msgstr "一本介绍如何用魔法召唤野兽及异界生物的入门书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of iron"
msgid ""
"An ancient, metal-bound spellbook, covered in dark red blotches. Are they\n"
"rust stains, or..?\n"
msgstr "一本古老的金属包边魔法书，布满暗红色斑点。是锈迹，还是……？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of power"
msgid ""
"A book of powerful and destructive magic spells, rumbling and shuddering with\n"
"barely-contained energies.\n"
msgstr "一本收录强大破坏魔法的书，勉强封住的能量使它隆隆作响、不断震颤。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of the dragon"
msgid ""
"A magical book of spells which allow some command over dragons and their\n"
"aspects.\n"
msgstr "一本魔法咒语书，能让人对龙及其特性获得一定的支配能力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:swamp dragon scales"
msgid "The scales of a swamp dragon. It confers resistance to poison on its wearer.\n"
msgstr "沼泽龙的鳞片，能赋予穿戴者毒素抗性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:orb"
msgid ""
"A sphere of crystal, carried in place of a shield. Magic scintillates within\n"
"its interior.\n"
msgstr "一颗代替盾牌携带的水晶球，内部闪烁着魔法。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:pearl dragon scales"
msgid ""
"The nacreous scales of a pearl dragon. It grants its wearer resistance to\n"
"negative energies.\n"
msgstr "珍珠龙泛着珠光的鳞片，能赋予穿戴者负能量抗性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of displacement"
msgid ""
"A book of spells to bring others closer, or sometimes farther, depending on the\n"
"user's whim.\n"
msgstr "一本魔法书，能随使用者的心意把别人拉近，有时则推远。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:halberd"
msgid ""
"A polearm consisting of an axe blade topped with a spike, mounted on a long\n"
"shaft.\n"
msgstr "一件长柄武器，长杆顶端装有斧刃，斧刃上方还有尖刺。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:lajatang"
msgid ""
"A very rare and extremely effective weapon, featuring a pole with half-moon\n"
"blades at both ends.\n"
msgstr "一件极其罕见、威力卓著的武器，长杆两端各装有半月形刀刃。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:orb of zot"
msgid ""
"An invaluable artefact. Once you have escaped to the surface with it, your\n"
"quest is complete.\n"
msgstr "一件无价神器。带着它逃回地表，你的使命就完成了。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of beasts"
msgid ""
"A book of spells focused on the summoning of beasts. Its pages nip at careless\n"
"readers' fingers.\n"
msgstr "一本专注于召唤野兽的魔法书，书页会咬住粗心读者的手指。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of unlife"
msgid ""
"An unholy book describing a variety of magical methods for the creation and\n"
"command of undead servants.\n"
msgstr "一本不洁之书，记述了创造与支配亡灵仆从的多种魔法方法。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:pair of gloves"
msgid ""
"A pair of gloves. They are worn on the hands, and cover all but the largest\n"
"claws.\n"
msgstr "一双戴在手上的手套，能遮住除最大利爪之外的爪子。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:parchment"
msgid ""
"A brief text on magic, perhaps excerpted from some larger work. It contains\n"
"knowledge of one spell.\n"
msgstr "一篇简短的魔法文字，或许摘自某部更大的著作，其中记载着一个法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:executioner's axe"
msgid ""
"A fearsome weapon covered in dried blood and crude engravings of torture and\n"
"death, bearing an enormous axehead.\n"
msgstr "一件可怕的武器，斧头巨大，表面覆着干涸的血迹，并粗刻着酷刑与死亡的图案。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:stone"
msgid ""
"A small chunk of dense but otherwise unremarkable natural mineral. It can be\n"
"thrown to cause minor damage.\n"
msgstr "一小块致密而平凡的天然矿物，可以投掷以造成少量伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of dangerous friends"
msgid ""
"A book describing the creation and use of magical entities best kept at arm's\n"
"reach. Or, preferably, even farther.\n"
msgstr "一本介绍如何创造与使用魔法实体的书。这些实体最好保持一臂距离，或者更远。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of death"
msgid ""
"A manuscript containing dark spells of Necromancy. Each page is filled with\n"
"grotesque art depicting scenes of disgusting decay.\n"
msgstr "一本记载黑暗死灵法术的手稿，每页都布满描绘恶心腐败景象的怪诞图画。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of fire"
msgid ""
"A book containing advanced spells in the elemental school of Fire, stolen from\n"
"the secret college of the djinn.\n"
msgstr "一本收录火系高阶法术的书，从灯灵的秘密学院偷来。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:pair of boots"
msgid ""
"A pair of boots. They are worn on the feet, and cover all but the largest\n"
"hooves and talons.\n"
msgstr "一双穿在脚上的靴子，能遮住除最大蹄子与脚爪之外的足部。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scythe"
msgid ""
"A farm implement, usually only used by untrained mobs in combat. In practice,\n"
"it's quite similar to a halberd.\n"
msgstr "一种农具，通常只有未经训练的暴民才拿来战斗。实际使用时，它与戟相当相似。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:triple sword"
msgid ""
"A formidable weapon created by a master craftsman. The blade of the sword forks\n"
"into three great razor-sharp edges.\n"
msgstr "一位工艺大师打造的惊人武器，剑身分成三道巨大的剃刀般锋刃。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of geomancy"
msgid ""
"A book containing basic spells involving the element of Earth. Readers are\n"
"recommended to wear a pair of gardening gloves.\n"
msgstr "一本收录土元素基础法术的书。建议读者戴上园艺手套。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:deck of destruction"
msgid ""
"A deck of magical cards, most of which hurl death and destruction at one's foes\n"
"(or, if unlucky, at oneself).\n"
msgstr "一副魔法卡牌，多数会把死亡与毁灭抛向敌人；若运气不好，也可能抛向使用者自己。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:eggplant"
msgid ""
"A rotten eggplant which you can throw at the Crawl developers. It's a bug if\n"
"you ever see this message.\n"
msgstr "一根烂茄子，可以拿来扔 Crawl 开发者。如果你看到了这条消息，那就是程序缺陷。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ice dragon scales"
msgid ""
"The scales of a cold-breathing dragon. It provides great protection from cold,\n"
"while rendering its wearer more susceptible to fire.\n"
msgstr "一条吐息寒气之龙的鳞片，能提供强大的寒冷防护，但会让穿戴者更容易受到火焰伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of annihilations"
msgid ""
"A tome of arcane fury, greatly sought after by sorcerers. It allows the gifted\n"
"and resourceful to conjure destruction with ease.\n"
msgstr "一本充满奥术狂怒的巨著，深受术士追捧。它使有天赋又足智多谋的人能轻松召来毁灭。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of ice"
msgid ""
"A book of advanced magical spells using the element of Ice. Readers are\n"
"recommended to wear a pair of warm gloves.\n"
msgstr "一本收录冰元素高阶魔法的书。建议读者戴上保暖手套。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:prismatic gem"
msgid ""
"[[gem]]\n"
"\n"
"Shining with every colour of the rainbow and a few others besides, some\n"
"consider this gem 'a bit tacky'. Preposterous!\n"
msgstr ""
"[[gem]]\n"
"\n"
"这颗宝石闪耀着彩虹的每一种颜色，甚至还有几种彩虹中没有的颜色。有人觉得它“有点俗气”。荒谬！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:young poisoner's handbook"
msgid ""
"An introductory book for the magic arts of poison. Readers are recommended to\n"
"wear a pair of very thick, non-absorbent gloves.\n"
msgstr "一本毒素魔法入门书。建议读者戴上非常厚实、不吸液体的手套。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:azure gem"
msgid ""
"[[gem]]\n"
"\n"
"As clear and blue as a cloudless sky or a depthless sea, this gem holds its\n"
"secrets locked within impenetrable depths.\n"
msgstr ""
"[[gem]]\n"
"\n"
"这颗宝石像无云的天空或无底的海洋一样澄澈湛蓝，把秘密锁在无法窥透的深处。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of dreams"
msgid ""
"The somniloquent utterings of a famed mystic, using uniquely bizarre imagery\n"
"and cryptic digressions to describe spells drawn from the mystic's visions.\n"
msgstr "一位著名神秘学者的梦呓，以独特怪异的意象和晦涩离题的叙述，描述从其幻梦中得来的法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of minor magic"
msgid ""
"A spellbook containing a variety of simple but useful magical incantations.\n"
"Many prominent spellcasters used this book to begin their arcane studies.\n"
msgstr "一本收录多种简单实用咒语的魔法书。许多著名施法者都用它开始奥术学习。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of necromancy"
msgid ""
"A macabre book containing basic Necromancy spells. Readers are recommended to\n"
"wear a pair of gloves they don't mind disposing of afterward.\n"
msgstr "一本阴森的基础死灵魔法书。建议读者戴上用完即可丢弃的手套。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of spatial translocations"
msgid ""
"A basic spellbook on the magical field of Translocations. Many would-be mages\n"
"have seen it disappear just as they needed it most.\n"
msgstr "一本位移系魔法领域的基础魔法书。许多准法师都曾发现，它偏偏在最需要的时候消失了。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:storm dragon scales"
msgid ""
"The scales of a lightning-breathing dragon. It is heavier than most dragon\n"
"scale armours, and gives its wearer resistance to electrical discharges.\n"
msgstr "一条吐息闪电之龙的鳞片，比大多数龙鳞甲沉重，能赋予穿戴者电击抗性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of spectacle"
msgid ""
"A book covered in glittering sequins. An impromptu lightshow bursts from every\n"
"page, clearly reserving this book for only the tackiest of wizards.\n"
msgstr "一本覆满闪亮亮片的书，每页都会迸发即兴灯光秀，显然只适合最俗气的巫师。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:eudemon blade"
msgid ""
"A sacred blade from the forges of Heaven, inhabited by a good spirit. It is a\n"
"favoured weapon of the Shining One's servants.\n"
msgstr "一把出自天堂熔炉的圣刃，里面寄居着善良的灵体，深受光明神的仆从喜爱。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:troll leather armour"
msgid ""
"The stiff and knobbly skin of a troll. It magically regenerates its wearer's\n"
"flesh, once attuned to the wearer's body at full health.\n"
msgstr "一张僵硬而凹凸不平的巨魔皮。穿戴者生命全满、使它与身体协调后，它就会以魔法再生穿戴者的血肉。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:arbalest"
msgid ""
"A large piece of machinery used for firing bolts, braced with steel and cranked\n"
"with a windlass. It takes some time to load and fire.\n"
msgstr "一件用于发射弩矢的大型机械，以钢材支撑，用绞盘上弦。装填与发射都需要一些时间。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:book of flames"
msgid ""
"The standard text used in arcane academies by students of the elemental magic\n"
"of Fire. Readers are recommended to wear a pair of insulated gloves.\n"
msgstr "奥术学院火元素魔法学生使用的标准教材。建议读者戴上隔热手套。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:sack of spiders"
msgid ""
"A woven silk bag. Opening it will cover the area with webs, spiders, and other\n"
"skittering things. Evocations skill increases spider quality, quantity and webbing.\n"
msgstr "一个用蛛丝编成的袋子。打开它，会使附近布满蛛网、蜘蛛及其他窸窣爬行的东西。唤发技能会提高蜘蛛的品质、数量以及蛛网的数量。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:starry gem"
msgid ""
"[[gem]]\n"
"\n"
"Odd lights twinkle within the depths of this gem. From what strange stuff is it\n"
"made, and from what distant land did it travel?\n"
msgstr ""
"[[gem]]\n"
"\n"
"奇异的光芒在宝石深处闪烁。它由何种奇异物质构成，又来自哪片遥远的土地？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:gem"
msgid ""
"A stone of unearthly beauty and almost immeasurable value outside the dungeon.\n"
"Within its confines, it is utterly useless.\n"
"\n"
"Zot hoards these gems jealously, and will spitefully smash them soon after an\n"
"adventurer enters the branch of the Dungeon in which they rest. Still, a very\n"
"quick-moving adventurer might seize one first and keep its precious shards.\n"
"Zot cannot track gems outside their home branches, so with truly astonishing\n"
"speed, it might be possible to abscond with one still intact... but such a\n"
"feat is difficult to credit, and likely pointless besides.\n"
"\n"
"Once the Orb of Zot is taken, Zot will be unable to smash any gems.\n"
msgstr ""
"一颗美得不似尘世之物的宝石，在地下城外价值几乎无法估量，但在其中却毫无用处。\n"
"\n"
"佐特嫉妒地囤积这些宝石；冒险者进入宝石所在的地下城分支后不久，佐特就会恶意地将其击碎。不过，行动足够迅速的冒险者，也许能抢先拿到宝石，留住珍贵的碎片。宝石离开原属分支后，佐特便无法追踪；若速度快得惊人，或许真能带着完整宝石逃走……但这种壮举令人难以置信，而且多半也毫无意义。\n"
"\n"
"佐特宝珠被取走后，佐特就无法再击碎任何宝石。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:infernal servant spell"
msgid "Summons a major demon.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只强大的恶魔。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:heal other spell"
msgid "Heals a nearby ally.\n"
msgstr "治疗附近的一名盟友。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:invisibility spell"
msgid "Turns the caster invisible.\n"
msgstr "使施法者隐形。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:invisibility other spell"
msgid "Turns a nearby ally invisible.\n"
msgstr "使附近的一名盟友隐形。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon drakes spell"
msgid "Summons multiple drakes and lindwurms.\n"
msgstr "召唤多只幼龙与林德龙。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon sin beast spell"
msgid "Summons a deadly sin beast.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只致命的罪兽。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon spiders spell"
msgid "Summons one or more spiders.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只或多只蜘蛛。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:thunderbolt spell"
msgid "Creates an arc of electricity.\n"
msgstr "产生一道电弧。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:banishment spell"
msgid "Banishes a creature into the Abyss.\n"
msgstr "将一个生物放逐到深渊。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:bolt of cold spell"
msgid "Fires a penetrating bolt of frost.\n"
msgstr "发射一道能够贯穿目标的冰霜射线。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:bolt of fire spell"
msgid "Fires a penetrating bolt of flames.\n"
msgstr "发射一道能够贯穿目标的火焰射线。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:dig spell"
msgid "Digs a tunnel through unworked rock.\n"
msgstr "在未经加工的岩石中挖出隧道。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:fireball spell"
msgid "Hurls an explosive ball of fire.\n"
msgstr "投出一颗会爆炸的火球。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:haste spell"
msgid "Speeds the actions of the caster.\n"
msgstr "加快施法者的行动。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:hellfire court spell"
msgid "Summons demons of flame and damnation.\n"
msgstr "召唤掌握烈焰与天谴的恶魔。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:shadow beam spell"
msgid "Fires a penetrating beam of shadow.\n"
msgstr "发射一道能够贯穿目标的阴影射线。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:slow spell"
msgid "Slows the actions of a creature.\n"
msgstr "减慢一个生物的行动。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:spit acid spell"
msgid "Spits acid at a targeted creature.\n"
msgstr "向目标生物喷吐酸液。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon air elementals spell"
msgid "Summons one or more air elementals.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只或多只气元素。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon earth elementals spell"
msgid "Summons one or more earth elementals.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只或多只土元素。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon fire elementals spell"
msgid "Summons one or more fire elementals.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只或多只火元素。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon ufetubus spell"
msgid "Summons multiple ufetubi; small, annoying demons.\n"
msgstr "召唤多只乌费图布斯，一种烦人的小恶魔。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon water elementals spell"
msgid "Summons one or more water elementals.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只或多只水元素。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:throw flame spell"
msgid "Throws a small puff of flame.\n"
msgstr "掷出一小团火焰。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:throw frost spell"
msgid "Throws a small puff of frost.\n"
msgstr "掷出一小团冰霜。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:venom bolt spell"
msgid "Fires a penetrating bolt of poison.\n"
msgstr "发射一道能够贯穿目标的毒素射线。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:acid ball spell"
msgid "Hurls an explosive ball of corrosive acid.\n"
msgstr "投出一颗会爆炸的腐蚀酸球。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:cold breath spell"
msgid "Exhales a focused blast of icy-cold air.\n"
msgstr "呼出一道集中的冰冷气流。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:corrosive bolt spell"
msgid "Fires a penetrating bolt of highly-corrosive acid.\n"
msgstr "发射一道能够贯穿目标的强腐蚀酸液射线。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:haste other spell"
msgid "Speeds the actions of a nearby ally.\n"
msgstr "加快附近一名盟友的行动。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:hunting call spell"
msgid "Inspires nearby allies to quicken their movement.\n"
msgstr "激励附近盟友，加快其移动速度。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:iron shot spell"
msgid "Hurls a large and heavy metal shot.\n"
msgstr "投出一颗又大又重的金属弹丸。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:lehudib's crystal spear spell"
msgid "Hurls a lethally sharp shard of crystal.\n"
msgstr "投出一块锋利致命的水晶碎片。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:might spell"
msgid "Significantly increases the caster's damage in melee.\n"
msgstr "大幅提高施法者的近战伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:slug dart spell"
msgid "Fires a sharp dart of hardened chitin.\n"
msgstr "发射一支由硬化几丁质构成的尖锐飞镖。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:spawn tentacles spell"
msgid "Extends large tentacles to attack nearby enemies.\n"
msgstr "伸出巨大的触手，攻击附近敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon emperor scorpions spell"
msgid "Summons multiple noble and monstrous emperor scorpions.\n"
msgstr "召唤多只威严而巨大的帝王蝎。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon scarabs spell"
msgid "Calls forth a swarm of death scarabs.\n"
msgstr "召来一群死亡圣甲虫。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon scorpions spell"
msgid "Calls forth a swarm of venomous scorpions.\n"
msgstr "召来一群毒蝎。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon vermin spell"
msgid "Summons multiple rats, spiders, worms, and frogs.\n"
msgstr "召唤多只老鼠、蜘蛛、蠕虫与青蛙。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:volley of thorns spell"
msgid "Launches a small hail of sharp thorns.\n"
msgstr "发射一阵锋利棘刺。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:warning cry spell"
msgid "Generates a loud noise, alerting nearby enemies.\n"
msgstr "发出巨响，惊动附近敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:flaming cloud spell"
msgid "Conjures up a large cloud of roaring flames.\n"
msgstr "召来一大片熊熊燃烧的火焰云雾。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:poisonous cloud spell"
msgid "Conjures forth a great cloud of lethal gases.\n"
msgstr "召来一大片致命毒气。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon holies spell"
msgid "Calls forth divine warriors to aid the caster.\n"
msgstr "召来神圣战士，帮助施法者。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:virulence spell"
msgid "Makes a targeted creature more vulnerable to poison.\n"
msgstr "使目标生物更容易受到毒素伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:doom bolt spell"
msgid "Fires a bolt of accursed malice which inflicts Doom.\n"
msgstr "发射一道蕴含诅咒恶意的射线，施加厄运。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:druid's call spell"
msgid "Recalls woodland creatures from elsewhere on the same level.\n"
msgstr "从同一楼层的其他地方召回林地生物。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:fire breath spell"
msgid "Breathes a blast of fire at a targeted creature.\n"
msgstr "向目标生物喷吐一道火焰。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:freezing cloud spell"
msgid "Conjures up a large cloud of lethally cold vapour.\n"
msgstr "召来一大片致命寒气构成的云雾。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:ink cloud spell"
msgid "Releases a thick cloud of ink to obscure vision.\n"
msgstr "释放浓厚的墨云，遮蔽视线。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:mass confusion spell"
msgid "Causes confusion in all who gaze upon the caster.\n"
msgstr "使所有注视施法者的生物陷入混乱。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:might other spell"
msgid "Significantly increases a nearby ally's damage dealt in melee.\n"
msgstr "大幅提高附近一名盟友造成的近战伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:pain spell"
msgid "Inflicts an extremely painful injury upon one living creature.\n"
msgstr "对一个活物造成极其痛苦的伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon minor demon spell"
msgid "Summons between one and three minor (rank 5) demons.\n"
msgstr "召唤一至三只低阶（第 5 阶）恶魔。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon tzitzimitl spell"
msgid "Summons a tzitzimitl, a demon of disease and despair.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只 兹兹米特尔，一种象征疾病与绝望的恶魔。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:abjuration spell"
msgid "Reduces the remaining duration of any nearby hostile summoned creatures.\n"
msgstr "缩短附近所有敌对召唤物的剩余存在时间。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:blink close spell"
msgid "Translocates the caster a short distance towards a targeted enemy.\n"
msgstr "将施法者朝目标敌人短距离易位。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:entropic weave spell"
msgid "Corrodes the target, with no direct line of fire required.\n"
msgstr "腐蚀目标，无须直线射击路径。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:major healing spell"
msgid "Heals a large amount of damage to the caster's body.\n"
msgstr "为施法者治疗大量身体伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:minor healing spell"
msgid "Heals a small amount of damage to the caster's body.\n"
msgstr "为施法者治疗少量身体伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:portal projectile spell"
msgid "Teleports a fired or thrown missile at a targeted enemy.\n"
msgstr "将射出或投出的投射物传送至目标敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:shadow shard spell"
msgid "Fires a shard of hardened shadow at a single enemy.\n"
msgstr "向单个敌人发射一块硬化阴影碎片。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:steam ball spell"
msgid "Throws a ball of hot steam towards a targeted creature.\n"
msgstr "向目标生物投出一团炽热蒸汽。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon executioners spell"
msgid "Summons multiple Executioners to tear apart foes of the caster.\n"
msgstr "召唤多只刽子手，撕碎施法者的敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon hell sentinel spell"
msgid "Summons a Hell Sentinel, a nightmarish edifice of animated hate.\n"
msgstr "召唤一只地狱哨卫，一座由活化仇恨构成的噩梦建筑。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon mushrooms spell"
msgid "Summons wandering mushrooms and deathcaps next to a targeted creature.\n"
msgstr "在目标生物旁召唤游荡蘑菇与毒鹅膏。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:confuse spell"
msgid "Induces a state of bewilderment and confusion in a creature's mind.\n"
msgstr "扰乱一个生物的心智，使其困惑混乱。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:death rattle spell"
msgid "Exhales the essence of the dying, creating clouds of noxious miasma.\n"
msgstr "呼出垂死者的精华，产生有害的瘴气云。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:electrical bolt spell"
msgid "Throws a bolt of electricity at the target, with high accuracy.\n"
msgstr "向目标发射一道命中率很高的闪电。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:major destruction spell"
msgid "Shoots a random harmful beam or explosion at the targeted creature.\n"
msgstr "向目标生物发射一道随机的有害射线或爆炸。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:malign offering spell"
msgid "Drains life from an enemy, healing nearby allies in the process.\n"
msgstr "吸取一个敌人的生命，同时治疗附近盟友。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:noxious cloud spell"
msgid "Creates a large cloud of noxious fumes, which may cause confusion.\n"
msgstr "产生一大片可能造成混乱的有害烟雾。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:paralyse spell"
msgid "Prevents a creature from taking any action for a short time.\n"
msgstr "使一个生物短时间内无法采取任何行动。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:shadow shot spell"
msgid "Fires a small bullet of hardened shadow at a single enemy.\n"
msgstr "向单个敌人发射一颗由硬化阴影构成的小弹丸。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:starburst spell"
msgid "Releases penetrating bolts of fire from the caster in every direction.\n"
msgstr "从施法者处向各个方向释放能够贯穿目标的火焰射线。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:blink allies away spell"
msgid "Blinks allies in sight of the caster away from a nearby enemy.\n"
msgstr "使施法者视野中的盟友闪烁，远离附近的一名敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:blink away spell"
msgid "Translocates the caster to a location further away from a targeted enemy.\n"
msgstr "将施法者易位到离目标敌人更远的位置。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:debugging ray spell"
msgid "Fires a ray which does massive damage (1500 hp) and always hits.\n"
msgstr "发射一道必定命中、造成巨大伤害（1500 点生命）的射线。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:shadowball spell"
msgid "Hurls a ball of flickering shadows, which explodes in a small area.\n"
msgstr "投出一颗闪烁的阴影球，在小范围内爆炸。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:chaos breath spell"
msgid "Exhales a large cloud of fumes filled with the very essence of chaos.\n"
msgstr "呼出一大片充满混沌本质的烟雾。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:diminish spells spell"
msgid "Irresistibly weakens the power of an enemy's spells for a period of time.\n"
msgstr "在一段时间内削弱敌人的法术强度，此效果无法抵抗。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:dispel undead range spell"
msgid ""
"Harms an undead creature greatly by interfering with the forces binding it\n"
"together.\n"
msgstr "干扰维系亡灵存在的力量，对一个亡灵生物造成严重伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:eruption spell"
msgid "Splits the earth to draw up a localised, short-lived volcano under the target.\n"
msgstr "裂开大地，在目标脚下升起一座范围有限、短暂存在的火山。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:fleetfoot spell"
msgid "Calls forth winds to increase the caster's movement speed for a short duration.\n"
msgstr "唤来疾风，短时间内提高施法者的移动速度。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:metal splinters spell"
msgid "Fires a burst of metal splinters. Its damage is strongly reduced by armour.\n"
msgstr "发射一阵金属碎片，其伤害会被护甲大幅削减。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:petrifying cloud spell"
msgid ""
"Exhales calcifying dust, which petrifies anyone affected for longer than a\n"
"brief moment.\n"
msgstr "呼出钙化粉尘，生物受其影响稍久便会石化。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:shred spell"
msgid ""
"Spins in place, dealing grievous damage to adjacent enemies with its serrated\n"
"body.\n"
msgstr "原地旋转，用带锯齿的身体对相邻敌人造成严重伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:smiting spell"
msgid "Smites any targeted enemy within sight, with no direct line of fire required.\n"
msgstr "惩击视野内的任意目标敌人，无须直线射击路径。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:spit lava spell"
msgid "Spits lava at a targeted creature. Half of its damage bypasses fire resistance.\n"
msgstr "向目标生物喷吐熔岩。一半伤害无视火焰抗性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:splinterspray spell"
msgid "Fires a burst of wooden splinters. Its damage is strongly reduced by armour.\n"
msgstr "发射一阵木质碎片，其伤害会被护甲大幅削减。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:stoke flames spell"
msgid "Adds malice to hellish fires, binding it with flame into a creeping inferno.\n"
msgstr "将恶意注入地狱之火，使其与烈焰结合，形成缓缓蔓延的炼狱。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon greater demon spell"
msgid "Calls forth one of the greater demons of Pandemonium to serve the caster.\n"
msgstr "召来一只魔窟中的高阶恶魔，为施法者效命。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon undead spell"
msgid ""
"Summons multiple undead monsters, creating various ghosts, vampires, wraiths\n"
"and other lesser undead.\n"
msgstr "召唤多只亡灵怪物，产生各种幽灵、吸血鬼、怨灵及其他低阶亡灵。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:blink allies encircling spell"
msgid ""
"Translocates a number of allies in the caster's sight to surround a targeted\n"
"enemy.\n"
msgstr "将施法者视野中的多名盟友易位到目标敌人周围，形成包围。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:blink other spell"
msgid ""
"Randomly translocates a targeted enemy a short distance. It cannot be resisted\n"
"by willpower.\n"
msgstr "使目标敌人随机短距离易位，无法用意志抵抗。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:bolt of devastation spell"
msgid "Fires a bolt of grief and heartache that cuts its victims' willpower in half.\n"
msgstr "发射一道充满悲恸与心碎的射线，使受害者的意志减半。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:bolt of draining spell"
msgid ""
"Fires a penetrating bolt of negative energy which drains any living creature\n"
"it strikes.\n"
msgstr "发射一道能够贯穿目标的负能量射线，对命中的活物造成吸能。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:bolt of magma spell"
msgid ""
"Fires a penetrating bolt of molten rock. Half of its damage bypasses fire\n"
"resistance.\n"
msgstr "发射一道能够贯穿目标的熔岩射线。一半伤害无视火焰抗性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:dispel undead spell"
msgid ""
"Harms an adjacent undead creature greatly by interfering with the forces\n"
"binding it together.\n"
msgstr "干扰维系亡灵存在的力量，对一个相邻亡灵生物造成严重伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:ghostly fireball spell"
msgid ""
"Hurls an exploding ball of negative energy which drains any living creature\n"
"it engulfs.\n"
msgstr "投出一颗会爆炸的负能量球，对卷入其中的活物造成吸能。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:polymorph spell"
msgid ""
"Randomly alters the form of a creature. It is especially effective against\n"
"shape-changing creatures.\n"
msgstr "随机改变一个生物的形态，对能够变形的生物尤其有效。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:shadow turret spell"
msgid ""
"Forms a stationary turret of solidified shadow that repeatedly fires upon the\n"
"caster's enemies.\n"
msgstr "形成一座固定的凝实阴影炮塔，反复向施法者的敌人射击。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:throw barbs spell"
msgid ""
"Fires a volley of barbs at the target, skewering them and making movement\n"
"painful.\n"
msgstr "向目标发射一阵倒刺，刺穿目标，使其移动时感到痛苦。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:agonising touch spell"
msgid ""
"Cuts the health of an adjacent creature in half. This damage is never\n"
"directly lethal.\n"
msgstr "使一个相邻生物的生命减半。这种伤害绝不会直接致死。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:agony spell"
msgid ""
"Cuts the health of a target creature in half. This damage is never directly\n"
"lethal.\n"
msgstr "使目标生物的生命减半。这种伤害绝不会直接致死。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:blinkbolt spell"
msgid ""
"Transforms the caster into a lightning bolt, and translocates the caster to\n"
"the bolt's destination.\n"
msgstr "使施法者化为一道闪电，并易位到闪电的终点。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:ensnare spell"
msgid "Shoots a stream of webbing at a creature, ensnaring the target in a sticky web.\n"
msgstr "向一个生物喷射蛛丝，使目标困在黏性蛛网中。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:sticks to snakes spell"
msgid ""
"Casts forth sticks and transforms them into snakes. Stronger casters will always\n"
"create stronger snakes.\n"
msgstr "抛出木棍并将其变成蛇。更强的施法者一定会造出更强的蛇。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:strip willpower spell"
msgid ""
"Greatly reduces the target's willpower, making them more vulnerable to a\n"
"variety of magical effects.\n"
msgstr "大幅降低目标的意志，使其更容易受到各种魔法效果影响。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:lee's rapid deconstruction spell"
msgid ""
"Fragments a wall or a suitably brittle visible monster into an explosion of\n"
"deadly shrapnel. It can be used on monsters made of ice, bone, or any wall-like\n"
"substance, as well as those turned to stone by petrification. Its damage is\n"
"strongly reduced by armour.\n"
"\n"
"Targets made from rock, stone, ice or bone will cause a small explosion. Metal\n"
"targets will cause a small but more damaging explosion, and targets made from\n"
"crystal will cause a large and more damaging explosion.\n"
msgstr ""
"将墙壁或视野中足够脆硬的怪物炸成致命的碎片。它可以用于由冰、骨或任何类似墙壁的物质构成的怪物，也能用于因石化而变成石头的怪物。护甲会大幅削减其伤害。\n"
"\n"
"岩石、石头、冰或骨质目标会产生小型爆炸。金属目标的爆炸范围小，但伤害更高；水晶目标则会产生范围更大、伤害也更高的爆炸。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:fire storm spell"
msgid ""
"Calls forth a mighty storm of roaring flame directly onto the target, dealing\n"
"damage in a large area and leaving behind short-lived fire vortices. Half of\n"
"its damage bypasses fire resistance.\n"
msgstr "直接在目标处召来猛烈咆哮的火焰风暴，对大片区域造成伤害，并留下短暂存在的火焰漩涡。一半伤害无视火焰抗性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:ignition spell"
msgid ""
"All foes in the caster's surroundings are engulfed in balls of fire. The caster\n"
"and their allies are protected from the fire and will never be harmed by this\n"
"spell.\n"
msgstr "施法者周围的所有敌人都会被火球吞没。施法者及其盟友受到火焰保护，绝不会被此法术伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:polar vortex spell"
msgid ""
"Turns the air around the caster into a freezing vortex, doing tremendous damage\n"
"to everyone caught in it that can only be half-mitigated by resistance to\n"
"cold. Those affected will also be swept up into the air and tossed around.\n"
"Only the eye of the storm is a safe place, and it follows the caster. The\n"
"vortex is unable to follow the caster through long-distance translocations.\n"
"The spell's effectiveness is greatly diminished in closed areas. After the\n"
"vortex fades, it cannot be called forth again for a short time.\n"
msgstr "将施法者周围的空气变成冰冻漩涡，对卷入其中的所有人造成巨量伤害；寒冷抗性只能削减其中一半伤害。受影响者还会被卷上空中，抛来甩去。只有风眼是安全的，它会跟随施法者移动，但漩涡无法随施法者进行远距离易位。在封闭区域中，法术效果会大幅减弱。漩涡消散后，短时间内无法再次召来。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:shatter spell"
msgid ""
"Causes an enormous burst of concussive force around the caster, dealing severe\n"
"damage to all nearby creatures. It is especially effective against those made\n"
"from ice, bone, or any wall-like substance (such as rock, metal or crystal), as\n"
"well as those turned to stone by petrification. It is less effective against\n"
"flying, gelatinous and insubstantial creatures. It may also destroy nearby\n"
"walls.\n"
msgstr "在施法者周围爆发巨大的震荡力，对附近所有生物造成严重伤害。对由冰、骨或类似墙壁的物质（如岩石、金属、水晶）构成的生物，以及因石化而变成石头的生物，效果尤其强。对飞行、胶质或无实体生物的效果较弱，也可能摧毁附近墙壁。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:dragon's call spell"
msgid ""
"Issues a powerful call to a draconic realm, beckoning forth dragon after dragon\n"
"to engage the summoner's enemies. The spell is taxing to maintain, and each new\n"
"dragon which answers the call will further drain the summoner's magical\n"
"reserves. After the call ends, it cannot be issued again for a short time. The\n"
"duration of the call and the species of dragons called depend on spell power.\n"
msgstr "向龙族领域发出强大的呼唤，召来一条又一条龙，与召唤者的敌人交战。维持呼唤十分吃力，每条响应的新龙还会进一步消耗召唤者的魔力。呼唤结束后，短时间内无法再次发出。呼唤持续时间及召来的龙种取决于法术强度。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon horrible things spell"
msgid ""
"Opens a gate to the Abyss and calls through two or more hideous abominations\n"
"from that dreadful place. While powerful, brushing one's mind against the fabric\n"
"of the Abyss in this manner invites Doom upon the caster and may eventually cost\n"
"them greatly.\n"
msgstr "打开通往深渊的大门，从那个可怕之地召来两只或更多丑恶的怪物。虽然威力强大，但以这种方式让心智接触深渊的结构，会给施法者招来厄运，最终可能付出沉重代价。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:malign gateway spell"
msgid ""
"Tears a gash in reality, creating a self-sustained but temporary portal to an\n"
"unknown, tainted otherworld. It requires open space to succeed. After a short\n"
"time, a powerful clawed tentacle will reach through the portal, remaining bound\n"
"to the caster's will for a duration depending on power. With the portal's\n"
"expiry, the tentacle will be severed and turn on the caster. The duration of\n"
"the portal increases with spell power.\n"
msgstr "撕裂现实，创造一道通往未知污秽异界、能自行维持的临时传送门。法术需要开阔空间才能成功。稍后，一条强大、带爪的触手会伸出传送门，在一段取决于法术强度的时间内受施法者意志约束。传送门消失时，触手会被切断，并转而攻击施法者。法术强度越高，传送门持续越久。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:ozocubu's refrigeration spell"
msgid ""
"Turns the air bitterly cold, freezing all other creatures in line of sight.\n"
"This is less effective against creatures packed tightly together - those\n"
"adjacent to their allies will be partly insulated from the cold, taking less\n"
"damage.\n"
msgstr "使空气变得酷寒，冻结视线范围内的所有其他生物。对紧密聚集的生物效果较弱：与盟友相邻的生物能部分隔绝寒冷，因此受到较少伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:borgnjor's revivification spell"
msgid ""
"Instantly heals any and all wounds suffered by the caster, but also permanently\n"
"damages their health, to a degree dependent on (and inversely related to) power.\n"
"\n"
"It is powerful enough to cancel the effects of Death's Door, although doing so\n"
"will briefly paralyse the caster. It has no effect on the undead.\n"
msgstr ""
"立即治愈施法者的全部伤势，但也会永久损害其生命，损害程度取决于法术强度；强度越高，损害越小。\n"
"\n"
"其力量足以解除死亡之门的效果，但这样做会使施法者短暂麻痹。对亡灵无效。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:death's door spell"
msgid ""
"Renders the caster nigh invulnerable to harm for a brief period, but brings\n"
"them dangerously close to death in the process. So close, in fact, that the\n"
"body believes itself to be dead — healing effects will do nothing.\n"
"\n"
"The caster will receive one warning shortly before the spell expires. After\n"
"expiry, the spell cannot immediately be recast, but with high power the caster\n"
"will be left further from death when the effect ends. It has no effect on those\n"
"who are already undead.\n"
msgstr ""
"使施法者短时间内几乎不受伤害，但也让其濒临死亡。身体会误以为自己已经死去，因此任何治疗效果都不起作用。\n"
"\n"
"法术即将结束时，施法者会收到一次警告。结束后无法立即重施；法术强度高时，效果结束后会离死亡更远一些。对已经是亡灵的生物无效。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:infestation spell"
msgid ""
"Calls forth a plague of scarabs, infesting affected creatures for a duration\n"
"depending on power and causing death scarabs to grow and burst from them upon\n"
"death.\n"
msgstr "召来圣甲虫瘟疫，使受影响生物在一段取决于法术强度的时间内受到寄生。它们死亡时，死亡圣甲虫会从体内生长并破体而出。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:death channel spell"
msgid ""
"Binds the souls of slain living, demonic and holy creatures, forcing their\n"
"spectres to remain and fight for the caster for as long as the channel lasts.\n"
msgstr "束缚被杀死的活物、恶魔与神圣生物的灵魂，迫使其幽灵留下，在法术持续期间为施法者作战。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:anguish spell"
msgid ""
"Afflicts nearby foes with supernatural anguish, causing all damage they deal to\n"
"rebound on them for the duration of the effect. Strong-willed foes can resist the\n"
"necromantic visions of pain and suffering, and mindless creatures are unaffected.\n"
msgstr "使附近敌人承受超自然的痛苦，在效果持续期间，它们造成的所有伤害都会反弹到自身。意志坚定的敌人可以抵抗这种充满痛苦与折磨的死灵幻象；没有心智的生物不受影响。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:manifold assault spell"
msgid ""
"Warps space into paradoxical configurations to strike many visible foes with\n"
"one melee attack. Power increases the number of foes attacked with one cast,\n"
"though unarmed attacks strike only half as many targets at once, as additional\n"
"care must be taken when warping one's own limbs.\n"
"\n"
"The time taken for the attack is exactly the same as a normal melee attack.\n"
"Attacks performed this way never miss, but the exact spot struck cannot be\n"
"controlled precisely, making them unable to do extra damage against unsuspecting\n"
"foes.\n"
msgstr ""
"将空间扭曲成悖论般的结构，以一次近战攻击打击视野中的多个敌人。法术强度提高时，每次施法攻击的敌人数会增加；徒手攻击一次只能打中一半数量的目标，因为扭曲自己的肢体需要格外谨慎。\n"
"\n"
"攻击耗时与普通近战攻击完全相同。这种攻击绝不会落空，但无法精确控制命中部位，因此不能对毫无防备的敌人造成额外伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:maxwell's capacitive coupling spell"
msgid ""
"Gradually builds up electric charge in the caster, so long as they maintain\n"
"focus (by waiting in place and not taking any other actions). When a threshold\n"
"is reached, the charge couples with the nearest foe, vaporising them instantly.\n"
"Higher spell power will allow the caster to accumulate charge more rapidly. The\n"
"spell requires a visible target to begin accumulating charge, though a different\n"
"foe may be targeted when the charge is released.\n"
msgstr "只要施法者保持专注（原地等待，不采取其他行动），就会逐渐积累电荷。达到阈值后，电荷会与最近的敌人耦合，将其瞬间汽化。法术强度越高，积累电荷越快。开始蓄能时必须有可见目标，但放电时可以命中另一名敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:irradiate spell"
msgid ""
"Transmutes an ultra-thin layer of the caster's skin (or equivalent) directly\n"
"into pure magical energy, blasting adjacent creatures. It may heavily deform\n"
"its victims, weakening them and reducing their armour. The caster is not left\n"
"entirely unaffected; some of the magic lingers, enough to leave them\n"
"dangerously contaminated after a few castings.\n"
msgstr "将施法者极薄的一层皮肤（或相应结构）直接转化为纯粹魔法能量，轰击相邻生物。它可能使受害者严重畸变，削弱其力量并降低护甲值。施法者也并非毫发无损；部分魔力会残留，施放数次后就足以造成危险的魔法污染。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:alistair's intoxication spell"
msgid ""
"Converts a small portion of the brain matter of those around you into alcohol,\n"
"attempting to confuse all intelligent creatures within view (although\n"
"poison-resistant creatures may resist the effects). The caster will experience\n"
"vertigo briefly if they successfully make contact with other minds. It is\n"
"frequently used as an icebreaker at wizard parties.\n"
msgstr "将周围生物少量的脑组织转化为酒精，尝试使视野内所有有智慧的生物混乱；具有毒素抗性的生物可能抵抗此效果。如果成功接触到其他心智，施法者会短暂眩晕。巫师聚会经常用它来打破冷场。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 exit"
msgid ""
":nowrap\n"
"<white>Tutorial 4 summary: Magic</white>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Spellcasting commands</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input>  learn a new spell\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_SPELLS]</input>  check spell proficiency\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_CAST_SPELL]</input>  cast a spell<localtiles>\n"
"  You can also learn new spells via the <w>memorisation tab</w>.\n"
"  You can cast memorised spells via <input>leftclick</input>, and read their descriptions and check your spell proficiency by <input>mouseover</input> or <input>rightclick</input></localtiles>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_QUIVER_ITEM]</input>  adjust your quiver\n"
"\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>  rest up to 100 turns to regain magic points and health\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_SHOUT]</input>  order allies\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_UNEQUIP]</input>  take off equipment\n"
msgstr ""
":nowrap\n"
"<white>教程 4 小结：魔法</white>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>施法命令</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input>  学习新法术\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_SPELLS]</input>  查看施法熟练程度\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_CAST_SPELL]</input>  施放法术<localtiles>\n"
"  也可以通过<w>记忆标签页</w>学习法术。\n"
"  <input>左键单击</input>可以施放已记忆法术；\n"
"  <input>鼠标悬停</input>或<input>右键单击</input>可以阅读描述并查看施法熟练程度。</localtiles>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_QUIVER_ITEM]</input>  调整备投物\n"
"\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>  休息最多 100 回合，恢复魔力与生命\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_SHOUT]</input>  命令盟友\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_UNEQUIP]</input>  卸下装备\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/help.txt:stash-search.prompt"
msgid ""
"<h>Searching the stash-tracker</h>\n"
"\n"
"You can search for items and dungeon features by name (or a substring of the\n"
"name). In the list of search results, you can select a search result by its\n"
"hotkey to travel to its location.\n"
"\n"
"Some examples of search strings:\n"
"<w>mutation</w>      find all potions of mutation, including potions in shops.\n"
"<w>throwing net</w>  finds every single throwing net and piles of nets.\n"
"<w>shop</w>          lists all shops. Press <w>!</w> and a shop's letter for the stock.\n"
"<w>Lair:2</w>        find everything known to be on Lair:2.\n"
"<w>/D:[2-4]</w>      finds everything on Dungeon levels 2-4. Regexes are allowed!\n"
"              Note that /D:[3-10] will not work as intended, since [x-y] is a\n"
"              regex character range.\n"
"<w>rPois</w>         finds all items with an rPois resistance.\n"
"<w>rC++</w>          finds all items with an rC++ resistance.\n"
"<w>+3</w>            finds all items with a +3 enchantment.\n"
"<w>/Lair.*axe</w> and <w>axe && Lair</w> both show all axes in the Lair.\n"
"\n"
"Some shortcuts:\n"
"<w>.</w>             lists everything on your current level.\n"
"<w>..</w>            lists all items you know.\n"
"<w>0</w> to <w>9</w>        lists all items at the specified waypoint.\n"
"<w>*</w>             lists all items at all waypoints.\n"
"<w>@<<query></w>      lists everything matching <<query> on your current level.\n"
"<w>/<<regex></w>      lists items matching <<regex> as a regular expression.\n"
"<w>=<<string></w>     lists items containing <<string> as a substring.\n"
"\n"
"You can also examine shops and items in the search results by pressing <w>?</w> and\n"
"then selecting the hotkey for the search result. This will give a description\n"
"of the item or the contents of the shop.\n"
"\n"
"The stash search string is case-insensitive.\n"
"\n"
"<h>Searching by item properties:</h>\n"
"\n"
"You can search for spell names (such as <w>Ignite Poison</w>) to find spellbooks\n"
"that contain the spell.\n"
"\n"
"You can search for artefact item properties (such as <w>/prevents.*teleport</w>)\n"
"to find artefacts that have the property.\n"
"\n"
"You can search by some additional item properties: <w>artefact</w> or\n"
"<w>artifact</w> will find identified artefacts, <w>ego</w> or <w>branded</w>\n"
"will find non-artefacts with a brand and unidentified items which may be\n"
"branded, <w>throwable</w> will find things you can throw, <w>dropped</w> will\n"
"find items you have dropped, <w>in_shop</w> will find items in shops, and (if\n"
"the autopickup_search option is enabled) <w>autopickup</w> will find items that\n"
"would be automatically picked up.\n"
"\n"
"Skill names (such as <w>Polearms</w> or <w>Long Blades</w>) will find all weapons that\n"
"train that skill. You can also look for <w>melee weapon</w> and <w>ranged weapon</w>.\n"
"\n"
"You can also search by item types such as <w>book</w> or <w>manual</w> or <w>jewellery</w>.\n"
"For armour slots, use <w>helmet</w> (all headgear), <w>gloves</w>, <w>shield</w>, and <w>body</w>.\n"
"Use <w>armour && !!body</w> to list all armour pieces except for body armour.\n"
"\n"
"<h>Finding Dungeon Features:</h>\n"
"\n"
"You can search for dungeon features by name: all shops will be found by a search\n"
"for <w>shop</w> (including shops that do not have \"shop\" in their name); other\n"
"dungeon features can also be found by name: <w>dispersal trap</w>, <w>altar</w>,\n"
"etc. You can also search for altars by deity name: <w>Zin</w>.\n"
"\n"
"<h>Non-regex operators:</h>\n"
"\n"
"You can use !! to negate a search string, && for a boolean AND, || for\n"
"boolean OR, and <<<< >> for grouping.\n"
"\n"
"For instance, to find rings (jewellery) but not ring mail you could use:\n"
"<w>ring && !!mail</w>\n"
"\n"
"Note that <w>/</w> and <w>=</w> apply to individual patterns, not the entire query:\n"
"you should search for <w>armour && /r(C|F|Pois|Elec)</w>, not\n"
"<w>/armour && r(C|F|Pois|Elec)</w>.\n"
msgstr "<h>搜索物品记录</h>\n\n你可以按名称或名称的一部分搜索物品与地下城设施。在搜索结果中，按对应快捷键即可前往结果所在位置。\n\n搜索词示例：\n<w>mutation</w>      查找所有变异药水，包括商店中的药水。\n<w>throwing net</w>  查找每张投掷网及投掷网堆。\n<w>shop</w>          列出所有商店；按 <w>!</w> 再按商店字母可查看货物。\n<w>Lair:2</w>        查找已知位于野兽巢穴第 2 层的一切。\n<w>/D:[2-4]</w>      查找主地下城第 2 至 4 层的物品；可以使用正则表达式！\n              注意：/D:[3-10] 不会按预期工作，因为 [x-y] 表示正则字符范围。\n<w>rPois</w>         查找具有 rPois 毒素抗性的物品。\n<w>rC++</w>          查找具有 rC++ 寒冷抗性的物品。\n<w>+3</w>            查找附魔值为 +3 的物品。\n<w>/Lair.*axe</w> 与 <w>axe && Lair</w> 都会列出野兽巢穴中的所有斧类。\n\n一些简写：\n<w>.</w>             列出当前层的一切。\n<w>..</w>            列出所有已知物品。\n<w>0</w> 至 <w>9</w>       列出指定导航点处的所有物品。\n<w>*</w>             列出所有导航点处的所有物品。\n<w>@<<query></w>      列出当前层中匹配 <<query> 的一切。\n<w>/<<regex></w>      将 <<regex> 作为正则表达式搜索物品。\n<w>=<<string></w>     搜索包含 <<string> 这一子串的物品。\n\n在搜索结果中按 <w>?</w>，再按对应结果的快捷键，也可以检查商店与物品，查看物品说明或商店货物。\n\n物品搜索不区分大小写。\n\n<h>按物品属性搜索：</h>\n\n你可以搜索法术名，例如 <w>Ignite Poison</w>，来查找包含该法术的魔法书。\n\n你可以搜索神器属性，例如 <w>/prevents.*teleport</w>，来查找具有该属性的神器。\n\n还可以使用额外的物品属性：<w>artefact</w> 或 <w>artifact</w> 查找已鉴定神器；<w>ego</w> 或 <w>branded</w> 查找带印记的非神器，以及可能带印记的未鉴定物品；<w>throwable</w> 查找可投掷物；<w>dropped</w> 查找你丢弃过的物品；<w>in_shop</w> 查找商店中的物品；如果启用了 autopickup_search 选项，<w>autopickup</w> 会查找将被自动拾取的物品。\n\n技能名，例如 <w>Polearms</w> 或 <w>Long Blades</w>，可以查找使用该技能的所有武器。也可以搜索 <w>melee weapon</w> 与 <w>ranged weapon</w>。\n\n还可以搜索物品类别，例如 <w>book</w>、<w>manual</w> 或 <w>jewellery</w>。防具栏位可使用 <w>helmet</w>（所有头部装备）、<w>gloves</w>、<w>shield</w> 与 <w>body</w>。使用 <w>armour && !!body</w> 可列出躯干防具以外的所有防具。\n\n<h>查找地下城设施：</h>\n\n你可以按名称搜索地下城设施：<w>shop</w> 会找到所有商店，包括名称中没有“shop”的商店。其他设施也能按名称查找，例如 <w>dispersal trap</w>、<w>altar</w> 等。还可以按神祇名称搜索祭坛，例如 <w>Zin</w>。\n\n<h>非正则运算符：</h>\n\n使用 !! 对搜索词取反，&& 表示逻辑“与”，|| 表示逻辑“或”，<<<< >> 用于分组。\n\n例如，要查找戒指（首饰）而排除环甲，可以使用：\n<w>ring && !!mail</w>\n\n注意：<w>/</w> 与 <w>=</w> 只作用于单个模式，而非整个查询。因此，应搜索 <w>armour && /r(C|F|Pois|Elec)</w>，而非 <w>/armour && r(C|F|Pois|Elec)</w>。\n\n\n中文搜索（仅中文语言配置）\n\n中文配置下，可使用已知物品、法术、商店和地形的中文译名搜索，英文搜索仍然可用。物品说明保留英文前缀，并追加可用的中文前缀。未鉴定物品只能按已知外观搜索，不会因中文搜索揭示真实名称或隐藏属性。\n\n治疗药水 查找已鉴定的治疗药水。\n治疗药水（配合当前层限定符） 只在当前层查找。\n防具 && !!躯干防具 查找躯干防具以外的防具。\n神器 && 火抗 查找符合条件的已知神器。\n魔法飞弹 查找已知包含此法术的魔法书。\n野兽巢穴:2 按中文分支名限定楼层，也接受中文冒号。\n\n=、/、当前层限定符 和布尔运算符保持原用法；中文译文缺失时，仍可使用原英文名称与前缀。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/help.txt:wiz-monster"
msgid ""
"<h>Create specified monster</h>\n"
"\n"
"To create a monster with the default equipment for its species, simply enter\n"
"the species name, such as <w>kobold</w> or <w>Yiuf</w>.\n"
"\n"
"A hydra or slymdra can be given a specific number of heads by calling it an\n"
"n<w>-headed</w> <w>hydra</w> or n<w>-headed</w> <w>slymdra</w> (with a maximum of 20 heads):\n"
"\n"
"<w>four-headed hydra</w>\n"
"\n"
"To set the colour a (very) ugly thing takes when it is first created, use:\n"
"\n"
"<w>white very ugly thing</w>\n"
"\n"
"The valid colours are <w>brown</w>, <w>cyan</w>, <w>green</w>, <w>purple</w>, <w>red</w> and <w>white</w>.\n"
"\n"
"A mutant beast can be customised by prefacing it with a maturity level and/or\n"
"hyphen-separated set of traits, as follows:\n"
"\n"
"<w>mature shock-weird mutant beast</w>\n"
"\n"
"The valid maturity levels are <w>larval</w>, <w>juvenile</w>, <w>mature</w>, <w>elder</w> and <w>primal</w>. The\n"
"facets are <w>sting</w>, <w>bat</w>, <w>fire</w>, <w>weird</w>, <w>shock</w> and <w>ox</w>.\n"
"\n"
"A slime creature's size can be set to other than normal using the prefixes\n"
"<w>large</w>, <w>very large</w>, <w>enormous</w> or <w>titanic</w>:\n"
"\n"
"<w>very large slime creature</w>\n"
"\n"
"If a monster is a member of a band, you can request that it be eligible for\n"
"band members by adding the keyword <w>band</w> to the name. For instance:\n"
"\n"
"<w>orc warlord band</w>\n"
"\n"
"Specifying <w>band</w> doesn't force bands to be placed - it requests that the game\n"
"use the normal chances of creating a band. A band will only be placed if there\n"
"is space for it.\n"
"\n"
"A monster can be given specific items by following the monster name with a\n"
"semi-colon and then with an item list. For example:\n"
"\n"
"<w>orc ; rapier | quick blade . chain mail | plate armour</w>\n"
"\n"
"will generate an orc wielding either a rapier or a quick blade and wearing\n"
"either chain mail or plate armour. Randarts and ego items are only generated\n"
"if they are explicitly requested. Note that any items that the monster was\n"
"originally generated with will be removed and destroyed. This can be used to\n"
"force a monster to have no items whatsoever:\n"
"\n"
"<w>orc; nothing</w>\n"
"\n"
"For further information, see <cyan>docs/develop/levels/syntax.txt</cyan>, section <cyan>ITEMS</cyan>.\n"
"Any reference to a slash (<w>/</w>) should be replaced with a pipe (<w>|</w>) and any comma\n"
"(<w>,</w>) with a full stop (<w>.</w>).\n"
"\n"
"The same syntax is also used to create a specific type of dancing weapon:\n"
"\n"
"<w>dancing weapon; rapier</w>\n"
"\n"
"Limitations: If a monster is given a random launcher, there is no way to force\n"
"the ammo type to match the launcher type. As a special case, however, a\n"
"launcher dancing weapon is always generated with some suitable ammunition.\n"
"\n"
"You can specify that a monster will always generate a corpse by using the tag\n"
"<w>always_corpse</w>, or that it will never generate a corpse with <w>never_corpse</w>.\n"
"\n"
"By default, monsters are generated asleep. This is changed by prefixing the\n"
"name with <w>generate_awake</w>.\n"
"\n"
"<w>generate_awake boulder beetle</w>\n"
"\n"
"A prefix of <w>patrolling</w> prevents it from walking out of sight of the the place\n"
"where it was created.\n"
"\n"
"You can set the monster's god using the <w>god</w>: specifier as follows:\n"
"\n"
"<w>orc god:the_shining_one</w>\n"
"\n"
"If the monster is to be a gift of the specified god, this should be suffixed\n"
"with <w>god_gift</w>:\n"
"\n"
"<w>orc god:the_shining_one god_gift</w>\n"
"\n"
"Note that the monster will not be considered a god gift unless <w>god_gift</w> is\n"
"explicitly set.\n"
"\n"
"You can set the monster's faction by specifying <w>att</w>: one of:\n"
"\n"
"* <w>att:hostile</w> -- the default\n"
"* <w>att:friendly</w> -- tame, will follow you\n"
"* <w>att:neutral</w> -- hostile to both you and att:hostile monsters\n"
"* <w>att:good_neutral</w> -- hostile to att:hostile\n"
"* <w>att:fellow_slime</w> -- tame, won't follow you\n"
"\n"
"Monsters can be given colours that override their default colour:\n"
"\n"
"<w>col:darkgrey fungus</w>\n"
"\n"
"The colour <w>any</w> can be given, in which case a random colour will be chosen.\n"
"\n"
"You can override the displayed monster tile using the <w>tile</w>: specifier as\n"
"follows:\n"
"\n"
"<w>rat tile:mons_giant_bat</w>\n"
"\n"
"In tiles version, this would create a monster that uses the \"<cyan>mons_giant_bat</cyan>\"\n"
"tile, but is otherwise identical to a rat. In ASCII mode, this will do\n"
"nothing.\n"
"\n"
"If you want to place a random monster suitable for the level the map is\n"
"generated on, you can use\n"
"\n"
"<w>random</w>\n"
"\n"
"If you want to place a random monster suitable for some other place, you can\n"
"use a place: tag in the monster spec:\n"
"\n"
"<w>place:Abyss</w>\n"
"\n"
"Using <w>place</w>: implies that you want a random monster. You can also request\n"
"zombies from random monsters suitable for some other depth as (e.g.):\n"
"\n"
"<w>place:Elf:3 zombie</w>\n"
"\n"
"The available modifiers are <w>zombie</w>, <w>draugr</w>, <w>simulacrum</w>, and <w>spectre</w>.\n"
"\n"
"<h>Overriding Monster Names</h>\n"
"\n"
"Individual monsters can be given names as follows:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold name:Durwent</w>\n"
"\n"
"This will cause the monster to appear as \"<cyan>Durwent the kobold</cyan>\". Spaces can be\n"
"placed in the name by substituting them with the _ symbol. It is worth noting\n"
"that \"<cyan>the <<race></cyan>\" will be appended to all names, which should be considered\n"
"when coming up with them.\n"
"\n"
"There are three different modifiers that can be used on a name:\n"
"<w>name_adjective</w>, <w>name_suffix and </w>name_replace. <w>name_adjective</w> makes the\n"
"name act as an adjective. For example:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold name:ugly name_adjective</w>\n"
"\n"
"Will cause \"<cyan>An ugly kobold</cyan>\", \"<cyan>The ugly kobold hits you</cyan>\", and so on.\n"
"\n"
"<w>name_suffix</w> does the same, but after the monster's base name:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold name:wearing_mittens name_suffix</w>\n"
"\n"
"Will give \"<cyan>A kobold wearing mittens</cyan>\", \"<cyan>The kobold wearing mittens hits you</cyan>\",\n"
"and so on.\n"
"\n"
"<w>name_replace</w> causes the base name to be replaced by given name, as if the\n"
"monster was a unique:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold name:Durwent name_replace</w>\n"
"\n"
"Will result in \"<cyan>Durwent</cyan>\" rather than \"<cyan>Durwent the kobold</cyan>\". The corpse will\n"
"still be a \"<cyan>kobold corpse of Durwent</cyan>\".\n"
"\n"
"<w>name_species</w> uses the name for corpses as-is, without prefixing it with\n"
"\"<cyan>kobold</cyan> <cyan>corpse of X</cyan>\" for <w>name_replace</w>. It also avoids the usual name tag\n"
"that displays above unique and renamed monsters in local tiles.\n"
"\n"
"In combination with <w>name_replace</w> or <w>name_species</w>, there are two further tags\n"
"that can be used when renaming monsters, but not giving them an actual \"name\":\n"
"<w>name_descriptor</w>, and <w>name_definite</w>.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold name:goblin name_replace</w>\n"
"\n"
"Will result in \"<cyan>goblin hits you</cyan>\". However, adding <w>name_descriptor</w> from the\n"
"above flags will result in \"<cyan>The goblin hits you</cyan>\" and in the description of the\n"
"monster, \"<cyan>A goblin</cyan>\".\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold name:goblin name_replace name_descriptor</w>\n"
"\n"
"The <w>name_definite</w> flag ensures that it is never referred to as \"<cyan>a</cyan>\" or \"<cyan>an</cyan>\",\n"
"but that the definite object is always used. Therefore, you will see \"<cyan>The\n"
"<cyan>goblin</cyan> <cyan>hits you</cyan>\", as per above, but also \"<cyan>The goblin</cyan>\" in its description.\n"
"Setting <w>name_definite</w> will automatically set the flag <w>name_descriptor</w>,\n"
"therefore meaning that:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold name:goblin name_replace name_definite</w>\n"
"\n"
"is exactly the same as:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold name:goblin name_replace name_descriptor name_definite</w>\n"
"\n"
"<w>name_zombie</w> can be used to redefine already zombified monsters (including\n"
"draugr, simulacra and spectrals).\n"
"\n"
"Finally, <w>name_nocorpse</w> will cause the name to be completely ignored for\n"
"corpses. For example:\n"
"\n"
"<w>wizard name:sad name_adjective name_nocorpse</w>\n"
"\n"
"will result in \"<cyan>a sad wizard</cyan>\" that leaves \"<cyan>a wizard corpse</cyan>\".\n"
"\n"
"For instances where space in definitions is limited, you can use abbreviated\n"
"forms of these tags:\n"
"\n"
"* <w>name_suffix</w> -> <w>n_suf</w>\n"
"* <w>name_adjective</w> -> <w>n_adj</w>\n"
"* <w>name_replace</w> -> <w>n_rpl</w>\n"
"* <w>name_species</w> -> <w>n_spe</w>\n"
"* <w>name_descriptor</w> -> <w>n_des</w>\n"
"* <w>name_definite</w> -> <w>n_the</w>\n"
"* <w>name_zombie</w> -> <w>n_zom</w>\n"
"* <w>name_nocorpse</w> -> <w>n_noc</w>\n"
"\n"
"<h>Overriding Monster Stats</h>\n"
"\n"
"Further monster customisation can be made by using <w>hd</w> and <w>hp</w>. These two tags\n"
"allow you to completely overwrite the original hit dice and hit points of a\n"
"monster:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold hd:20</w>\n"
"\n"
"Creates a kobold with a hit dice of 20. As its hp is randomised, based on its\n"
"hit dice, this will also be re-rolled. Monsters with a specific hit point\n"
"value will not have this value change.\n"
"\n"
"You can also have a specific value for hit points:\n"
"\n"
"<w>kobold hp:20</w>\n"
"\n"
"Creates a kobold with 20 hit points. This is also useful for monsters (such as\n"
"statues) which come with non-randomised HP values.\n"
"\n"
"Monsters can be marked as summoned by using <w>dur</w> and <w>sum</w> tags. The <w>dur</w> tag\n"
"accepts an integer between 1 and 6 inclusive. The <w>sum</w> tag accepts the name of\n"
"a spell (parsed as per the <w>spells</w> tag, described below) or any of <w>clone</w>\n"
"(Rakshasa), <w>animate</w> (from animate dead), <w>chaos</w> (made from pure chaos), <w>miscast</w>\n"
"(summoned from by spell miscast effect), <w>zot</w> (summoned by a Zot trap), <w>wrath</w>\n"
"(summoned by a god in an act of retribution), <w>aid</w> (summoned by a god in order\n"
"to give aid).\n"
"\n"
"Of the spells, <w>shadow_creatures</w> has the most significant effect, in that\n"
"monsters will dissipate into the shadows rather than disappear in a puff of\n"
"smoke. Using non-summoning spells will also have no effect.\n"
"\n"
"Tagging a monster with <w>seen</w> will override the system and force that monster to\n"
"be marked as already viewed; this means that it won't generate messages such\n"
"as \"<cyan>A kobold comes into view</cyan>\".\n"
"\n"
"<h>Overriding Monster Spells</h>\n"
"\n"
"Monster spell sets can be overridden with a <w>spells</w>: tag, used as follows:\n"
"\n"
"*<w>goblin spells:throw_flame.50.wizard</w>\n"
"*<w>ancient lich spells:symbol_of_torment.26.wizard; glaciate.51.wizard</w>\n"
"\n"
"(a list of spell slots, consisting of a spell name with spaces replaced with\n"
"underscores, a frequency of casting and set of spell slot flags specified\n"
"afterwards with <w>.</w>, with slots separated by <w>;</w>. There should be no spaces around\n"
"the <w>;</w> or after the <w>spells</w>: prefix)\n"
"\n"
"Spell names must exactly match the names in <cyan>spl-data.h</cyan>, with spaces replaced\n"
"by underscores. Spell frequencies are an (x in 200) chance that that spell\n"
"will be cast. Spell flags include:\n"
"\n"
"* <w>natural</w>, <w>magical</w>, <w>demonic</w>, <w>wizard</w>, or <w>priest</w> - the manner in which this\n"
"spell is being cast. Wizards and priests can be silenced and will trigger\n"
"appropriate conducts (Trog will appreciate killing wizards, Beogh will\n"
"appreciate killing priests). Magical, demonic, and wizard spells are subject\n"
"to anti-magic effects. Natural spells do not generate noise.\n"
"* <w>emergency</w> - the monster will only cast the spell when low on health.\n"
"* <w>breath</w> - the spell is a breath weapon, and using it triggers a breath\n"
"timeout during which the spell cannot be cast again.\n"
"* <w>no_silent</w> - the spell cannot be used while silent, even if it is an ability\n"
"type normally not subject to silence.\n"
"* <w>instant</w> - the spell does not expend the monster's energy; they may take\n"
"another action on the same turn.\n"
"* <w>noisy</w> - forces the spell to make noise even if it is a natural ability.\n"
"\n"
"You may use <w>none</w> specify that a slot should be left empty. You can force a\n"
"spell-less monster with:\n"
"\n"
"<w>orc wizard spells:none</w>\n"
"\n"
"<h>Setting enchantments</h>\n"
"\n"
"You may give a monster any number of enchantments. It may start hasted, blind,\n"
"have permanent RMsl, etc. The syntax is <w>ench:<<name>:<<duration>:<<degree></w> or\n"
"<w>perm_ench:<<name>:<<degree></w>. The <w><<degree></w> and <w><<duration></w> fields may be\n"
"omitted.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"* <w>orc perm_ench:blind perm_ench:mad</w>\n"
"* <w>dream sheep ench:sticky_flame</w>\n"
"* <w>stone giant dur:1 ench:berserk</w>\n"
"\n"
msgstr "<h>创建指定怪物</h>\n\n若要创建携带其种族默认装备的怪物，只需输入种族名称，例如 <w>kobold</w> 或 <w>Yiuf</w>。\n\n可以用 n<w>-headed</w> <w>hydra</w> 或 n<w>-headed</w> <w>slymdra</w> 指定多头蛇或黏液多头蛇的头数，最多 20 个头：\n\n<w>four-headed hydra</w>\n\n要指定丑陋怪或极丑陋怪刚生成时的颜色，请使用：\n\n<w>white very ugly thing</w>\n\n有效颜色为 <w>brown</w>、<w>cyan</w>、<w>green</w>、<w>purple</w>、<w>red</w> 和 <w>white</w>。\n\n可以在名称前添加成熟程度，以及用连字符分隔的特征组，来自定义变异兽：\n\n<w>mature shock-weird mutant beast</w>\n\n有效成熟程度为 <w>larval</w>、<w>juvenile</w>、<w>mature</w>、<w>elder</w> 和 <w>primal</w>。特征为 <w>sting</w>、<w>bat</w>、<w>fire</w>、<w>weird</w>、<w>shock</w> 和 <w>ox</w>。\n\n使用 <w>large</w>、<w>very large</w>、<w>enormous</w> 或 <w>titanic</w> 前缀，可将黏液生物设为非普通体型：\n\n<w>very large slime creature</w>\n\n如果怪物属于某个怪物群，可以在名称后添加 <w>band</w>，请求按通常规则为它生成同群成员。例如：\n\n<w>orc warlord band</w>\n\n指定 <w>band</w> 并不强制生成怪物群，而是请求使用正常概率。只有空间足够时才会放置怪物群。\n\n在怪物名后添加分号，再列出物品，可以指定怪物携带的物品。例如：\n\n<w>orc ; rapier | quick blade . chain mail | plate armour</w>\n\n这会生成一个持有西洋剑或快剑、穿着链甲或板甲的兽人。只有明确指定时，才会生成随机神器或带词缀物品。怪物原本生成的所有物品都会被移除并摧毁；因此也可以用它强制怪物不携带任何物品：\n\n<w>orc; nothing</w>\n\n更多信息见 <cyan>docs/develop/levels/syntax.txt</cyan> 的 <cyan>ITEMS</cyan> 章节。其中出现的斜杠（<w>/</w>）应换成竖线（<w>|</w>），逗号（<w>,</w>）应换成句点（<w>.</w>）。\n\n同一语法也用于创建指定种类的舞动武器：\n\n<w>dancing weapon; rapier</w>\n\n限制：如果给怪物随机远程发射武器，就无法强制弹药类型与之匹配。不过，远程舞动武器是特例，总会附带一些合适的弹药。\n\n使用 <w>always_corpse</w> 可以指定怪物必定留下尸体，使用 <w>never_corpse</w> 则指定它绝不留下尸体。\n\n怪物默认以睡眠状态生成。给名称添加 <w>generate_awake</w> 前缀可改变这一点。\n\n<w>generate_awake boulder beetle</w>\n\n添加 <w>patrolling</w> 前缀，可防止怪物走出其生成地点的视野范围。\n\n使用 <w>god</w>: 指定怪物信奉的神祇，例如：\n\n<w>orc god:the_shining_one</w>\n\n如果怪物应当是指定神祇的恩赐，还需要添加 <w>god_gift</w> 后缀：\n\n<w>orc god:the_shining_one god_gift</w>\n\n注意：除非明确设置了 <w>god_gift</w>，否则怪物不会被视为神赐。\n\n使用 <w>att</w>: 指定怪物的阵营，可选值为：\n\n* <w>att:hostile</w> -- 默认状态\n* <w>att:friendly</w> -- 驯服，会跟随你\n* <w>att:neutral</w> -- 敌视你及 att:hostile 怪物\n* <w>att:good_neutral</w> -- 敌视 att:hostile 怪物\n* <w>att:fellow_slime</w> -- 驯服，但不会跟随你\n\n可以给怪物指定颜色，以覆盖其默认颜色：\n\n<w>col:darkgrey fungus</w>\n\n可以指定颜色 <w>any</w>，此时会随机选择颜色。\n\n使用 <w>tile</w>: 指定显示的怪物图块，例如：\n\n<w>rat tile:mons_giant_bat</w>\n\n在图块版中，这会创建一个使用“<cyan>mons_giant_bat</cyan>”图块、其他方面与老鼠完全相同的怪物。在 ASCII 模式下则没有效果。\n\n要生成适合地图所在楼层的随机怪物，可以使用：\n\n<w>random</w>\n\n要生成适合其他地点的随机怪物，可以在怪物定义中使用 place: 标签：\n\n<w>place:Abyss</w>\n\n使用 <w>place</w>: 就意味着请求随机怪物。也可以请求从适合其他深度的随机怪物生成僵尸，例如：\n\n<w>place:Elf:3 zombie</w>\n\n可用修饰词为 <w>zombie</w>、<w>draugr</w>、<w>simulacrum</w> 和 <w>spectre</w>。\n\n<h>覆盖怪物名称</h>\n\n可以为单个怪物命名，例如：\n\n<w>kobold name:Durwent</w>\n\n这会让怪物显示为“<cyan>Durwent the kobold</cyan>”。名称中的空格可以用 _ 代替。命名时请注意，所有名称后都会添加“<cyan>the <<race></cyan>”。\n\n名称可用三种不同的修饰词：<w>name_adjective</w>、<w>name_suffix and </w>name_replace。<w>name_adjective</w> 使名称充当形容词。例如：\n\n<w>kobold name:ugly name_adjective</w>\n\n这会生成“<cyan>An ugly kobold</cyan>”“<cyan>The ugly kobold hits you</cyan>”等表达。\n\n<w>name_suffix</w> 作用相似，但位于怪物基础名称之后：\n\n<w>kobold name:wearing_mittens name_suffix</w>\n\n这会生成“<cyan>A kobold wearing mittens</cyan>”“<cyan>The kobold wearing mittens hits you</cyan>”等表达。\n\n<w>name_replace</w> 用指定名称替代基础名称，就像独特怪物一样：\n\n<w>kobold name:Durwent name_replace</w>\n\n结果会是“<cyan>Durwent</cyan>”，而非“<cyan>Durwent the kobold</cyan>”。其尸体仍会是“<cyan>kobold corpse of Durwent</cyan>”。\n\n<w>name_species</w> 会让尸体直接使用该名称；对于 <w>name_replace</w>，不再添加“<cyan>kobold</cyan> <cyan>corpse of X</cyan>”前缀。它还会隐藏本地图块版中通常显示在独特怪物与改名怪物上方的名称标签。\n\n与 <w>name_replace</w> 或 <w>name_species</w> 配合时，还有两个标签可用于修改称呼方式，而不赋予实际“姓名”：<w>name_descriptor</w> 与 <w>name_definite</w>。\n\n例如：\n\n<w>kobold name:goblin name_replace</w>\n\n这会生成“<cyan>goblin hits you</cyan>”。但加入上述 <w>name_descriptor</w> 标记后，会生成“<cyan>The goblin hits you</cyan>”，怪物说明中则显示“<cyan>A goblin</cyan>”。\n\n<w>kobold name:goblin name_replace name_descriptor</w>\n\n<w>name_definite</w> 保证称呼永远不使用“<cyan>a</cyan>”或“<cyan>an</cyan>”，而始终使用定冠词。因此，除了上述“<cyan>The\n<cyan>goblin</cyan> <cyan>hits you</cyan>”，说明中也会显示“<cyan>The goblin</cyan>”。设置 <w>name_definite</w> 会自动设置 <w>name_descriptor</w>，因此：\n\n<w>kobold name:goblin name_replace name_definite</w>\n\n与以下写法完全相同：\n\n<w>kobold name:goblin name_replace name_descriptor name_definite</w>\n\n<w>name_zombie</w> 可用于重新定义已经亡灵化的怪物，包括尸鬼、冰像及幽灵。\n\n最后，<w>name_nocorpse</w> 会让尸体完全忽略该名称。例如：\n\n<w>wizard name:sad name_adjective name_nocorpse</w>\n\n这会生成“<cyan>a sad wizard</cyan>”，留下的则是“<cyan>a wizard corpse</cyan>”。\n\n如果定义空间有限，可以使用这些标签的缩写：\n\n* <w>name_suffix</w> -> <w>n_suf</w>\n* <w>name_adjective</w> -> <w>n_adj</w>\n* <w>name_replace</w> -> <w>n_rpl</w>\n* <w>name_species</w> -> <w>n_spe</w>\n* <w>name_descriptor</w> -> <w>n_des</w>\n* <w>name_definite</w> -> <w>n_the</w>\n* <w>name_zombie</w> -> <w>n_zom</w>\n* <w>name_nocorpse</w> -> <w>n_noc</w>\n\n<h>覆盖怪物属性</h>\n\n使用 <w>hd</w> 与 <w>hp</w> 可以进一步自定义怪物，完全覆盖其原有生命骰与生命值：\n\n<w>kobold hd:20</w>\n\n这会创建生命骰为 20 的狗头人。由于生命值依据生命骰随机生成，其生命值也会重新随机。具有固定生命值的怪物则不会因此改变生命值。\n\n也可以指定确切的生命值：\n\n<w>kobold hp:20</w>\n\n这会创建生命值为 20 的狗头人。对于生命值不随机的怪物，例如雕像，这也很有用。\n\n使用 <w>dur</w> 与 <w>sum</w> 标签可以将怪物标记为召唤物。<w>dur</w> 接受 1 至 6（含两端）的整数。<w>sum</w> 接受法术名（按下述 <w>spells</w> 标签的规则解析），或以下任一值：<w>clone</w>（罗刹的复制体）、<w>animate</w>（操纵死尸）、<w>chaos</w>（纯混沌构成）、<w>miscast</w>（施法失误效果召来）、<w>zot</w>（佐特陷阱召来）、<w>wrath</w>（神祇为惩戒而召来）、<w>aid</w>（神祇为援助而召来）。\n\n法术中，<w>shadow_creatures</w> 的效果最显著：怪物会散入阴影，而非化为烟雾消失。使用非召唤法术则不会产生这类效果。\n\n使用 <w>seen</w> 标记，会强制将怪物设为已经见过，因此不会出现“<cyan>A kobold comes into view</cyan>”等消息。\n\n<h>覆盖怪物法术</h>\n\n使用 <w>spells</w>: 标签可以覆盖怪物法术组，例如：\n\n*<w>goblin spells:throw_flame.50.wizard</w>\n*<w>ancient lich spells:symbol_of_torment.26.wizard; glaciate.51.wizard</w>\n\n（这里是一组法术槽。每个槽由法术名、施放频率及法术槽标记构成；名称中的空格用下划线替换，后续字段以 <w>.</w> 分隔，各槽以 <w>;</w> 分隔。<w>;</w> 两侧及 <w>spells</w>: 前缀之后都不应有空格。）\n\n法术名必须与 <cyan>spl-data.h</cyan> 中的名称完全匹配，并将空格替换为下划线。施放频率表示每次以 x/200 的概率施展该法术。法术标记包括：\n\n* <w>natural</w>、<w>magical</w>、<w>demonic</w>、<w>wizard</w> 或 <w>priest</w> -- 指定施放方式。巫师和祭司可被沉默，并触发相应神祇行为判定：特洛戈赞赏击杀巫师，比欧弗赞赏击杀祭司。魔法、恶魔和巫师法术受反魔法影响。自然能力不制造噪音。\n* <w>emergency</w> -- 怪物只在生命值较低时施展此法术。\n* <w>breath</w> -- 该法术是吐息武器；使用后会进入一段无法再次施展的吐息冷却时间。\n* <w>no_silent</w> -- 沉默时无法使用，即使这种能力通常不受沉默影响。\n* <w>instant</w> -- 不消耗怪物行动能量，因此它可以在同一回合再次行动。\n* <w>noisy</w> -- 强制法术制造噪音，即使它是自然能力。\n\n使用 <w>none</w> 可以指定空法术槽。要强制怪物没有任何法术，可使用：\n\n<w>orc wizard spells:none</w>\n\n<h>设置附魔状态</h>\n\n你可以赋予怪物任意数量的附魔状态，例如生成时加速、失明或永久偏转投射物。语法为 <w>ench:<<name>:<<duration>:<<degree></w> 或 <w>perm_ench:<<name>:<<degree></w>。<w><<degree></w> 与 <w><<duration></w> 字段可以省略。\n\n例如：\n\n* <w>orc perm_ench:blind perm_ench:mad</w>\n* <w>dream sheep ench:sticky_flame</w>\n* <w>stone giant dur:1 ench:berserk</w>\n\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/help.txt:macro-menu"
msgid ""
"<h>Editing macros and keymaps</h>\n"
"\n"
"To edit a current macro/keymap, select from the menu using the arrow keys or\n"
"by hotkey. (Hotkeys that are used to navigate the menu can be selected by\n"
"arrow keys). To create a new mapping by entering a key, use the [<w>~</w>] key\n"
"or the corresponding menu item, and then enter the key. This allows you to\n"
"create (and edit) mappings that use menu keys. Use the [<w>!</w>] key to switch\n"
"to keymap editing mode (see below for more information on keymaps).\n"
"\n"
"<w>Macros</w> allow remapping keys that are sent to the game when inputting\n"
"commands. This can be used to redefine a command key, or to define an unused\n"
"key. They map a key to a sequence of keystrokes, and keystrokes do carry over\n"
"into submenus.\n"
"\n"
"Example 1: mapping <w>e</w> to <w>p</w> would let the `e` key trigger the same\n"
"command as the `p` key (which on the default settings is autofire).\n"
"\n"
"Example 2: mapping <w>1</w> to the sequence <w>zaf</w> would let the `1` key\n"
"cast a spell that is on the letter `a` with default targeting.\n"
"\n"
"Example 3: mapping <w>F1</w> to <w>Q&a</w> would let the F1 key quiver the spell\n"
"that is on letter `a`.\n"
"\n"
"<w>Keymaps</w> are lower-level key substitutions that replace keys entirely with\n"
"a sequence of keystrokes. They are recommended for changing keys uniformly to\n"
"deal with alternative keyboard layouts. Keymaps are contextual, and the\n"
"default/\"regular\" context is used anywhere that a non-specialised context is not\n"
"active. Macros take the result of keymaps as input.\n"
"\n"
"Example: In some European keyboard layouts, the § symbol replaces ~. Therefore,\n"
"it could be useful to keymap § to ~ in both the regular and menu keymap contexts\n"
"so that the main menu and macro menu become a bit easier to access. (In other\n"
"layouts, this applies instead to ½.)\n"
"\n"
"When used for mapping commands, keymaps can have unexpected side effects: e.g.\n"
"mapping <w>1</w> to <w>zaf</w> via keymap is not recommended, because this will\n"
"make it hard to type `1` when entering a skill target.\n"
"\n"
"<w>Keycodes</w>: Both macros and keymaps accept keycodes when describing the\n"
"action, in the form of <w>\\{n}</w> to enter keycode <w>n</w>. (Use <w>\\\\</w> to\n"
"enter a backslash.) For example, use <w>\\{9}</w> to enter the keycode for the\n"
"<w>tab</w> button. You can bind macros and keymaps by keycode by using <w>~~</w>\n"
"at the macro edit menu.\n"
"\n"
"<w>Saving</w>: Bindings edited at this menu are saved in a .macro file in your\n"
"save directory. They will be overridden by settings in your options file. See\n"
"the `macro` command in options_guide.txt for more information.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<h>编辑宏与按键映射</h>\n"
"\n"
"要编辑已有宏或按键映射，可用方向键或快捷键在菜单中选择。用于菜单导航的快捷键，可以通过方向键选中。要通过输入按键创建新映射，请按 [<w>~</w>] 或选择对应菜单项，再输入按键。这样也能创建和编辑使用菜单按键的映射。按 [<w>!</w>] 切换至按键映射编辑模式；下文有更详细的说明。\n"
"\n"
"<w>宏</w>可重映射输入游戏命令时发送的按键。它既能重新定义命令键，也能定义尚未使用的按键。宏将一个按键映射为一连串按键，且这串按键会继续送入随后打开的子菜单。\n"
"\n"
"例 1：把 <w>e</w> 映射为 <w>p</w>，即可用 `e` 触发与 `p` 相同的命令；默认设置中，该命令为自动发射。\n"
"\n"
"例 2：把 <w>1</w> 映射为 <w>zaf</w>，即可用 `1` 按默认瞄准方式施展字母 `a` 对应的法术。\n"
"\n"
"例 3：把 <w>F1</w> 映射为 <w>Q&a</w>，即可用 F1 将字母 `a` 对应的法术设为备选。\n"
"\n"
"<w>按键映射</w>属于更底层的按键替换，会把一个按键完全替换为一串按键。它适合统一修改按键，以适应不同键盘布局。按键映射具有上下文；当没有专用上下文生效时，使用默认的“常规”上下文。宏接收按键映射的输出作为输入。\n"
"\n"
"例如，某些欧洲键盘布局用 § 代替 ~。此时可在常规及菜单两种上下文中，把 § 映射为 ~，以便更容易打开主菜单和宏菜单。某些其他布局则使用 ½。\n"
"\n"
"用按键映射绑定命令，可能产生意外的副作用。例如，不建议通过按键映射把 <w>1</w> 改成 <w>zaf</w>，因为这样在输入技能目标时就很难输入 `1`。\n"
"\n"
"<w>按键码</w>：宏和按键映射都允许在动作中用 <w>\\{n}</w> 输入按键码 <w>n</w>。使用 <w>\\\\</w> 输入反斜杠。例如，用 <w>\\{9}</w> 输入 <w>tab</w> 键的按键码。在宏编辑菜单中使用 <w>~~</w>，可以通过按键码绑定宏和按键映射。\n"
"\n"
"<w>保存</w>：此菜单编辑的绑定保存在存档目录的 .macro 文件中，并会被选项文件中的设置覆盖。更多信息见 options_guide.txt 的 `macro` 命令。\n"
"\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/help.txt:console-keycodes"
msgid ""
"<h>Keycodes for console and webtiles</h>\n"
"\n"
"Keycodes can be entered as numbers, or in some cases, human readable strings.\n"
"The following tables give both the numeric keycode, and the string; modified\n"
"keys generally must be entered by number. When entering a keycode  as part of a\n"
"macro action, it should be wrapped using the following syntax for keycode n:\n"
"<w>\\{n}</w>. This should also be used when defining a keycode by number in your\n"
"rc file. Example: when defining a macro that triggers F1, you can write\n"
"\"\\{F1\\}\" or \"\\{-265}\". For named keys as part of a macro definition, the \\{}\n"
"may be omitted.\n"
"\n"
"Positive numeric values are ASCII character codes. Negative values are\n"
"crawl-internal keycodes for special keys. The sign is required for these to\n"
"be interpreted correctly. Keyboards vary quite a bit, and so not all of these\n"
"bindings are available on all keyboards; cases where there is often variation\n"
"are indicated specifically below.\n"
"\n"
"The following is a quick-reference for some of the main keys you might want to\n"
"bind.\n"
"\n"
"<w>8</w>: Backspace (and/or Delete, depending on keyboard)\n"
"<w>9</w>: Tab\n"
"<w>13</w>: Enter (and/or the Return key, depending on keyboard)\n"
"<w>27</w>: Esc\n"
"\n"
"<w>-233</w>: Shift-Tab\n"
"<w>-222</w>: Ctrl-Tab (on some keyboards)\n"
"<w>-255</w>: Delete (on some keyboards)\n"
"<w>-265</w>: F1   <w>-264</w>: F2   <w>-263</w>: F3   <w>-262</w>: F4   <w>-261</w>: F5\n"
"<w>-260</w>: F6   <w>-259</w>: F7   <w>-258</w>: F8   <w>-257</w>: F9   <w>-256</w>: F10\n"
"\n"
"Keycodes up to F22 are defined, but may not work on all builds. (On webtiles,\n"
"F11 and F12 are reserved.)\n"
"\n"
"<w>Number pad and navigation keys:</w>\n"
"\n"
"On many keyboards, <w>numlock</w> switches between the number keys and\n"
"navigation keys. Modifiers for these keys may not work on all keyboards. When\n"
"modified number pad keys do work, Shift and Ctrl typically treats those keys as\n"
"modified navigation keys regardless of numlock status.\n"
"\n"
"Navigation keys:\n"
"\n"
"<w>-245</w>: PgDn    <w>-234</w>: Shift-PgDn    <w>-223</w>: Ctrl-PgDn\n"
"<w>-246</w>: PgUp    <w>-235</w>: Shift-PgUp    <w>-224</w>: Ctrl-PgUp\n"
"<w>-247</w>: Clear   <w>-236</w>: Shift-Clear   <w>-225</w>: Ctrl-Clear\n"
"<w>-248</w>: End     <w>-237</w>: Shift-End     <w>-226</w>: Ctrl-End\n"
"<w>-249</w>: Home    <w>-238</w>: Shift-Home    <w>-227</w>: Ctrl-Home\n"
"<w>-250</w>: Insert  <w>-239</w>: Shift-Insert  <w>-228</w>: Ctrl-Insert\n"
"<w>-251</w>: Right   <w>-240</w>: Shift-Right   <w>-229</w>: Ctrl-Right\n"
"<w>-252</w>: Left    <w>-241</w>: Shift-Left    <w>-230</w>: Ctrl-Left\n"
"<w>-253</w>: Down    <w>-242</w>: Shift-Down    <w>-231</w>: Ctrl-Down\n"
"<w>-254</w>: Up      <w>-243</w>: Shift-Up      <w>-232</w>: Ctrl-Up\n"
"\n"
"Number pad keys:\n"
"\n"
"<w>-1007</w>: NP7   <w>-1008</w>: NP8   <w>-1009</w>: NP9\n"
"<w>-1004</w>: NP4   <w>-1005</w>: NP5   <w>-1006</w>: NP6\n"
"<w>-1001</w>: NP1   <w>-1002</w>: NP2   <w>-1003</w>: NP3\n"
"<w>-1000</w>: NP0\n"
"<w>-1010</w>: NPenter\n"
"<w>-1012</w>: NP/   <w>-1015</w>: NP*   <w>-1016</w>: NP+   <w>-1018</w>: NP-\n"
"<w>-1019</w>: NP.   <w>-1021</w>: NP=\n"
"\n"
"Some number pad punctuation keys may not be distinguished from their \"regular\"\n"
"counterparts, again depending on keyboard and build.\n"
msgstr ""
"<h>终端版与 WebTiles 的按键码</h>\n"
"\n"
"按键码可以用数字输入，有些也可以用可读的名称输入。下表同时列出数字按键码及名称；带修饰键的组合通常必须用数字输入。若在宏动作中输入按键码 n，应写成 <w>\\{n}</w>；在 rc 文件中用数字定义按键码时，也应采用此语法。例如，定义由 F1 触发的宏时，可以写成“\\{F1\\}”或“\\{-265}”。在宏定义中使用命名按键时，可以省略 \\{}。\n"
"\n"
"正数为 ASCII 字符码，负数为 Crawl 内部的特殊按键码。负号不可省略，否则无法正确解析。键盘之间差异很大，并非所有键盘都支持这些绑定；下文会特别指出常见差异。\n"
"\n"
"以下是一些常用绑定按键的速查表。\n"
"\n"
"<w>8</w>: Backspace（某些键盘上也可能是 Delete）\n"
"<w>9</w>: Tab\n"
"<w>13</w>: Enter（某些键盘上也可能是 Return）\n"
"<w>27</w>: Esc\n"
"\n"
"<w>-233</w>: Shift-Tab\n"
"<w>-222</w>: Ctrl-Tab（部分键盘）\n"
"<w>-255</w>: Delete（部分键盘）\n"
"<w>-265</w>: F1   <w>-264</w>: F2   <w>-263</w>: F3   <w>-262</w>: F4   <w>-261</w>: F5\n"
"<w>-260</w>: F6   <w>-259</w>: F7   <w>-258</w>: F8   <w>-257</w>: F9   <w>-256</w>: F10\n"
"\n"
"游戏定义了直到 F22 的按键码，但并非每种构建都能使用。WebTiles 保留了 F11 与 F12。\n"
"\n"
"<w>数字小键盘与导航键：</w>\n"
"\n"
"许多键盘用 <w>numlock</w> 在数字键与导航键之间切换。修饰键组合并非在所有键盘上都有效。即使带修饰键的小键盘按键能用，Shift 和 Ctrl 通常也会将它们当作对应的导航键组合，而不受 numlock 状态影响。\n"
"\n"
"导航键：\n"
"\n"
"<w>-245</w>: PgDn    <w>-234</w>: Shift-PgDn    <w>-223</w>: Ctrl-PgDn\n"
"<w>-246</w>: PgUp    <w>-235</w>: Shift-PgUp    <w>-224</w>: Ctrl-PgUp\n"
"<w>-247</w>: Clear   <w>-236</w>: Shift-Clear   <w>-225</w>: Ctrl-Clear\n"
"<w>-248</w>: End     <w>-237</w>: Shift-End     <w>-226</w>: Ctrl-End\n"
"<w>-249</w>: Home    <w>-238</w>: Shift-Home    <w>-227</w>: Ctrl-Home\n"
"<w>-250</w>: Insert  <w>-239</w>: Shift-Insert  <w>-228</w>: Ctrl-Insert\n"
"<w>-251</w>: Right   <w>-240</w>: Shift-Right   <w>-229</w>: Ctrl-Right\n"
"<w>-252</w>: Left    <w>-241</w>: Shift-Left    <w>-230</w>: Ctrl-Left\n"
"<w>-253</w>: Down    <w>-242</w>: Shift-Down    <w>-231</w>: Ctrl-Down\n"
"<w>-254</w>: Up      <w>-243</w>: Shift-Up      <w>-232</w>: Ctrl-Up\n"
"\n"
"数字小键盘按键：\n"
"\n"
"<w>-1007</w>: NP7   <w>-1008</w>: NP8   <w>-1009</w>: NP9\n"
"<w>-1004</w>: NP4   <w>-1005</w>: NP5   <w>-1006</w>: NP6\n"
"<w>-1001</w>: NP1   <w>-1002</w>: NP2   <w>-1003</w>: NP3\n"
"<w>-1000</w>: NP0\n"
"<w>-1010</w>: NPenter\n"
"<w>-1012</w>: NP/   <w>-1015</w>: NP*   <w>-1016</w>: NP+   <w>-1018</w>: NP-\n"
"<w>-1019</w>: NP.   <w>-1021</w>: NP=\n"
"\n"
"某些小键盘标点按键可能无法与普通键区的对应按键区分，这同样取决于键盘和构建。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/help.txt:level-map"
msgid ""
"<h>Level Map ('<w>X</w>' in the main screen):</h>\n"
"<w>Esc</w>        : Leave level map (also <w>Space</w> or any unused key).\n"
"<w>Dir.</w>       : Move the cursor.\n"
"<w>Shift-Dir.</w> : Move the cursor in larger steps (7 by default).\n"
"<w>-</w> or <w>+</w>     : Scroll level map 20 grids up or down.\n"
"<w>.</w>          : Start travel (also <w>Enter</w> and <w>,</w> and <w>;</w>).\n"
"             (Moves cursor to the last travel destination if still on @.)\n"
"<w>[</w> or <w>]</w>     : Examine the next higher or lower level.\n"
"             (Moves cursor to the staircase destination if a known staircase is\n"
"             highlighted.)\n"
"<w>G</w>          : View another level by choosing a branch and depth.\n"
"<w>o</w>          : Move the cursor to the next autoexplore target.\n"
"<w>{</w> or <w>}</w>     : Zoom out or in (tiles only).\n"
"\n"
"<h>Travel exclusions</h>\n"
"<w>e</w>          : Create a travel exclusion, change its radius, or remove it.\n"
"<w>R#</w>         : Create a travel exclusion with a specified radius or change\n"
"             its radius to #, where # is a number from 1 to 8.\n"
"<w>E</w>          : Cycle through travel exclusions.\n"
"<w>Ctrl-E</w>     : Erase all travel exclusions on the level.\n"
"\n"
"<h>Waypoints</h>\n"
"<w>w</w>          : Set waypoint to current position.\n"
"<w>W</w>          : Cycle through all waypoints on the level.\n"
"\n"
"<h>Cycle through features</h>\n"
"<w><<</w> or <w>></w>     : Cycle through up or down stairs.\n"
"<w>^</w>          : Cycle through traps.\n"
"<w>\\</w> or <w>Tab</w>   : Cycle through shops and portals.\n"
"<w>I</w>          : Cycle forward through all items.\n"
"<w>O</w>          : Cycle backward through all items.\n"
"<w>_</w>          : Cycle through altars.\n"
"\n"
"<h>Other</h>\n"
"<w>v</w>          : Examine the last remembered state of the indicated tile.\n"
"<w>!</w>          : Annotate level.\n"
"<w>Ctrl-C</w>     : Clear monster memory.\n"
"<w>Ctrl-F</w>     : Forget level map.\n"
"<w>Ctrl-U</w>     : Restore forgotten level map.{{\n"
"if you.wizard() then\n"
"    return \"\\n\\n\"\n"
"          .. \"<h>Wizard commands</h>\\n\"\n"
"          .. \"<w>T</w>          : Teleport to cursor.\\n\"\n"
"          .. \"<w>Ctrl-X</w>     : Completely wipe out map.\"\n"
"end }}\n"
msgstr "<h>楼层地图（主界面的“<w>X</w>”）：</h>\n<w>Esc</w>        ：离开楼层地图，也可用 <w>Space</w> 或任何未占用按键。\n<w>Dir.</w>       ：移动光标。\n<w>Shift-Dir.</w> ：大步移动光标，默认每次 7 格。\n<w>-</w> 或 <w>+</w>     ：向上或向下滚动地图 20 格。\n<w>.</w>          ：开始旅行，也可用 <w>Enter</w>、<w>,</w> 和 <w>;</w>。\n             如果光标仍在 @ 上，则移至上次旅行目的地。\n<w>[</w> 或 <w>]</w>     ：查看更高或更低的一层。\n             如果当前选中已知楼梯，则光标移至该楼梯的目的地。\n<w>G</w>          ：选择分支和深度，查看另一层。\n<w>o</w>          ：将光标移至下一个自动探索目标。\n<w>{</w> 或 <w>}</w>     ：缩小或放大，仅限图块版。\n\n<h>旅行禁区</h>\n<w>e</w>          ：创建旅行禁区、改变半径或移除禁区。\n<w>R#</w>         ：创建指定半径的禁区，或把现有半径改为 #；# 为 1 至 8。\n<w>E</w>          ：在旅行禁区之间循环。\n<w>Ctrl-E</w>     ：清除本层所有旅行禁区。\n\n<h>导航点</h>\n<w>w</w>          ：在当前位置设置导航点。\n<w>W</w>          ：在本层所有导航点之间循环。\n\n<h>循环选择设施</h>\n<w><<</w> 或 <w>></w>     ：循环选择上楼梯或下楼梯。\n<w>^</w>          ：循环选择陷阱。\n<w>\\</w> 或 <w>Tab</w>   ：循环选择商店和传送门。\n<w>I</w>          ：正向循环选择所有物品。\n<w>O</w>          ：反向循环选择所有物品。\n<w>_</w>          ：循环选择祭坛。\n\n<h>其他</h>\n<w>v</w>          ：检查指定位置最后记住的状态。\n<w>!</w>          ：为楼层添加注释。\n<w>Ctrl-C</w>     ：清除怪物记忆。\n<w>Ctrl-F</w>     ：遗忘本层地图。\n<w>Ctrl-U</w>     ：恢复已遗忘的本层地图。{{\nif you.wizard() then\n    return \"\\n\\n\"\n          .. \"<h>巫师命令</h>\\n\"\n          .. \"<w>T</w>          : 传送至光标位置。\\n\"\n          .. \"<w>Ctrl-X</w>     : 彻底清空地图。\"\nend }}\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:goal"
msgid "What exactly is the goal of this game?\n"
msgstr "这个游戏的目标到底是什么？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:goal"
msgid ""
"A: To survive and to win, obviously. For this you need to find the fabled Orb\n"
"of Zot deep down in the dungeon and bring it back to the surface. To enter the\n"
"realm of Zot, you'll first need to collect three runes to be found in various\n"
"branches of the dungeon.\n"
"\n"
"However, if you're new to the game, you really shouldn't worry about this. Just\n"
"try to delve as deeply as possible and have fun exploring the many side\n"
"branches in Crawl with various characters of different species, skill sets, and\n"
"religions.\n"
msgstr "答：当然是活下去并赢得胜利！你需要找到藏在地下城深处的传说之物——佐特宝珠，再把它带回地表。要进入佐特领域，你必须先在地下城各分支中收集三枚符文。\n\n不过，初次接触游戏时不必为此操心。先尝试尽可能深入，使用不同种族、技能组合与信仰的角色，享受探索 Crawl 各种分支的乐趣吧。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:userdir"
msgid "I can't find my save files, morgue and character dumps. Where are they?\n"
msgstr "找不到存档、死亡记录和角色信息导出文件，它们在哪里？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:userdir"
msgid ""
"If you're playing locally (i.e. not on one of the servers), the chardump\n"
"command will tell you where the morgue file is written, and this information is\n"
"also displayed below the highscore at the end of a game.\n"
"\n"
"The saves/ directory can be found in the same directory as the morgue/ one.\n"
"\n"
"If you'd like to change either location, modify the morgue_dir and/or save_dir\n"
"options in the init file.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果你在本地游玩（而非服务器上），导出角色信息的命令会告诉你死亡记录文件写到了哪里。游戏结束时，最高分下方也会显示这个位置。\n"
"\n"
"saves/ 目录与 morgue/ 目录位于同一目录中。\n"
"\n"
"若要更改位置，请修改初始化文件中的 morgue_dir 和／或 save_dir 选项。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:roguelike difference"
msgid "What are the biggest differences to other popular roguelike games?\n"
msgstr "本作与其他流行的 roguelike 游戏有哪些主要区别？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:roguelike difference"
msgid ""
"A: First, you might want to read the philosophy section in the manual ('?N') to\n"
"read about general important principles in Stone Soup's game design.\n"
"\n"
"As for specific differences, the most important are probably the following:\n"
"\n"
"* Species is *much* more important than the character background (or \"class\").\n"
"\n"
"* Bones files only contain ghosts, never their equipment or cause of death.\n"
"\n"
"* You cannot sell items to shops or elsewhere.\n"
"\n"
"* Resistances can be gained via mutations or items, never through eating.\n"
"\n"
"* There are inevitable deaths, but new players can win without spoilers, if\n"
"  they learn from their mistakes. Very good players can win several consecutive\n"
"  games.\n"
"\n"
"Also, our aim is to give Crawl a really smooth interface, so you should really\n"
"read through the command list ('??') some time. The following commands are\n"
"particularly convenient:\n"
"\n"
"* 'o', for automatic exploration of an unknown level\n"
"\n"
"* 'G', for automatic travel to another level ('G?' for help)\n"
"\n"
"* 'X', to access the level map for travelling and other tasks ('X?')\n"
"\n"
"* 'Ctrl-F', to find and travel to items you've seen before ('Ctrl-F?')\n"
"\n"
"* 'Tab', to move towards or attack the nearest monster\n"
msgstr ""
"答：首先，可以阅读手册中的设计理念部分（'?N'），了解 Stone Soup 游戏设计所遵循的重要原则。\n"
"\n"
"具体而言，最重要的区别大概有：\n"
"\n"
"* 种族的影响*远大于*角色背景（或“职业”）。\n"
"\n"
"* 遗骨文件只保存幽灵，不会保存其装备或死因。\n"
"\n"
"* 你不能向商店或其他地方出售物品。\n"
"\n"
"* 抗性可以通过变异或物品获得，不能通过进食获得。\n"
"\n"
"* 有些死亡无法避免，但新玩家只要能从错误中学习，即使不看剧透也能获胜。顶尖玩家可以连续赢下多局。\n"
"\n"
"我们也希望 Crawl 的界面十分顺手，因此建议找时间通读命令列表（'??'）。以下命令尤其方便：\n"
"\n"
"* 'o'：自动探索未知楼层\n"
"\n"
"* 'G'：自动前往另一楼层（'G?' 查看帮助）\n"
"\n"
"* 'X'：打开楼层地图，用于旅行及其他操作（'X?'）\n"
"\n"
"* 'Ctrl-F'：查找以前见过的物品并前往其位置（'Ctrl-F?'）\n"
"\n"
"* 'Tab'：走向或攻击最近的怪物\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:survival"
msgid "How can I avoid dying all the time? Can you give me some playing tips?\n"
msgstr "怎样才能不总是死掉？能给我一些游玩建议吗？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:survival"
msgid ""
"A: If you've got trouble even reaching the Temple, you might want to try a game\n"
"or two in hints mode for some general playing hints.\n"
"\n"
"Also, there are easy playing combinations and more challenging ones (marked in\n"
"dark grey on the selection screen). If you are new to Crawl, sticking to the\n"
"easier ones is advisable. In general, treat each new monster you meet with\n"
"utmost caution, try to choose the location where you fight monsters, and keep\n"
"an eye on your health and magic.\n"
"\n"
"For specific hints dealing with a particular character, you can press '#'\n"
"in-game to create a \"character dump\" in your morgue directory that details your\n"
"equipment, items, skilling, and available spells. You can share this with other\n"
"players to get feedback and advice through any of the community discussion\n"
"resources listed at http://crawl.develz.org/.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"答：如果连抵达众神殿都很困难，可以先玩一两局提示模式，了解一些基本建议。\n"
"\n"
"有些种族与背景组合比较容易，另一些则更具挑战性（在选择界面以深灰色标出）。新玩家最好先选容易的组合。一般来说，每遇到一种新怪物都应格外谨慎，尽量选择交战地点，并时刻留意自己的生命与魔力。\n"
"\n"
"若想获得针对某个角色的具体建议，可以在游戏中按 '#'，在 morgue 目录生成“角色信息导出文件”，其中详列装备、物品、技能训练和可用法术。你可以通过 http://crawl.develz.org/ 列出的社区讨论渠道，把文件分享给其他玩家，听取反馈与建议。\n"
"\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:downstairs"
msgid "I can't find any downstairs. Am I missing something?\n"
msgstr "找不到下楼梯，是不是漏了什么？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:downstairs"
msgid ""
"A: They may be in a part of the level that is not reachable from the upstairs\n"
"you came from. Try going up to the previous level and coming back down from\n"
"there via a different set of stairs. Note that most levels feature three\n"
"downstairs as well as three upstairs, not counting any escape hatches.\n"
"\n"
"Alternatively, if you are in one of the branches, you might also have reached\n"
"its lowest level and have to turn around to explore another one. Check the\n"
"dungeon overview ('Ctrl-O') to see how deep you've delved into a given branch,\n"
"or the database ('?/b') for the number of levels for unseen branches.\n"
msgstr ""
"答：下楼梯可能位于本层另一片区域，从你来时的上楼梯无法到达。试着先返回上一层，再换一组楼梯下来。多数楼层有三处下楼梯和三处上楼梯，不计逃生舱口。\n"
"\n"
"如果你身处某个分支，也可能已经到了底层，需要折返探索其他分支。查看地下城总览（'Ctrl-O'）可以知道自己深入各分支多少层；描述数据库（'?/b'）则可查询尚未见过的分支有多少层。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:cheating"
msgid "Is there a cheating mode to Crawl where I can play without dying?\n"
msgstr "Crawl 有没有一种不会死的作弊模式？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:cheating"
msgid "A: Press '+'!\n"
msgstr "答：按 '+'！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:weapons"
msgid "I've got two cool weapons. How can I tell which one is better?\n"
msgstr "我有两把很棒的武器，怎么判断哪把更好？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:weapons"
msgid ""
"A: \"Better\" depends on a number of factors, such as your weapon skills, whether\n"
"it's one- or two-handed, the randart properties, the weapon brand, and the\n"
"monsters you're about to face. In general, switching from a weapon type at\n"
"which you are already highly skilled to another one that you have no skill in\n"
"is a waste of time. The brands may greatly differ in damage output, but you can\n"
"get a good idea by bashing a few comparatively harmless monsters with each and\n"
"comparing the results.\n"
"\n"
"The delay in swinging a weapon can be reduced by the corresponding weapon skill.\n"
"You can view your delay and damage rating with a weapon by reading its\n"
"description or pressing '@' while the weapon is equipped. '@' works while\n"
"unarmed too.\n"
msgstr "答：“更好”取决于许多因素，例如武器技能、单手或双手、随机神器属性、武器印记，以及即将面对的怪物。一般来说，放弃已经练得很高的武器类型，改用完全没练过的类型，是浪费时间。不同印记的伤害可能相差很大；分别用两把武器打几个相对无害的怪物，比较结果，就能大致判断。\n\n相应的武器技能可以缩短挥动武器的耗时。查看武器描述，或在装备武器时按 '@'，都能看到攻击耗时和伤害评级。徒手时也可以使用 '@'。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:religion"
msgid "Which gods would you recommend to a beginning player?\n"
msgstr "推荐新手信仰哪些神祇？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:religion"
msgid ""
"A: The most straightforward gods to play are probably Trog or Okawaru (for melee\n"
"combat), Hepliaklqana or Okawaru (for ranged combat), Vehumet or Sif Muna (for\n"
"spellcasting). Also, while unreliable, Xom can be a lot of fun.\n"
"\n"
"Whenever you encounter an altar, be sure to read the corresponding god's\n"
"description (by praying on the altar with '>') and take your time in deciding\n"
"whether to pick this deity or not. As a follower, you can reread your god's\n"
"description, now more detailed via the '!' toggle, on the '^' screen.\n"
"\n"
"You're guaranteed to find altars to almost every god on the first ten levels of\n"
"the main dungeon.\n"
msgstr ""
"答：比较容易上手的神祇大概有特洛戈或奥格瓦如（近战）、惠普利亚卡纳或奥格瓦如（远程），以及维胡梅特或席夫·穆纳（施法）。此外，佐姆虽然不可靠，却也很有趣。\n"
"\n"
"每当遇见祭坛，记得站在上面按 '>' 祈祷，阅读神祇描述，再慢慢决定是否信奉。成为信徒后，可以在 '^' 界面重读描述，并用 '!' 切换到更详细的说明。\n"
"\n"
"主地下城前十层保证会出现几乎所有神祇的祭坛。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:ghosts"
msgid "I keep getting murdered by my own ghosts. Can I deactivate them?\n"
msgstr "我总被自己的幽灵杀死，能关闭它们吗？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:ghosts"
msgid ""
"A: There isn't any such option, and we're not planning to add one, either.\n"
"\n"
"Keep in mind that you don't absolutely have to fight every monster you\n"
"meet, and with ghosts it's even easier: they are generated in sealed\n"
"vaults, and it is your choice whether to open each ghost vault.\n"
"\n"
"Alternatively, you could play a couple characters of strong species/background\n"
"combinations for the sole purpose of busting those ghosts, e.g. Troll\n"
"Berserkers. Or play online, where you'll mostly be killed by others' ghosts\n"
"instead!\n"
msgstr ""
"答：没有这个选项，我们也不打算添加。\n"
"\n"
"请记住，你不必击败遇见的每一只怪物。对幽灵而言，避战更容易：它们出现在封闭的密室内，你可以自行决定要不要打开每一间幽灵密室。\n"
"\n"
"你也可以专门用强力的种族与背景组合玩几局来清理幽灵，例如巨魔狂战士。或者改玩在线版，那样杀死你的主要就会是其他玩家的幽灵了！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:abyss"
msgid "I've somehow ended up in a place called \"Abyss\". How do I get out of here?\n"
msgstr "我莫名其妙到了一个叫“深渊”的地方，怎样离开？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:abyss"
msgid ""
"A: If you are in the Abyss for the first time, chances of getting out are\n"
"slim. Still, here are a few general hints:\n"
"\n"
"* You need to find a gateway leading out of the Abyss. These are rare!\n"
"\n"
"* Don't stick around to fight; move as much as possible!\n"
"\n"
"* If you have it, use defensive equipment (weapons of protection, etc.).\n"
"\n"
"* Use teleportation to end up in a completely new part of the Abyss. (But keep\n"
"  in mind that teleportation will take much longer to kick in than in the\n"
"  Dungeon...)\n"
"\n"
"* Consider switching your allegiance to Lugonu, the god of the Abyss. Upon\n"
"  conversion, you will be able to escape the Abyss immediately (but you may\n"
"  anger your previous god!).\n"
"\n"
"* Descending deeper in the Abyss will increase the chance of finding an exit\n"
"  out, but also increase the danger you face.\n"
"\n"
"* Killing enemies can create a gateway out, but most enemies will be\n"
"  too dangerous to fight; pick your battles carefully!\n"
msgstr ""
"答：第一次掉进深渊时，逃出的希望往往很小。不过，仍有一些通用建议：\n"
"\n"
"* 你需要找到通往深渊外的出口。这些出口很少见！\n"
"\n"
"* 别停下来缠斗，尽可能多移动！\n"
"\n"
"* 如果有防御型装备（如防护武器），就用上它们。\n"
"\n"
"* 使用传送可以到达深渊中完全不同的区域。（但要记住，传送生效所需时间比地下城中长得多……）\n"
"\n"
"* 可以考虑改信深渊之神卢戈努。皈依后，你就能立即逃出深渊，但这可能激怒原来的神祇！\n"
"\n"
"* 深入深渊会提高发现出口的机会，同时也会增加危险。\n"
"\n"
"* 杀死敌人可能产生出口，但大多数敌人都过于危险，不宜交战。请谨慎选择战斗！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:randart"
msgid "What do the terms \"randart\" and \"unrandart\" signify?\n"
msgstr "“randart”和“unrandart”是什么意思？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:randart"
msgid ""
"A: Apart from the standard items you'll find lying around in the dungeon, you\n"
"might also stumble upon artefacts which come in two varieties:\n"
"\n"
"* randart: a random artefact, usually a weapon, armour or jewellery, with\n"
"  random properties such as conferring resistances or abilities.\n"
"\n"
"* unrandart: a rarer variety of artefact that is predefined instead of randomly\n"
"  generated. Most unrandarts are identified on sight, and some come with\n"
"  special effects or unique abilities that are not available elsewhere.\n"
"\n"
"Neither of these types can be enchanted or branded, either temporarily or\n"
"permanently.\n"
msgstr ""
"答：除了地下城中随处可见的普通物品，你也可能找到神器。神器分两类：\n"
"\n"
"* randart：随机神器，通常为武器、防具或首饰，带有随机属性，例如提供抗性或能力。\n"
"\n"
"* unrandart：更稀有的固定神器，其属性预先设定，而非随机生成。大多数固定神器一见到便会鉴定，有些还带有其他地方无法获得的特殊效果或独特能力。\n"
"\n"
"这两种神器都不能附魔或添加词缀，无论临时还是永久。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:interact"
msgid "Is there a way for me to interact with other players?\n"
msgstr "能与其他玩家互动吗？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:interact"
msgid ""
"A: If you play online you can watch games in progress, other players can watch\n"
"you while you play, and you can kill other players' ghosts. You can even send\n"
"and receive messages.\n"
"\n"
"See http://crawl.develz.org/ to find an online server. The website also lists\n"
"community discussion resources for Discord, Reddit, and IRC.\n"
msgstr ""
"答：在线游玩时，你可以观看进行中的游戏，其他玩家也可以旁观你，还可以杀死其他玩家的幽灵。你们甚至可以收发消息。\n"
"\n"
"请到 http://crawl.develz.org/ 查找在线服务器。网站还列出了 Discord、Reddit 和 IRC 社区讨论渠道。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:version"
msgid "When will development reach the \"stable\" version 1.0?\n"
msgstr "什么时候会开发到“稳定”的 1.0 版？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:version"
msgid ""
"A: Actually, by now we consider Stone Soup to be reasonably stable for a game\n"
"of such active development, so please don't get hung up about the 0.X\n"
"versioning and give it a try.\n"
"\n"
"We've mostly kept the versioning for historic reasons and because it might\n"
"cause undue confusion. We might decide to change that at some point, but maybe\n"
"we won't.\n"
msgstr ""
"答：实际上，对于一款开发如此活跃的游戏，我们已经认为 Stone Soup 相当稳定。所以不必纠结于 0.X 的版本号，来试试吧。\n"
"\n"
"沿用这种版本号主要是出于历史原因，也因为改动可能造成不必要的困惑。将来我们也许会改，也许不会。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:beta"
msgid "Is there a way for me to play the new version before it is released?\n"
msgstr "能在新版正式发布前抢先玩吗？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:beta"
msgid ""
"A: There certainly is! You can play \"trunk\" (what will eventually become the\n"
"next version) online on any of the online servers; https://crawl.develz.org\n"
"also hosts Windows and Mac binaries you can download. Note that trunk may be\n"
"buggy, and that very rarely a bug may invalidate your saved games. If that\n"
"doesn't bother you, go ahead and play!\n"
"\n"
"Please report bugs on github (https://github.com/crawl/crawl/issues).\n"
"\n"
"When doing so, please mention the version (see '?v') you're currently playing,\n"
"in case the bug's already been fixed or the feature already implemented.\n"
msgstr ""
"答：当然可以！各在线服务器都可游玩“trunk”（最终将成为下一版本的开发版）；https://crawl.develz.org 也提供 Windows 和 Mac 的可执行文件下载。请注意，trunk 可能有缺陷，极少数情况下还会导致旧存档失效。如果你不介意，就来玩吧！\n"
"\n"
"请在 GitHub 报告缺陷：https://github.com/crawl/crawl/issues\n"
"\n"
"报告时请注明当前游戏版本（可按 '?v' 查看），以便确认相关缺陷是否已经修复，或功能是否已经实现。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:bug"
msgid "The game keeps crashing. / I think I found a bug. What do I do?\n"
msgstr "游戏总是崩溃／我好像发现了缺陷，怎么办？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:bug"
msgid ""
"A: Please submit a bug report on github (https://github.com/crawl/crawl/issues),\n"
"and give as much information as you can:\n"
"\n"
"* What were you doing at the time?\n"
"\n"
"* What did you expect to happen, what happened instead, etc.\n"
"\n"
"* Most importantly, what version are you playing?\n"
"  (If you're not sure, you can check in-game with '?v'.)\n"
"\n"
"* Console or tiles?\n"
"\n"
"For crashes or monsters/items/levels behaving oddly, we probably need a save\n"
"file. If you're playing online console, you can create a copy of your save file\n"
"for the developers to access by selecting the version you are playing and then\n"
"pressing 'A' for Advanced options. Don't forget to include the server and your\n"
"username in your bug report!\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes a screenshot can be helpful. If there are error messages, please\n"
"write them down. Short of a save file, a guide on how to reproduce the crash\n"
"(or bug) can be useful; you can use wizard mode for this.\n"
"\n"
"Thanks in advance!\n"
msgstr ""
"答：请在 GitHub 提交缺陷报告（https://github.com/crawl/crawl/issues），尽量提供完整信息：\n"
"\n"
"* 当时你在做什么？\n"
"\n"
"* 你预期会发生什么，实际发生了什么？\n"
"\n"
"* 最重要的是，你玩的是哪个版本？（不确定时可在游戏中按 '?v' 查看。）\n"
"\n"
"* 字符版还是图形版？\n"
"\n"
"对于崩溃，或怪物、物品、楼层的异常行为，我们可能需要存档。如果你在在线字符版游玩，可以先选择正在玩的版本，再按 'A' 进入高级选项，创建一份开发者能够访问的存档副本。别忘了在报告中写明服务器和用户名！\n"
"\n"
"截图有时也很有用。若出现错误消息，请记录下来。没有存档时，说明如何重现崩溃或缺陷也很有帮助；可以使用巫师模式来重现。\n"
"\n"
"提前感谢你的帮助！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:idea"
msgid "I've got a cool idea! What can I do with it?\n"
msgstr "我有个好主意！该怎么提出？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:idea"
msgid ""
"A: If you'd like your idea to get in, your surest bet is to put it in a place\n"
"where a developer can see it. One good place is the official forum, at\n"
"https://tavern.dcss.io/. If it catches the interest of at least one coder,\n"
"chances are it'll make it into the game.\n"
"\n"
"Note that your idea has a better chance of being accepted if you present the\n"
"ramifications on gameplay. (\"How does [adding/removing X] make the game\n"
"better?\") A suggestion for how to improve the interface may go in without much\n"
"ado, but other suggestions will probably require to defend & justify them.\n"
msgstr ""
"答：如果希望主意被采纳，最可靠的办法就是把它放到开发者看得到的地方。官方论坛 https://tavern.dcss.io/ 就很合适。只要至少一位程序员感兴趣，它就有机会进入游戏。\n"
"\n"
"说明这个主意会如何影响玩法，能提高获采纳的机会。（“增加或删除 X 怎样让游戏变得更好？”）改善界面的建议可能很快就能通过；其他建议通常需要你解释并论证。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:help"
msgid "I'd like to help improve the game. What can I do?\n"
msgstr "我想帮助改进游戏，能做些什么？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:help"
msgid ""
"A: There are several areas where you can get creative and outside help is much\n"
"appreciated. These are:\n"
"\n"
"* maps/vaults (see dat/ directory, docs/develop/levels/introduction.txt)\n"
"\n"
"* monster speech (see dat/database/, docs/develop/monster_speech.txt)\n"
"\n"
"* monster/item/spell descriptions (see dat/descript/)\n"
"\n"
"* tiles (see source/rltiles/, docs/develop/tiles_creation.txt)\n"
"\n"
"Also, if you'd like to write a patch but don't know how to go about it, read\n"
"patch_guide.txt in the docs/develop/ directory. Submit it and other new things\n"
"at our github repository: https://github.com/crawl/crawl/issues\n"
"\n"
"Keep in mind that without previous discussions, we may not be able to use the\n"
"patch, or it might need heavy modification. It's possible that it won't be\n"
"accepted, usually for one of three reasons:\n"
"\n"
"* It doesn't fit into the Crawl world as we see it.\n"
"\n"
"* It violates Crawl's philosophy to avoid grinding and spoiler-heavy stuff.\n"
"\n"
"* We just don't think it's interesting enough to ever be implemented.\n"
"\n"
"Thanks a lot for your support!\n"
msgstr ""
"答：有几个领域很适合发挥创意，我们非常欢迎外界帮助：\n"
"\n"
"* 地图／密室（参见 dat/ 目录及 docs/develop/levels/introduction.txt）\n"
"\n"
"* 怪物台词（参见 dat/database/ 及 docs/develop/monster_speech.txt）\n"
"\n"
"* 怪物／物品／法术描述（参见 dat/descript/）\n"
"\n"
"* 图块（参见 source/rltiles/ 及 docs/develop/tiles_creation.txt）\n"
"\n"
"如果你想编写补丁，却不知如何开始，请阅读 docs/develop/ 目录的 patch_guide.txt。补丁及其他新内容可提交至 GitHub 仓库：https://github.com/crawl/crawl/issues\n"
"\n"
"请注意，未经事先讨论的补丁可能无法采用，或需要大幅修改。补丁也可能被拒绝，常见原因有三种：\n"
"\n"
"* 它不符合我们心目中的 Crawl 世界。\n"
"\n"
"* 它违背了 Crawl 避免反复刷取及过分依赖剧透内容的设计理念。\n"
"\n"
"* 我们认为它不够有趣，不值得实现。\n"
"\n"
"非常感谢你的支持！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:changes"
msgid "What did you change in the most recent version?\n"
msgstr "最新版本改了什么？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:changes"
msgid ""
"A: The admittedly highly subjective highlights of the most recent major release\n"
"are listed along with the version information under '?v'. For older releases'\n"
"changes, check out changelog.txt in the docs/ directory.\n"
msgstr "答：最新主要版本的亮点会与版本信息一起显示在 '?v' 中，不过这份选择确实非常主观。旧版本的改动请查阅 docs/ 目录中的 changelog.txt。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:q:tiles lag"
msgid "The Tiles version is awfully slow! How can I improve that?\n"
msgstr "图形版特别慢！怎样改善？\n"

msgctxt "textdb:database/FAQ.txt:a:tiles lag"
msgid ""
"A: Crawl renders its graphics using OpenGL and SDL. Because it uses OpenGL, it\n"
"depends on a little bit of hardware acceleration to not run slowly. If your\n"
"system is not set up to enable this, then Crawl will run quite poorly.\n"
"\n"
"On Windows, the default driver that ships with Windows is extremely slow. Make\n"
"sure to update your graphics card driver to the latest one available. On Linux,\n"
"you should be sure to enable DRI.\n"
"\n"
"In addition to these suggestions, you can also try to see whether tweaking some\n"
"options will improve performance. See docs/tiles_help.txt for details. If\n"
"things are still too laggy after all of that, you could try the non-graphical\n"
"console version, or wait for a future version that does not depend on OpenGL.\n"
msgstr ""
"答：Crawl 使用 OpenGL 和 SDL 绘图。由于采用 OpenGL，需要一定的硬件加速才能流畅运行。如果系统没有启用相应支持，游戏就会很慢。\n"
"\n"
"Windows 自带的默认显卡驱动非常慢，请把显卡驱动更新至最新可用版本。Linux 下应确保启用 DRI。\n"
"\n"
"除上述建议外，还可以尝试调整选项，看能否改善性能，详情见 docs/tiles_help.txt。如果这样仍然很卡，可以尝试没有图形的字符版，或等待将来不依赖 OpenGL 的版本。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial intro"
msgid ""
"You can reread all messages at any time with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_REPLAY_MESSAGES]</input>. Also, press <input>Space</input>\n"
"<localtiles> or <input>left click</input> with mouse</localtiles> to clear the\n"
"<cyan>--more--</cyan> prompts.\n"
msgstr "随时可按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REPLAY_MESSAGES]</input> 重读全部消息。按 <input>Space</input><localtiles>，或用鼠标<input>左键单击</input></localtiles>，可关闭 <cyan>--more--</cyan> 提示。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial death"
msgid ""
"You die...\n"
"\n"
"In Crawl, death is a sad but common occurrence. Note that there's usually\n"
"something you could have done to survive, for example by using some kind of\n"
"item, running away, resting between fights, or by avoiding combat entirely.\n"
"Keep trying, eventually you'll prevail!\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"你死了……\n"
"\n"
"在 Crawl 中，死亡令人难过，却也很常见。通常你本来还有活下来的办法，例如使用某件物品、逃跑、在战斗之间休息，或干脆避免交战。继续尝试，你终会成功！\n"
"\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 start"
msgid ""
"In this lesson you're going to learn how to move around and explore a level.\n"
"You can move <localtiles>by clicking somewhere with your <input>Mouse</input>,\n"
"or </localtiles>with the <input>arrow keys</input>.\n"
msgstr "本课介绍如何移动和探索楼层。你可以<localtiles>用<input>鼠标</input>点击目标位置，或</localtiles>使用<input>方向键</input>移动。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 go_on"
msgid "You're doing great! Now, explore a bit until you reach the next blue square.\n"
msgstr "做得很好！继续探索，直到抵达下一个蓝色方格。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 diagonal"
msgid ""
":nowrap\n"
"Move diagonally with the <input>number pad</input> (try Numlock on/off)<localtiles>,</localtiles> <console>or the </console><input>vi keys</input><console>.</console><localtiles>, or <input>mouse</input>.</localtiles>\n"
"\n"
"  Numpad:     <w>7 8 9</w>       vi-keys: <w>   $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP_LEFT] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP_RIGHT]</w><localtiles>    Mouse:     <w>click</w> on the floor</localtiles>\n"
"               \\|/                     \\|/\n"
"              <w>4</w>-<w>.</w>-<w>6</w> <w>                  $cmd[CMD_MOVE_LEFT]</w>-<w>.</w>-<w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_RIGHT]</w>\n"
"               /|\\                     /|\\\n"
"              <w>1 2 3</w> <w>                  $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN_LEFT] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN_RIGHT]</w>\n"
msgstr ""
":nowrap\n"
"用<input>数字键盘</input>（试试开关 Numlock）<localtiles>、</localtiles><console>或</console><input>vi 键</input><console>斜向移动。</console><localtiles>，或用<input>鼠标</input>斜向移动。</localtiles>\n"
"\n"
"  数字键盘： <w>7 8 9</w>       vi-keys: <w>   $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP_LEFT] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP_RIGHT]</w><localtiles>    鼠标：<w>点击</w>地面</localtiles>\n"
"               \\|/                     \\|/\n"
"              <w>4</w>-<w>.</w>-<w>6</w> <w>                  $cmd[CMD_MOVE_LEFT]</w>-<w>.</w>-<w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_RIGHT]</w>\n"
"               /|\\                     /|\\\n"
"              <w>1 2 3</w> <w>                  $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN_LEFT] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN_RIGHT]</w>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 shiftmove"
msgid ""
"A quicker way to “run” through a corridor is to press <input>Shift</input>\n"
"along with the <input>number pad</input> (try Numlock on/off) or <input>vi\n"
"keys</input>.\n"
msgstr "同时按住 <input>Shift</input> 和<input>数字键盘</input>（试试开关 Numlock）或 <input>vi 键</input>，可以沿走廊快速“奔跑”。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 downstairs"
msgid ""
"When standing on a staircase leading downwards, you can enter the next level\n"
"with <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input><localtiles> or with\n"
"a <input>left click</input> on your character</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "站在下楼梯上时，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input><localtiles>，或在角色身上<input>左键单击</input></localtiles>，即可进入下一层。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 levelmap"
msgid ""
"What's this? To find out where you are, <tiles>have a look at the\n"
"<w>minimap</w> to the right of the screen.</tiles><localtiles> You can have a\n"
"closer look at a part of the map with a <input>right mouse click</input> and\n"
"also can travel there with a <input>left click</input>.</localtiles><webtiles>\n"
"You can </webtiles><nomouse>enter the overmap view with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]</input> and then move the cursor around to look\n"
"around the level. You also can travel wherever your cursor is pointing by\n"
"pressing <input>.</input> or <input>Enter</input>. Press <input>Escape</input>\n"
"to return to the normal game mode.</nomouse>\n"
msgstr "这是哪里？<tiles>查看屏幕右侧的<w>小地图</w>，就能知道自己的位置。</tiles><localtiles>用<input>鼠标右键</input>点击地图某处，可以仔细查看；用<input>左键单击</input>则能前往那里。</localtiles><webtiles>你也可以</webtiles><nomouse>按 <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]</input> 进入楼层地图，然后移动光标查看各处。按 <input>.</input> 或 <input>Enter</input>，即可前往光标位置。按 <input>Escape</input> 返回正常游戏。</nomouse>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 autoexplore"
msgid ""
"Exploring manually can get tedious after a while, so you might want to let that\n"
"happen automatically. Try it by pressing <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input>\n"
"<localtiles>, or by clicking on 'autoexplore', the first button in the command\n"
"bar below the minimap.</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "手动探索久了可能有些乏味，可以试试自动探索。按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input><localtiles>，或点击小地图下方命令栏的第一个按钮“自动探索”</localtiles>。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 exclusion"
msgid ""
"Some dangerous ground is marked with <w>exclusions</w>. Autotravel\n"
"<localtiles>(including <input>mouseclick</input>!) </localtiles>will not lead\n"
"you into exclusions. Instead you will automatically stop.\n"
"\n"
"However, autoexplore will move you safely around exclusions: so, you can safely\n"
"continue by pressing <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input>.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些危险区域设有<w>禁行区</w>标记。自动旅行<localtiles>（包括<input>鼠标点击</input>移动！）</localtiles>不会把你带进禁行区，而会自动停下。\n"
"\n"
"不过，自动探索会安全地绕过禁行区，所以你可以放心按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input> 继续。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 autoexplore_announce"
msgid ""
"Autoexplore will stop when you first see items or dungeon features, like these\n"
"stairs. To travel directly to the stairs, you can\n"
"<localtiles><input>click</input> on them; or you can </localtiles>press\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]</input> to enter the map overview, then\n"
"<input><<</input> to move the cursor to the nearest up-stairs, and\n"
"<input>Enter</input> to go there.\n"
msgstr "首次发现物品或楼梯等地下城设施时，自动探索会停下。要直接前往楼梯，可以<localtiles><input>点击</input>它；也可以</localtiles>按 <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]</input> 打开楼层地图，再按 <input><<</input> 把光标移到最近的上楼梯，最后按 <input>Enter</input> 前往。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 tutorial_end"
msgid ""
"Congratulations! You've completed the first lesson!\n"
"\n"
"To exit the tutorial, simply go up these stairs with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_GO_UPSTAIRS]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>left clicking</input> on your character</localtiles>. Confirm the\n"
"resulting prompt with an uppercase <input>Y</input>.\n"
msgstr ""
"恭喜！你完成了第一课！\n"
"\n"
"按 <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_UPSTAIRS]</input><localtiles>，或在角色身上<input>左键单击</input></localtiles>，沿这处楼梯向上即可退出教程。出现提示时，用大写 <input>Y</input> 确认。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 newlevel"
msgid ""
"A new level! To begin with, head over to that door to the right.\n"
"\n"
"Also, remember: You can reread old messages with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_REPLAY_MESSAGES]</input>.\n"
msgstr ""
"新的一层！先去右边那扇门吧。\n"
"\n"
"别忘了：按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REPLAY_MESSAGES]</input> 可以重读旧消息。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 door"
msgid "You can open a closed door by walking into it.\n"
msgstr "朝关闭的门走去，就能把它打开。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 close_door"
msgid "To close an open door, press <input>$cmd[CMD_CLOSE_DOOR]</input>.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_CLOSE_DOOR]</input> 可以关上打开的门。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 water"
msgid "Note how you can move through shallow but not through deep water.\n"
msgstr "注意，你可以穿过浅水，却不能穿过深水。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 upstairs"
msgid ""
"When standing on a staircase leading upwards, you can enter the previous level\n"
"with <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_UPSTAIRS]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>left clicking</input> on your character</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "站在上楼梯上时，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_UPSTAIRS]</input><localtiles>，或在角色身上<input>左键单击</input></localtiles>，即可返回上一层。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial1 exit"
msgid ""
":nowrap\n"
"<white>Tutorial 1 summary: Movement</white>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Movement commands</yellow>\n"
"   Numpad:       <w>7 8 9</w>           vi-keys:    <w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP_LEFT] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP_RIGHT]</w>\n"
"                  \\|/                         \\|/\n"
"                 <w>4</w>-<w>.</w>-<w>6</w>                       <w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_LEFT]</w>-<w>.</w>-<w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_RIGHT]</w>\n"
"                  /|\\                         /|\\\n"
"                 <w>1 2 3</w>                       <w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN_LEFT] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN_RIGHT]</w>\n"
"\n"
"  <input>Shift + direction</input> moves you several squares in this direction.<localtiles>\n"
"  You also can move by <input>clicking</input> somewhere in sight or on the <w>minimap</w>.</localtiles>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Staircases</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_UPSTAIRS]</input>  go back to the previous level\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input>  enter the next level\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]></input>/<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]<<</input> travel to the nearest up/downstairs\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Doors</yellow> can be opened by walking into them\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_CLOSE_DOOR]</input>  close an open door\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Travel</yellow><localtiles>\n"
"  mouseclick on the <w>minimap</w></localtiles><nomouse>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]</input>  enter the level map, travel with <input>Enter</input></nomouse>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input>  autoexplore\n"
msgstr ""
":nowrap\n"
"<white>教程 1 小结：移动</white>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>移动命令</yellow>\n"
"   数字键盘：   <w>7 8 9</w>           vi-keys:    <w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP_LEFT] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_UP_RIGHT]</w>\n"
"                  \\|/                         \\|/\n"
"                 <w>4</w>-<w>.</w>-<w>6</w>                       <w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_LEFT]</w>-<w>.</w>-<w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_RIGHT]</w>\n"
"                  /|\\                         /|\\\n"
"                 <w>1 2 3</w>                       <w>$cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN_LEFT] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN] $cmd[CMD_MOVE_DOWN_RIGHT]</w>\n"
"\n"
"  <input>Shift + 方向键</input>  向该方向移动数格。<localtiles>\n"
"  也可以<input>点击</input>视野中的位置或<w>小地图</w>来移动。</localtiles>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>楼梯</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_UPSTAIRS]</input>  返回上一层\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input>  进入下一层\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]></input>/<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]<<</input>  前往最近的下／上楼梯\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>门</yellow>  朝门走去即可开门\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_CLOSE_DOOR]</input>  关门\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>旅行</yellow><localtiles>\n"
"  鼠标点击<w>小地图</w></localtiles><nomouse>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_MAP]</input>  打开楼层地图，按 <input>Enter</input> 前往</nomouse>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input>  自动探索\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 start"
msgid ""
"This lesson will teach you about monsters and fighting. First, we need a\n"
"weapon! Go and grab the one lying over there.\n"
msgstr "本课介绍怪物与战斗。首先，我们需要一把武器！去拿起那边地上的武器吧。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 pickup_weapon"
msgid ""
"Pick up this weapon<localtiles> by clicking on it in the inventory panel, and\n"
"then wield it by clicking on it again. Alternatively, pick it up</localtiles>\n"
"with <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input> or <input>g</input> and then wield it with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input>.\n"
msgstr "拾取这把武器<localtiles>时，可以在物品面板点击它，再点一次便能装备。也可以</localtiles>按 <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input> 或 <input>g</input> 拾取，再按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input> 装备。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 melee"
msgid ""
"To attack a monster with your bare hands or wielded weapon, simply walk into\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr "朝怪物走去，就能用徒手或手持武器攻击它。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 resting"
msgid ""
"Very good! You can heal by resting with <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>\n"
"<localtiles>, or by clicking the 'rest' button in the command bar below the\n"
"minimap</localtiles>. This will make you rest until your health is full, but\n"
"will be interrupted by important events.\n"
msgstr "很好！按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input><localtiles>，或点击小地图下方命令栏的“休息”按钮</localtiles>，可以休息恢复生命。你会一直休息到生命全满，但重要事件会打断休息。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 wait"
msgid ""
"Rather than storm the room and get swarmed by monsters, you can also step back\n"
"and wait (with <input>$cmd[CMD_WAIT]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>clicking</input> on your character</localtiles>) for them to come to you.\n"
msgstr "与其冲进房间被怪物围住，你也可以后退，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_WAIT]</input><localtiles>，或在角色身上<input>点击</input></localtiles>，等待它们走来。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 resting_reminder"
msgid "Remember, you can rest up with <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>.\n"
msgstr "记住，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input> 可以休息恢复。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 compare_monster_desc"
msgid ""
"Examine these monsters (<localtiles>via <input>mouseover</input></localtiles>\n"
"<nomouse>by pressing <input>$cmd[CMD_LOOK_AROUND]</input> to enter examine mode,\n"
"and then <input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_CYCLE_FORWARD]</input> to cycle through nearby\n"
"monsters</nomouse>)\n"
"and compare their descriptions (<localtiles>with <input>rightmouseclick</input></localtiles>\n"
"<nomouse>by pressing <input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_DESCRIBE]</input> while selecting\n"
"them in examine mode</nomouse>)\n"
"to find out which of these cages is safer to fight through.\n"
msgstr "查看这些怪物（<localtiles>将<input>鼠标悬停</input>其上</localtiles><nomouse>按 <input>$cmd[CMD_LOOK_AROUND]</input> 进入查看模式，再按 <input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_CYCLE_FORWARD]</input> 循环选择附近怪物</nomouse>），并比较它们的描述（<localtiles>用<input>鼠标右键单击</input></localtiles><nomouse>在查看模式中选中怪物后，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_DESCRIBE]</input></nomouse>），判断从哪间牢笼杀过去更安全。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 downstairs"
msgid ""
"Well done! After resting to full health continue to the next level with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input><localtiles> or by <input>clicking</input>\n"
"on your character</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "干得好！休息至生命全满后，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input><localtiles>，或在角色身上<input>点击</input></localtiles>，前往下一层。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 newlevel"
msgid ""
"Remember: You can reread old messages with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_REPLAY_MESSAGES]</input>.\n"
msgstr "记住：按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REPLAY_MESSAGES]</input> 可以重读旧消息。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 boomerangs"
msgid ""
"Now, for ranged combat! Pick up these boomerangs with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input> or <input>g</input><localtiles>, or by\n"
"<input>mouseclick</input>,</localtiles> and continue.\n"
msgstr "接下来学习远程战斗！按 <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input> 或 <input>g</input><localtiles>，或用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>拾取这些回旋镖，再继续前进。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 throwing"
msgid ""
"You can fire your boomerangs at a monster with <input>$cmd[CMD_FIRE]</input>\n"
"<localtiles> or by <input>clicking</input> on them in the inventory\n"
"panel</localtiles>. To confirm the auto-targeted monster, press\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_SELECT]</input> or <input>Enter</input>. You can skip\n"
"this and fire at the closest monster with <input>shift-tab</input> or <input>p</input>.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_FIRE]</input><localtiles>，或在物品面板<input>点击</input>回旋镖</localtiles>，可以向怪物投掷。按 <input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_SELECT]</input> 或 <input>Enter</input> 确认自动选中的目标。也可以跳过选目标这一步，按 <input>shift-tab</input> 或 <input>p</input> 直接攻击最近的怪物。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 wield_bow"
msgid ""
"Pick up this shortbow and wield it with <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input>\n"
"<localtiles> or by <input>mouseclick</input></localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "拾取这把短弓，然后按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles>，或用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>装备。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 firing"
msgid ""
"Firing arrows from your wielded shortbow works a bit differently from throwing boomerangs.\n"
"Use <input>$cmd[CMD_PRIMARY_ATTACK]</input><localtiles> or <input>mouseclick</input>\n"
"</localtiles>. You can change the targeted monster by pressing\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_CYCLE_FORWARD]</input> while in target mode. The worm is\n"
"harmless behind the lava, so concentrate on the dummy which can fire at you.\n"
"Again, confirm your choice with <input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_SELECT]</input> or\n"
"<input>Enter</input>.\n"
msgstr "用手中的短弓射箭，与投掷回旋镖略有不同。按 <input>$cmd[CMD_PRIMARY_ATTACK]</input><localtiles>，或用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>射击。在选目标模式中，可以按 <input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_CYCLE_FORWARD]</input> 切换目标。熔岩后的蠕虫伤不到你，所以先对付会向你射击的假人。仍用 <input>$cmd[CMD_TARGET_SELECT]</input> 或 <input>Enter</input> 确认目标。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 travel_reminder"
msgid "Remember that you can autoexplore using <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input>.\n"
msgstr "记住，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input> 可以自动探索。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 explore"
msgid ""
"Find the exit! Remember that you can autoexplore using\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input>.\n"
msgstr "找到出口！别忘了按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input> 可以自动探索。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 tutorial_end"
msgid ""
"Congratulations! You've survived your first batch of monsters! To exit the\n"
"tutorial, simply go down these stairs.\n"
msgstr "恭喜！你击败了第一批怪物，活了下来！沿这处楼梯向下，即可退出教程。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial2 exit"
msgid ""
":nowrap\n"
"<white>Tutorial 2 summary: Combat</white>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Weapons<console> <cyan>)</cyan></console></yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input>  pick up an item\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input>  equip an item<localtiles>\n"
"  You can also do this by <input>clicking</input> on the weapon in your inventory.</localtiles>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_QUIVER_ITEM]</input>  adjust your quiver\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Monsters</yellow><localtiles>\n"
"  <input>mouseover</input>  examine a monster\n"
"  <input>rightclick</input> read a more detailed description</localtiles><nomouse>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_LOOK_AROUND]</input>  examine a monster\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_LOOK_AROUND]$cmd[CMD_TARGET_DESCRIBE]</input> read a more detailed description</nomouse>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_PRIMARY_ATTACK]</input> fire held weapon\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_FIRE]$cmd[CMD_TARGET_SELECT]</input> fire quiver at pre-targeted monster\n"
"  <input>shift-tab</input>, <input>p</input> fire quiver at closest monster\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_FIRE]$cmd[CMD_TARGET_CYCLE_FORWARD]</input> target another monster<localtiles>\n"
"  You can also fire a missile by <input>clicking</input> on it, then confirming the target with <input>Enter</input>.</localtiles>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Resting</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_WAIT]</input>  wait and rest a single turn\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>  wait and rest up to 100 turns\n"
msgstr ":nowrap\n<white>教程 2 小结：战斗</white>\n\n<yellow>武器<console> <cyan>)</cyan></console></yellow>\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input>  拾取物品\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input>  装备物品<localtiles>\n  也可以在物品栏中<input>点击</input>武器来操作。</localtiles>\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_QUIVER_ITEM]</input>  调整备投物\n\n<yellow>怪物</yellow><localtiles>\n  <input>鼠标悬停</input>  查看怪物\n  <input>右键单击</input>  阅读详细描述</localtiles><nomouse>\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_LOOK_AROUND]</input>  查看怪物\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_LOOK_AROUND]$cmd[CMD_TARGET_DESCRIBE]</input>  阅读详细描述</nomouse>\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_PRIMARY_ATTACK]</input>  使用手持武器射击\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_FIRE]$cmd[CMD_TARGET_SELECT]</input>  向预选目标发射备投物\n  <input>shift-tab</input>、<input>p</input>  向最近怪物发射备投物\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_FIRE]$cmd[CMD_TARGET_CYCLE_FORWARD]</input>  选择另一目标<localtiles>\n  也可以<input>点击</input>投射物，再按 <input>Enter</input> 确认目标。</localtiles>\n\n<yellow>休息</yellow>\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_WAIT]</input>  等待并休息一回合\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>  等待并休息最多 100 回合\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 start"
msgid "In this lesson you're going to learn about items and how to use them.\n"
msgstr "本课介绍物品及其使用方法。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 armour"
msgid ""
"Pick up these boots with <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input> and wear them with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input>.<localtiles> Or simply <input>mouseclick</input>\n"
"on them in the inventory panel.</localtiles>\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input> 拾取这双靴子，再按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input> 穿上。<localtiles>也可以直接在物品面板用<input>鼠标点击</input>它们。</localtiles>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 autopickup"
msgid ""
"Some types of items<tiles>, marked with a green frame,</tiles> are picked up\n"
"automatically as you step on them.\n"
msgstr "有些类型的物品<tiles>带有绿色边框，</tiles>走到上面就会自动拾取。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 scroll"
msgid ""
"Many items are unidentified when you find them. One way to find out what they\n"
"do is to use them. Try reading this scroll with <input>$cmd[CMD_READ]</input>\n"
"<localtiles> or with <input>mouseclick</input> in the inventory\n"
"panel</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "许多物品刚发现时尚未鉴定。使用它们，是了解其效果的一种办法。试试按 <input>$cmd[CMD_READ]</input><localtiles>，或在物品面板用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>阅读这张卷轴。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 scroll_noautopickup"
msgid ""
"Autopickup does not work if there's a monster around. You can either pick up\n"
"this scroll now with <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input><localtiles> or\n"
"<input>clicking</input> on your character,</localtiles> or you can fight the\n"
"nearby enemy and pick it up afterwards.\n"
msgstr "附近有怪物时，不会自动拾取物品。你可以现在就按 <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input><localtiles>，或在角色身上<input>点击</input></localtiles>拾取卷轴；也可以先击败附近的敌人，再回来拿。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 ego_weapon"
msgid ""
"An item described as <lightblue>runed</lightblue> or\n"
"<lightblue>glowing</lightblue> will always be enchanted, or have special\n"
"properties, or both. Once you step on top of such an item, its properties will\n"
"be revealed to you.\n"
msgstr "描述为<lightblue>刻有符文</lightblue>或<lightblue>发光</lightblue>的物品，一定带有附魔、特殊属性，或两者兼有。走到这种物品上面，就会揭示其属性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 inventory"
msgid ""
"To view the description of your new weapon, find and select it in your\n"
"inventory (<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_INVENTORY]</input>). <localtiles>You can\n"
"also <input>mouseover</input> or <input>right click</input> it in the inventory\n"
"panel. </localtiles>Notice that all the item commands also work from the item\n"
"description screens.\n"
msgstr "要查看新武器的描述，请在物品栏（<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_INVENTORY]</input>）中找到并选中它。<localtiles>也可以在物品面板将<input>鼠标悬停</input>其上，或用<input>右键单击</input>。</localtiles>注意，物品描述界面也能执行所有物品操作命令。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 battle"
msgid ""
"Once you've successfully managed to poison a monster, it is sometimes best to\n"
"retreat and let the poison do the work. Don't forget to retreat to heal too, if\n"
"necessary.\n"
msgstr "成功让怪物中毒后，有时最好先后退，让毒素发挥作用。必要时也别忘了撤退恢复生命。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 downstairs"
msgid ""
"Well fought! If necessary, rest up with <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>, then\n"
"continue downwards with <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input><localtiles> or\n"
"with a <input>click</input> on your character</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "打得好！如有需要，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input> 休息恢复，再按 <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input><localtiles>，或在角色身上<input>点击</input></localtiles>继续下楼。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 command_help"
msgid ""
"If the many commands are too confusing, you can also look them up in the\n"
"command help <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_COMMANDS]</input>. <localtiles>A number of\n"
"commands are also available in the clickable <w>command panel</w> to the right\n"
"of the screen. </localtiles>Rereading old messages with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_REPLAY_MESSAGES]</input> is available as usual.\n"
msgstr "命令太多记不住时，可以按 <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_COMMANDS]</input> 查阅命令帮助。<localtiles>屏幕右侧可点击的<w>命令面板</w>也提供了许多命令。</localtiles>仍可随时按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REPLAY_MESSAGES]</input> 重读旧消息。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 trap"
msgid ""
"Traps can have a variety of unpleasant effects, such as alerting monsters or\n"
"teleporting you into danger. Some traps are permanent and will always be\n"
"revealed as part of the map, but other traps can be triggered by exploring new\n"
"tiles, and won't exist after being triggered. If there's no way around, you'll\n"
"have to trigger the trap and deal with the consequences.\n"
msgstr "陷阱会造成各种不利影响，例如惊动怪物，或将你传送进险境。有些陷阱永久存在，始终会作为地图的一部分显示；另一些可能在探索新方格时触发，触发后便不再存在。如果无路可绕，你就得触发陷阱并应对后果。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 potion"
msgid ""
"Potions may provide vital healing or useful enchantments, but some have less\n"
"desirable effects. You can quaff this potion with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_QUAFF]</input><localtiles> or with\n"
"<input>mouseclick</input></localtiles> to discover what it does.\n"
msgstr "药水可能提供救命的治疗或有益的魔法效果，但有些效果不那么令人满意。按 <input>$cmd[CMD_QUAFF]</input><localtiles>，或用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>喝下这瓶药水，看看它有什么作用。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 artefact_armour"
msgid ""
"Items with <w>unusual names</w> are artefacts. Artefacts can have a number of\n"
"special properties. Some unique artefacts (such as this cloak) are always\n"
"identified and may have special properties that cannot be found anywhere else!\n"
"Others are generated with a random selection of properties, and are\n"
"unidentified until you step on top of them. Try equipping this cloak with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles> or <input>mouseclick</input>\n"
"in the inventory panel</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "带有<w>特殊名称</w>的物品是神器，可能具有多种特殊属性。有些独特神器（例如这件斗篷）始终处于已鉴定状态，还可能拥有其他物品没有的特殊属性！另一些则随机生成属性，要走到上面才会鉴定。试着按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles>，或在物品面板用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>装备这件斗篷。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 wand_fire"
msgid ""
"You can evoke a wand with <input>$cmd[CMD_EVOKE]</input><localtiles> or with\n"
"<input>mouseclick</input> in the inventory panel</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EVOKE]</input><localtiles>，或在物品面板用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>，可以唤发魔杖。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 wand_digging"
msgid ""
"A wand of digging can destroy rock walls. Use\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_LOOK_AROUND]][$cmd[CMD_TARGET_DESCRIBE]</input> <localtiles>or\n"
"<input>mouseover</input>/<input>right click</input> </localtiles>to check wall\n"
"types.\n"
msgstr "挖掘魔杖能够摧毁岩壁。用 <input>$cmd[CMD_LOOK_AROUND]][$cmd[CMD_TARGET_DESCRIBE]</input><localtiles>，或<input>鼠标悬停</input>／<input>右键单击</input></localtiles>，可以查看墙壁类型。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 amulet"
msgid ""
"Jewellery is put on with <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles>\n"
"or with <input>mouseclick</input> in the inventory panel</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles>，或在物品面板用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>，可以戴上首饰。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 drop"
msgid ""
"This amulet would be very powerful if your character had a god to worship,\n"
"but here and now, it's useless. You may want to drop it with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_DROP]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>Shift-leftclicking</input> it in the inventory panel</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "如果角色信奉神祇，这枚护身符会非常强大；但此时此地它毫无用处。你可以按 <input>$cmd[CMD_DROP]</input><localtiles>，或在物品面板按住 <input>Shift 并左键单击</input>它</localtiles>，将它丢下。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 gold"
msgid "Gold can be spent in shops. It takes no inventory space and cannot be dropped.\n"
msgstr "金币可以在商店消费，不占物品栏空间，也不能丢弃。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 shop"
msgid "Shops offer a variety of items, but they don't buy items from anyone.\n"
msgstr "商店出售各种物品，但不会收购物品。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 enter_shop"
msgid ""
"To enter this shop, press <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_UPSTAIRS]</input><localtiles> or\n"
"<input>click</input> on your character</localtiles>. To buy items,\n"
"select them with their hotkey, hit <input>Enter</input> and confirm with\n"
"<input>y</input>es. You can switch to description mode with <input>!</input>.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_UPSTAIRS]</input><localtiles>，或在角色身上<input>点击</input></localtiles>进入商店。用物品快捷键选中想买的物品，按 <input>Enter</input>，再按 <input>y</input> 确认购买。按 <input>!</input> 可以切换到描述模式。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 autoexplore_reminder"
msgid ""
"Remember, you can explore the level automatically with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input><localtiles> or by <input>clicking</input> the\n"
"autoexplore command button in the <w>command panel</w></localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "记住，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input><localtiles>，或在<w>命令面板</w><input>点击</input>自动探索按钮</localtiles>，可以自动探索楼层。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 go_shopping"
msgid ""
"You now have enough gold to do some serious shopping! The quickest way back to\n"
"the shop is by searching for it. Type <input>$cmd[CMD_SEARCH_STASHES]</input>,\n"
"and then enter “<w>shop</w>”. Select the result to start travelling.<localtiles>\n"
"You can also <input>click</input> on the search button in the command panel, or\n"
"use the minimap to return to the shop.</localtiles>\n"
msgstr "你现在的金币足够买些好东西了！返回商店最快的办法是搜索它：按 <input>$cmd[CMD_SEARCH_STASHES]</input>，再输入“<w>shop</w>”。选择搜索结果即可开始旅行。<localtiles>也可以<input>点击</input>命令面板的搜索按钮，或利用小地图返回商店。</localtiles>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 optional_battle"
msgid ""
"Warning, this way leads to <lightred>a difficult battle</lightred>. You may\n"
"choose to use what you've learned so far in a fight, or try to reach the other\n"
"exit on the island. Either way, it may be a good idea to do some shopping, if\n"
"you haven't already.\n"
msgstr "警告，这条路通向<lightred>一场艰难的战斗</lightred>。你可以运用所学迎战，也可以尝试抵达岛上的另一个出口。无论如何，如果还没买东西，先去商店看看或许是个好主意。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 tutorial_end"
msgid "Well done! To exit the tutorial, simply go down these stairs.\n"
msgstr "做得好！沿这处楼梯向下，即可退出教程。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial3 exit"
msgid ""
":nowrap\n"
"<white>Tutorial 3 summary: Items</white>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Item commands</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input>  pick up an item\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DROP]</input>  drop an item\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input>  equip armour, weapons, and jewellery\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_UNEQUIP]</input>  unequip armour, weapons, and jewellery\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_READ]</input>  read a scroll\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_QUAFF]</input>  quaff a potion\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_EVOKE]</input>  evoke a wand\n"
"\n"
"  Use and (un)equip commands are also available from item descriptions in the inventory menu (<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_INVENTORY]</input>).<localtiles>\n"
"  And of course, <input>mouseclicks</input> also work.</localtiles>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Other</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_COMMANDS]?</input> access the command help\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input>  explore automatically\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_SEARCH_STASHES]</input> search for items/features previously seen<localtiles>\n"
"  Several of these commands can also be executed by clicking in the <w>command panel</w>.</localtiles>\n"
msgstr ":nowrap\n<white>教程 3 小结：物品</white>\n\n<yellow>物品命令</yellow>\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_PICKUP]</input>  拾取物品\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_DROP]</input>  丢弃物品\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input>  装备防具、武器和首饰\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_UNEQUIP]</input>  卸下防具、武器和首饰\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_READ]</input>  阅读卷轴\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_QUAFF]</input>  喝下药水\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_EVOKE]</input>  唤发魔杖\n\n  物品栏菜单（<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_INVENTORY]</input>）的物品描述中，也能使用物品或穿脱装备。<localtiles>\n  当然，也能用<input>鼠标点击</input>操作。</localtiles>\n\n<yellow>其他</yellow>\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_COMMANDS]?</input>  查看命令帮助\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_EXPLORE]</input>  自动探索\n  <input>$cmd[CMD_SEARCH_STASHES]</input>  搜索见过的物品或设施<localtiles>\n  其中一些命令也可以在<w>命令面板</w>点击执行。</localtiles>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 start"
msgid "In this lesson you're going to learn how to memorise and cast spells.\n"
msgstr "本课介绍如何记忆与施放法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 spellbook"
msgid ""
"You can memorise a spell from your spell library with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>clicking</input> on the memorisation tab and selecting the spell\n"
"tile</localtiles>. At experience level 1, only level 1 spells are available to\n"
"you. This will change as you gain experience. To find new spells, find and pick\n"
"up spellbooks, and the spells will be added to your library.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input><localtiles>，或<input>点击</input>记忆标签页并选择法术图标</localtiles>，可以从法术库记忆法术。经验等级为 1 时，你只能学习 1 级法术；获得更多经验后，就能学习更高级的法术。寻找并拾取法术书，其中的法术就会加入法术库。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 spellcasting"
msgid ""
"To cast a spell, first memorise it with <input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input>.\n"
"You can then cast it with <input>$cmd[CMD_CAST_SPELL]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>clicking</input> on the spell tile</localtiles>.\n"
"\n"
"Press <input>$cmd[CMD_CAST_SPELL]</input>, then press <input>?</input> to get a\n"
"list of your spells.\n"
msgstr ""
"施法前，先用 <input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input> 记忆法术。之后按 <input>$cmd[CMD_CAST_SPELL]</input><localtiles>，或<input>点击</input>法术图标</localtiles>，即可施放。\n"
"\n"
"按 <input>$cmd[CMD_CAST_SPELL]</input>，再按 <input>?</input>，可以列出你的法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 spellquivering"
msgid ""
"Spells, like ammo, are shown in the quiver slot, so you can use\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_QUIVER_ITEM]</input> to ready a spell in the quiver. Use\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_FIRE]</input> or <input>shift-tab</input> to fire the currently\n"
"quivered spell.\n"
"\n"
"Once you are out of magic points, retreat and rest to regain them with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input><localtiles> or by <input>clicking</input> the\n"
"rest icon in the command panel</localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "法术与投掷物一样，会显示在备投栏中，因此可以用 <input>$cmd[CMD_QUIVER_ITEM]</input> 将法术设为备投。按 <input>$cmd[CMD_FIRE]</input> 或 <input>shift-tab</input> 施放当前备投法术。\n\n魔力耗尽后，请撤退并按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input><localtiles>，或<input>点击</input>命令面板的休息图标</localtiles>，通过休息恢复魔力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 ring_power"
msgid ""
"Put on this ring with <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles> or\n"
"by <input>clicking</input> it in the inventory panel</localtiles>, and then\n"
"rest up to your new full potential.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles>，或在物品面板<input>点击</input></localtiles>戴上这枚戒指，然后休息，恢复到新的上限。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 undead"
msgid ""
"Unlike most monsters, zombies and skeletons do not regenerate health.\n"
"<localtiles> You can also attempt to re-cast the last spell you used by\n"
"pressing <input>Ctrl+leftclick</input> on the monster.</localtiles>\n"
msgstr "与大多数怪物不同，僵尸和骷髅不会恢复生命。<localtiles>你也可以在怪物身上按住 <input>Ctrl 并左键单击</input>，尝试再次施放上一次使用的法术。</localtiles>\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 spell_success"
msgid ""
"To check your spell proficiency, press <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_SPELLS]</input>\n"
"<localtiles> or <input>mouseover</input> over your memorised\n"
"spells</localtiles>. Compare your spell failure rates before and after wearing\n"
"this ring.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_SPELLS]</input><localtiles>，或将<input>鼠标悬停</input>在已记忆法术上</localtiles>，可以查看施法熟练程度。比较一下戴上这枚戒指前后的法术失败率。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 mephitic_cloud"
msgid ""
"Mephitic Cloud is a level 3 spell, so you can't memorise it yet. To level up\n"
"quickly, here are more training dummies — without stones to throw this time.\n"
"\n"
"At experience level 3, you'll be able to increase one of your stats — choosing\n"
"<input>I</input>ntelligence will help your spellcasting even further.\n"
msgstr ""
"臭云术是 3 级法术，所以你现在还不能记忆。这里还有一些训练假人，能让你快速升级——这回它们没有石头可扔。\n"
"\n"
"经验等级达到 3 时，你可以提高一项属性；选择智力（<input>I</input>）能进一步帮助施法。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 meph_reminder"
msgid ""
"Don't forget to memorise your newly-available spell, by pressing\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>clicking</input> on the memorisation tab and selecting the spell\n"
"tile</localtiles>!\n"
msgstr "别忘了按 <input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input><localtiles>，或<input>点击</input>记忆标签页并选择法术图标</localtiles>，记忆刚刚解锁的法术！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 aiming_clouds"
msgid ""
"Mephitic Cloud covers an area in noxious fumes when cast, and you'll be able to\n"
"see the area it affects as you target it. Try to catch multiple enemies in a\n"
"single cloud in order to be more efficient with your magic.\n"
msgstr "施放臭云术会让一片区域充满有害烟雾，选择目标时就能看到影响范围。尽量用一团云雾笼罩多个敌人，提高魔力的使用效率。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 forget_spell"
msgid ""
"Gaining experience levels and raising your Spellcasting skill gives you spell\n"
"slots to spend on spells. You can also <w>forget a memorised spell</w> to make\n"
"space for a new one by reading a scroll of amnesia. Read the scroll (with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_READ]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>clicking</input> on it</localtiles>), and then select the spell you want\n"
"to forget. You can relearn forgotten spells from your spell library later, as\n"
"long as you have spell slots available.\n"
msgstr "提高经验等级或施法技能，会获得用于记忆法术的法术栏位。你也可以阅读遗忘卷轴，<w>遗忘一个已记忆的法术</w>，为新法术腾出空间。按 <input>$cmd[CMD_READ]</input><localtiles>，或<input>点击</input>卷轴</localtiles>阅读，再选择要遗忘的法术。以后只要有空余法术栏位，仍可从法术库重新学习。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 memorise2"
msgid ""
"After forgetting one of your old spells to make space, memorise this new spell\n"
"with <input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>clicking</input> on the memorisation tab and selecting the spell\n"
"tile</localtiles>. Then try your new spell and summon some demonic allies!\n"
msgstr "遗忘一个旧法术、腾出空间后，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_MEMORISE_SPELL]</input><localtiles>，或<input>点击</input>记忆标签页并选择法术图标</localtiles>，学习这个新法术。接着试一试，召唤一些恶魔盟友！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 displace_allies"
msgid ""
"Did you notice you can swap positions with your allies by moving into them?\n"
"Among other things, displacing a friendly creature can be a good way to escape\n"
"a fight.\n"
msgstr "发现了吗？朝盟友走去，就能与其交换位置。与友方生物换位的用途很多，例如帮助你脱离战斗。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 order_allies"
msgid ""
"Try to let your allies do the killing! If necessary, you can order them about\n"
"with <input>$cmd[CMD_SHOUT]</input>. Before opening this gate, you may want to\n"
"wait with <input>$cmd[CMD_WAIT]</input> until your allies have caught\n"
"up with you. Your summons will only stick around for a short time, so don't\n"
"wait too long, or summon some new ones before starting a fight.\n"
msgstr "试着把杀敌的工作交给盟友！必要时可以按 <input>$cmd[CMD_SHOUT]</input> 下达命令。打开这扇门前，不妨按 <input>$cmd[CMD_WAIT]</input> 等待盟友跟上。召唤物只会短暂停留，所以别等太久，或者在开战前重新召唤。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 heavy_armour"
msgid ""
"Heavy armour really hampers spellcasting. Try putting on that mail and shield\n"
"(with <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>clicking</input> on them</localtiles>), and compare your spellcasting\n"
"failure rates with <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_SPELLS]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>mouseovering</input> your memorised spells</localtiles>. You can take\n"
"armour off again with <input>$cmd[CMD_UNEQUIP]</input><localtiles> or,\n"
"again, via <input>mouseclick</input></localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "重甲会严重妨碍施法。试着按 <input>$cmd[CMD_EQUIP]</input><localtiles>，或<input>点击</input></localtiles>装备这件甲与盾，再按 <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_SPELLS]</input><localtiles>，或将<input>鼠标悬停</input>在已记忆法术上</localtiles>，比较施法失败率。之后可以按 <input>$cmd[CMD_UNEQUIP]</input><localtiles>，或再次用<input>鼠标点击</input></localtiles>卸下防具。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 resting_reminder"
msgid ""
"Make sure you are at full health and magic points before entering a new area.\n"
"If necessary, rest up with <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input><localtiles> or by\n"
"<input>mouseclick</input> in the command panel</localtiles>.\n"
"\n"
"You can only summon a limited number of allies at once from any given spell,\n"
"so try to take advantage of a wide range of spells. For example, your summoned\n"
"imps are resistant to poison, so you can cast Mephitic Cloud to fight alongside\n"
"them without harming your allies.\n"
msgstr ""
"进入新区域前，请确保生命与魔力全满。必要时按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input><localtiles>，或用<input>鼠标点击</input>命令面板</localtiles>休息恢复。\n"
"\n"
"每种法术能同时召唤的盟友数量有限，因此尽量使用多种法术。例如，你召唤的小恶魔抵御毒素，所以可以施放臭云术协同作战，而不会伤害它们。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial4 tutorial_end"
msgid ""
"Congratulations, you're a real wizard now! To exit the tutorial, simply go down\n"
"these stairs.\n"
msgstr "恭喜，你现在是真正的法师了！沿这处楼梯向下，即可退出教程。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 start"
msgid "In this lesson you're going to learn about gods and how to use their powers.\n"
msgstr "本课介绍神祇，以及如何使用神赐能力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 dungeon_overview"
msgid ""
"Up ahead is an altar to Trog the Wrathful! Trog is just one of many gods. In a\n"
"real game, you can check <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_OVERMAP]</input><localtiles>\n"
"or <input>click the dungeon overmap button</input> in the command\n"
"panel</localtiles> for a list of all altars and other interesting features\n"
"found so far.\n"
msgstr "前方是愤怒之神特洛戈的祭坛！特洛戈只是众多神祇之一。正式游戏中，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_OVERMAP]</input><localtiles>，或在命令面板<input>点击地下城总览按钮</input></localtiles>，可以列出目前发现的所有祭坛和其他重要设施。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 altar"
msgid ""
"You can pray on an altar with <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input>\n"
"<localtiles> (or by <input>left clicking</input> on your character)</localtiles>\n"
"to get an idea what a god offers you, and to join the faith. If\n"
"you press <input>!</input><localtiles> or\n"
"<input>rightclick</input></localtiles> on the religion screen, you can see a\n"
"more detailed description.\n"
"\n"
"Confirm your choice with <input>J</input> or <input>Enter</input>.\n"
msgstr ""
"站在祭坛上，按 <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input><localtiles>（或在角色身上<input>左键单击</input>）</localtiles>祈祷，可以了解神祇提供的恩赐，并加入信仰。在宗教界面按 <input>!</input><localtiles>，或用<input>右键单击</input></localtiles>，可以查看更详细的描述。\n"
"\n"
"按 <input>J</input> 或 <input>Enter</input> 确认选择。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 religion"
msgid ""
"Have a look at your current religious standing with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_RELIGION]</input><localtiles> (or via the <w>religion\n"
"button</w> in the command panel, or by <input>Shift-rightclicking</input> on\n"
"the player tile)</localtiles>. Again, pressing <input>!</input><localtiles> or\n"
"<input>rightclicking</input></localtiles> will bring up a more detailed\n"
"description of your god.\n"
msgstr "按 <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_RELIGION]</input><localtiles>（或使用命令面板的<w>宗教按钮</w>，或在角色图标上按住 <input>Shift 并右键单击</input>）</localtiles>，可以查看当前信仰状况。同样，按 <input>!</input><localtiles>，或用<input>右键单击</input></localtiles>，可以显示更详细的神祇描述。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 piety_on_kill"
msgid ""
"Some gods really like it if you kill monsters in their name. Let the slaughter\n"
"begin!\n"
msgstr "有些神祇非常喜欢信徒以其名义杀死怪物。开始杀戮吧！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 berserk"
msgid ""
"Against particularly tough foes, you may want to use Trog's Berserk power with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_USE_ABILITY]</input><localtiles> or via the <w>command\n"
"panel</w></localtiles>.\n"
msgstr "面对格外强悍的敌人，可以按 <input>$cmd[CMD_USE_ABILITY]</input><localtiles>，或通过<w>命令面板</w></localtiles>使用特洛戈的狂暴能力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 exhaustion"
msgid ""
"A berserker rage is truly exhausting. After it ends, you cannot berserk again\n"
"for a short while and are slowed. It's best to rest with\n"
"<input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input><localtiles> (or via the\n"
"<w>command panel</w>)</localtiles> until you feel fit again.\n"
msgstr "狂暴非常消耗体力。结束后，你会短暂减速，并在一段时间内无法再次狂暴。最好按 <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input><localtiles>（或使用<w>命令面板</w>）</localtiles>休息，直到恢复状态。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 berserk2"
msgid ""
"Berserk is also really useful against multiple enemies — as long as you don't\n"
"run out of steam in-between.\n"
msgstr "对付多个敌人时，狂暴也很有用——只要别在战斗中途耗尽劲头。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 tutorial_end"
msgid ""
"Congratulations! You've finished the last tutorial lesson and are now ready for\n"
"the real game. Good luck!\n"
"\n"
"To exit the tutorial, just go down these stairs.\n"
msgstr ""
"恭喜！你完成了最后一课，已经可以挑战正式游戏了。祝你好运！\n"
"\n"
"沿这处楼梯向下，即可退出教程。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/tutorial.txt:tutorial5 exit"
msgid ""
":nowrap\n"
"<white>Tutorial 5 summary: Religion</white>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Religious commands</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input>  pray at an altar to join a god\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_USE_ABILITY]</input>  use a divine ability\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_RELIGION]</input>  check your religious standing<localtiles>\n"
"  A <input>rightclick</input> on the player tile will also bring up the religion screen.</localtiles>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Resting</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_WAIT]</input>  wait and rest a single turn\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>  wait and rest up to 100 turns\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>Other commands</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_OVERMAP]</input> display an overview of the dungeon\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_COMMANDS]/</input>  search the description database\n"
msgstr ""
":nowrap\n"
"<white>教程 5 小结：信仰</white>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>宗教命令</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_GO_DOWNSTAIRS]</input>  在祭坛祈祷，信奉神祇\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_USE_ABILITY]</input>  使用神赐能力\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_RELIGION]</input>  查看信仰状况<localtiles>\n"
"  在角色图标上<input>右键单击</input>也能打开宗教界面。</localtiles>\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>休息</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_WAIT]</input>  等待并休息一回合\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_REST]</input>  等待并休息最多 100 回合\n"
"\n"
"<yellow>其他命令</yellow>\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_OVERMAP]</input>  显示地下城总览\n"
"  <input>$cmd[CMD_DISPLAY_COMMANDS]/</input>  搜索描述数据库\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:velocity card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts an empty, well-worn pair of boots. Sand, ashes, and turf\n"
"coat the boots' soles.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card can grant great speed to allies or terrible slowness to foes.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上是一双空荡荡、磨损严重的靴子，鞋底沾满沙土、灰烬与草皮。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌可以让盟友大幅加速，或让敌人严重减速。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the tomb card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a royal crypt, its entrance sealed by a heavy stone slab.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card entombs its user in protective, temporary walls of solid rock.\n"
"At lower power levels or with adjacent creatures, the tomb may be imperfect.\n"
"\n"
"The tomb is sustained by the presence of its creator within it, and moving from\n"
"the centre of the tomb will cause its walls to crumble away.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上是一座皇家墓室，入口被沉重的石板封住。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会在使用者周围筑起临时的坚固岩壁，形成保护性的坟墓。威力较低或附近有生物时，坟墓可能并不完整。\n"
"\n"
"坟墓依赖创造者留在其中才能维持；一旦离开中心，墓墙就会崩塌。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:exile card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts ceaseless hands from a yawning portal overcoming a panicked\n"
"figure.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card can banish nearby creatures to the abyss, with more being banished\n"
"at higher power levels. It will never banish the user.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，无数只手从大开的传送门中伸出，淹没了一个惊慌失措的人影。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌可以把附近的生物放逐到深渊，威力越高，放逐的生物越多。它绝不会放逐使用者。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the shaft card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a traveller plummeting into a chasm that has opened beneath\n"
"them.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will create a shaft beneath the user, and possibly beneath\n"
"their enemies.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一名旅人正坠入脚下突然裂开的深渊。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会在使用者脚下产生竖井，也可能在敌人脚下产生竖井。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the elixir card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a smug smile formed out of nine chalices.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card rapidly restores the user's health and magic.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，九只圣杯排列成一张得意的笑脸。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会迅速恢复使用者的生命与魔力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the cloud card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts an iron gate enshrouded in mist.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card enshrouds the user's foes in rings of detrimental clouds. The\n"
"effects of such clouds will vary with card power.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上是一扇笼罩在迷雾中的铁门。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会用一圈圈有害云雾笼罩使用者的敌人。云雾效果随卡牌威力而变化。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:vitriol card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts an oklob plant, dripping with its distinctive corrosive sap.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will unleash a corrosive attack spell.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上是一株奥克罗布植物，滴落着它特有的腐蚀性汁液。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会释放一道腐蚀性的攻击法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the storm card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a ship at sea sinking in a thunderstorm.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card unleashes a storm of wind and electrical discharges.\n"
"Increasing card power will result in a stronger wind force and stronger, more\n"
"numerous discharges.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一艘海船正在雷暴中沉没。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会释放狂风与电击交织的风暴。卡牌威力越高，风力越强，电击也越强、越密集。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:pain card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts an iron wheel, menacing with spikes and rusted with blood.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card unleashes a necromantic attack spell.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上是一只铁轮，尖刺狰狞，血迹锈结。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会释放一道死灵攻击法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the orb card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a figure surrounded by floating, glowing orbs of energy.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card unleashes one or possibly more destructive orbs of pure magic.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一个人影被悬浮发光的能量球环绕。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会释放一颗或多颗由纯粹魔力构成的毁灭之球。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:degeneration card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a dragon whose scales are sloughing off, revealing a sheep\n"
"underneath.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will attempt to polymorph and malmutate nearby enemies into\n"
"weaker forms, and will briefly daze those that cannot be polymorphed.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一条龙的鳞片正在剥落，露出下面的一只绵羊。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会尝试让附近敌人变形成更弱的形态，并施加有害变异；无法变形的敌人则会短暂晕眩。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:wild magic card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a pointy wizard's hat, scorched and resting on a pile of ashes.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card causes wild magic (as if from miscasting a spell) to act upon\n"
"its user's enemies. Each creature affected will restore some of the user's\n"
"magic.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一顶烧焦的尖顶法师帽落在灰烬堆中。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会使狂野魔法（如同法术失控）作用于使用者的敌人。每影响一个生物，都会为使用者恢复一些魔力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the elements card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts the figures of great beasts lurking in a sandstorm.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will summon three beasts of the four elements.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，巨兽的身影潜伏在沙暴中。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会召唤三只属于四大元素的野兽。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the pentagram card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts cultists marking out a ritual pentagram on the floor.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will summon a pair of demons to the user's aid. There is a\n"
"small chance one of the demons will be hostile.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一群邪教徒正在地板上绘制仪式用的五芒星。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会召唤两只恶魔帮助使用者。其中一只有小概率敌对。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the dance card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts an extravagantly-dressed, masked figure dancing alone in a\n"
"vast room.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will summon a dancing weapon. Its quality, brand, and\n"
"friendliness are all affected by card power.\n"
msgstr "牌面上，一个衣着华丽、戴着面具的人独自在宽阔的房间里起舞。\n\n抽出此牌，会召唤一把舞动武器。其品质、印记与是否友好，都受卡牌威力影响。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the swarm card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a bear surrounded by a swarm of bees. It hums ominously.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will summon bees.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一只熊被蜂群包围。卡牌发出不祥的嗡鸣。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会召唤蜜蜂。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the rangers card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts an arrow in a bull's-eye, which has been split by a second\n"
"arrow.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will summon several archers.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一支正中靶心的箭，被第二支箭从中劈开。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会召唤数名弓箭手。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the illusion card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts someone standing in a hall of mirrors, surrounded by their own\n"
"reflections.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will summon an illusion of the user. Its power will depend\n"
"upon one's own.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一个人站在镜厅中，被自己的倒影包围。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会召唤使用者的幻象，其实力取决于使用者自身。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:wrath card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts the hand of the divine, reaching down from the heavens to hurl\n"
"furious lightning.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will draw a god's wrath against the user.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一只神明之手从天际伸下，掷出狂怒的闪电。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会招来某位神祇对使用者的愤怒。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the wraith card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts absolutely nothing.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will drain the user.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上什么也没有。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会使使用者受到吸能。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:the swine card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts several feral hogs wallowing in a mud pit.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will make its user turn pink and root for truffles.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，几头野猪正在泥坑里打滚。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会让使用者变得粉红，并开始拱土寻找松露。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:torment card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a screaming figure being tortured on the rack.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card will cause agonising injury to the user.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一个人在刑架上受刑，痛苦地尖叫。\n"
"\n"
"抽出此牌，会使使用者遭受剧痛的伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:a buggy card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts a Crawl player filing a bug report on Mantis.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card is a bug, if one ever encounters it as such.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，一名 Crawl 玩家正在 Mantis 上提交缺陷报告。\n"
"\n"
"如果你真的抽到了这张牌，那就是程序缺陷。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/cards.txt:a very buggy card"
msgid ""
"The card depicts several Crawl players angrily filing several bug reports on\n"
"Mantis.\n"
"\n"
"Drawing this card is a bug, if one ever encounters it as such.\n"
msgstr ""
"牌面上，几名 Crawl 玩家正在 Mantis 上愤怒地提交多份缺陷报告。\n"
"\n"
"如果你真的抽到了这张牌，那就是程序缺陷。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/unident.txt:amulet"
msgid ""
"An amulet to be worn as jewellery around the neck, charged with arcane powers\n"
"of unknown provenance.\n"
msgstr "一枚戴在颈间的护身符，蕴含来源不明的奥术力量。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/unident.txt:book"
msgid "An arcane textbook containing magical spells of unknown origin.\n"
msgstr "一本记载着来源不明的魔法咒语的奥术教科书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/unident.txt:potion"
msgid "An unlabelled flask containing a single dose of unknown liquid.\n"
msgstr "一只没有标签的小瓶，装着一剂未知液体。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/unident.txt:ring"
msgid ""
"A ring charged with arcane forces of unknown provenance, to be worn as jewellery\n"
"on a finger.\n"
msgstr "一枚戴在手指上的戒指，蕴含来源不明的奥术力量。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/unident.txt:scroll"
msgid ""
"A disposable arcane formula inscribed on parchment by a professional scribe or\n"
"sorcerer. Anyone can evoke the power of the arcane formula by reading it out\n"
"loud, but the nature of that power is not a priori apparent.\n"
msgstr "由专业抄写员或术士写在羊皮纸上的一次性奥术公式。任何人都能通过高声诵读来唤发其中的力量，但事先无法看出这种力量的性质。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/unident.txt:staff"
msgid "A staff improved with arcane powers of unknown nature.\n"
msgstr "一根经由未知性质的奥术力量强化的法杖。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/unident.txt:wand"
msgid "An unusually magical sort of stick.\n"
msgstr "一根异常神奇的短杖。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:dungeon"
msgid ""
"It is still a mystery how this bizarre place was created. Some claim that it is\n"
"the playground of bored gods, whereas others maintain that it was shaped by all\n"
"kinds of species who fled the overworld and shunned the light. No matter what\n"
"its origin, this deep cavern is filled with riches unheard of as well as with\n"
"ample dangers to any intruder. Few have escaped alive, and even fewer have kept\n"
"some sliver of sanity sufficient to tell the tale.\n"
msgstr "这个离奇之地究竟如何形成，至今仍是谜。有些人说它是无聊神祇的游乐场，另一些人则认为，是逃离地表、躲避阳光的各种族塑造了它。无论起源如何，这片深邃洞窟既有闻所未闻的财富，也有足以威胁任何入侵者的重重危险。逃出生天的人寥寥无几，而其中还能保留些许神智、讲述经历的人就更少了。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:temple"
msgid ""
"The Ecumenical Temple is a place of peace and refuge from the insanity of the\n"
"dungeon. It usually contains altars to most of the known gods. Gods that value\n"
"exploration grant no piety for exploring the Temple.\n"
msgstr "众神殿是一片安宁的庇护所，让人暂避地下城的疯狂。这里通常设有大多数已知神祇的祭坛。即使是重视探索的神祇，也不会因探索众神殿而赐予虔诚。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:orcish mines"
msgid ""
"The Orcish Mines are home to the orcs that have settled in the Dungeon, their\n"
"humanoid allies, and piles of freshly mined gold. Enterprising merchants who\n"
"sell to all comers have set up trading posts among the orcs and their brethren\n"
"to make good use of that gold.\n"
msgstr "兽人矿井住着在地下城定居的兽人及其类人盟友，还堆着刚开采出来的金币。精明的商人来者不拒，在兽人与同族之间设下贸易站，好把这些金币赚到手。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:elven halls"
msgid ""
"The Elven Halls are home to the deep elves, a race that turned their backs on\n"
"the sun long ago. Their halls are filled with riches, but a deadly welcome\n"
"awaits any would-be robbers. In their long seclusion, the deep elves have\n"
"perfected dark sorceries of a power the orcs can only dream of!\n"
msgstr "精灵大厅是深地精灵的家园，这个种族早在很久以前便背弃了太阳。大厅中满是财富，但等待妄图抢掠者的，是致命的迎接。在漫长的隐居岁月中，深地精灵完善了黑暗魔法，其威力远超兽人的想象！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:lair"
msgid ""
"Most adventurers find the Lair of Beasts to be an exciting change of climate.\n"
"And indeed, there is something to be said about getting gored, mauled and eaten\n"
"rather than sliced, burnt or stabbed.\n"
"\n"
"The Lair contains the entrances to one of the Swamp or the Shoals, one of the\n"
"Snake Pit or the Spider Nest, and to the Pits of Slime.\n"
msgstr ""
"对多数冒险者来说，野兽巢穴带来令人兴奋的环境变化。的确，与其被砍、被烧、被刺，换成被角顶、被爪撕、被吞食，倒也别有一番滋味。\n"
"\n"
"巢穴通往沼泽或海滩之一、蛇穴或蜘蛛巢之一，以及史莱姆巢穴。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:swamp"
msgid ""
"A swampy wasteland, the Swamp is filled with ooze, muck, flies and large\n"
"slavering carnivorous monsters.\n"
"\n"
"A dungeon features only one of the Swamp and Shoals branches.\n"
msgstr ""
"沼泽是一片湿地荒原，遍布黏泥、污淖、苍蝇，以及流着涎液的大型食肉怪物。\n"
"\n"
"一座地下城只会出现沼泽与海滩中的一个分支。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:shoals"
msgid ""
"The exotic underground beaches of the Shoals make up a few small islands in a\n"
"seemingly endless sea. The merfolk have made it their home, alongside many\n"
"dreaded sea creatures.\n"
"\n"
"A dungeon features only one of the Shoals and Swamp branches.\n"
msgstr ""
"海滩由几座小岛构成，奇异的地下沙滩散布在看似无边的大海中。人鱼与许多可怕的海洋生物在这里安家。\n"
"\n"
"一座地下城只会出现海滩与沼泽中的一个分支。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:snake pit"
msgid ""
"The corridors of the Snake Pit are home to all varieties of serpent, and are\n"
"inhabited by a society of powerful nagas and salamanders.\n"
"\n"
"A dungeon features only one of the Snake Pit and Spider Nest branches.\n"
msgstr ""
"蛇穴的走廊中生活着各式蛇类，也住着由强大娜迦与蝾螈组成的族群。\n"
"\n"
"一座地下城只会出现蛇穴与蜘蛛巢中的一个分支。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:spider nest"
msgid ""
"The crumbling, web-choked caverns of the Spider Nest are packed with poisonous\n"
"arthropods and assorted creepy-crawlies.\n"
"\n"
"A dungeon features only one of the Spider Nest and Snake Pit branches.\n"
msgstr ""
"蜘蛛巢的洞窟破败不堪、蛛网密布，里面挤满有毒节肢动物与各种爬虫。\n"
"\n"
"一座地下城只会出现蜘蛛巢与蛇穴中的一个分支。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:slime pits"
msgid ""
"The Slime Pits are the amorphous realm of acids, jellies and slimes. Even the\n"
"walls drip with painful acid. Any trace of intelligent beings has long been\n"
"dissolved. Still, there are rumours of great treasures deep down, hidden safely\n"
"away in secret chambers without any entrance.\n"
msgstr "史莱姆巢穴是酸液、胶怪与史莱姆的无定形国度。连墙壁都滴着令人痛苦的酸液。智慧生物的痕迹早已被溶解殆尽。尽管如此，仍有传闻说深处藏着巨大的财富，被安全地封存在没有入口的密室中。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:vaults"
msgid ""
"The Vaults are said to be home to great treasures and sealed evils alike, its\n"
"origin known only to its guardians: the Ironbound Order. Intruders face an\n"
"organised defence of trained maneuvers, arms and arcana, animated constructs,\n"
"coerced allies, and tamed beasts, all in common cause.\n"
msgstr "据说，宝库既收藏着巨额财富，也封印着邪恶。只有守护它的铁缚教团知道其起源。入侵者将面对严密组织的防御：训练有素的战术、武器与奥术，以及活动构装体、被迫效命的盟友和驯服的野兽，全都为同一目标而战。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:crypt"
msgid ""
"The Crypt is a huge repository for the ancient dead. The air is chill and\n"
"fetid, the walls cold and damp. Bones are strewn liberally everywhere, and\n"
"every noise echoes worryingly, violating the overbearing silence of the grave.\n"
msgstr "墓室是安放古老死者的巨大场所。空气寒冷腐臭，墙壁冰凉潮湿，骸骨四处散落。每一声响动都会激起令人不安的回声，冒犯坟墓压倒一切的寂静。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:tomb"
msgid ""
"The Tomb of the Ancients is a place of damnation, of horrors animated by the\n"
"vilest necromancy. The list of those who have returned from this place of pure\n"
"death is exceedingly short.\n"
msgstr "古人灵庙是受诅咒之地，其中的恐怖存在由最恶毒的死灵魔法驱动。从这片纯粹死亡之地生还的人，屈指可数。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:hell"
msgid ""
"The Vestibule of Hell is guarded by Geryon, along with various denizens of\n"
"each of the hells themselves.\n"
"\n"
"Portals to the Vestibule of Hell are found abundantly in the Depths.\n"
msgstr "地狱前庭由革律翁守卫，还有来自各层地狱的居民。\n\n地底中有许多通往地狱前庭的传送门。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:dis"
msgid ""
"The Iron City of Dis is home to many of the most resilient guardians of hell.\n"
"Those who do not belong in the halls of Dis will find the very earth itself\n"
"opposing them.\n"
"\n"
"The malice of this metal realm corrodes equipment.\n"
msgstr ""
"冥府铁城是许多最坚韧地狱守卫的家园。不属于冥府殿堂的人，会发现连大地本身都在与自己作对。\n"
"\n"
"这个金属国度的恶意会腐蚀装备。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:gehenna"
msgid ""
"Gehenna is a realm of lava, flames and damnation. Those who linger will have\n"
"fire and brimstone rained down upon them.\n"
"\n"
"The acrid smoke renders scrolls unreadable.\n"
msgstr ""
"欣嫩谷充满熔岩、烈焰与天谴。逗留者将遭受火焰与硫磺之雨。\n"
"\n"
"刺鼻的浓烟使卷轴无法阅读。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:cocytus"
msgid ""
"Cocytus is a grim and frost-bitten wasteland. Intruders will find the biting\n"
"winds and icy inhabitants of the wastes impeding their progress.\n"
"\n"
"The frigid cold congeals potions.\n"
msgstr ""
"悲叹河是一片阴森、冰封的荒原。刺骨寒风与栖居其中的冰冷生物，都会阻挡入侵者前进。\n"
"\n"
"严寒会凝结药水。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:tartarus"
msgid ""
"Tartarus is a decaying netherworld. Over time, the undead, demons and devils of\n"
"this place drain the life from any who dare to enter.\n"
"\n"
"The all-pervading rot saps visitors' willpower.\n"
msgstr ""
"塔尔塔罗斯是一个腐朽的地下世界。此地的亡灵、恶魔与魔鬼，会逐渐吸走所有胆敢闯入者的生命。\n"
"\n"
"无处不在的腐败会削弱来访者的意志。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:zot"
msgid ""
"The Realm of Zot is a region of the dungeon that is so terrifying, so full of\n"
"madness, frenzy and lunacy, that it has been locked securely against random\n"
"trespassers. Only the most demented adventurers would dare gather the required\n"
"keys, break the seal and penetrate deeper — all in the vain hope for a fabled\n"
"artefact no one has ever laid eyes on before.\n"
msgstr "佐特领域是地下城的一片区域。这里如此恐怖，充满狂乱、暴躁与癫狂，因此被严密封锁，阻止闲杂人等闯入。只有最疯癫的冒险者，才敢收集所需钥匙、打破封印、继续深入——全为徒劳追寻一件从来无人亲眼见过的传说神器。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:abyss"
msgid ""
"The Abyss is a truly bizarre place, ever-changing and twisted. It is filled\n"
"with all sorts of monsters, mostly of demonic nature, whose common aim is to\n"
"feast on intruders. It is also the garbage dump for many sorcerers, who delight\n"
"in sending would-be champions like you to these proving grounds of madness.\n"
"Reportedly, there is some structure to the chaos, as Lugonu seems to concoct\n"
"schemes around this place and its denizens.\n"
"\n"
"Portals to the Abyss are found abundantly in the Depths.\n"
"\n"
"The Abyss consists of seven infinite levels. The abyssal rune of Zot can be\n"
"found from the third level onwards, and is more common at greater depths.\n"
"Portals back to the dungeon are scattered throughout the Abyss, and are found\n"
"more commonly at greater depths or while carrying the abyssal rune.\n"
"\n"
"Killing monsters will warp the substance of the Abyss, eventually generating a\n"
"gateway out. Further persistence will wear holes in the Abyss, allowing descent\n"
"into deeper layers.\n"
"\n"
"The fabric of the Abyss takes greater notice of the powerful; no matter how\n"
"they arrive, more experienced adventurers will find themselves drawn deeper\n"
"within the maddening expanse of that realm.\n"
msgstr ""
"深渊是真正离奇之地，永远变化、永远扭曲。这里满是各种怪物，多数具有恶魔本性，共同的目标就是吞食入侵者。它也是许多术士的垃圾场；他们乐于把你这样自命英雄的人送进这片疯狂试炼场。据说混沌中仍有某种秩序，因为卢戈努似乎正围绕此地及其居民策划阴谋。\n"
"\n"
"地底中有许多通往深渊的传送门。\n"
"\n"
"深渊由七个无限大的楼层构成。从第三层开始可以找到深渊符文，越深越常见。返回地下城的出口散布各处；越深入，或身上带着深渊符文时，越容易发现出口。\n"
"\n"
"击杀怪物会扭曲深渊的物质，最终产生出口。继续坚持下去，还会在深渊撕开裂隙，让你进入更深的楼层。\n"
"\n"
"深渊的结构对强者格外敏感：无论以何种方式到来，经验更丰富的冒险者都会发现，自己被吸入这片疯狂国度的更深处。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:pandemonium"
msgid ""
"Pandemonium is an infinite realm of pain and suffering. While there are many\n"
"treasures to be found within, they are guarded by cruel demons and even\n"
"crueller demon lords.\n"
"\n"
"Portals to Pandemonium are found abundantly in the Depths.\n"
"\n"
"Pandemonium is endless. Each area of Pandemonium has a small chance of\n"
"containing a portal back to the dungeon, either directly or via the Abyss.\n"
"\n"
"No fewer than five runes of Zot can be found in Pandemonium:\n"
" • the fiery rune resides in the blazing realm of Cerebov\n"
" • the glowing rune can be found in the contaminated domain of Mnoleg\n"
" • the magical rune is guarded by the arcane powers of Lom Lobon\n"
" • the dark rune is hidden in the shadowy abode of Gloorx Vloq\n"
" • the demonic rune exists in multiple places, owned by less famous lords\n"
msgstr "魔窟是痛苦与折磨的无限国度。这里虽有许多财富，却由残忍的恶魔与更加残忍的恶魔领主看守。\n\n地底中有许多通往魔窟的传送门。\n\n魔窟没有尽头。每片区域都有小概率出现返回地下城的出口，可能直达地下城，也可能经过深渊。\n\n魔窟中至少可以找到五种佐特符文：\n • 炽焰符文位于 瑟雷波夫 的烈焰国度\n • 辉光符文位于 姆诺莱格 的污染领地\n • 魔法符文由 洛姆·洛邦 的奥术力量守护\n • 黑暗符文藏在 格洛克斯·弗洛克 的阴影居所\n • 恶魔符文存在于多个地点，由名气较小的领主拥有\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:ziggurat"
msgid ""
"A ziggurat is a strange tower constructed of incrementally larger combat\n"
"arenas, each containing greater wealth and even greater danger than the last.\n"
"Beware, for a ziggurat is not a place for the faint of heart: even the bravest\n"
"and most skilled adventurers have met their ends in one. While a portal to\n"
"safety will be present on every level, once left, a ziggurat cannot be\n"
"re-entered.\n"
"\n"
"One ziggurat is guaranteed in the Depths. Tales tell of a magical item found\n"
"at the bottom of each ziggurat, granting access to a new ziggurat in turn. Such\n"
"an item is also said to be found at the bottom of the Tomb of the Ancients. Each\n"
"time a ziggurat is conquered by exiting it from the final floor, subsequent\n"
"ziggurats will become increasingly dangerous and lucrative.\n"
msgstr "神塔是一座奇异高塔，每层的战斗场地都比上一层更大，财富更多，危险也更甚。请小心，这里容不得胆怯：即使最勇敢、最娴熟的冒险者，也曾在此丧命。每层都有通往安全地带的出口，但离开之后便无法重新进入。\n\n地底保证会出现一座神塔。传说每座神塔底层都有一件魔法物品，可以开启下一座神塔；据说古人灵庙底层也有这种物品。每当你从神塔最后一层离开、完成征服后，之后的神塔就会更危险，也更富饶。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:gauntlet"
msgid ""
"An elaborate complex designed to lure foolhardy adventurers seeking riches and\n"
"glory. Those who enter must choose a path through several combat arenas, each\n"
"of which contains treasure guarded by dangerous and sometimes exotic creatures.\n"
"At the end awaits a fearsome minotaur, guarding a large hoard of loot taken from\n"
"the bodies of foolish adventurers.\n"
"\n"
"Long-range teleports are impossible in Gauntlets.\n"
msgstr "一座精心设计的复杂建筑，诱惑鲁莽的冒险者追逐财富与荣耀。进入后，必须选择一条穿越多个战斗场地的路线。每个场地都有宝物，由危险且有时奇异的生物守护。尽头则是一名可怕的牛头人，看守从愚蠢冒险者尸体上搜刮的大量战利品。\n\n竞技场中无法进行远距离传送。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:bazaar"
msgid ""
"While some merchants set up shop in the dungeon, others travel in caravans from\n"
"place to place. The bazaars of these itinerant traders feature a number of\n"
"different shops and often have better stock than the sedentary ones, sometimes\n"
"even at a bargain.\n"
msgstr "有些商人在地下城定居开店，另一些则随商队四处旅行。这些行商的集市有多家不同商店，货品往往比固定商店更好，有时还更便宜。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:trove"
msgid ""
"Once upon a time, an enterprising thief and wizard created a system of portals\n"
"leading into the secret treasure troves and chambers of the rich. Too scared to\n"
"loot them himself, he instead charged an extortionate fee for entry to anyone\n"
"who wanted to rifle through them.\n"
"\n"
"The items inside such troves are likely to be useful, but beware: the wizard is\n"
"long dead, and even while alive he never offered a money-back guarantee.\n"
msgstr ""
"从前，一名精明的盗贼兼巫师创建了一套传送门系统，通向富人的秘密宝藏与密室。他胆子太小，不敢亲自抢掠，便向想进去搜刮的人收取高得离谱的入场费。\n"
"\n"
"这些宝藏中的物品很可能有用，但请小心：巫师早已死去，而且即使活着时，他也从未承诺退款。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:necropolis"
msgid ""
"While many locales across the Dungeon are dedicated to the long-interred\n"
"restless dead, those whose remains are fresh or lost are collected in the\n"
"floating ceremonial chambers of the Necropolis. Each soul is enshrined and\n"
"tended to by the maintenance staff recreating both their lives and their moments\n"
"of death, helping visitors bid farewell to the departed. With the advent of\n"
"adventurers seeking the Orb of Zot, these realms have been repurposed: such\n"
"ghosts are blinded by rage and impossible to control, so both they and their\n"
"stolen possessions are sealed away in these realms of reconciliation.\n"
msgstr "地下城中有许多地方供奉着入土已久、不得安息的死者，而刚死去或遗骸失落之人的魂灵，则被收容在亡者之城漂浮的仪式厅中。每个魂灵都受到供奉与照料，工作人员重现其生前经历与临终时刻，帮助来访者与逝者告别。寻找佐特宝珠的冒险者出现后，这些领域被改作他用：这种幽灵被狂怒蒙蔽，无法控制，因此它们与其被夺走的财物，一同被封存在这些原本用于和解的领域中。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:sewer"
msgid ""
"Every inhabited place needs to dispose of its waste products. The Dungeon too\n"
"has its stinking sewers and drains, full of filthy water and ignored by most\n"
"but used as hideaways by the disgusting and the desperate. Old tales speak of\n"
"dangerous creatures stalking through the foul-smelling green water, preying on\n"
"each other without mercy. The tales also allude to valuable items accidentally\n"
"washed into the drainage tunnels, forgotten and left to grow mouldy in the damp\n"
"caverns.\n"
msgstr "每个有人居住的地方都需要处理废物，地下城也不例外。这里有臭气熏天的下水道与排水沟，污水遍地，多数人避而远之，却成了肮脏之辈与走投无路者的藏身处。古老传说讲述危险生物如何游荡在恶臭的绿水中，毫不留情地互相捕食，也提到意外冲进排水隧道的贵重物品，被遗忘在潮湿洞窟里，慢慢发霉。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:ossuary"
msgid ""
"The ossuary is a small tomb containing the remains and grave goods of some\n"
"distant relatives of the pharaohs, along with the corpses of their retainers\n"
"and household animals. It is undoubtedly riddled with many traps, and its\n"
"undead denizens are unlikely to take kindly to looting.\n"
msgstr "埋骨地是一座小型陵墓，埋着法老某些远亲的遗骸与陪葬品，还有侍从和家养动物的尸体。这里无疑布满陷阱，亡灵居民大概也不会欢迎盗墓者。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:bailey"
msgid ""
"The bailey is the occupied and well-guarded fortress of a ruthless warlord.\n"
"The treasures within are protected by both physical barriers and large numbers\n"
"of well-armed humanoid warriors.\n"
msgstr "这处堡场由一名无情军阀占据，守备森严。实体屏障与大批全副武装的类人战士，共同保护着其中的财富。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:ice cave"
msgid ""
"The {{ if you.branch() == \"Elf\" or you.branch() == \"Swamp\" or\n"
"you.branch() == \"Snake\" or you.branch() == \"Shoals\" or you.branch() == \"Spider\"\n"
"then return \"glacial chasm\"; else return \"ice cave\"; end }} is a desolate cavern\n"
"shaped from solid ice and filled with the echoes of bestial howls. The intricate\n"
"carvings and statues which once lined its walls have been warped and obscured by\n"
"centuries of slow melting and refreezing.\n"
msgstr ""
"{{ if you.branch() == \"Elf\" or you.branch() == \"Swamp\" or\n"
"you.branch() == \"Snake\" or you.branch() == \"Shoals\" or you.branch() == \"Spider\"\n"
"then return \"冰川裂隙\"; else return \"冰窟\"; end }}是一座由坚冰塑成的荒凉洞窟，回荡着野兽的嚎叫。墙边昔日精致的雕刻与塑像，经过数百年缓慢融化与再度冻结，早已扭曲模糊。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:volcano"
msgid ""
"Built from enormous blocks of obsidian, the volcano's sweltering chambers may\n"
"once have served as a temple to some strange deity, or perhaps the dwelling of\n"
"a mighty fire giant. The air shimmers with oppressive heat, and the dull roar\n"
"of the volcano's heart never ceases.\n"
msgstr "火山内部闷热的厅室由巨大黑曜石砌成，或许曾是某位奇异神祇的庙宇，也可能是一名强大火巨人的住所。逼人的热浪使空气扭曲，火山深处低沉的轰鸣从未停歇。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:wizlab"
msgid ""
"In ages past, the most powerful mages would frequently find or construct small\n"
"realms sealed off from the rest of the world, where they could isolate\n"
"themselves in the pursuit of ever-greater magical knowledge and power. The\n"
"mages are long gone, but many of their arcane laboratories still exist, filled\n"
"with the results of their experiments. Those willing to explore these\n"
"laboratories may find powerful magical treasures, but be warned: any wizard\n"
"capable of constructing such a realm deserved their reputation.\n"
msgstr "远古时代，最强大的法师常会寻找或建造与世隔绝的小型领域，独自追求更深的魔法知识与力量。法师们早已不在，但许多奥术实验室依然留存，里面满是实验成果。愿意探索的人可能找到强大的魔法宝物，但请小心：能够创造这种领域的巫师，绝非浪得虚名。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:depths"
msgid ""
"The Depths are the deepest part of the dungeon proper, subject to the\n"
"corrupting influence of the Realm of Zot without being considered a part of it.\n"
msgstr "地底是地下城主体最深的部分，受到佐特领域的腐化影响，却不属于佐特领域。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:desolation"
msgid ""
"The Desolation was once ruled by the divines Sheza and Sargol. After the dread\n"
"twins were cast down, the good gods reduced their former realm to salt, that\n"
"such a terrible cult would never rise again. Amidst the ruins, only the last\n"
"cultists of the dead gods, their heretical constructs, and the guardians\n"
"of the cult's legendary treasure yet remain.\n"
"\n"
msgstr "荒盐之地曾由神明 西泽 与 赛格尔 统治。可怕的双神被推翻后，善神将他们昔日的国度化为盐土，以免如此恐怖的邪教再次兴起。如今，废墟中只剩亡神最后的信徒、他们异端的构装体，以及邪教传说宝藏的守卫。\n\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:arena"
msgid ""
"Okawaru's most favoured followers are granted access to the Arena to duel\n"
"against their foes.\n"
msgstr "奥格瓦如最宠爱的信徒获准进入奥格瓦如竞技场，与敌人决斗。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/branches.txt:crucible"
msgid ""
"The Crucible of Flesh is an infernal pit where Makhleb's most devoted and\n"
"detested alike are made to sanctify themselves in blood. No sane mortal would\n"
"ever choose to come here, and yet even victims of the Destroyer's greatest ire\n"
"may be granted passage out once more, should they mete out mutilation equal to\n"
"the demonic torturers of this realm.\n"
msgstr "血肉熔炉是一处地狱深坑，马科列布最虔诚与最憎恶的人，都会被迫在此以鲜血圣化自身。没有神志正常的凡人会自愿来这里。然而，即使是承受毁灭者最深愤怒的受害者，只要造成的残害能与此地的恶魔刑吏相比，也可能再次获准离开。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ashenzari wrath"
msgid ""
"Those who abandon Ashenzari will immediately have their curses shattered,\n"
"destroying whichever items they imbued with divine wisdom. Thereafter,\n"
"Ashenzari's wrath is constant and unrelenting for its duration. Victims will\n"
"find their skills impaired, and their enemies divinely guided – never losing\n"
"track of them, never ending the hunt.\n"
msgstr "背弃 艾申扎利 的人，其诅咒会立即破碎，所有注入神圣智慧的物品也会随之摧毁。此后，在神罚持续期间，祂的怒火始终不息，毫不留情。受罚者的技能会受损，敌人则得到神明指引，永不失去其踪迹，永不停止追猎。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:beogh wrath"
msgid ""
"Blasphemers against the word of Beogh find themselves assaulted by waves of\n"
"orcish warriors, or by dancing electric weapons. Beogh may also simply smite\n"
"such blasphemers – and when smiting true sinners, Beogh has a heavy hand\n"
"indeed! Those who still worship Beogh will also find their followers regularly\n"
"deserting them.\n"
msgstr "亵渎 比欧弗 教诲的人，会遭到一波波兽人战士或舞动的电击武器袭击。祂也可能直接降下惩击；面对真正的罪人，祂下手尤其沉重！仍然信奉祂的人，还会不断遭遇追随者叛离。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:cheibriados wrath"
msgid ""
"Offenders against Cheibriados will find their movements remain slow while\n"
"the attention of Cheibriados remains upon them, and may have any magical hasting\n"
"stripped away. They may also become further slowed, be put to sleep, or be\n"
"beset by the unparalleled volume of the inevitable passage of time ringing\n"
"throughout the Dungeon.\n"
msgstr "只要 切布理亚多 仍然关注冒犯者，他们的移动就会保持缓慢，身上的魔法加速也可能被剥除。他们还可能进一步减速、陷入沉睡，或遭受时间必然流逝的震耳巨响；那声音回荡在整座地下城之中。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:dithmenos wrath"
msgid ""
"When angered, Dithmenos turns the shadows against victims. Monsters emerge from\n"
"the darkness, both illusions woven from shadow and the very shadow themselves\n"
"turning against sinners. Dithmenos' subtle punishments are, if anything, more\n"
"dangerous: victims find the shadows ripped away from them, hunted with nowhere\n"
"to hide; or find themselves smothered in shadow and sleeping, perhaps forever.\n"
msgstr "迪斯姆诺 愤怒时，会让阴影反过来对付受罚者。怪物从黑暗中现身，既有阴影编织的幻象，也有阴影本身，向罪人发起攻击。祂更隐秘的惩罚或许还要危险：受罚者身边的阴影可能被剥去，在追猎中无处藏身；也可能被阴影吞没，沉睡不醒，甚至永不醒来。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:elyvilon wrath"
msgid ""
"Elyvilon is not a god known for wrath. Still, those earning Elyvilon's ire will\n"
"find the Healer occasionally protecting their foes from their attacks, and even\n"
"from death.\n"
msgstr "艾利维隆 并不以愤怒著称。不过，招致祂不满的人会发现，治疗者偶尔会保护他们的敌人，使其免受攻击，甚至免于死亡。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:fedhas wrath"
msgid ""
"Those who offend Fedhas will find the forces of nature invoked against them\n"
"through a dramatic increase in greenery. They may find themselves transmuted\n"
"into the plants they have forsaken, or surrounded by impenetrable walls of\n"
"briars plus vicious acid-spitting oklob plants.\n"
msgstr "冒犯 费德哈 的人，会看到周围的绿色植物剧增，自然之力转而与自己为敌。他们可能被变成自己曾经背弃的植物，也可能被无法穿越的荆棘墙及凶猛的喷酸奥克罗布草包围。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:hepliaklqana wrath"
msgid ""
"Hepliaklqana believes that the only reasonable punishment for turning one's\n"
"back on the path of memory is to be denied its use. All new experience is\n"
"denied to the unfortunate apostate, until Hepliaklqana decides they have\n"
"been punished enough. The life essence sacrificed to manifest an ancestor will\n"
"not be returned until Hepliaklqana is mollified, and this will not be quick:\n"
"unlike some, Hepliaklqana has a long memory.\n"
msgstr "惠普利亚卡纳 认为，背离记忆之道的唯一合理惩罚，就是剥夺使用记忆的权利。不幸的叛教者将无法获得任何新经验，直到祂认为惩罚已经足够。为使先祖显现而牺牲的生命精华，也要等祂息怒后才会归还；这不会很快，因为祂不像某些神祇那样健忘。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:gozag wrath"
msgid ""
"The first of Gozag's punishments is commercial: all shops opened through\n"
"Gozag's intervention shut their doors forever. The disloyal are advised to\n"
"finish their shopping before they launch their betrayal. For as long as Gozag\n"
"remains angered, ex-worshippers may sometimes be bedazzled by the glint of coin,\n"
"and their potions will have a chance to fail when quaffed. Any foes that are\n"
"encountered may also be granted potions of their own to assist them against\n"
"those who resign from Gozag's service.\n"
msgstr "哥萨戈 的第一项惩罚与商业有关：经祂介入开设的商店会永久关门。背信者最好在叛离之前买完所需物品。在祂愤怒期间，昔日信徒有时会被钱币的光芒晃花眼，饮用的药水也有一定概率失效。他们遇到的敌人还可能得到自己的药水，用来对付这些离开 哥萨戈 的人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ignis wrath"
msgid ""
"The wrath of Ignis is now weaker than that of most other gods. Apostates will\n"
"find their resistance to fire stripped away completely, and will be periodically\n"
"assaulted by fire elementals, find their enemies strengthened by fire, or even\n"
"have the floor burned out from beneath them. Experienced and cautious\n"
"adventurers will likely overmaster these assaults.\n"
msgstr "如今 伊格尼斯 的神罚比大多数神祇都弱。叛教者的火焰抗性会被完全剥除，并定期遭受火元素袭击；他们的敌人可能获得火焰强化，甚至脚下的地板也可能被烧穿。经验丰富且谨慎的冒险者，很可能能够应付这些攻击。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:jiyva wrath"
msgid ""
"Jiyva's vengeance is swift and gurgling. All slimes turn against those who\n"
"offend Jiyva, and Jiyva ensures a plentiful supply of further slimes. Victims,\n"
"too, will find their own bodies becoming unstable; acquiring debilitating\n"
"mutations or contamination, as well as having any gifts of slime mutations\n"
"stripped away from them.\n"
msgstr "吉瓦 的复仇迅速而咕噜作响。所有软泥怪都会敌视冒犯者，而祂还会确保更多软泥怪源源不断地出现。受罚者的身体也会变得不稳定，获得削弱自身的变异或魔法污染，同时失去所有作为恩赐获得的软泥变异。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:kikubaaqudgha wrath"
msgid ""
"Kikubaaqudgha's wrath brings forth all the dread powers of necromancy. Victims\n"
"may witness the devastating Sign of Ruin form upon themselves, or both doomed\n"
"and drained without any respect for their negative energy resistance.\n"
"Furthermore, Kikubaaqudgha's gifts become tainted: the dead rise again as foes,\n"
"and those that attempt to use necromantic magic to fend off wrath will find it\n"
"backfiring on them when least expected.\n"
msgstr "奇库巴库哈 的怒火会唤出死灵术的一切可怖力量。受罚者可能看到毁灭性的毁灭征兆出现在自己身上，也可能同时遭受厄运和吸能，完全无视负能量抗性。此外，祂的恩赐会遭到玷污：死者重新起身成为敌人；试图用死灵系魔法抵御神罚的人，也会在最意想不到的时候遭到反噬。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:lugonu wrath"
msgid ""
"Lugonu's ire renders the barrier between reality and the Abyss weak and\n"
"permeable. Space warps, hurling victims across the dungeon, or even directly\n"
"into the Abyss. Lugonu also reaches out and sends the chaotic inhabitants of\n"
"the Abyss against victims, with veteran adventurers facing the greatest horrors\n"
"of the Abyss. Lugonu does not forgive easily, and will not allow ex-worshippers\n"
"to rejoin the fold while Lugonu's wrath still lasts.\n"
msgstr "卢戈努 的怒火会使现实与深渊之间的屏障变得脆弱而易于穿透。空间扭曲，将受罚者抛向地下城各处，甚至直接投入深渊。祂也会派出深渊中的混沌居民袭击受罚者；资深冒险者面对的，将是深渊最可怕的存在。祂不轻易宽恕，只要神罚尚未结束，昔日信徒就无法重新皈依。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:makhleb wrath"
msgid ""
"Those who invite the fury of Makhleb are buried in demons and destruction.\n"
"The greatest punishments are reserved for the strongest sinners; crystal spears\n"
"and Executioners are hurled with abandon only at those Makhleb finds truly\n"
"deserving!\n"
msgstr "招致 马科列布 愤怒的人，会被恶魔与毁灭淹没。最严厉的惩罚留给最强大的罪人；唯有祂认为真正罪有应得的人，才会毫无节制地迎来水晶矛与刽子手恶魔！\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:nemelex xobeh wrath"
msgid ""
"Those who abandon Nemelex Xobeh have all of their gifted decks revoked\n"
"immediately. They are also regularly forced to draw from the deck of\n"
"Punishment, inflicting a range of unpleasant effects including draining,\n"
"torment and polymorphing, as well as calling upon other gods to assist in\n"
"inflicting wrath.\n"
msgstr "背弃 尼姆雷斯・索布 的人，会立即被收回所有获赐的牌组。他们还会定期被迫从惩罚牌组抽牌，承受吸能、折磨、变形等各种不良效果，甚至引来其他神祇协助施罚。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:okawaru wrath"
msgid ""
"Okawaru's most vicious warriors are sent against rebellious servants. Novices\n"
"find themselves swarmed by packs of ogres and gnolls, while champions are\n"
"surrounded by titans and elvish blademasters.\n"
msgstr "奥格瓦如 会派出最凶狠的战士对付叛逆的仆从。新手会被成群的食人魔和豺狼人围攻，强者则会被泰坦与精灵剑圣包围。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:pakellas wrath"
msgid ""
"Those that offend Pakellas will find themselves completely unable to make use\n"
"of their devices for the duration of Pakellas' displeasure. Those who abandon\n"
"Pakellas altogether will also continue to be unable to regenerate their magical\n"
"power so long as Pakellas' attention remains on them.\n"
msgstr "只要 帕克拉斯 仍然不满，冒犯者就完全无法使用器械。彻底背弃祂的人，只要仍受到祂的关注，还会一直无法恢复魔力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:qazlal wrath"
msgid ""
"Qazlal's wrath is swift and unmistakable. Sinners are stripped of their\n"
"resistances and assaulted by furious elemental creatures, and Qazlal will\n"
"create mighty thunderclaps to alert their foes.\n"
msgstr "卡兹拉尔 的神罚迅速而鲜明。罪人的抗性会被剥除，狂暴的元素生物会向其发起袭击，祂还会制造震耳雷鸣，惊动他们的敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ru wrath"
msgid ""
"Those who leave Ru's service will not receive any further punishment; however,\n"
"their piety will be lost even upon rejoining, and their sacrifices remain\n"
"forever.\n"
msgstr "离开 入 的人不会受到额外惩罚。不过，他们的虔诚会丧失，即使重新皈依也不会恢复，而已经作出的牺牲将永久保留。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:sif muna wrath"
msgid ""
"Those in Sif Muna's ill graces find the very forces of magic rebelling against\n"
"them. They are confused and stupefied, their magical reserves drained, their\n"
"enchantments unravelled. Casting spells, too, becomes unreliable – and even\n"
"dangerous.\n"
msgstr "失去 席夫·穆纳 青睐的人，会发现魔法之力本身也在反抗自己。他们会陷入混乱与迟钝，魔力储备被抽空，身上的魔法效果被解除。施法也会变得不可靠，甚至危险。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:the shining one wrath"
msgid ""
"The Shining One's wrath is straightforward and unmistakable. Its victims find\n"
"themselves smitten with holy fire and beset with holy warriors. Sinners will be\n"
"silenced, and the Shining One will also shout to alert the victim's foes.\n"
msgstr "光明神 的神罚直截了当，不容错认。受罚者会被神圣火焰惩击，并遭到神圣战士围攻。罪人会遭受沉默，祂还会大声呼喊，惊动受罚者的敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:trog wrath"
msgid ""
"Trog's wrath is incandescent. Offenders find themselves swarmed by berserkers –\n"
"from packs of bears to, for the most powerful, mobs of giants and trolls.\n"
"Otherwise, those who anger Trog will regularly lose both their strength and\n"
"self-control as they thoughtlessly thrash in place.\n"
msgstr "特洛戈 的怒火炽烈无比。冒犯者会被狂暴的生物围攻，从成群的熊，到对付最强者的巨人与巨魔大军。此外，激怒祂的人还会定期失去力量和自制力，在原地无意识地胡乱挣扎。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:uskayaw wrath"
msgid ""
"Uskayaw's wrath turns the powers of the dance against the offender. The prude\n"
"will find their foes going berserk and will be forced to helplessly watch as\n"
"foes execute their own solos. When the dance is getting too slow, Uskayaw will\n"
"cause noise to attract more revellers.\n"
msgstr "阿斯卡亚 的神罚会让舞蹈之力反过来对付冒犯者。这些扫兴之人会看到敌人陷入狂暴，并被迫无助地旁观敌人的独舞。若舞蹈的节奏太慢，祂就会制造噪音，招来更多狂欢者。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:vehumet wrath"
msgid ""
"Those that anger Vehumet find destruction amply heaped upon them. Novices are\n"
"struck by flame and frost; archmages by crystal spears and firestorms. Their\n"
"own conjurations, too, are wont to misfire at the worst possible moments.\n"
msgstr "激怒 维胡梅特 的人，会遭受无尽的毁灭。新手迎来火焰与冰霜，大法师迎来水晶矛和火焰风暴。他们自己的塑能法术，也容易在最糟糕的时刻出错。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:wu jian wrath"
msgid ""
"Those who turn against the Council must be prepared to endure death by a\n"
"thousand cuts. No hiding place is secure, no disguise perfect enough to avoid\n"
"the sudden spring of traps, the flying daggers and the armies of animated\n"
"weapons that will ambush the betrayer.\n"
msgstr "背叛 武剑会 的人，必须准备承受千刀万剐。没有藏身之处足够安全，也没有伪装足够完美，能够躲过突然发动的陷阱、飞来的匕首，以及伏击叛徒的活化武器大军。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:xom wrath"
msgid ""
"Unfaithful ex-followers will find themselves suffering through Xom's bad moods\n"
"for so long as Xom can be bothered to remember about them. Still, Xom's caprice\n"
"remains; the unfaithful are rewarded just as the faithful are punished.\n"
msgstr "只要 佐姆 还愿意记得他们，背信的昔日信徒就得忍受祂的坏心情。不过，祂依旧反复无常；如同忠诚信徒会受罚一样，背信者也会得到赏赐。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:yredelemnul wrath"
msgid ""
"Those who anger Yredelemnul find themselves beset by legions of the dead.\n"
"Sometimes, the god will also intervene directly, binding the unfaithful in\n"
"inescapable chains as Yredelemnul's dark army demonstrates the price of\n"
"betrayal.\n"
msgstr "激怒 伊莱德莱姆努尔 的人，会遭到亡者军团围攻。有时，祂还会亲自干预，用无法逃脱的锁链束缚背信者，让黑暗大军向其展示背叛的代价。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:zin wrath"
msgid ""
"Those under Zin's wrath will find their beneficial mutations stripped away,\n"
"their enemies alerted, and their senses confounded by the axioms of Law;\n"
"confusion, fainting, blindness and complete paralysis will be their lot.\n"
msgstr "遭受 辛 神罚的人，会被剥除有益变异，敌人会被惊动，感官也会在法则公理之下陷入混乱。混乱、昏厥、失明乃至完全麻痹，都会成为他们的命运。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:wu jian extra"
msgid ""
":nowrap\n"
"  .......       .......  (.) <lightred>Lunge</lightred>: Move directly towards an enemy to deal\n"
"  ..<lightred>@</lightred>.O..  -->  ...<lightred>@</lightred>O..  extra damage.\n"
"  .......       .......\n"
"\n"
"  .......       ...<lightred>@</lightred>...  (*) <lightred>Whirlwind</lightred>: Move between two tiles adjacent to\n"
"  ...<lightred>@</lightred>O..  -->  ....O..  an enemy to strike them lightly. Multiple adjacent\n"
"  .......       .......  foes can be attacked simultaneously this way.\n"
"\n"
"  ..#....       ..#....  (**) <lightred>Wall Jump</lightred>: Vault off a nearby wall and strike\n"
"  ..#<lightred>@</lightred>O..  -->  ..#.O<lightred>@</lightred>.  enemies adjacent to the landing spot. Vaulting takes\n"
"  ..#....       ..#....  two turns. Activated via the (a)bility menu.\n"
"\n"
"These prevent enemies from getting free attacks on you while you move away.\n"
msgstr ""
":nowrap\n"
"  .......       .......  (.) <lightred>突刺</lightred>：直接朝敌人移动，造成\n"
"  ..<lightred>@</lightred>.O..  -->  ...<lightred>@</lightred>O..  额外伤害。\n"
"  .......       .......\n"
"\n"
"  .......       ...<lightred>@</lightred>...  (*) <lightred>旋风</lightred>：在与敌人相邻的两格之间移动，\n"
"  ...<lightred>@</lightred>O..  -->  ....O..  对其发动轻击。以这种方式可以同时攻击\n"
"  .......       .......  多个相邻敌人。\n"
"\n"
"  ..#....       ..#....  (**) <lightred>蹬墙跳</lightred>：借助附近墙壁跃起，攻击\n"
"  ..#<lightred>@</lightred>O..  -->  ..#.O<lightred>@</lightred>.  落点相邻的敌人。跳跃耗时\n"
"  ..#....       ..#....  两回合。通过能力菜单（a）发动。\n"
"\n"
"这些武技可防止敌人在你移开时获得免费攻击。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:acid dragon scales"
msgid ""
"The scales of an acid dragon. Although it does not provide its wearer with as\n"
"much protection as the armour made from the scales of some larger dragons, it is\n"
"somewhat lighter and less encumbering. It is also remarkably smooth, letting\n"
"corrosive slime flow off it like water.\n"
msgstr "酸龙的鳞片。它的防护不如某些大型龙类的鳞甲，但稍轻，累赘也较少。表面还异常光滑，腐蚀性黏液会像水一样滑落。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:bardiche"
msgid "A long pole with an enormous, cleaving blade on one end.\n"
msgstr "一根长杆，一端装着巨大的劈砍刀刃。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:barding"
msgid "Armour for the scaly midsections of nagas and armataurs.\n"
msgstr "保护娜迦与犰狳人鳞片覆盖的躯干中段的防具。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:battleaxe"
msgid "A large war axe with a formidable double-sided head.\n"
msgstr "一柄大型战斧，装着令人生畏的双面斧头。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:blade talisman"
msgid ""
"A jagged cluster of blades, almost impossible to grasp without injury. Causes\n"
"long, needle-thin blades to grow from the wearer's body, allowing them to\n"
"perform rapid auxiliary melee attacks and even parry blows. Having so many\n"
"fragments of metal inside one's body reduces the effectiveness of body armour,\n"
"but Shapeshifting skill mitigates this effect as well as increases the damage\n"
"dealt.\n"
msgstr "一簇参差的刀刃，几乎不可能在握持时不受伤。它会使佩戴者体内长出细长如针的刀刃，能够迅速发动额外近战攻击，甚至招架打击。体内如此多的金属碎片会削弱躯干防具的效果；变形术技能可以减轻这一影响，并提高造成的伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:broad axe"
msgid "An axe with langets, spikes, a lengthed haft and a single-bladed crescent head.\n"
msgstr "一柄带有护条、尖刺、加长斧柄及单面新月形斧头的斧子。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:crystal plate armour"
msgid "An incredibly heavy but extremely effective suit of crystalline armour.\n"
msgstr "一套由晶体构成的板甲，极其沉重，却有极佳的防护。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:demon trident"
msgid "A terrible three-pronged weapon, moulded by fire and brimstone.\n"
msgstr "一柄可怕的三叉武器，由烈火与硫磺铸成。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:double sword"
msgid "A fearsome weapon with a forked, razor-sharp blade.\n"
msgstr "一把令人生畏的剑，分叉的剑刃锋利如剃刀。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:eveningstar"
msgid ""
"The opposite of a morningstar. A balanced mace with a long shaft and a metal\n"
"head covered in lethal spikes.\n"
msgstr "与晨星锤相对的武器。一柄平衡良好的钉头锤，长柄顶端的金属锤头布满致命尖刺。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:fire dragon scales"
msgid ""
"The scales of a fire-breathing dragon. It provides great protection from fire,\n"
"while rendering its wearer more susceptible to cold.\n"
msgstr "喷火龙的鳞片。它能极大地抵御火焰，却使佩戴者更容易受到寒冷伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:fortress talisman"
msgid ""
"A miniature battlement, carved from a piece of shell. Transforms the wearer into\n"
"a heavily armoured crab, fusing whatever body armour they are wearing into the\n"
"shell in the process. In this form, they are slow-moving, but well-defended and\n"
"even capable of wielding a weapon in their large main claw. Despite all this\n"
"bulk, they are well-adapted to the water. They can also breathe clouds of rust\n"
"at the cost of their own HP, which corrode and weaken enemies.\n"
msgstr "一座用贝壳雕成的微型城垛。它会把佩戴者变成重甲螃蟹，并将所穿的躯干防具融入甲壳。此形态移动缓慢，但防护坚实，甚至能用巨大的主螯持用武器。尽管如此笨重，它仍很适应水中环境。它还可以消耗自身生命，吐出能腐蚀并削弱敌人的锈蚀云雾。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:golden dragon scales"
msgid ""
"The scales of a golden dragon. It is much heavier than most dragon scale\n"
"armours, and grants its wearer resistance to poison, fire and cold.\n"
msgstr "金龙的鳞片。它比大多数龙鳞甲沉重得多，并赋予佩戴者毒素、火焰及寒冷抗性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:granite talisman"
msgid ""
"A heavy stone icon, bearing the countenance of some long-forgotten king or god.\n"
"Transforms the wearer into a slow, stone statue. The wearer's stone body is\n"
"immune to poison and miasma, and gains resistance to electricity, negative\n"
"energy, and torment. Shapeshifting skill increases armour granted.\n"
msgstr "一尊沉重的石像，面容属于某位早已被遗忘的君王或神祇。它会把佩戴者变成缓慢的石像。石质身体免疫毒素与瘴气，并抵御电击、负能量及折磨。变形术技能会提高获得的护甲值。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:hive talisman"
msgid ""
"A preserved and decorated hive, still dripping with ambrosial nectar. Transforms\n"
"the wearer into a living beehive, filled with the buzz of countless insects\n"
"labouring inside them. The nectar produced within greatly increases the wearer's\n"
"health and magic regeneration and if they become seriously injured, angry bees\n"
"will swarm out to defend their hive.\n"
msgstr "一个经过保存与装饰的蜂巢，仍滴着甘美的花蜜。它会把佩戴者变成活蜂巢，体内满是无数劳作昆虫的嗡鸣。内部产生的花蜜会大幅加快生命与魔力恢复；如果佩戴者伤势严重，愤怒的蜜蜂便会蜂拥而出，保卫蜂巢。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:inkwell talisman"
msgid ""
"A small bottle filled with mystical ink. Transforms the wearer into a walking\n"
"scroll whose body is tattooed with the knowledge of a hundred mages. Being an\n"
"omnibus of magical techniques gives them increased skill with all spell schools,\n"
"which improves with Shapeshifting skill, but the form's ability to channel such\n"
"magic is limited, and it cannot cast spells above level 4.\n"
"\n"
"Its attacks are also very weak, but have a chance of restoring 1 MP when they\n"
"hit.\n"
msgstr ""
"一小瓶神秘墨水。它会把佩戴者变成行走的卷轴，身上纹着百名法师的知识。身为魔法技艺的汇编，佩戴者所有魔法学派的技能都会提高，提升幅度随变形术技能增长。但此形态引导魔法的能力有限，无法施展高于 4 级的法术。\n"
"\n"
"它的攻击也十分微弱，不过命中时有一定概率恢复 1 点魔力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:lupine talisman"
msgid ""
"A painted eyepatch made from a scrap of wolf pelt. Transforms the wearer into a\n"
"vicious werewolf, muscles surging with predatory instinct. Killing enemies with\n"
"melee attacks in this form will give a stacking bonus to your damage and\n"
"accuracy, and slaying enough of them in a row will cause you to unleash a\n"
"vicious howl that makes any still alive cower in fear - and leaves them\n"
"susceptible to a devastating leaping takedown.\n"
msgstr "一块狼皮做成的彩绘眼罩。它会把佩戴者变成凶猛的狼人，肌肉充满捕猎本能。此形态下以近战击杀敌人，会获得可叠加的伤害与命中加成。连续杀死足够多的敌人后，会发出凶狠的嚎叫，使幸存者畏缩，并容易遭受毁灭性的跳跃扑杀。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:maw talisman"
msgid ""
"A miniature, desiccated head of some ferocious and hopefully extinct creature.\n"
"Transforms the wearer's midsection into a giant mouth, gnashing and ready to devour\n"
"foes. This maw confers a powerful bite attack which scales additionally with the\n"
"wearer's own strength and can devour slain creatures to temporariy increase\n"
"one's regeneration. Unfortunately, it also confers such profound hunger that it\n"
"can be difficult to pull oneself away from particularly appetising foes.\n"
msgstr "一颗微小而干瘪的头颅，来自某种凶猛的生物——希望它早已灭绝。它会把佩戴者的躯干中段变成巨口，咬牙切齿，准备吞食敌人。这张巨口赋予强大的啮咬攻击，其威力还随佩戴者自身力量提高，并能吞食被杀死的生物，暂时提高恢复速度。不幸的是，它也带来极度的饥饿，让佩戴者难以从格外诱人的敌人身边抽身。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:medusa talisman"
msgid ""
"A fossilised jellyfish polyp, inscribed with sigils. Causes a mane of long\n"
"stinging tendrils to sprout from the wearer's head which lash out at nearby\n"
"enemies whenever the wearer attacks, poisoning them. When they feel their host's\n"
"life is in danger, they can even turn these poisoned foes to stone.\n"
msgstr "一块刻有符印的水母水螅体化石。它会使佩戴者头上长出一丛细长的刺丝触须，在佩戴者攻击时抽打附近敌人，使其中毒。当触须感到宿主生命受到威胁时，甚至能把这些中毒的敌人变成石头。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:morningstar"
msgid "A mace with a head covered in short spikes.\n"
msgstr "一柄锤头覆满短刺的钉头锤。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:protean talisman"
msgid ""
"An ever-changing fragment of something primordial; its substance seems to\n"
"undulate between flesh and bone and perhaps even metal. A sufficiently skilled\n"
"shapeshifter can stabilise it into a useable - if unpredictable - form.\n"
"\n"
"(If your Shapeshifting skill is at least 6, attempting to put this on will\n"
"transform it into a random one of: Rimehorn, Scarab, Medusa, or Spore talismans.)\n"
msgstr ""
"一块不断变化的原始物质碎片，似乎在血肉、骨骼，甚至金属之间波动。技艺足够熟练的变形者，能够将它稳定为可用的形态，尽管结果不可预测。\n"
"\n"
"（如果你的变形术技能至少为 6，尝试佩戴它时，它就会随机变成霜角护符、圣甲虫护符、美杜莎护符或孢子护符中的一种。）\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:quicksilver dragon scales"
msgid ""
"The scales of a quicksilver dragon. Although it does not provide its wearer\n"
"with as much protection as the scales of some heavier dragons, it is somewhat\n"
"lighter and less encumbering. The armour repels both attacks on the wearer's\n"
"willpower and magical modification of itself - it cannot be enchanted.\n"
msgstr "水银龙的鳞片。它的防护不如某些更沉重的龙鳞，但稍轻，累赘也较少。它既能抵御针对佩戴者意志的攻击，也会排斥对自身的魔法改造，因此无法附魔。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:quill talisman"
msgid ""
"A spiny trinket reminiscent of a cactus. Causes sharp quills to grow all over\n"
"the wearer's body which may cause injury to anyone unwise enough to attack them\n"
"in melee.\n"
msgstr "一件长满尖刺、形似仙人掌的饰物。它会使佩戴者全身长出锋利的棘刺，任何鲁莽地近战攻击佩戴者的人，都可能因此受伤。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:rapier"
msgid "A slender, sharply pointed sword, with an uncommonly elegant design.\n"
msgstr "一把修长而尖锐的剑，设计格外优雅。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:sacred scourge"
msgid ""
"A blessed weapon, woven by the saints in Heaven and hated by the unholy. It is\n"
"a favoured weapon of the Shining One's servants.\n"
msgstr "一件由天界圣者编织、为邪恶生物所憎恨的祝福武器。它深受 光明神 的仆从喜爱。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:sanguine talisman"
msgid ""
"A vial of roiling blood that pulses with the beat of an unseen heart. Transforms\n"
"the wearer into a fearsome vampire - a creature that straddles the border between\n"
"life and undeath. They can drink the lifeblood of the living to heal themselves,\n"
"and even turn those they slay stealthily into vampiric thralls, but do not heal\n"
"in the presence of monsters. At great effort, they may scatter into a swarm of\n"
"bats - either to flee or to assail their enemies.\n"
msgstr "一瓶翻滚的鲜血，随一颗看不见的心脏搏动。它会把佩戴者变成可怕的吸血鬼，一种游走于生命与亡灵边界的生物。他们可以饮用活物的鲜血治疗自己，甚至能把悄然杀死的生物变成吸血奴仆，但有怪物在场时无法自然恢复生命。付出巨大努力后，他们还能散成一群蝙蝠，用于逃离或袭击敌人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scarab talisman"
msgid ""
"A small golden cameo of a beetle. Transforms the wearer into a sun scarab, a\n"
"fiery insect that carries around a mote of searing heat and light outside\n"
"itself, like a tiny sun.\n"
"\n"
"This solar ember burns adjacent enemies whenever the scarab attacks, and can be\n"
"healed by swapping with it. In addition, the scarab's own mandibles can reduce\n"
"enemies' fire resistance and Fire spells are easier for the wearer to cast.\n"
msgstr ""
"一枚甲虫形状的小巧金色浮雕。它会把佩戴者变成太阳圣甲虫，一种炽热的昆虫，在体外携带一小团灼热而明亮的火种，如同微型太阳。\n"
"\n"
"每当圣甲虫攻击，太阳余烬就会灼烧相邻的敌人，并可通过与圣甲虫交换位置得到治疗。此外，圣甲虫的颚能够降低敌人的火焰抗性，佩戴者也更容易施展火系法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scarf"
msgid ""
"A length of stylish fabric. At its creation, enchantments were woven into it,\n"
"and as such it cannot accept further enchantment.\n"
msgstr "一条时髦的布料。它在制作时就织入了魔法，因此无法接受进一步附魔。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:serpent talisman"
msgid ""
"A jade snake coiled around a fossilised egg. Transforms the wearer into an\n"
"amphisbaena - a legendary two-headed serpent. It is capable of wearing two\n"
"pieces of headgear at once and its powerful coils can wind around foes and crush\n"
"them to death, but its cold blood leaves it succeptible to being slowed by cold\n"
"attacks.\n"
msgstr "一条盘绕在化石蛋上的玉蛇。它会把佩戴者变成传说中的双头蛇，能够同时佩戴两件头部装备，并以强大的身体缠住敌人，将其绞死。但冷血的身体容易被寒冷攻击减速。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:spider talisman"
msgid ""
"A strange charm made from shed arachnid exoskeletons bound together with silk.\n"
"Transforms the wearer into an agile jumping spider who can move swiftly towards\n"
"foes and inflict grievous damage on any it catches unaware. It cannot be\n"
"ensnared by webs, but its attacks can ensnare its enemies in them. It can also\n"
"leap briskly away from many dangers.\n"
msgstr "一件奇异的饰物，由蛛丝捆扎蜕下的蜘蛛外骨骼制成。它会把佩戴者变成敏捷的跳蛛，能迅速接近敌人，对毫无防备的目标造成重伤。它不会被蛛网困住，但攻击可以用蛛网缠住敌人。它也能敏捷地跳离许多危险。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:spore talisman"
msgid ""
"A small charm made from a still-living mushroom. Transforms one of the wearer's\n"
"arms and parts of their lower body into a vibrant mass of multicoloured fungus.\n"
"Melee attacks in this form may release spores that weaken their target, as well\n"
"as cause mushrooms to sprout on the ground behind them which will release their\n"
"own bursts of dazing spores if allowed to grow. Shapeshifting skill increases\n"
"the durability of these mushrooms as well as their damage.\n"
msgstr "一件由仍然活着的蘑菇制成的小护符。它会把佩戴者的一条手臂与部分下半身变成色彩斑斓、充满活力的真菌团。此形态的近战攻击可能释放孢子，使目标虚弱，并在目标身后长出蘑菇；如果任其长大，它们还会释放令人晕眩的孢子。变形术技能会提高这些蘑菇的耐久与伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:shadow dragon scales"
msgid ""
"The scales of a great umbral dragon. It is heavier than most dragon scale\n"
"armours, but its encumbrance does not penalise the wearer's stealth. It also\n"
"grants additional stealth to the wearer.\n"
msgstr "巨大影龙的鳞片。它比大多数龙鳞甲沉重，但其累赘不会降低佩戴者的潜行能力。它还会额外提高潜行。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:storm talisman"
msgid ""
"Lightning trapped, impossibly, in a bottle. Lets the wearer walk through the air\n"
"as a raging, lightning-filled tempest. The wearer's melee attacks are electrified\n"
"and strike all adjacent foes. The wearer also flies, gains immunity to poison,\n"
"miasma, petrification, constriction, and sticky flame, and also resists\n"
"electricity. They can launch themselves as a lightning bolt, blasting through\n"
"everything in their way.\n"
msgstr "一瓶以不可思议的方式封住的闪电。它让佩戴者化为充满雷电的狂暴风暴，在空中行走。佩戴者的近战攻击带有电力，并打击所有相邻敌人。佩戴者还能飞行，免疫毒素、瘴气、石化、缠绕和黏附火焰，并抵御电击。他们可以化作一道闪电飞出，轰穿沿途的一切。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:talisman of death"
msgid ""
"A grey-black vessel, infused with dark power through a sickening ritual.\n"
"Transforms the wearer into an undying offence against life itself.\n"
"\n"
"Foes struck by wearer's melee weapons or hands are weakened, slowed, and drained.\n"
"The wearer can also heal themself by tormenting living foes nearby; Shapeshifting\n"
"skill increases the amount healed. Further, the wearer resists cold, has enhanced\n"
"willpower, and is immune to poison, miasma, negative energy, and torment.\n"
"\n"
"The wearer also gains some of the more dubious benefits of having an undead body.\n"
"They are vulnerable to holy damage and Dispel Undead, and cannot consume potions.\n"
msgstr ""
"一个灰黑色的容器，经由令人作呕的仪式注入黑暗力量。它会把佩戴者变成不死的存在，亵渎生命本身。\n"
"\n"
"被佩戴者近战武器或双手击中的敌人，会遭到虚弱、减速与吸能。佩戴者还能折磨附近活物来治疗自己，变形术技能会提高治疗量。此外，佩戴者抵御寒冷，意志增强，并免疫毒素、瘴气、负能量与折磨。\n"
"\n"
"亡灵躯体还带来一些好坏难言的特性：佩戴者容易受到神圣伤害与驱散亡灵法术伤害，并且无法饮用药水。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:war axe"
msgid "A military axe with a long haft and a single-bladed head.\n"
msgstr "一柄军用斧，具有长柄与单面斧头。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wellspring talisman"
msgid ""
"A small amphora from which pours a seemingly unending quantity of water.\n"
"Transforms the wearer's flesh into elemental water, allowing them to move flexibly\n"
"and reach to attack from a great distance. From time to time, they can even\n"
"cause the water around them to rise up and drown their enemies.\n"
"\n"
"The malleability of this water even allows them to retain the benefits of their\n"
"physical mutations, but cold attacks can freeze it solid and fire may cause it\n"
"to erupt with steam.\n"
msgstr ""
"一只小双耳瓶，似乎有无穷无尽的水从中流出。它会把佩戴者的血肉变成元素之水，使其灵活移动，并能伸展身体，从很远的地方发动攻击。有时，他们甚至能让周围的水升起，淹没敌人。\n"
"\n"
"水的可塑性还让他们保留身体变异带来的益处，但寒冷攻击会使其冻结，火焰则可能引发蒸汽喷发。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ashenzari"
msgid ""
"While it seems inconceivable that the divine could be shackled, Ashenzari is\n"
"just that: bound to the sky for eternity, the unbudging god is all-knowing,\n"
"all-seeing. Devoted worshippers are allowed to grasp shreds of this knowledge\n"
"and foresight, but be warned: to Ashenzari, power and blessing and curse are\n"
"all the same thing.\n"
msgstr "神明竟也会身陷枷锁，实在令人难以想象，但 艾申扎利 正是如此：这位永远被束缚在天空、无法移动的神祇，无所不知，无所不见。虔诚的信徒得以领略这份知识与先见的片段。但请记住：在 艾申扎利 看来，力量、祝福与诅咒本就是同一回事。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:beogh"
msgid ""
"A god of outcasts, pariahs, and the dispossessed, Beogh's altars are rarely\n"
"found among those of other faiths, but Beogh's missionaries may always be sought\n"
"by those looking for a place to belong. Worshippers will find many friends\n"
"within the dungeon, and those who prove their strength to Beogh may gain\n"
"lifelong companions the equal of any adventurer. To worship Beogh is to believe\n"
"there is strength that transcends species and bloodline. To worship Beogh is to\n"
"be an orc.\n"
msgstr "比欧弗 是流亡者、受排斥者与失去一切之人的神。祂的祭坛很少与其他信仰的祭坛同处一地，但渴望归属的人总能去寻找祂的传教士。信徒会在地下城里找到许多朋友，而向 比欧弗 证明实力的人，更可能获得足以媲美任何冒险者的终身伙伴。信奉 比欧弗，就是相信力量可以超越种族与血脉；信奉 比欧弗，就是成为兽人。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:cheibriados"
msgid ""
"Cheibriados is a god of deliberation. Those following Cheibriados travel more\n"
"slowly the further they progress in their faith, and are forbidden from using\n"
"any means to hasten themselves. In the process of so imitating their god, they\n"
"attain perfection of mind and body, and the mysteries of time unfold before\n"
"them. Especially devout followers may even momentarily abandon the flow of\n"
"time and its needless disturbances.\n"
msgstr "切布理亚多 是审慎之神。信徒的信仰越深，行进就越缓慢，并且不得以任何手段使自己加速。在效法神祇的过程中，他们的身心趋于完美，时间的奥秘也向他们展开。尤其虔诚的信徒甚至能暂时脱离时间之流，远离其中无谓的纷扰。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:dithmenos"
msgid ""
"Dithmenos is the god of night and of things half-seen in flickering torchlight.\n"
"Worshipped by actors as often as thieves, followers of Dithmenos can learn to\n"
"control their own shadow as if it were an extension of their body - misdirecting\n"
"onlookers and acting upon the world with force as tangible as anything that has\n"
"ever been imagined lurking in the dark.\n"
msgstr "迪斯姆诺 是黑夜之神，也掌管摇曳火光中若隐若现的事物。演员与盗贼同样崇拜祂。信徒可以学会把自己的影子当作身体的延伸来操控，迷惑旁观者，并以切实的力量影响世界——如同人们想象中潜伏在黑暗里的任何东西一样真实。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:elyvilon"
msgid ""
"Elyvilon the Healer welcomes all kind souls prepared to help others. Those\n"
"individuals can expect to gain powerful healing abilities, by which they can\n"
"avoid bloodshed. Elyvilon appreciates exploration of the dungeon. Elyvilon's\n"
"followers can convert to the Shining One or Zin while keeping some piety.\n"
msgstr "治疗者 艾利维隆 欢迎所有愿意帮助他人的善良灵魂。这些人可以获得强大的治疗能力，借此避免流血。艾利维隆 赞赏对地下城的探索。祂的信徒改信 光明神 或 辛 时，可以保留一部分虔诚。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:fedhas"
msgid ""
"Fedhas is the god of plant and fungal life. Followers are prevented from\n"
"harming any species under Fedhas' protection. In return, Fedhas grants a number\n"
"of abilities that promote the growth of plants and fungi. These abilities may\n"
"incidentally prove useful to adventurers.\n"
msgstr "费德哈 是植物与真菌生命之神。信徒不得伤害任何受祂保护的物种。作为回报，费德哈 赐予多种促进植物与真菌生长的能力。这些能力也可能顺便给冒险者带来帮助。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:gozag"
msgid ""
"Gozag Ym Sagoz the Greedy teaches that the world belongs to the rich. Those\n"
"accepting this principle may exchange their gold for divine assistance.\n"
"Followers of Gozag do not earn piety; the only way to impress this god is by\n"
"amassing a fortune, and worshippers may request as much assistance as they can\n"
"afford. Fortunately, Gozag's worshippers are said to have the touch of gold.\n"
msgstr "贪婪的 哥萨戈 Ym Sagoz 教导世人：世界属于富人。接受这一原则的人，可以用黄金换取神助。哥萨戈 的信徒不积累虔诚；唯有积聚财富才能打动这位神祇，只要付得起钱，信徒就能不断请求帮助。幸运的是，据说 哥萨戈 的信徒拥有点石成金的本领。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:hepliaklqana"
msgid ""
"Hepliaklqana the Forgotten accepts the worship of those who would remember\n"
"their forebears, and fight alongside the greatest of them all. Acolytes of\n"
"Hepliaklqana sacrifice a small part of their life essence to manifest their\n"
"ancestor into the world; as they explore and form new experiences, they will\n"
"find themselves able to shape and control their ancestor's memory, eventually\n"
"bringing them into the ranks of the mythical heroes.\n"
msgstr "被遗忘者 惠普利亚卡纳 接受那些愿意铭记先祖、并与其中最伟大的一位并肩作战的人所献上的信仰。信徒牺牲少量生命精华，使先祖显现于世。随着探索与阅历的增长，他们将逐渐能够塑造和掌控对先祖的记忆，最终使其跻身神话英雄之列。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ignis"
msgid ""
"Ignis the Dying Flame offers followers power over fire in many forms. All of\n"
"Ignis' power is offered unconditionally to any who would deign to worship, but\n"
"once used, it can never be replenished. Ignis' other worshippers deserted long\n"
"ago; the divine fire burns low, and soon it will go out.\n"
msgstr "垂灭之焰 伊格尼斯 给予信徒多种操纵火焰的力量。只要有人愿意信奉，伊格尼斯 便无条件献出全部神力，但这些力量一旦用去，便永远无法补充。其他信徒早已离去，神圣的火焰日渐衰弱，不久就将熄灭。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:jiyva"
msgid ""
"Jiyva is the ancient deity of the slimes. Followers are expected to\n"
"support the spread and satiation of their fellow slimes by allowing them to\n"
"consume items, and are prevented from harming any slimes. Especially favoured\n"
"followers will become as shapeless as their god, mutating wildly.\n"
msgstr "吉瓦 是软泥怪的古老神祇。信徒应当允许同类软泥怪吞食物品，帮助它们扩散并填饱肚子，而且不得伤害任何软泥怪。尤其受宠的信徒会像神祇一样形体无定，发生剧烈的变异。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:kikubaaqudgha"
msgid ""
"Kikubaaqudgha is a terrible Demon-God, served by those who wish to indulge in\n"
"the powers of death. An evil god, Kikubaaqudgha requires worshippers to cause\n"
"the death and destruction of as many creatures as possible. In exchange,\n"
"Kikubaaqudgha offers great assistance to the aspiring necromancer: a supply of\n"
"useful bodies, knowledge of dark magic, and protection against necromantic\n"
"backlash.\n"
msgstr "奇库巴库哈 是可怕的魔神，渴望沉迷于死亡力量的人为祂效力。作为邪神，祂要求信徒尽可能多地杀戮和毁灭生灵。作为交换，祂为有志于死灵术的人提供极大的帮助：有用的尸体、黑暗魔法知识，以及抵御死灵术反噬的庇护。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:lugonu"
msgid ""
"Banished to the chaotic realm of the Abyss, Lugonu the Unformed seeks followers\n"
"to spread bloodshed and corruption in the overworld. Those who gain Lugonu's\n"
"favour will be granted some of the power of the Abyss itself, allowing them to\n"
"call forth eldritch horrors, and even to travel between the overworld and the\n"
"Abyss at will.\n"
msgstr "无形者 卢戈努 被放逐到混乱的深渊，祂寻找信徒，在现世传播流血与腐化。获得祂青睐的人会得到深渊本身的一部分力量，能够唤出诡异的恐怖存在，甚至随意往返于现世与深渊。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:makhleb"
msgid ""
"Makhleb the Destroyer is a fearsome deity of bloodshed and mortification of the\n"
"flesh. Followers are expected to cleanse others by inflicting suffering and\n"
"death on them in Makhleb's name. Dedicated followers may also access the raw\n"
"energies and hell-spawned servants of chaos, so that they may better break the\n"
"impure world and its false laws for their evil god's glory.\n"
msgstr "毁灭者 马科列布 是掌管流血与肉体苦修的可怖神祇。祂要求信徒以祂之名，给他人带来苦难和死亡，以此净化他们。忠诚的信徒还可以运用混沌的原始能量与地狱仆从，为邪神的荣耀，更有效地粉碎这个不洁的世界及其虚伪法则。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:nemelex xobeh"
msgid ""
"Nemelex is a strange and unpredictable chaotic trickster god, whose powers are\n"
"invoked through magical packs of cards painted in the ichor of demons. Followers\n"
"will be granted decks of cards as they traverse the dungeon, and are encouraged\n"
"to trust in the cards to provide them with divine assistance. However, the\n"
"Trickster can also ensure that fortune favours the bold.\n"
msgstr "尼姆雷斯・索布 是古怪而难以预测的混沌诡术之神，祂的力量通过以恶魔灵液绘制的魔法牌组施展。信徒探索地下城时会获得牌组，并被鼓励信赖卡牌带来的神助。不过，这位诡术之神也能让命运眷顾勇者。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:okawaru"
msgid ""
"Okawaru is a dangerous and powerful god of battle. Followers are expected to\n"
"constantly prove themselves in combat, and may channel Okawaru's might to\n"
"enhance their prowess. Okawaru demands that followers prove themselves by their\n"
"own strength alone, and so worshippers are forbidden from gaining allies by any\n"
"means. Okawaru pays little heed to easy victories, but will reward worshippers\n"
"for heroic feats against mighty foes.\n"
msgstr "奥格瓦如 是危险而强大的战斗之神。祂要求信徒不断在战斗中证明自己，并允许他们借助神力提高战斗本领。祂要求信徒只凭自身力量证明实力，因此禁止他们以任何方式获得盟友。奥格瓦如 不在意轻易取胜，却会奖赏对抗强敌的英勇壮举。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:pakellas"
msgid ""
"Pakellas the Inventive believes in the supremacy of devices, magical or\n"
"otherwise, over spells and other forms of magic. Followers, although cut off\n"
"from ambient magical power, are provided with magical energy to empower their\n"
"devices so long as they use them to assert Pakellas' supremacy. Pakellas will\n"
"grant devout worshippers access to increasingly powerful devices.\n"
msgstr "发明家 帕克拉斯 相信器械无论是否具有魔力，都胜过法术和其他形式的魔法。信徒虽被切断了与周围魔力的联系，但只要用器械彰显祂的至高地位，就能获得为器械赋能的魔法能量。祂会赐予虔诚信徒越来越强大的器械。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:qazlal"
msgid ""
"Qazlal Stormbringer is a violent god of tempests, who delights in unleashing\n"
"the forces of nature against the unsuspecting. Those who invite Qazlal's gaze\n"
"will find themselves the eye in a storm of elemental destruction, from which\n"
"only their God can protect them. Pious worshippers of Qazlal will gain the\n"
"ability to direct and control the destructive might of the storm.\n"
msgstr "风暴使者 卡兹拉尔 是狂暴的风暴之神，乐于向毫无防备者释放自然之力。招来祂注视的人，会置身于元素毁灭风暴的中心，唯有这位神祇能够保护他们。虔诚的信徒将获得指引和控制风暴破坏力的能力。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ru"
msgid ""
"Of all the gods, only Ru opposed creation. Not as folly, but as distraction.\n"
"Initiates of Ru can open channels to the powers underlying the visible world by\n"
"renouncing the fetters that bind them here. These sacrifices are not made to\n"
"Ru, but rather given up freely and permanently. Having made such sacrifices,\n"
"initiates will become able to draw upon this immense power to aid themselves,\n"
"eventually gaining the ability to unleash its destructive might against their\n"
"foes.\n"
msgstr "众神之中，唯有 入 反对创世。祂认为创造并非愚举，却是分心之事。入门者通过舍弃将自己束缚于此世的羁绊，打开通往可见世界之下力量的通道。这些牺牲并非献给 入，而是自愿且永久地放弃。作出牺牲后，入门者便能借助这股浩瀚力量帮助自己，最终向敌人释放其毁灭之威。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:sif muna"
msgid ""
"Sif Muna the Loreminder is a contemplative but powerful deity, served by those\n"
"who seek magical knowledge. Followers who triumph over their foes can call upon\n"
"the Loreminder for magical power and the ability to cast spells beyond their\n"
"magical training. The devout are rewarded with a supply of spellbooks taken\n"
"directly from Sif Muna's legendary library.\n"
msgstr "知识守护者 席夫·穆纳 是沉思而强大的神祇，寻求魔法知识的人为祂效力。战胜敌人的信徒可以请求祂赐予魔法能量，以及施展超出自身魔法修为之法术的能力。虔诚者会获得直接取自祂传奇藏书的法术书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:the shining one"
msgid ""
"Followers of the Shining One are bound to the code of the honourable warrior,\n"
"soldiers in their god's eternal crusade against evil. For forsaking dark magic\n"
"and underhanded tactics, the Shining One rewards them and their allies with the\n"
"power they need to slay demons and the undead. Especially devout warriors can\n"
"even call upon angels in times of need. The Shining One's followers can convert\n"
"to Elyvilon or Zin while keeping some piety.\n"
msgstr "光明神 的信徒恪守荣耀战士的准则，是祂对抗邪恶的永恒圣战中的士兵。作为放弃黑暗魔法与卑劣手段的回报，祂赐予信徒及其盟友斩杀恶魔与亡灵所需的力量。尤其虔诚的战士甚至能在危难时召来天使。信徒改信 艾利维隆 或 辛 时，可以保留一部分虔诚。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:trog"
msgid ""
"Trog is an ancient god of anger and violence. Followers are expected to kill in\n"
"Trog's name, and especially to slay wizards. In return, worshippers of Trog\n"
"gain the ability to go berserk at will in combat, and will be granted\n"
"assistance in the form of powerful weapons and mighty allies. Followers are\n"
"absolutely forbidden the use of spell magic.\n"
msgstr "特洛戈 是古老的愤怒与暴力之神。祂要求信徒以祂之名杀戮，尤其要杀死巫师。作为回报，信徒能够在战斗中随意狂暴，并获得强大武器与强力盟友的援助。信徒绝对不得使用法术魔法。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:uskayaw"
msgid ""
"Uskayaw the Reveller is a god of ecstatic dance. In the dungeon, Uskayaw\n"
"appreciates the passion and rhythm of combat, rewarding followers for each\n"
"strike they deliver and for the damage they deal their foes. The longer the\n"
"dance continues, the greater powers Uskayaw offers. When the dance ends,\n"
"Uskayaw quickly loses interest.\n"
msgstr "狂欢者 阿斯卡亚 是狂喜之舞的神祇。在地下城中，祂欣赏战斗的激情与节奏，奖励信徒的每一次出击及其对敌人造成的伤害。舞蹈持续越久，祂赐予的力量就越强。舞蹈一结束，祂很快便会失去兴趣。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:vehumet"
msgid ""
"Vehumet is a god of the destructive powers of magic. Followers will gain divine\n"
"assistance in commanding the hermetic arts, and the most favoured stand to gain\n"
"access to some of the fearsome spells in Vehumet's library. One's devotion to\n"
"Vehumet can be proven by the causing of as much carnage and destruction as\n"
"possible.\n"
msgstr "维胡梅特 是掌管魔法毁灭之力的神祇。信徒在驾驭奥术时会得到神助，而最受宠者有望学到祂藏书中的一些可怕法术。尽可能多地制造杀戮和毁灭，便能证明对祂的虔诚。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:wu jian"
msgid ""
"The Wu Jian Council is a congregation of martial monks, ascended to divinity\n"
"after battling their way out of the afterlife. Disciples of the Council are\n"
"able to execute acrobatic martial maneuvers, such as wall jumps, spinning\n"
"attacks and punishing lunges. They will eventually become able to request\n"
"help in the form of a storm of heavenly clouds.\n"
msgstr "武剑会由一群武僧组成；他们从死后世界一路奋战而出，最终升格为神。武剑会弟子能够施展灵巧的武技，例如蹬墙跳、旋风攻击和凶狠的突刺。最终，他们还能请求天界云雾风暴的援助。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:xom"
msgid ""
"Xom is a wild and unpredictable god of chaos, who seeks not worshippers but\n"
"playthings with which to toy. Many choose to follow Xom in the hope of\n"
"receiving fabulous rewards and mighty powers, but Xom is nothing if not\n"
"capricious. There is nothing a follower can do to influence Xom's mood.\n"
msgstr "佐姆 是狂野而难以预测的混沌之神，祂寻找的不是信徒，而是可供摆弄的玩物。许多人追随祂，盼望得到惊人的赏赐与强大的力量，但祂最显著的特点就是反复无常。信徒无论做什么，都无法左右祂的心情。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:yredelemnul"
msgid ""
"Cast down by the good gods eons ago, Yredelemnul seeks to despoil their\n"
"creations and chain all living souls within their inexorable grip. Followers who\n"
"would conquer in Yredelemnul's name are granted the power to reap an army of the\n"
"dead and bind powerful souls into eternal service - provided they can sweep\n"
"across the land in a tide as inexorable as their god.\n"
msgstr "远古时被善神打落的 伊莱德莱姆努尔，企图玷污祂们的造物，把所有生灵的魂魄锁在自己不可抗拒的掌握之中。以祂之名征服的信徒，将获得收割亡者大军、束缚强大灵魂为其永远效劳的力量——前提是他们能像神祇一样，以不可阻挡的浪潮席卷大地。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:zin"
msgid ""
"Zin is a god of discipline. Followers must remain pure of body and soul,\n"
"refraining from dark magic and chaotic acts. They must also tithe a fraction of\n"
"all gold gained, preferably followed by donations of more. In exchange,\n"
"worshippers may invoke Zin's wrath upon sinners, and eventually gain various\n"
"divine protections. Zin's followers can convert to Elyvilon or the Shining One\n"
"while keeping some piety.\n"
msgstr "辛 是纪律之神。信徒必须保持身心纯净，远离黑暗魔法与混沌行为。他们还必须将获得的所有黄金按一定比例缴作什一税，最好再多加捐献。作为交换，信徒可以召唤祂的怒火惩戒罪人，并最终获得多种神圣庇护。改信 艾利维隆 或 光明神 时，可以保留一部分虔诚。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ashenzari powers"
msgid ""
"Ashenzari exhorts followers to curse their possessions, periodically offering\n"
"these curses to worshippers as they explore. These curses grant improvements\n"
"to specific skills, but cursed equipment cannot normally be enchanted and can\n"
"only be removed by shattering it forever. As worshippers equip more cursed\n"
"equipment, Ashenzari will grant increasing knowledge of the surrounding dungeon.\n"
"Eventually, Ashenzari will reveal the invisible, grant clarity of mind, and\n"
"protect worshippers from the Dungeon's malevolent forces.\n"
msgstr "艾申扎利 鼓励信徒诅咒自己的财物，并在探索时定期提供这些诅咒。诅咒会提高特定技能，但受诅咒装备通常无法附魔，只有将其永久粉碎才能卸下。穿戴的受诅咒装备越多，祂就会赐予越多关于周围地下城的知识。最终，祂会揭示隐形事物、使信徒保持头脑清醒，并保护信徒免遭地下城中的恶意力量侵害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:beogh powers"
msgid ""
"Worshippers will gain the power to call down Beogh's wrath upon their\n"
"oppressors, and other orcs will start to see them as one of their own.\n"
"Especially promising adherents will find themselves beset by rivals for Beogh's\n"
"favour, but overcoming these trials without fleeing will gain them loyal\n"
"companions whom Beogh will resurrect time and time again, so long as they\n"
"continue to fight and avenge in Beogh's name. A true chosen one may even rally\n"
"an entire orcish army to avenge a wrongful death.\n"
msgstr "信徒将能够召来 比欧弗 的怒火惩罚压迫者，其他兽人也会开始将其视为同类。尤其有潜力的信徒会遭到争夺神宠的对手挑战，但只要不逃避并战胜这些考验，就能获得忠诚伙伴。只要他们继续以 比欧弗 之名战斗与复仇，祂就会一次又一次地复活这些伙伴。真正的神选者甚至可以召集整支兽人大军，为不公的死亡复仇。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:cheibriados powers"
msgid ""
"Followers of Cheibriados move more slowly as they gain favour. As they move\n"
"slower, worshippers of Cheibriados are granted increased attributes.\n"
"Cheibriados rewards the faithful with the power to slow other creatures and the\n"
"power to briefly distort the flow of time. Devout worshippers will gain the\n"
"ability to inflict great harm on all those who move more quickly than they do,\n"
"and finally the ability to step out of the flow of time entirely.\n"
msgstr "信徒获得的神宠越多，移动就越慢；移动越慢，得到的属性提升就越多。切布理亚多 赐予忠诚信徒减慢其他生物、短暂扭曲时间流动的力量。虔诚者能够重创所有比自己移动更快的生物，最终甚至可以完全踏出时间之流。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:dithmenos powers"
msgid ""
"Followers of Dithmenos are surrounded by an unnatural quiet, which helps the\n"
"sounds they make go unnoticed. As they rise in devotion, they will find their\n"
"own shadow begins to imitate some of their actions, attacking when they attack\n"
"and even casting shadowy magics that mimic the form - if not the substance - of\n"
"whichever schools of magic they had been utilising.\n"
"\n"
"More devout worshippers additionally gain the ability to swap places with their\n"
"shadow to mislead enemies, grasp other beings' shadows to unleash their magic on\n"
"the worshipper's behalf, and finally call down a night so dark that it hides all\n"
"denizens of the dungeon from each other.\n"
msgstr "信徒周围笼罩着异样的寂静，使其发出的声音不易引人注意。随着虔诚加深，他们的影子会开始模仿部分行动：在他们攻击时攻击，甚至施展影子魔法，模仿他们所使用魔法学派的形式，尽管其本质并不相同。\n\n更虔诚的信徒还能够与影子交换位置以迷惑敌人，攫住其他生物的影子，使其替自己释放魔法，最终还能召来深沉的黑夜，让地下城中的所有生物彼此无法看见。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:elyvilon powers"
msgid ""
"The Healer offers followers a number of means to heal themselves from damage\n"
"and other ill effects. Followers may also attempt to pacify hostile monsters\n"
"and turn them neutral. Elyvilon may directly intervene to save a follower's\n"
"life, and if there has been no such intervention recently, is sure to prevent\n"
"a killing blow against especially pious followers. Elyvilon may also\n"
"occasionally protect the follower's allies from death.\n"
msgstr "治疗者提供多种手段，让信徒治疗伤害及其他不良效果。信徒也可以尝试安抚敌对怪物，使其变为中立。艾利维隆 可能直接干预，挽救信徒的生命；对于尤其虔诚的信徒，只要近期没有进行过这类干预，祂就一定会阻止致命一击。祂有时也会保护信徒的盟友免于死亡。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:fedhas powers"
msgid ""
"Plants and fungi will not attack Fedhas' worshippers without provocation.\n"
"Worshippers may walk through plants or fungi, and even fire missiles or spells\n"
"through them without causing harm. Fedhas grants powers to temporarily grow a\n"
"menagerie of plant allies whose strength and duration increase with Invocations\n"
"skill. Worshippers may grow a protective wall of briar patches as well as\n"
"ballistomycetes that fire damaging spores whose explosions confuse living\n"
"creatures. Devout followers can overgrow a stretch of solid terrain with a\n"
"cluster of plant allies or even summon a mighty oklob plant.\n"
msgstr "植物与真菌若未受挑衅，便不会攻击信徒。信徒可以穿过它们，也能让投射物与法术穿过它们而不造成伤害。费德哈 赐予暂时培育多种植物盟友的力量，其强度和持续时间随祈祷技能提高。信徒能培育起保护作用的荆棘墙，以及发射伤害性孢子的球菌；孢子爆炸会使活物混乱。虔诚者可以让一片坚实地形长出成簇的植物盟友，甚至召来强大的奥克罗布植物。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:gozag powers"
msgid ""
"For Gozag, both flesh and spirit are inferior to wealth, and therefore all\n"
"monsters are turned to gold upon death. Other monsters may then be briefly\n"
"distracted by imaginings of great wealth. Stalwarts can purchase immediate help\n"
"in the form of potions, and may also pay to attract shopkeepers into the\n"
"dungeon. Particularly well-off adherents may bribe the inhabitants of a branch\n"
"of the dungeon to turn a blind eye to their presence, or even to change their\n"
"allegiance.\n"
msgstr "在 哥萨戈 看来，血肉与灵魂都不及财富，因此所有怪物死亡时都会化为黄金。其他怪物可能因幻想巨额财富而短暂分心。坚定的信徒可以购买药水以获得即时帮助，也可以付费吸引商人进入地下城。尤其富有的信徒能够贿赂某个地下城分支的居民，让他们对自己的存在视而不见，甚至倒戈。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:hepliaklqana powers"
msgid ""
"Hepliaklqana's worshippers are served by a guardian formed from a part of their\n"
"life essence, in the shape of their greatest ancestor. This ancestor is at\n"
"first remembered as they were at the start of their fabled adventures, but will\n"
"advance in skill as their descendant does. Hepliaklqana always allows followers\n"
"to recall their ancestor to their side, and, even if the ancestor is destroyed,\n"
"Hepliaklqana will call it forth again not long after. Further advancement in\n"
"Hepliaklqana's service allows worshippers to restore and strengthen their\n"
"ancestor, to swap them with other creatures, and to choose how to remember\n"
"their life's talents.\n"
msgstr "信徒由一位守护者侍奉，祂以信徒的部分生命精华构成，具有其最伟大先祖的形象。起初，先祖的记忆停留在传奇冒险刚开始时，但其本领会随子孙一同增长。惠普利亚卡纳 始终允许信徒将先祖召回身边；即使先祖被摧毁，祂也会在不久后将其重新召来。进一步效力后，信徒能够恢复并强化先祖、让先祖与其他生物交换位置，并选择如何铭记先祖生前的才能。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ignis powers"
msgid ""
"Followers can armour themselves in flame, call a swarm of foxfires against their\n"
"foes, or let Ignis' heat lift them to another level of the dungeon. However, the\n"
"guttering flames of Ignis' power will only sustain a limited number of\n"
"invocations before only flickering embers remain. No matter how depleted, Ignis\n"
"will always grant followers resistance to fire.\n"
msgstr "信徒可以用火焰护身，召来一群狐火攻击敌人，或借助 伊格尼斯 的热力升到地下城的另一层。但祂日渐衰弱的火焰只能支持有限次数的祈祷，随后便只剩闪烁的余烬。无论力量多么枯竭，祂始终会给予信徒火焰抗性。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:jiyva powers"
msgid ""
"Jiyva will gradually fill the dungeon with jellies. These and any other fellow\n"
"slimes will rapidly consume nearby items, as well as slowly consuming items from\n"
"elsewhere in the dungeon. As they spread slime across more of the dungeon, Jiyva\n"
"will grant followers increasingly rapid health and magic regeneration, and will\n"
"begin mutating them to better reflect Jiyva's image. Followers will later become\n"
"able to call forth acidic ooze from the walls of the dungeon, and to turn\n"
"monsters to slime with a touch.\n"
msgstr "吉瓦 会逐渐让地下城遍布果冻怪。它们和其他同类软泥怪会迅速吞食附近物品，也会缓慢吞食地下城其他地方的物品。软泥遍及的范围越大，祂就赐予信徒越快的生命与魔力恢复，并开始使他们变异，更接近祂的形象。之后，信徒能够从地下城墙壁中唤出酸性黏液，也能以触碰将怪物化为软泥。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:kikubaaqudgha powers"
msgid ""
"Kikubaaqudgha will enhance servants' necromantic prowess with gifts of\n"
"Necromancy spells. Kikubaaqudgha will protect followers from the effects of\n"
"necromantic miscasts and death curses, and may even shield them from unholy\n"
"torment. Followers can unearth dying wretches as necromantic fodder, and may\n"
"invoke the sign of ruin to harm their enemies. Kikubaaqudgha will eventually\n"
"allow followers to either receive knowledge of the most forbidden necromantic\n"
"magic, or to have their weapon imbued with pain.\n"
msgstr "奇库巴库哈 通过赐予死灵系魔法的法术来增强仆从的死灵术本领。祂会保护信徒免受死灵术施法失误与死亡诅咒的影响，甚至可能使其免遭邪恶的折磨。信徒可以掘出濒死的可怜生物，作为死灵术的素材，并召唤毁灭征兆伤害敌人。最终，祂会让信徒在最禁忌的死灵术知识与为武器灌注痛苦之间作出选择。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:lugonu powers"
msgid ""
"Followers of Lugonu gain powers to depart the Abyss at will, to banish monsters\n"
"there, and to flee back inside when needed. Lugonu will also banish nearby foes\n"
"if any other god attempts to interfere with their followers. Later, followers\n"
"will be able to corrupt the ordered world, opening a gate for creatures\n"
"of the Abyss to pass through, and to gate themselves directly into this realm of\n"
"chaos. Lugonu will protect followers who unwield weapons imbued with the\n"
"distorting energies of the Abyss, and eventually will offer to distort a\n"
"follower's melee weapon. Lugonu expects followers to spread unceasing\n"
"chaos in the overworld, and as such does not grant piety to worshippers while\n"
"they remain in the Abyss itself.\n"
msgstr "信徒能够随意离开深渊，将怪物放逐到那里，并在需要时逃回其中。如果其他神祇试图干涉祂的信徒，卢戈努 还会放逐附近的敌人。之后，信徒能够腐化有序的世界，为深渊生物打开通道，并直接进入这片混乱领域。祂会保护卸下扭曲武器的信徒，最终还会提出为信徒的一件近战武器赋予扭曲。祂要求信徒在现世不停传播混乱，因此不会向停留在深渊中的信徒赐予虔诚。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:makhleb powers"
msgid ""
"Makhleb offers followers the ability to unleash bolts of chaotic destruction at\n"
"the cost of their own health as well as call in help from powerful (if sometimes\n"
"uncooperative) demons. The most devoted of worshippers will eventually be gifted\n"
"with knowledge of Infernal Marks, allowing them to ritually brand their own\n"
"bodies in exchange for one of the Destroyer's many hellish powers.\n"
"\n"
"Makhleb's powers all come with a price in blood. However, Makhleb will grant\n"
"followers renewed health in return for killing beings of all kinds.\n"
msgstr ""
"马科列布 允许信徒以自身生命为代价释放混沌毁灭的射线，也能召来强大但有时不肯合作的恶魔。最虔诚的信徒最终会获得地狱印记的知识，以仪式在自己身上烙印，换取毁灭者诸多地狱力量中的一种。\n"
"\n"
"祂的所有力量都要付出鲜血的代价。不过，祂会以恢复生命作为信徒杀死各种生物的回报。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:nemelex xobeh powers"
msgid ""
"The Trickster's followers gain various ways to influence fate when playing\n"
"their cards. The effects of the cards will be more powerful with higher piety\n"
"and with greater Invocations skill. Later, followers will gain powerful\n"
"abilities to manipulate the cards, allowing them to choose one of three drawn\n"
"cards, to gain the effects of multiple cards at once, and finally to stack\n"
"decks and re-order their contents.\n"
msgstr "诡术之神的信徒能够在出牌时以多种方式影响命运。虔诚和祈祷技能越高，卡牌效果就越强。之后，信徒会获得强大的操牌能力：从抽出的三张牌中选择一张，同时获得多张牌的效果，最终还能预排牌组，重新安排其中的顺序。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:okawaru powers"
msgid ""
"Followers of Okawaru will gain the ability to temporarily increase their skills\n"
"in combat, and, much later, to deal much faster blows. Okawaru will eventually\n"
"gift followers with ammunition, weapons and armour. The most favoured of\n"
"Okawaru may challenge their foes to honourable single combat.\n"
msgstr "信徒能够暂时提高战斗技能，在更晚的时候还能大幅加快攻击。奥格瓦如 最终会赐予弹药、武器和防具。最受宠者可以向敌人发起光荣的一对一决斗。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:pakellas powers"
msgid ""
"Followers of Pakellas do not regenerate their magic power naturally, and are\n"
"forbidden from using external means to do so; instead, they are granted\n"
"magical energy on killing beings. They may use increasing amounts of magical\n"
"energy to strengthen their devices, temporarily granting them additional\n"
"power, and can also use their magical energy to recharge their devices.\n"
"Sufficiently devout followers will receive new devices from Pakellas, and may\n"
"eventually petition Pakellas to personally charge one of their devices beyond\n"
"its normal limits.\n"
msgstr "信徒不会自然恢复魔力，也不得借助外部手段恢复；作为替代，他们在杀死生物时会获得魔法能量。他们可以消耗越来越多的魔力，暂时增强器械的力量，也能用魔力为器械充能。足够虔诚的信徒会得到新的器械，并最终能够恳请 帕克拉斯 亲自为一件器械充能，使其超出正常上限。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:qazlal powers"
msgid ""
"Followers of Qazlal are protected from all clouds. As a follower of Qazlal\n"
"gains divine favour, they are slowly surrounded by a loud storm. In addition to\n"
"generating noise, the storm causes elemental clouds to appear near followers,\n"
"blocks attacks, and (for the particularly devout) deflects incoming\n"
"projectiles. Qazlal allows followers to incite nature against their foes,\n"
"causing a localised natural disturbance or, for particularly devout followers,\n"
"a more widespread disaster. Followers of Qazlal eventually gain temporary\n"
"resistances after taking damage, and can give life to clouds, turning them into\n"
"allied elementals.\n"
msgstr "信徒受到保护，不受任何云雾伤害。随着神宠增长，他们周围逐渐形成喧嚣的风暴。风暴除了制造噪音，还会在附近生成元素云雾、格挡攻击，并为尤其虔诚者偏转来袭投射物。卡兹拉尔 允许信徒驱使自然对抗敌人，制造局部的自然扰动，或让尤其虔诚者引发更广泛的灾难。最终，信徒受到伤害后会暂时获得抗性，还能赋予云雾生命，使其成为友方元素生物。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:ru powers"
msgid ""
"Ru will offer followers a number of sacrifices as they travel the dungeon. On\n"
"accepting these sacrifices, followers will gradually gain an aura of immense\n"
"power. This aura will initially cause foes that attempt to harm them to falter\n"
"and become stricken with maladies. After making further sacrifices, followers\n"
"will be able to draw on this power to restore their health and magic, or to\n"
"make a lightning-fast explosive leap. Exceptional sacrificants can unleash\n"
"their power in a massive strike against all their foes. Each of the powers of\n"
"Ru's sacrificants increases in strength with more piety from more sacrifices.\n"
msgstr "信徒探索地下城时，入 会提供多种牺牲选项。接受牺牲后，信徒逐渐获得蕴含巨大力量的光环。起初，光环会使试图伤害他们的敌人畏缩，并遭受不良状态。作出更多牺牲后，信徒便能借助这股力量恢复生命与魔力，或进行迅疾如电的爆炸跳跃。作出非凡牺牲者可以释放力量，对所有敌人发动一次猛烈打击。牺牲带来的虔诚越多，这些能力就越强。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:sif muna powers"
msgid ""
"Sif Muna grants followers the ability to rapidly restore their magical energy,\n"
"and to forget spells at will, so as to learn new ones. Worshippers can call\n"
"upon the Loreminder to help cast any spell they've discovered, even if it's\n"
"well beyond their current magical training. Over time, devout followers will\n"
"receive spellbooks containing a vast range of spells.\n"
msgstr "信徒能够迅速恢复魔法能量，并随意遗忘法术，以学习新的法术。他们可以请求知识守护者帮助施展任何已经发现的法术，即使远远超出当前的魔法修为。随着时间推移，虔诚信徒会获得包含广泛法术的法术书。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:the shining one powers"
msgid ""
"Followers of the Shining One are surrounded by a halo that reveals their\n"
"enemies to them. Followers will gain power by killing evil beings, and with\n"
"growing piety their life force will be protected. The Shining One will keep\n"
"summoned and charmed allies on their side longer, should the allies prove\n"
"worthy of the crusade. Followers will gain use of a divine shield to protect\n"
"them in battle. Later, they can channel blasts of cleansing flame that are\n"
"particularly damaging to unholy beings, and can call upon powerful divine\n"
"beings as temporary allies. Highly pious followers may request the Shining\n"
"One's blessing upon a weapon. The Shining One may occasionally directly\n"
"intervene to save a follower's life.\n"
msgstr "信徒周围环绕着光环，能够显露敌人。他们通过杀死邪恶生物获得力量；随着虔诚提高，其生命能量会受到保护。只要召唤与魅惑的盟友证明自己配得上这场圣战，光明神 就会使其更长时间地留在信徒一方。信徒可以使用神圣护盾保护自己，之后还能引导净化之焰，对邪恶生物造成尤其严重的伤害，并召来强大的神圣生物作为临时盟友。高度虔诚者可以请求祂祝福一件武器。祂有时也会直接干预，挽救信徒的生命。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:trog powers"
msgid ""
"Trog offers various powers to help followers in battle. Followers will gain the\n"
"ability to go berserk at will, and Trog will extend the duration of their\n"
"berserk rage on killing foes. Trog will grant followers the ability to rapidly\n"
"heal their wounds while fortifying their willpower, and later the ability to\n"
"call in powerful raging allies. Eventually, Trog will gift followers with\n"
"weapons, often with antimagic effects.\n"
msgstr "特洛戈 提供多种帮助战斗的力量。信徒能够随意狂暴，杀死敌人时祂会延长狂暴时间。祂还允许信徒迅速疗伤，同时强化意志，之后更能召来强大的狂暴盟友。最终，祂会赐予武器，且常常带有反魔法效果。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:uskayaw powers"
msgid ""
"Worshippers of Uskayaw can stomp to damage foes around them, and rapidly move\n"
"through a line of creatures while confusing them. When a worshipper's dance\n"
"reaches a certain point, Uskayaw will immediately stop all foes so that the\n"
"dancer may take a solo. As the dance continues, Uskayaw will link the emotions\n"
"of foes, forcing them to share their pain. The duration of these effects will\n"
"increase with Invocations skill, and as long as the intensity of the dance is\n"
"sufficient they may be repeated after a short time. If the dance continues\n"
"further, Uskayaw allows worshippers to end it by melding with and then\n"
"violently exploding from a foe, killing it instantly.\n"
msgstr "信徒能够践踏以伤害周围敌人，也能迅速穿过一列生物并使其混乱。舞蹈达到一定程度时，阿斯卡亚 会立刻让所有敌人停下，让舞者独舞。随着舞蹈继续，祂会连接敌人的情绪，迫使他们分担痛苦。这些效果的持续时间随祈祷技能提高；只要舞蹈足够激烈，短暂间隔后就可能再次发生。如果舞蹈进一步持续，祂允许信徒融入一名敌人体内，再猛烈爆发而出，立即将其杀死，作为舞蹈的终结。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:vehumet powers"
msgid ""
"Worshippers of Vehumet will quickly be able to recover their magical energy\n"
"upon killing beings. As they gain favour, they will also gain enhancements to\n"
"their destructive spells — first assistance in casting such spells and then\n"
"increased range for conjurations. Vehumet will offer followers the knowledge of\n"
"increasingly powerful destructive spells as they gain piety.\n"
msgstr "信徒很快就能在杀死生物时恢复魔法能量。随着神宠增长，毁灭性法术也会得到增强：先是更容易施展，随后塑能系法术的射程增加。祂会随虔诚提高，传授越来越强大的毁灭性法术。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:wu jian powers"
msgid ""
"Disciples of the Council learn to perform three martial techniques while moving\n"
"around in combat. They will also be taught to move at unfathomable speeds for\n"
"short distances, and become able to summon a storm of golden clouds to increase\n"
"their precision and damage for as long as they keep using martial attacks.\n"
msgstr "武剑会弟子会学到在战斗移动中施展的三种武技。他们还会学到以难以想象的速度短距离移动，并能够召来金色云雾风暴；只要继续使用武技，风暴就会增强其精准度与伤害。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:xom powers"
msgid ""
"To worship Xom is to live riskily. In a good mood Xom may shower worshippers\n"
"with gifts, while at other times this capricious god could decide to “spice\n"
"things up a little” and send worshippers to their doom. If such toys of Xom\n"
"prove to be interesting, so much the better; if not, well, there'll be other\n"
"playthings...\n"
msgstr "信奉 佐姆，就是与风险为伴。心情好时，祂可能用礼物淹没信徒；其他时候，这位反复无常的神祇可能决定“添点乐子”，把信徒送向毁灭。如果这些玩物的表现足够有趣，那自然再好不过；若非如此，反正总还会有别的玩物……\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:yredelemnul powers"
msgid ""
"Followers of Yredelemnul carry the Black Torch, allowing them to gather souls\n"
"and surround themselves in darkness. They can raise foes who die in the light of\n"
"the torch as mindless servants, hurl torchlight to scour the living and empower\n"
"the dead, and bind especially noteworthy souls to fight for them in death with\n"
"the full capacities they held in life. Especially devout worshippers can even\n"
"call down the inescapable grip of the Fallen directly, binding foes helplessly\n"
"in place as the very life is sucked from them. Yredelemnul will also dispatch\n"
"undead servants to aid followers at the start of each new conquest.\n"
msgstr "信徒携带黑色火炬，借此收集灵魂，并让黑暗环绕自身。他们能够把死于火炬光芒中的敌人唤起为无意识的仆从，投掷炬光以侵蚀活物、强化亡者，并束缚尤其出众的灵魂，使其死后仍能以生前的全部本领作战。尤其虔诚者甚至可以直接召来堕落者不可逃脱的掌握，将敌人束缚在原地，任其生命被吸走。每次开始新的征服时，伊莱德莱姆努尔 也会派遣亡灵仆从帮助信徒。\n"

msgctxt "textdb:descript/gods.txt:zin powers"
msgid ""
"Zin grants followers the ability to preach to the unenlightened masses, and\n"
"powers to vitalise their bodies, protecting them from various afflictions.\n"
"Later, followers gain the ability to imprison their foes temporarily. Followers\n"
"can eventually find temporary safety in a divine refuge. As piety grows,\n"
"followers will be protected from mutation and the Hells, and Zin may even\n"
"occasionally directly intervene to save a follower's life.\n"
msgstr "信徒能够向未开悟的大众布道，并使自身充满活力，抵御各种不良状态。之后，信徒能够暂时囚禁敌人。最终，他们可以在神圣庇护所中获得暂时的安全。随着虔诚提高，信徒将受到保护，抵御变异及地狱的影响；辛 有时甚至会直接干预，挽救信徒的生命。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of chemistry"
msgid ""
"An amulet which allows the wearer to extract small amounts of magical energy\n"
"from any potion they drink and also enhances the power of their alchemy spells.\n"
"The magic restoration effect requires the amulet to attune itself to the\n"
"wearer's body while their reserves of magic are full.\n"
msgstr "一种护身符，能让佩戴者从饮用的任何药水中提取少量魔法能量，还能增强炼金术法术的强度。恢复魔力的效果需要护身符先在佩戴者魔力全满时与其身体完成调谐。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of dissipation"
msgid ""
"An amulet which causes magic contamination and negative status effects upon the\n"
"wearer to expire twice as quickly with time.\n"
msgstr "一种护身符，能使佩戴者身上的魔法污染和负面状态随时间消退的速度加倍。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of faith"
msgid ""
"A charm crafted to call the attention of the gods to its wearer. This divine\n"
"attention makes it easier to please your god, but your god will also take more\n"
"notice of your transgressions. The amulet will drain some of your divine favour\n"
"when removed.\n"
msgstr "一种用来吸引神祇注意佩戴者的饰物。神祇的关注让你更容易取悦祂，但祂也会更留意你的过失。卸下护身符会损失一部分神恩。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of guardian spirit"
msgid ""
"An amulet containing a protective spirit which will cause any damage taken to\n"
"be divided between the wearer's reserves of health and magic.\n"
msgstr "一种容纳着守护精魂的护身符，会使佩戴者受到的所有伤害由生命和魔力储备共同承担。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of magic regeneration"
msgid ""
"An amulet that increases the wearer's rate of magic regeneration. In order to\n"
"function, it must first attune itself to the wearer's body with full reserves\n"
"of magic.\n"
msgstr "一种能加快佩戴者魔力恢复的护身符。要发挥效果，必须先在佩戴者魔力全满时与其身体完成调谐。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of nothing"
msgid "An amulet with no special properties.\n"
msgstr "一种没有特殊属性的护身符。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of reflection"
msgid ""
"An amulet which improves its wearer's ability to shield against attacks. If\n"
"no shield is worn, the force the amulet emits can serve as a weak shield on\n"
"its own. Regardless, any ranged attacks the wearer blocks will be reflected\n"
"back toward the attacker.\n"
msgstr "一种能增强佩戴者格挡能力的护身符。即使没有装备盾牌，它发出的力量本身也能充当一面弱小的盾。无论是否持盾，佩戴者格挡的所有远程攻击都会反射回攻击者。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of regeneration"
msgid ""
"An amulet that increases the wearer's rate of health regeneration. In order to\n"
"function, it must first attune itself to the wearer's body at full health.\n"
msgstr "一种能加快佩戴者生命恢复的护身符。要发挥效果，必须先在佩戴者生命全满时与其身体完成调谐。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of the acrobat"
msgid ""
"An amulet that allows the user to tumble and roll to evade the blows of their\n"
"enemies, but only while moving and waiting. While taking other actions\n"
"(including climbing stairs) the amulet conveys no benefits.\n"
msgstr "一种能让佩戴者翻滚闪躲敌人攻击的护身符，但只在移动和等待时有效。进行其他动作时，包括上下楼梯，护身符都不提供任何益处。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:amulet of wildshape"
msgid "An amulet which improves its wearer's skill with Shapeshifting.\n"
msgstr "一种能提高佩戴者变形术技能的护身符。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of ambrosia"
msgid ""
"A strange substance, produced by ghost moths. Consuming it causes regeneration\n"
"of health and magic, along with total befuddlement. The two effects are\n"
"fundamentally linked – the regeneration ends the moment the confusion does.\n"
msgstr "一种由幽灵蛾产生的奇异物质。饮用后会恢复生命和魔力，同时陷入彻底的混乱。两种效果紧密相连：混乱一结束，再生效果也会立即结束。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of berserk rage"
msgid ""
"A potion which can send one into an incoherent rage, granting them a great but\n"
"temporary increase to their health, damage, and speed. In exchange, their mind\n"
"is clouded by anger, only allowing them to move and attack in melee. The rage\n"
"will wear off quickly if they do not attack monsters, and upon expiry, the\n"
"imbiber will be fatigued, causing them to slow dramatically and rendering them\n"
"unable to berserk again for a short duration.\n"
msgstr "一种能使饮用者陷入失去理智的狂暴的药水，暂时大幅提高生命、伤害和速度。代价是愤怒蒙蔽了心智，只能移动和进行近战攻击。不攻击怪物时，狂暴会迅速消退；结束后饮用者会感到疲惫，速度大幅降低，且短时间内无法再次狂暴。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of blood"
msgid "A potion containing the essence of life.\n"
msgstr "一种含有生命精华的药水。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of brilliance"
msgid ""
"A potion which increases the power of the drinker's spells and halves their\n"
"magic cost (rounding up).\n"
msgstr "一种能提高饮用者法术强度的药水，还能使法术的魔力消耗减半，并向上取整。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of cancellation"
msgid ""
"A potion which ends most magical effects, good or bad, affecting one who drinks\n"
"it. It also reduces magical contamination.\n"
msgstr "一种能终止饮用者身上大多数魔法效果的药水，无论效果好坏。它还会减少魔法污染。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of enlightenment"
msgid ""
"A potion which uplifts both the body and mind of its drinkers, lifting them\n"
"from the ground and increasing their Will to resist the world's temptations.\n"
msgstr "一种能使饮用者身心升华的药水，让其离开地面，并增强抵御世间诱惑的意志。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of experience"
msgid "A truly wonderful and very rare drink, which grants experience when consumed.\n"
msgstr "一种极为珍稀的奇妙饮品，饮用后能获得经验。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of lignification"
msgid ""
"A potion which transforms the imbiber into an animated tree with sap for blood and\n"
"branches capable of holding weapons. Such a tree has minimal evasion but increased\n"
"health and natural armour, and is resistant to poison, and immune to torment and\n"
"drowning. However, it is rooted in place while the transformation lasts, and\n"
"cannot teleport.\n"
msgstr "一种能使饮用者变成活动树木的药水，树液化为血液，枝干可以持用武器。这棵树的闪避极低，但生命和天然护甲值提高，具备毒素抗性，并免疫折磨和溺水。然而，变形持续期间会扎根原地，无法传送。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of moonshine"
msgid ""
"A potent alcohol, distilled in some dubious corner of the dungeon. Drinking it\n"
"reduces the imbiber's accuracy, evasion, and spellcasting success for a while.\n"
msgstr "一种在地下城某个可疑角落蒸馏出的烈酒。饮用后会在一段时间内降低命中率、闪避值和施法成功率。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of mutation"
msgid ""
"A potion which mutates the drinker, removing several mutations then\n"
"granting a few random mutations, which are likely (but not guaranteed) to be\n"
"beneficial.\n"
msgstr "一种能使饮用者发生变异的药水，会先移除若干变异，再赋予一些随机变异。新变异很可能有益，但并不保证。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of resistance"
msgid ""
"A potion which grants temporary resistance to a variety of harmful effects:\n"
"fire, cold, electricity, poison, and acid.\n"
msgstr "一种能暂时抵御多种有害效果的药水：火焰、寒冷、电击、毒素和酸液。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:potion of attraction"
msgid ""
"A potion which makes the drinker attract enemies, translocating them quickly closer\n"
"for the duration of the effect. The effect is surprisingly subtle, and unwary\n"
"victims may sleep through it entirely.\n"
msgstr "一种能让饮用者吸引敌人的药水，在效果持续期间将敌人迅速位移到更近的位置。这种效果出奇地轻微，毫无防备的受害者甚至可能在被拉动时一直熟睡。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of dexterity"
msgid "A ring that increases the dexterity of its wearer.\n"
msgstr "一种能提高佩戴者敏捷的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of evasion"
msgid "A ring that makes its wearer more capable of avoiding attacks.\n"
msgstr "一种能让佩戴者更善于躲避攻击的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of flight"
msgid "A ring that grants its wearer flight.\n"
msgstr "一种能使佩戴者飞行的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of intelligence"
msgid "A ring that increases the intelligence of its wearer.\n"
msgstr "一种能提高佩戴者智力的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of resist corrosion"
msgid "A ring that protects its wearer from the effects of acid and corrosion.\n"
msgstr "一种能保护佩戴者免受酸液和腐蚀影响的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of magical power"
msgid ""
"A ring that increases its wearer's reserves of magical power for so long as it\n"
"is worn.\n"
msgstr "一种在佩戴期间增加佩戴者魔力储备的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of poison resistance"
msgid "A ring that protects its wearer from poison.\n"
msgstr "一种能保护佩戴者抵御毒素的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of positive energy"
msgid "A ring that protects its wearer from the effects of negative energy.\n"
msgstr "一种能保护佩戴者抵御负能量影响的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of protection"
msgid "A ring that protects its wearer from most sources of damage.\n"
msgstr "一种能保护佩戴者、抵御大多数伤害来源的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of protection from cold"
msgid "A ring that protects its wearer from cold.\n"
msgstr "一种能保护佩戴者抵御寒冷的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of protection from fire"
msgid "A ring that protects its wearer from fire.\n"
msgstr "一种能保护佩戴者抵御火焰的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of willpower"
msgid ""
"A ring that increases its wearer's willpower, protecting against certain\n"
"magical effects.\n"
msgstr "一种能增强佩戴者意志、抵御某些魔法效果的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of see invisible"
msgid "A ring that allows its wearer to see invisible things.\n"
msgstr "一种能让佩戴者看见隐形事物的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of slaying"
msgid ""
"A ring that increases the wearer's accuracy and damage with ranged weapons and\n"
"melee attacks.\n"
msgstr "一种能提高佩戴者远程武器与近战攻击的命中率和伤害的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of strength"
msgid "A ring that increases the strength of its wearer.\n"
msgstr "一种能提高佩戴者力量的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:ring of wizardry"
msgid "A ring that increases the success rate of its wearer's magical spells.\n"
msgstr "一种能提高佩戴者法术成功率的戒指。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of acquirement"
msgid ""
"A wonderful scroll which causes the creation of a valuable item, with the\n"
"reader choosing from a small selection. The items offered will often be a\n"
"good match for the reader's skills; and if nothing recommends itself, the\n"
"reader can always choose a heap of gold.\n"
msgstr "一种能创造贵重物品的奇妙卷轴，阅读者可以从少量选项中挑选。提供的物品通常很适合阅读者的技能；如果没有中意的物品，也总能选择一堆金币。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of amnesia"
msgid ""
"A scroll that allows its reader to selectively erase one spell from memory to\n"
"recapture the magical energy bound up with it.\n"
msgstr "一种能让阅读者有选择地从记忆中抹去一个法术、收回其所占魔法能量的卷轴。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of brand weapon"
msgid ""
"A scroll that imbues a weapon with a random brand. Any existing brand will be\n"
"replaced with a different one, and any brand forbidden by your current god will\n"
"not be chosen. Artefacts cannot be branded in this way.\n"
"\n"
"Melee weapons will commonly be branded with the flaming, freezing, heavy,\n"
"venom or protection brand (or with the special brand exclusive to the category\n"
"of weapon being branded), and rarely with the draining, electrocution, spectral,\n"
"vampiric or chaos brand.\n"
"\n"
"Ranged weapons will commonly be branded with the flaming, freezing, heavy or\n"
"draining brand, and rarely with the electrocution or chaos brand.\n"
msgstr ""
"一种能为武器赋予随机印记的卷轴。已有印记会被另一种不同的印记替换，且不会选中你当前神祇禁止的印记。神器无法用这种方式赋予印记。\n"
"\n"
"近战武器常见的印记为火焰、寒冰、重型、毒液和防护，或该武器类别独有的特殊印记；较少见的印记为吸能、电击、幽魂、吸血和混沌。\n"
"\n"
"远程武器常见的印记为火焰、寒冰、重型和吸能，较少见的为电击和混沌。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of butterflies"
msgid ""
"A scroll that surrounds its user with a flight of beautiful butterflies, blowing\n"
"back other creatures nearby with the flapping of their wings.\n"
msgstr "一种能在使用者周围召来一群美丽蝴蝶的卷轴。蝴蝶拍动翅膀，将附近其他生物吹退。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of fear"
msgid ""
"A scroll that causes great fear in nearby foes, causing them to flee until\n"
"attacked, cornered, or enough time has passed.\n"
"\n"
"Non-living, undead and plant monsters cannot be feared, and berserk or frenzied\n"
"monsters are also immune.\n"
msgstr ""
"一种能使附近敌人极度恐惧的卷轴，令其逃跑，直到遭到攻击、被逼入绝境，或经过足够长时间。\n"
"\n"
"非生命、亡灵和植物怪物不会恐惧，狂暴或狂乱的怪物也免疫此效果。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of fog"
msgid ""
"A scroll that surrounds the reader with a dense cloud of fog, which can block\n"
"vision temporarily. The fog takes a short time to fully spill out.\n"
msgstr "一种能在阅读者周围产生浓密雾气、暂时遮蔽视线的卷轴。雾气需要一点时间才能完全弥漫开来。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of immolation"
msgid ""
"A scroll that fills the creatures around the reader with an unstable and\n"
"powerful inner flame. This fire is released any time the victims are hit, and\n"
"explosively released upon their death. Giant creatures cause bigger explosions.\n"
msgstr "一种能使阅读者周围生物体内充满不稳定而强大的心火的卷轴。受害者每次被击中都会释放火焰，死亡时则会猛烈爆炸。巨型生物会造成更大的爆炸。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of noise"
msgid "A prank scroll that creates a loud noise when read.\n"
msgstr "一种恶作剧卷轴，阅读时会制造巨响。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of poison"
msgid ""
"A scroll that fills the air with poison, covering every unoccupied space in\n"
"sight with toxic fumes.\n"
msgstr "一种能使空气充满毒素的卷轴，以毒雾覆盖视野内每一个没有生物占据的格子。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of revelation"
msgid ""
"A scroll that reveals its reader's surroundings. The layout of the current\n"
"floor is fully mapped, and everything within a moderate radius, including\n"
"both visible and invisible monsters, is momentarily shown.\n"
msgstr "一种能揭示阅读者周围情况的卷轴。它会完整绘出当前楼层的布局，并短暂显示中等范围内的一切，包括可见和隐形的怪物。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of silence"
msgid ""
"A scroll that eliminates all sound near the reader. This makes reading scrolls,\n"
"casting spells, invoking divine abilities, or shouting impossible in the\n"
"reader's vicinity.\n"
"\n"
"Certain monsters have innate magical or special abilities which will still be\n"
"usable while silenced.\n"
"\n"
"The effect starts out with a large radius, which will then shrink, eventually\n"
"covering only the reader, before it times out.\n"
msgstr ""
"一种能消除阅读者附近所有声音的卷轴。在阅读者周围，任何生物都无法阅读卷轴、施放法术、调用神赐能力或喊叫。\n"
"\n"
"某些怪物拥有天赋魔法或特殊能力，即使被沉默也依然能够使用。\n"
"\n"
"效果起初范围很大，随后逐渐缩小，最终只覆盖阅读者自身，再完全消失。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of summoning"
msgid ""
"A scroll that calls forth several allied creatures woven from shadow into the\n"
"shapes of those beings found within the reader's immediate vicinity.\n"
msgstr "一种能召来数个盟友的卷轴。这些生物由阴影编织而成，形态取自阅读者当前附近的生物。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of torment"
msgid ""
"A scroll that calls on the powers of darkness to inflict great pain on any\n"
"nearby creature — including the reader! This halves the resilience of all\n"
"living creatures and cuts down all holy creature resilence by about a third,\n"
"although it is never directly fatal.\n"
msgstr "一种会召来黑暗力量、使附近生物遭受极大痛苦的卷轴，连阅读者也不例外！它会使所有活物的生命减半，使所有神圣生物的生命减少约三分之一，但绝不会直接致命。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:scroll of vulnerability"
msgid ""
"A scroll that briefly halves the willpower of the reader and any nearby beings,\n"
"rendering them vulnerable to many magical effects. The scroll cannot affect\n"
"those fully immune to such effects.\n"
msgstr "一种能短暂削减阅读者及附近生物一半意志的卷轴，使其更易受到多种魔法效果影响。对完全免疫此类效果的生物无效。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of acid"
msgid "A magical device which throws bolts of corrosive acid.\n"
msgstr "一种能射出腐蚀性酸液束的魔法装置。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of charming"
msgid ""
"A magical device which causes a creature to become fiercely, but briefly,\n"
"loyal to the user.\n"
msgstr "一种能使生物短暂而热烈地效忠使用者的魔法装置。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of digging"
msgid "A magical device which drills tunnels through unworked rock.\n"
msgstr "一种能在未经开凿的岩石中钻出隧道的魔法装置。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of flame"
msgid "A magical device which throws little puffs of flame.\n"
msgstr "一种能喷出小团火焰的魔法装置。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of iceblast"
msgid ""
"A magical device which creates a loud explosion of ice shards, bypassing half\n"
"of victims' resistance to cold.\n"
msgstr "一种能制造响亮冰片爆炸的魔法装置，其中一半伤害不受受害者寒冷抗性减免。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of light"
msgid ""
"A magical device which fires a ray of searing light, injuring and blinding\n"
"those struck. Only living, undead, demonic and angelic monsters can be blinded,\n"
"and tougher monsters will recover their vision more quickly.\n"
msgstr "一种能射出灼热光线、伤害并致盲命中者的魔法装置。只有活物、亡灵、恶魔和天使怪物能够被致盲；更强壮的怪物恢复视力更快。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of mindburst"
msgid ""
"A magical device which launches a psychic attack on a target creature. If it\n"
"overcomes their willpower, it 'blows their mind' in a violently literal fashion,\n"
"dealing damage that bypasses their armour entirely. It is useless against\n"
"mindless creatures.\n"
msgstr "一种能对目标生物发动精神攻击的魔法装置。若克服了目标的意志，就会以极其直白而猛烈的方式“炸裂其心智”，造成完全无视护甲的伤害。对无心智的生物无效。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of paralysis"
msgid ""
"A magical device which can render a creature immobile, incapable of moving any\n"
"of its limbs.\n"
msgstr "一种能使生物全身僵住、无法移动任何肢体的魔法装置。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of polymorph"
msgid ""
"A magical device which causes a creature to be transmogrified into another\n"
"form. It is especially effective against shape-changing creatures.\n"
msgstr "一种能将生物变为另一种形态的魔法装置，对能够改变形态的生物尤其有效。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of quicksilver"
msgid ""
"A magical device which fires a beam of destructive energy, dispelling\n"
"enchantments on creatures struck.\n"
msgstr "一种能射出破坏性能量束、驱散命中者附魔效果的魔法装置。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of roots"
msgid ""
"A magical device which fires a magical seed, entangling its target and adjacent\n"
"foes in quick-growing tree roots. Those entangled will be immobilised and take\n"
"damage over time until they escape or the roots wither away. The roots will only\n"
"sprout from solid ground.\n"
msgstr "一种能射出魔法种子的魔法装置，以迅速生长的树根缠住目标及相邻敌人。被缠住者无法移动，并持续受到伤害，直到挣脱或树根枯萎。树根只能从坚实地面上长出。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/items.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/items.txt:wand of warping"
msgid ""
"A magical device which creates a brief but violent rift in space, damaging\n"
"everything caught in its wake and sometimes blinking them a short distance away.\n"
msgstr "一种能制造短暂而猛烈的空间裂隙的魔法装置，伤害所有被卷入其中的目标，并有时使其向短距离外闪烁。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:sting spell"
msgid ""
"Conjures a jagged shard of crystallised toxins. The stinger's impact will always\n"
"poison a susceptible target. Even resistant targets have a chance to be poisoned\n"
"and immune monsters will still be damaged by the physical impact of the stinger.\n"
msgstr "创造一片锯齿状的结晶毒素碎片。毒刺命中时，总会使易受毒素影响的目标中毒。即使有毒素抗性的目标也有一定几率中毒；完全免疫毒素的怪物仍会受到毒刺的物理冲击伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:construct spike launcher spell"
msgid ""
"Constructs a simple mechanical trap within an adjacent wall which repeatedly\n"
"skewers random adjacent enemies. Protected by the wall itself, it is\n"
"invulnerable to most forms of damage, but will fall apart if the caster leaves\n"
"its vicinity.\n"
msgstr "在相邻墙壁内建造一个简单的机械陷阱，反复刺穿随机的相邻敌人。由于受到墙壁保护，它对大多数伤害免疫；但施法者离开附近后，它就会散架。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:kinetic grapnel spell"
msgid ""
"Weaves a thin kinetic filament around the caster's melee weapon and launches the\n"
"other end of it at a nearby enemy. If this grapnel successfully hits and does\n"
"damage, it will become lodged in them, allowing the next melee attack the caster\n"
"performs against them to strike with perfect accuracy and a small slaying bonus.\n"
msgstr "在施法者的近战武器上缠绕一根细小的动能丝线，再将另一端射向附近敌人。如果抓钩命中并造成伤害，就会嵌入目标体内，使施法者下一次对该目标的近战攻击必定命中，并获得少量杀戮加成。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:launch clockwork bee spell"
msgid ""
"Constructs a mechanical bee and winds its clockwork mechanisms over several\n"
"turns before unleashing it against a targeted foe. The bee is swift and\n"
"powerful, but its clockwork quickly winds down as it attacks, eventually leaving\n"
"it helpless and unable to move.\n"
"\n"
"The caster may repair and rewind a dormant bee by attempting to move into it, at\n"
"the cost of 1 MP.\n"
"\n"
"Spellpower increases the number of attacks the bee may perform before going\n"
"dormant.\n"
msgstr ""
"创造一只机械蜜蜂，花数回合为其发条上弦，然后放出它攻击选定敌人。蜜蜂迅捷而强大，但随着攻击，发条很快就会耗尽，最终使其无力行动、无法移动。\n"
"\n"
"施法者可以尝试向休眠的蜜蜂移动，消耗 1 点魔力，为其修复并重新上弦。\n"
"\n"
"法术强度提高蜜蜂休眠前能够进行的攻击次数。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:jinxbite spell"
msgid ""
"Calls the attention of trickster spirits. While it holds, the spirits will\n"
"follow up on the caster's attacks. If the spell overcomes victims' willpower,\n"
"they will suffer minor damage and be drained by the sprites' playful malice.\n"
"\n"
"Fae assistance is fickle, however; they cannot be beckoned unless a susceptible\n"
"victim is visible, and will depart rapidly once no more remain. Calling on the\n"
"fae also reduces the caster's own willpower for a time.\n"
msgstr ""
"吸引恶作剧精魂的注意。法术持续期间，它们会跟随施法者的攻击发动追击。若法术克服了受害者的意志，精魂顽皮的恶意就会造成少量伤害并施加吸能。\n"
"\n"
"然而，妖精的帮助反复无常：只有视野内存在会受其影响的受害者时才能召来它们，而此类目标一旦全部消失，它们也会迅速离去。呼唤妖精还会在一段时间内削弱施法者自身的意志。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:sigil of binding spell"
msgid ""
"Creates two sigils nearby. Anyone who passes over them will be bound, able to\n"
"act and dodge normally but unable to move away. When the effect wears off,\n"
"their movement speed will rebound, giving them temporary swiftness. Swiftness\n"
"from any source grants immunity to binding.\n"
"\n"
"Only one set of sigils can be maintained at a time, and they will expire\n"
"prematurely if they leave your sight.\n"
msgstr ""
"在附近创造两个符印。任何经过符印的生物都会被束缚，仍可正常行动和闪避，但无法移开。效果结束后，其移动速度会反弹，暂时获得迅捷。来自任何来源的迅捷都能使生物免疫束缚。\n"
"\n"
"同时只能维持一组符印，且符印离开你的视野时会提前消失。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:ensorcelled hibernation spell"
msgid ""
"Lowers its target's metabolic rate, inducing hibernation. After awakening, the\n"
"target will be unable to be put to sleep again for some time.\n"
msgstr "降低目标的代谢速率，使其进入冬眠。醒来后，目标在一段时间内无法再次被催眠。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:confusing touch spell"
msgid ""
"Enchants the caster's dominant hand with magical energy. This energy is\n"
"released when the caster touches a monster, and may induce a state of confusion\n"
"in the monster. The caster's attacks do no damage while attempting to touch a\n"
"monster in this way.\n"
msgstr "以魔法能量为施法者的惯用手附魔。接触怪物时能量会释放，可能使怪物混乱。尝试以这种方式接触怪物时，施法者的攻击不造成伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:tukima's dance spell"
msgid ""
"Animates the weapon of a targeted foe, ripping it from their hands and causing\n"
"it to attack them relentlessly. Once the target dies, the weapon will fall to\n"
"the ground shortly thereafter.\n"
"\n"
"Certain powerful named artefacts cannot be animated, and any properties that\n"
"require skill in evocations will not be active.\n"
msgstr ""
"使目标敌人的武器活化，将其从手中夺走，转而不停攻击原主人。目标死去后不久，武器就会掉落地面。\n"
"\n"
"某些强大的具名神器无法被活化，且任何依赖唤发技能的属性都不会生效。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:searing ray spell"
msgid ""
"Fires a continuous piercing ray of arcane energy from the caster's hands. So\n"
"long as the caster maintains focus upon the spell and supplies it with magical\n"
"power (by waiting in place and not taking any other actions), the ray will\n"
"follow the caster's target if it should move.\n"
msgstr "从施法者手中射出一道持续、具有穿透力的奥术能量射线。只要施法者保持专注并持续供给魔力，也就是原地等待、不做其他动作，即使目标移动，射线也会持续追踪它。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:fulminant prism spell"
msgid ""
"Conjures a shining prism of an unstable soft gold alloy. This is useless as\n"
"legal tender, however, as it will unfortunately violently explode with arcane\n"
"force after a short duration. If destroyed prematurely, its blast will be much\n"
"weaker.\n"
msgstr "创造一个由不稳定软金合金构成的闪亮棱晶。可惜它并不能充当货币，因为短时间后就会因奥术力量而猛烈爆炸。如果提前被摧毁，爆炸威力会小得多。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:iskenderun's mystic blast spell"
msgid ""
"Detonates a crackling sphere of destructive energy. The explosion will hit all\n"
"nearby monsters with physical force, knocking them back if damage is done.\n"
"Spellpower increases damage and knockback distance.\n"
msgstr "引爆一团噼啪作响的破坏性能量。爆炸会以物理冲击命中附近所有怪物，造成伤害时还会将其击退。法术强度提高伤害和击退距离。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:scorch spell"
msgid ""
"Scorches a random foe. Those injured by this have their resistance to fire\n"
"burned away for a short time.\n"
msgstr "灼烧一个随机敌人。受伤者的火焰抗性会被暂时烧蚀。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:inner flame spell"
msgid ""
"Fills an enemy with an intense fire. This fire is released any time the target\n"
"is hit, and explosively released upon death. The size of the explosion caused\n"
"is dependent on the size of the target.\n"
msgstr "使一个敌人体内充满炽烈火焰。目标每次被击中都会释放火焰，死亡时则会猛烈爆炸。爆炸范围取决于目标的体型。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:flame wave spell"
msgid ""
"Blasts the caster's surroundings with a wave of fire. If the caster maintains\n"
"focus and supplies the spell with magical power (by waiting in place and not\n"
"taking any other actions), more and larger flame waves will radiate outward.\n"
msgstr "以火焰波浪轰击施法者周围。若施法者保持专注并持续供给魔力，也就是原地等待、不做其他动作，就会继续向外释放更多、更大的火焰波浪。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:static discharge spell"
msgid ""
"Releases electrical charges against those next to the caster. These may arc to\n"
"other adjacent creatures, or back to the caster, before eventually grounding\n"
"out. It deals reduced damage when arcing to the caster, and the damage dealt\n"
"bypasses half of defenders' armour.\n"
msgstr "向施法者身旁的生物释放电荷。电流可能传导到其他相邻生物，也可能传回施法者，最后才导入地面。传回施法者时造成的伤害较低；此法术的伤害会穿透防御者一半的护甲。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:swiftness spell"
msgid ""
"Calls forth winds to greatly increase the caster's movement speed. After the\n"
"effect ends, the caster's movements will be sluggish for a time.\n"
msgstr "呼唤风来大幅提高施法者的移动速度。效果结束后，施法者的移动会暂时变得迟缓。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:airstrike spell"
msgid ""
"Causes the air around a creature to twist itself into a whirling vortex of\n"
"meteorological fury. It does more damage to targets surrounded by empty space.\n"
msgstr "使一个生物周围的空气扭曲成猛烈旋转的气象涡旋。目标周围的空位越多，伤害越高。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:passwall spell"
msgid ""
"Allows the caster to travel a short distance through an adjacent rock wall and\n"
"emerge again on the other side. This spell takes an unusally long time to cast,\n"
"during which the caster will be unable to act, but also gain increased armour\n"
"from their attunement to the rock.\n"
msgstr "允许施法者短距离穿过相邻岩壁，从另一侧重新出现。施放此法术需要异常长的时间，期间施法者无法行动，但与岩石的调谐也会提高护甲值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:stone arrow spell"
msgid "Fires a sharp spine of rock.\n"
msgstr "射出一根尖锐的石刺。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:petrify spell"
msgid ""
"Petrifies a targeted creature and up to two other foes in a chain. Those which\n"
"do not muster the Will to resist are briefly slowed, and then turned to stone.\n"
"Until they return to flesh, they are unable to act, but also take half damage.\n"
"The spell's power is lessened against secondary targets.\n"
msgstr "石化目标生物，并沿连锁路径影响至多两个其他敌人。无法以意志抵抗的生物会先短暂减速，再变成石头。恢复血肉之躯前，它们无法行动，但受到的伤害减半。法术对次级目标的强度较低。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:grave claw spell"
msgid ""
"Calls forth the spite of the recently dead to skewer a targeted enemy with\n"
"shards of bone. This spell never misses, and will pin its target in place for\n"
"several turns, but casting it rapidly consumes the remnants of death that linger\n"
"upon the caster.\n"
"\n"
"You can stockpile enough malice to cast this spell at most three times, and this\n"
"can only be replenished by causing the death of a sufficient number of living\n"
"beings.\n"
msgstr ""
"唤起新近死者的怨恨，以骨片刺穿目标敌人。此法术绝不会打偏，并会将目标定在原地数回合，但施放时会迅速消耗施法者身上残留的死亡余韵。\n"
"\n"
"你最多能储存足以施放三次的怨恨；只有使足够多的活物死亡，才能补充这种力量。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:vampiric draining spell"
msgid "Steals the life of an adjacent living creature and grants it to the caster.\n"
msgstr "窃取相邻活物的生命，并将其给予施法者。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:animate dead spell"
msgid ""
"For some time after casting this, living creatures killed by the caster will rise\n"
"as zombies. The chance of reanimating a monster and the duration of the effect\n"
"increase with spell power. Re-casting this spell will return zombies to dust, as\n"
"will leaving the floor.\n"
msgstr "施法后的一段时间内，被施法者杀死的活物会作为僵尸复起。怪物复生的几率和效果持续时间都会随法术强度增加。重新施放此法术，或离开当前楼层，都会使僵尸化为尘土。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:call imp spell"
msgid ""
"Calls forth a minor demon from the pits of Hell, equipped with a spear with\n"
"which to jab at the caster's enemies. The quality of the imp's weaponry rises\n"
"with spell power.\n"
msgstr "从地狱深处召来一只小恶魔，它装备一根矛，用来刺击施法者的敌人。小恶魔的武器品质随法术强度提高。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:call canine familiar spell"
msgid ""
"Summons an inugami to the caster's aid. These mystical canines form a bond with\n"
"their summoner, strengthening them in direct proportion with the caster's\n"
"spellpower.\n"
"\n"
"Recasting this spell while your familiar is nearby will imbue it with additional\n"
"magic, mending some of its wounds, cleansing it of poison, and causing its next\n"
"attack to strike more quickly and cleave adjacent foes.\n"
msgstr ""
"召来一只犬神帮助施法者。这些神秘的犬类会与召唤者建立纽带，其力量与施法者的法术强度成正比。\n"
"\n"
"魔宠在附近时重新施法，会为其灌注额外魔力，治疗部分伤势、清除毒素，并使其下一次攻击更快，还能劈砍相邻敌人。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon ice beast spell"
msgid ""
"Calls forth a beast of ice to serve the caster. The strength of the beast\n"
"depends on spell power.\n"
msgstr "召来一只冰兽为施法者服务。冰兽的力量取决于法术强度。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:summon seismosaurus egg spell"
msgid ""
"Summons the egg of a brutish lizard, just on the verge of hatching. So long as\n"
"there are foes nearby and the caster remains adjacent to the egg, it will hatch\n"
"several turns after being summoned to wreak havoc upon its summoner's foes.\n"
"\n"
"Even as a juvenile, a seismosaurus is a force to be reckoned with. It is nearly\n"
"as hardy as a mountain, and its footfalls are capable of creating violent\n"
"seismic shockwaves. Each shockwave deals considerable damage to non-flying\n"
"enemies, and may sometimes even cause them to lose their footing altogether.\n"
"\n"
"Spell power increases the egg's durability and the strength of the seismosaur\n"
"within, but not the time it takes to hatch.\n"
msgstr ""
"召来一枚即将孵化的凶猛蜥蜴蛋。只要附近有敌人，且施法者一直与蛋相邻，它就会在召来数回合后孵化，重创召唤者的敌人。\n"
"\n"
"即使还很年幼，震龙也不可小觑。它几乎像山一样坚韧，脚步还能制造猛烈的地震冲击波。每次冲击波都会对不飞行的敌人造成可观伤害，有时甚至使其站立不稳。\n"
"\n"
"法术强度提高蛋的耐久和其中震龙的力量，但不会改变孵化所需时间。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:forge blazeheart golem spell"
msgid ""
"Constructs a shell of slag iron around a volatile elemental spark. It is capable\n"
"of raining down powerful blows on its creator's adversaries - so powerful that\n"
"the golem itself is often damaged by their impact.\n"
"\n"
"Only tenuously independent of its creator's magic, the flames within it will\n"
"rapidly go dormant if the two ever leave each other's side. If its shell is\n"
"destroyed while the golem is still active, its exposed core will violently\n"
"detonate a moment later.\n"
"\n"
"It gains greater explosive damage at higher power.\n"
msgstr ""
"围绕一粒不稳定的元素火花铸造一层铁渣外壳。它能猛烈打击创造者的敌人，打击之强，往往连魔像自身都会被冲击所伤。\n"
"\n"
"它只能勉强独立于创造者的魔法存在。一旦双方不再相邻，其内部火焰就会迅速休眠。如果魔像仍在活动时外壳被毁，暴露的核心便会在片刻后猛烈爆炸。\n"
"\n"
"法术强度越高，爆炸伤害越大。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:lesser beckoning spell"
msgid "Beckons the target forward, attempting to place them adjacent to the caster.\n"
msgstr "将目标向前召引，试图使其出现在施法者身旁。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:momentum strike spell"
msgid ""
"Blasts a target with energy borrowed from the caster's own future movement. For\n"
"a short time afterward, the caster will be left immotile - unable to walk, fly\n"
"around, slither, etc. Only motile creatures can cast this spell.\n"
msgstr "借用施法者未来移动的能量轰击目标。随后短时间内，施法者将无法自行移动，不能行走、飞行、爬行等。只有具备移动能力的生物才能施放此法术。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:vhi's electric charge spell"
msgid ""
"Sends the caster hurtling at a chosen nearby enemy, launching a high-accuracy\n"
"melee attack on arrival. Additional electric damage will be dealt based on the\n"
"length of the charge, the power of the spell, and the physical damage of the\n"
"attack. The caster is wrapped in an envelope of twisted space, allowing them\n"
"to safely pass through creatures, traps, and harmful terrain, and to displace\n"
"creatures at their destination. The time taken by the spell is the greater of\n"
"the time normally needed to cast a spell or that needed to launch one melee\n"
"attack.\n"
msgstr "使施法者冲向选定的附近敌人，抵达时发动一次高命中率的近战攻击。额外电击伤害取决于冲锋距离、法术强度和该次攻击的物理伤害。施法者被扭曲空间包裹，能安全穿过生物、陷阱和有害地形，并挤开目的地上的生物。此法术的耗时取正常施法耗时与一次近战攻击耗时中的较大值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:mephitic cloud spell"
msgid ""
"Conjures a fragile flask that explodes into short-lived clouds of noxious fumes.\n"
"These clouds may cause confusion in any creature not resistant to poison.\n"
"Tougher, more experienced creatures are less likely to be affected.\n"
msgstr "创造一个脆弱的瓶子，爆开后产生短暂的恶臭烟雾。烟雾可能使没有毒素抗性的生物混乱。更强壮、经验更丰富的生物不易受影响。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:mercury arrow spell"
msgid ""
"Conjures an arrow of elemental mercury which deals direct poison damage to\n"
"whatever it hits and may also weaken their melee attacks for a short while.\n"
"\n"
"The physical force of the arrow inflicts a small amount of damage even to those\n"
"immune to poison, and the weakening effect can splash to adjacent targets and\n"
"ignores poison resistance altogether.\n"
msgstr ""
"创造一支元素汞箭，对命中的目标造成直接毒素伤害，还可能暂时削弱其近战攻击。\n"
"\n"
"即使目标免疫毒素，箭的物理冲击仍会造成少量伤害。削弱效果还能溅射到相邻目标，且完全无视毒素抗性。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:olgreb's toxic radiance spell"
msgid ""
"Causes the caster to radiate toxic energy, continuously inflicting poison on\n"
"everything in line of sight for as long as the spell lasts.\n"
msgstr "使施法者放射有毒能量，在法术持续期间不断使视野内的一切生物中毒。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:sticky flame spell"
msgid ""
"Unleashes a short-ranged spray of incendiary goo that clings to an adjacent\n"
"creature and deals armour-ignoring fire damage over several turns. If the victim\n"
"is allowed to move, it will put out the fire prematurely.\n"
"\n"
"If the target is insubstantial, the liquid fire will fail to stick.\n"
msgstr ""
"向相邻生物喷射短距离的燃烧黏液，黏附后在数回合内造成无视护甲的火焰伤害。若受害者能够移动，就会提前扑灭火焰。\n"
"\n"
"若目标没有实体，液态火焰便无法黏附。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:ignite poison spell"
msgid ""
"Converts all nearby poison into liquid flame, burning poisoned creatures from\n"
"within. It also turns clouds of poison and mephitic gases into flame. The\n"
"caster is not affected directly.\n"
msgstr "将附近所有毒素转化为液态火焰，从内部焚烧中毒的生物。它还会使毒云和恶臭气体云变为火焰。施法者自身不会直接受到影响。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:frozen ramparts spell"
msgid ""
"Encases surrounding walls with ice for a short time. Foes that wander near the\n"
"icy walls will be damaged, and this may temporarily slow cold-blooded creatures.\n"
"Each victim is only ever affected by one icy wall at a time.\n"
"\n"
"The ice will crack and fall away if the caster moves to a new position.\n"
msgstr ""
"短时间内为周围墙壁覆上冰层。靠近冰墙的敌人会受到伤害，冷血生物还可能暂时减速。每个受害者同一时间只会受到一面冰墙影响。\n"
"\n"
"施法者移动到其他位置时，冰层就会碎裂脱落。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:ozocubu's armour spell"
msgid ""
"Envelops the caster's body in a protective layer of thick ice, granting a\n"
"substantial bonus to armour as long as they remain in their current location.\n"
"The ice will crack and fall away if the caster moves to a new position. The\n"
"spell decreases in effectiveness in heavier armour, granting a lower bonus the\n"
"higher the encumbrance rating of the caster's armour.\n"
msgstr "以厚实冰层包裹施法者，提供可观的护甲值加成，只要施法者留在原地就能维持。施法者移动到其他位置时，冰层就会碎裂脱落。穿戴越重的防具，法术效果越弱：防具累赘值越高，加成就越低。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:hailstorm spell"
msgid ""
"Conjures a cannonade of hail, battering nearby creatures that fail to dodge.\n"
"The eye of the storm is wide enough that monsters adjacent to the caster are\n"
"unaffected. Due to the strong impact and cutting edges, half of its damage\n"
"bypasses cold resistance.\n"
msgstr "召来一阵猛烈冰雹，打击附近未能闪避的生物。风暴中心的空隙足够宽，使与施法者相邻的怪物不受影响。由于强劲冲击和锋利棱角，一半伤害不受寒冷抗性减免。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:brom's barrelling boulder spell"
msgid ""
"Unleashes a massive rolling boulder in a given compass direction. This boulder\n"
"damages any creature it hits, rolling over those who perish beneath it and\n"
"pushing any others helplessly backwards (along with anyone else unfortunate\n"
"enough to be standing behind them).\n"
"\n"
"Its size and reckless locomotion make it difficult to use in confined areas; if\n"
"launched down narrow passages, it will rapidly abrade against the walls and fall\n"
"apart. It will also crumble if it leaves the caster's sight or strikes a wall\n"
"or otherwise unmoveable creature.\n"
msgstr ""
"沿指定的罗盘方向放出一块巨大的滚石。它会伤害撞上的所有生物，碾过被压死者，将其他生物无力地向后推去，也会推走不幸站在它们后面的生物。\n"
"\n"
"巨大的体型和横冲直撞的运动方式使它难以在狭窄处使用；若沿狭窄通道放出，它会迅速与墙壁摩擦而碎裂。离开施法者视野，或撞上墙壁或其他无法移动的生物时，它也会碎裂。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:volatile blastmotes spell"
msgid ""
"Brings forth a cloud of volatile blastmotes around the caster. These explode\n"
"on contact with open flame or with creatures - including any caster foolish\n"
"enough to linger in them! The explosion is concussive, knocking adjacent\n"
"creatures away. Damage done rises with the spell's power.\n"
msgstr "在施法者周围产生一团不稳定爆炸微粒。接触明火或生物时，它们会爆炸，愚蠢到留在其中的施法者也不例外！爆炸产生的冲击波会将相邻生物击退。伤害随法术强度提高。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:dimensional bullseye spell"
msgid ""
"Weaves a link between the caster's weaponry and a chosen target. Whenever the\n"
"caster fires or throws something at a *different* enemy, a matching projectile\n"
"will be teleported at the target. Spellpower increases their accuracy.\n"
msgstr "在施法者的武器与选定目标之间编织联系。每当施法者向另一个敌人发射或投掷物品时，就会有一个相应的投射物传送到被选定的目标处。法术强度提高这些投射物的命中率。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:cause fear spell"
msgid ""
"Causes fear in those near to the caster, causing those affected to be unable to\n"
"approach the caster, and to sometimes fail to attack them in melee. Leaving the\n"
"caster's line of sight will end the effect.\n"
msgstr "使施法者附近的生物恐惧。受影响者无法接近施法者，尝试近战攻击施法者时也可能失败。离开施法者视野就会终止效果。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:teleport other spell"
msgid ""
"Attempts to teleport a targeted creature out of the caster's sight, after a\n"
"short delay.\n"
msgstr "尝试在短暂延迟后，将目标生物传送到施法者视野之外。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:rending blade spell"
msgid ""
"Condenses the caster's magical energy into the form of a violently crackling\n"
"blade. Each time the caster successfully hits with a melee attack while the\n"
"spell is active, this blade will rend a path back and forth through nearby foes,\n"
"dealing irresistible damage.\n"
"\n"
"Casting this spell temporarily drains *all* of the caster's remaining magical\n"
"power to constitute the blade, but this energy will be returned to them as soon\n"
"as the blade ceases to exist. Each point of magical power sequestered this way\n"
"slightly increases the damage the blade inflicts.\n"
msgstr ""
"将施法者的魔法能量凝成一把猛烈迸发能量的利刃。法术持续期间，施法者每次近战攻击成功命中，利刃就会在附近敌人之间往返撕出一条路径，造成无法以抗性抵挡的伤害。\n"
"\n"
"施法会暂时抽取施法者剩余的全部魔力来构成利刃，但利刃一旦消失，这些能量就会归还。以此方式封存的每一点魔力，都会略微提高利刃造成的伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:maxwell's portable piledriver spell"
msgid ""
"Compresses an envelope of space around the caster and an adjacent enemy (or a\n"
"contiguous line of enemies), then allows it to decompress abruptly, propelling\n"
"everyone forward until the unfortunate being at the far end collides with\n"
"something solid, inflicting damage on them proportional to the distance\n"
"travelled.\n"
msgstr "压缩施法者与相邻敌人周围的一层空间，也可包裹一条连续排列的敌人，然后令其骤然解压，将其中所有生物向前推进，直到最前端不幸的生物撞上坚实物体。它会受到与移动距离成正比的伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:curse of agony spell"
msgid ""
"Curses a foe, halving their remaining health after each of the next two times\n"
"that the caster strikes them in melee.\n"
msgstr "诅咒一个敌人，使施法者接下来两次近战命中它时，每次都将其剩余生命减半。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:forge lightning spire spell"
msgid ""
"Constructs an immobile lightning spire at a nearby location. This spire\n"
"irregularly discharges bolts of electricity at the caster's foes, prioritizing\n"
"whichever of them is most distant from it.\n"
msgstr "在附近位置创造一座无法移动的闪电尖塔。它会不定时向施法者的敌人释放电流束，优先攻击距离自身最远的敌人。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:gloom spell"
msgid ""
"Emits a wave of pernicious gloom which attempts to smother the light around\n"
"nearby creatures. Any living, demonic or holy creature caught in the effect may\n"
"briefly lose their eyesight and be left stumbling blindly.\n"
"\n"
"Willpower is useless against this spell, but stronger creatures may still shrug\n"
"off its effects.\n"
msgstr ""
"释放一波有害的幽暗，试图吞没附近生物周围的光线。受影响的活物、恶魔或神圣生物可能短暂失明，盲目踉跄。\n"
"\n"
"意志对此法术无用，但更强大的生物仍可能摆脱其影响。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/spells.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/spells.txt:eringya's surprising crocodile spell"
msgid ""
"Summons a toothy crocodile to assault an adjacent enemy. The crocodile will\n"
"appear beneath the caster in a surge of murky water and perform an empowered\n"
"attack against the chosen target, dragging both it and the caster backward\n"
"before allowing the latter to dismount safely behind it. It cannot be recast\n"
"while the crocodile is still active.\n"
msgstr "召来一条利齿鳄鱼攻击相邻敌人。鳄鱼会在一股浑水中从施法者身下出现，对选定目标发动一次强化攻击，将目标和施法者一起向后拖动，再让施法者安全地从它后方下来。鳄鱼仍在活动时，无法重新施放此法术。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:mesm status"
msgid ""
"You are mesmerised and cannot move away from the monster mesmerising you. The\n"
"effect can be broken by killing or confusing the responsible monster or by\n"
"breaking line of sight with them.\n"
msgstr "你受到魅惑牵引，无法远离魅惑你的怪物。杀死或混乱该怪物，或切断与其之间的视线，都能解除效果。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-tele status"
msgid "You are prevented from teleporting or blinking.\n"
msgstr "你无法传送或闪烁。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-move status"
msgid ""
"You cannot walk, fly around, slither, etc. You can still take other actions,\n"
"and can still be moved via translocations or by being pushed, pulled, and so on.\n"
msgstr "你无法自行行走、飞行、爬行等，但仍能进行其他动作，也仍可通过位移魔法或被推、被拉等方式移动。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:fire status"
msgid ""
"You are covered with sticky fire, which causes damage over a moderate duration.\n"
"Moving will quell the fire much more rapidly, and entering water will extinguish\n"
"it immediately.\n"
msgstr "你身上附着着黏性火焰，会在一段时间内受到伤害。移动能更快地扑灭火焰，进入水中则会立即灭火。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:fire+ status"
msgid "<Fire status>\n"
msgstr "<Fire status>\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:fire++ status"
msgid "<Fire status>\n"
msgstr "<Fire status>\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:corona status"
msgid ""
"You are surrounded by light, greatly reducing your stealth and making you\n"
"easier to hit.\n"
msgstr "你被光芒包围，潜行能力大幅降低，也更容易被击中。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:barbs status"
msgid ""
"There are barbs embedded in your skin, and moving around will cause you to take\n"
"damage. Remaining in place for a short time will allow you to remove the barbs\n"
"without taking damage.\n"
msgstr "有倒刺嵌入你的皮肤，移动会使你受到伤害。原地停留一小段时间后，就能拔出倒刺而不受伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:sick status"
msgid "You have been sickened, and your health will no longer regenerate.\n"
msgstr "你生病了，生命将不再自然恢复。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:vertigo status"
msgid ""
"You are disoriented and dizzy, reducing your accuracy, evasion, and\n"
"spellcasting success rate.\n"
msgstr "你头晕目眩、方向感混乱，命中率、闪避值和施法成功率降低。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:corr status"
msgid ""
"You are corroded, reducing your damage in physical combat and your armour by an\n"
"amount depending on the severity of the corrosion.\n"
msgstr "你遭到腐蚀，物理战斗伤害和护甲值都会降低，降低程度取决于腐蚀的严重程度。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:flay status"
msgid ""
"You are covered in illusionary wounds, causing severe damage while the effect\n"
"remains active. Destroying the source of the illusion will restore all health\n"
"lost to the flaying.\n"
msgstr "你的身体布满幻象伤口，在效果持续期间会受到严重伤害。摧毁幻象的源头，就能恢复因剥皮而失去的全部生命。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:weak status"
msgid "Your melee attacks do 25% less damage.\n"
msgstr "你的近战攻击伤害降低 25%。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:frozen status"
msgid "You are covered in ice, and your movement speed is reduced.\n"
msgstr "你被冰覆盖，移动速度降低。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:sap status"
msgid ""
"Your magic is sapped. Casting a spell will cause you to lose access to your\n"
"magic, briefly preventing you from casting any further spells.\n"
msgstr "你的魔力被削弱。施放法术会使你暂时失去魔法能力，短时间内无法继续施法。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-cast status"
msgid "You are unable to cast spells.\n"
msgstr "你无法施放法术。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:crippled status"
msgid ""
"At least one of your strength, intelligence, or dexterity has fallen to 0 or\n"
"below. You will act slowly until this situation is remedied.\n"
msgstr "你的力量、智力或敏捷至少有一项降至 0 或以下。在恢复之前，你的行动会变慢。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:dchan status"
msgid ""
"You are channelling the dead, causing any living creatures killed in your\n"
"vicinity to be raised as spectral servants.\n"
msgstr "你正在引导死者，使附近死去的活物作为幽魂仆从复起。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:vit status"
msgid ""
"You are divinely vitalised, providing protection from poison, confusion,\n"
"petrification, and sickness, and increasing and sustaining your strength,\n"
"intelligence and dexterity.\n"
msgstr "你被神力赋予活力，受到中毒、混乱、石化和疾病防护，力量、智力和敏捷也会提高并得到维持。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:will/2 status"
msgid "Your willpower is weaker, making you vulnerable to many magical effects.\n"
msgstr "你的意志被削弱，更易受到多种魔法效果影响。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:stone status"
msgid ""
"You are petrified, and completely unable to act. You are very easy to hit,\n"
"but all damage taken is substantially reduced.\n"
msgstr "你已完全石化，无法进行任何动作，也非常容易被击中，但受到的所有伤害都大幅降低。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:petr status"
msgid ""
"You are turning to stone. Your actions are slowed, all damage taken is slightly\n"
"reduced, and you will soon be completely petrified (gaining the Stone status).\n"
msgstr "你正在变成石头。行动速度降低，受到的所有伤害略微减少，而且很快就会完全石化，获得已石化状态。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:resist status"
msgid "You are more resistant to fire, cold, electricity, poison and acid.\n"
msgstr "你的火焰、寒冷、电击、毒素和酸液抗性提高。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:slime status"
msgid ""
"Your wielded weapon or your fists are coated in slime, and will turn the next\n"
"living or corporeal undead monster you hit into a neutral slime.\n"
msgstr "你手持的武器或双拳被黏液覆盖，下一次命中活物或有实体的亡灵怪物时，会将其变为中立的史莱姆。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-swift status"
msgid "You are covering ground slowly.\n"
msgstr "你的移动变得迟缓。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:ddoor status"
msgid ""
"You are temporarily invulnerable to harm, but are brought close to death in the\n"
"process and cannot be affected by healing while the effect is active. After the\n"
"spell expires, it cannot be immediately recast.\n"
msgstr "你暂时不会受到伤害，但代价是濒临死亡，且效果持续期间无法接受治疗。法术结束后，不能立即重新施放。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-ddoor status"
msgid ""
"You are still close to death's doorway, and cannot recast Death's Door for a\n"
"short duration.\n"
msgstr "你仍徘徊在死亡门口，短时间内无法重新施放死亡之门。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:quad status"
msgid "QUAD DAMAGE!\n"
msgstr "四倍伤害！\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:flooded status"
msgid ""
"Your lungs are filled with liquid, preventing you from breathing properly. This\n"
"makes reading scrolls, casting spells, and invoking divine abilities impossible.\n"
"You will also take asphyxiation damage every turn.\n"
msgstr "你的肺部充满液体，无法正常呼吸，因此无法阅读卷轴、施放法术或调用神赐能力。你每回合还会受到窒息伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:stealth status"
msgid "Your stealth is greatly increased.\n"
msgstr "你的潜行能力大幅提高。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:vortex status"
msgid ""
"You are in the eye of a mighty ice storm. After the vortex fades, it cannot be\n"
"called forth again for a short time.\n"
msgstr "你位于一场强劲冰风暴的中心。涡旋消退后，短时间内无法再次唤起。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-vortex status"
msgid ""
"You are surrounded by unstable winds, and cannot recast Polar Vortex for a short\n"
"duration.\n"
msgstr "你周围的风尚不稳定，短时间内无法重新施放极地涡流。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:liquid status"
msgid ""
"You are liquefying the ground around you, slowing the movement of all creatures\n"
"in the area.\n"
msgstr "你正在液化周围地面，使区域内所有生物的移动变慢。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:hero status"
msgid "Your combat skills are temporarily increased.\n"
msgstr "你的战斗技能暂时提高。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:finesse status"
msgid "Your combat speed is greatly increased.\n"
msgstr "你的战斗速度大幅提高。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:duel status"
msgid ""
"You are duelling a foe in Okawaru's Arena, and will be returned whence you came\n"
"if you are victorious.\n"
msgstr "你正在奥格瓦如的竞技场中与敌人决斗。如果获胜，就会被送回原处。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:disjoin status"
msgid ""
"You are destabilising space around yourself, causing nearby monsters to be\n"
"randomly blinked away from you.\n"
msgstr "你正在扰乱自身周围的空间，使附近怪物随机闪烁到远离你的位置。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:fugue status"
msgid ""
"Your weapon is temporarily enhanced by the souls of the damned, providing\n"
"slaying bonuses that increase with every enemy killed. At the maximum bonus,\n"
"foes adjacent to your attacks' targets suffer pain damage.\n"
msgstr "你的武器暂时被受诅咒的灵魂强化，每杀死一个敌人，杀戮加成就会提高。达到最大加成后，与你攻击目标相邻的敌人会受到痛楚伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:debt status"
msgid ""
"You have lived beyond your means. You cannot spend gold again until you earn\n"
"enough to cancel out your debt.\n"
msgstr "你的支出超出了财力。在赚到足够金币偿清债务之前，无法再次花费金币。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:toxic status"
msgid ""
"You are radiating toxic energy, and will continuously inflict poison on all\n"
"nearby creatures.\n"
msgstr "你正在放射有毒能量，会持续使附近所有生物中毒。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:recite status"
msgid ""
"You are reciting Zin's laws to nearby monsters, with a range of effects\n"
"depending on the target. After finishing a recitation, it cannot be repeated\n"
"for a short time.\n"
msgstr "你正在向附近怪物诵读辛的律法，效果随目标而异。诵读结束后，短时间内无法再次诵读。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-recite status"
msgid ""
"You have recently finished reciting Zin's laws, and cannot recite again for a\n"
"short duration.\n"
msgstr "你刚结束诵读辛的律法，短时间内无法再次诵读。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:rf- status"
msgid "You are more vulnerable to fire.\n"
msgstr "你更容易受到火焰伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:rp- status"
msgid "You are more vulnerable to poison.\n"
msgstr "你更容易受到毒素影响。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:bullseye status"
msgid ""
"You have targeted an enemy with a dimensional bullseye, causing missiles fired\n"
"or thrown at a different enemy to also be teleported at the target.\n"
msgstr "你已用空间靶心锁定一个敌人，向其他敌人发射或投掷的投射物也会传送到被锁定的目标处。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:forest status"
msgid ""
"You are calling a forested plane into temporary existence, and awakening nearby\n"
"trees to damage your foes.\n"
msgstr "你正使一个森林位面暂时显现，并唤醒附近树木来伤害敌人。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:dragoncall status"
msgid ""
"You are calling forth mighty dragons to attack your foes. Each dragon which\n"
"answers the call will drain your magical energy. After the call ends, it cannot\n"
"be issued again for a short time.\n"
msgstr "你正在召来强大的龙攻击敌人。每条响应召唤的龙都会消耗你的魔力。召唤结束后，短时间内无法再次发动。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-dragoncall status"
msgid ""
"You have recently called forth dragons, and cannot recast Dragon's Call for a\n"
"short duration.\n"
msgstr "你刚刚召唤过龙，短时间内无法重新施放巨龙呼唤。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-potion status"
msgid "You are unable to quaff potions.\n"
msgstr "你无法饮用药水。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:relec+ status"
msgid "You are more resistant to electricity.\n"
msgstr "你的电击抗性提高。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:horr status"
msgid ""
"You are terrified of nearby monsters, reducing your damage and accuracy in\n"
"combat as well as the power of your spells.\n"
msgstr "附近的怪物使你惊恐，战斗伤害、命中率和法术强度都会降低。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-scroll status"
msgid "You are unable to read scrolls.\n"
msgstr "你无法阅读卷轴。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:cleave status"
msgid "Your melee attacks cleave, hitting all adjacent targets.\n"
msgstr "你的近战攻击可以劈砍，命中所有相邻目标。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:ambros status"
msgid ""
"You are regenerating health and magic, but are also confused. Curing the\n"
"confusion will also end the regeneration.\n"
msgstr "你正在恢复生命和魔力，但同时处于混乱状态。治愈混乱也会终止再生效果。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:surge status"
msgid ""
"Your next use of an evokable device will have its power enhanced, at the cost\n"
"of some of your magic.\n"
msgstr "你下一次使用唤发装置时，其威力会增强，但会消耗你的一部分魔力。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:howl status"
msgid ""
"A terrifying howl is echoing in your mind, calling forth powerful creatures to\n"
"attack you.\n"
msgstr "一道可怕的嚎叫在你脑中回响，召来强大的生物攻击你。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:blood status"
msgid ""
"Your body is covered in congealed blood, serving as armour for as long as you\n"
"remain seriously injured.\n"
msgstr "你的身体覆盖着凝固的血液；只要你仍身受重伤，这层血液就能充当护甲。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:channel status"
msgid "You are channelling magical energy.\n"
msgstr "你正在引导魔法能量。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-hop status"
msgid ""
"Your legs are tired, and you are unable to hop. This status will only recover\n"
"after you spend several turns not moving. (Other actions, such as attacking or\n"
"casting spells, are fine.)\n"
msgstr "你的双腿疲惫，无法跳跃。只有连续数回合不移动，此状态才会恢复；攻击、施法等其他动作不受限制。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:-blink status"
msgid ""
"You are unstable and cannot cast Blink or activate evoked blink abilities\n"
"for a short period of time. Powerful sources of translocation magic such as\n"
"scrolls of blinking ignore this limitation, as do external sources of blinking\n"
"outside of your control.\n"
msgstr "你的状态不稳定，短时间内无法施放闪烁或发动唤发闪烁能力。闪烁卷轴等强大的位移魔法来源不受此限制，不受你控制的外部闪烁来源也不受限制。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:blind status"
msgid ""
"Your vision is badly impaired. All spells and attacks you perform (which do not\n"
"automatically hit) have an increased chance to miss. This chance is much greater\n"
"the further away you are from your target.\n"
msgstr "你的视力严重受损。你施放的法术和发动的攻击，只要不是自动命中，打偏的几率都会提高；与目标距离越远，这种几率就越大。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:drowsy status"
msgid "You are rapidly growing sleepy and may soon fall asleep completely.\n"
msgstr "你正迅速变得困倦，可能很快就会完全睡着。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:doom status"
msgid ""
"A malevolent fate is gathering around you. If your Doom reaches 100%, you will\n"
"be afflicted by a random bane and your Doom will reset to 0. Banes have diverse\n"
"negative effects that can significantly endanger your character for an extended\n"
"period of time.\n"
"\n"
"Both Doom and Banes are only cured by gaining experience, though Banes typically\n"
"last much longer.\n"
msgstr ""
"恶毒的命运正在你身边聚集。厄运达到 100% 时，你会遭受一种随机灾厄，随后厄运重置为 0。灾厄具有多种负面效果，可能在很长时间内严重危及角色。\n"
"\n"
"厄运与灾厄都只能靠获取经验消除，不过灾厄通常持续得更久。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:ostracised status"
msgid ""
"Your connection to the divine has been partially cut-off, temporarily reducing\n"
"your effective piety. Gaining experience will eventually recover all piety that\n"
"has been locked away this way.\n"
msgstr "你与神祇的联系被部分切断，有效虔诚暂时降低。获取经验最终会恢复所有以这种方式被封锁的虔诚。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:contam status"
msgid ""
"You are glowing with mutagenic radiation. This can inflict mutations over time\n"
"(usually negative) or even cause you to suffer damage as the unstable magic\n"
"explodes violently. In addition, your glow prevents invisibility and reduces\n"
"your stealth.\n"
"{{\n"
"    local dmg = you.contam_max_damage();\n"
"    if dmg > 0 then\n"
"        return \"\\nAn explosion at your current level of contamination could \" ..\n"
"               \"inflict up to \" .. dmg .. \" damage.\"\n"
"    end\n"
"}}\n"
msgstr "你因能引起变异的辐射而发光。随着时间推移，这可能引发变异，通常是负面的；不稳定的魔法甚至会猛烈爆炸，使你受到伤害。此外，发光会阻止隐形，并削弱潜行。\n{{\n    local dmg = you.contam_max_damage();\n    if dmg > 0 then\n        return \"\\n以你当前的魔法污染程度，一次爆炸可能\" ..\n               \"最多造成 \" .. dmg .. \" 点伤害。\"\n    end\n}}\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1, glossary and current mechanism constraints; batch phase3-static-02.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/status.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:app status"
msgid ""
"{{\n"
"    if you.race() == \"Octopode\" then\n"
"        return \"A vicious spike has grown from one of your tentacles, \" ..\n"
"               \"increasing the damage of your extra tentacle attacks.\"\n"
"    else\n"
"        return \"Monstrous horns or talons have grown from your body, \" ..\n"
"               \"granting a chance of making an extra attack in melee.\"\n"
"    end\n"
"}}\n"
msgstr ""
"{{\n"
"    if you.race() == \"Octopode\" then\n"
"        return \"你的一条触手上长出一根凶狠的尖刺，\" ..\n"
"               \"提高了额外触手攻击的伤害。\"\n"
"    else\n"
"        return \"你的身体上长出怪异的角或利爪，\" ..\n"
"               \"使你有一定几率在近战中发动额外攻击。\"\n"
"    end\n"
"}}\n"

#. Terminology correction against reviewed glossary; batch phase3-static-02.
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:warper"
msgid ""
"Warpers start with a weapon of their choice, a scroll of blinking, darts of\n"
"disjunction, and some Translocation spells in their library.\n"
msgstr "位移术士起始携带自选武器、闪烁卷轴和离散飞镖，法术库中还有一些位移系法术。\n"

#. Terminology correction against reviewed glossary; batch phase3-static-02.
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:dodging"
msgid ""
"The Dodging skill will affect your chance of dodging an attack, be it melee,\n"
"ranged or magical. Certain types of attack cannot be dodged, however, such as\n"
"enchantments (which must be resisted with willpower) and explosions.\n"
msgstr "闪避技能影响躲开攻击的几率，无论是近战、远程还是魔法攻击。但某些攻击无法闪避，例如附魔效果（必须靠意志抵抗）和爆炸。\n"

#. Terminology correction against reviewed glossary; batch phase3-static-02.
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:hexes"
msgid ""
"Hexes try to bestow various enchantments on nearby things. While none do direct\n"
"damage, being ensorcelled can effectively take an opponent out of combat,\n"
"although they often require overcoming an opponent's willpower to have an effect.\n"
"Skill in Hexes can help overcome this.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Hexes increases the success rate and spell power of spells in\n"
"this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools, in which\n"
"case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill in these\n"
"schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"妖术系魔法试图对附近的事物施加各种附魔效果。虽然不直接造成伤害，但中招的对手可能完全失去战斗力；不过，这类法术往往必须克服对手的意志才能生效。精通妖术系魔法有助于克服这种抵抗。\n"
"\n"
"精通妖术系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Terminology correction against reviewed glossary; batch phase3-static-02.
msgctxt "textdb:descript/ability.txt:word of chaos ability"
msgid "Speaks a word of chaos, forcing enemies nearby to blink away from the user.\nAdditionally, those affected may be slowed, ensnared, or terrified by the\nexperience. Invoking a word of chaos is no easy feat and will drain the user's\nmaximum health somewhat, and the ability then cannot be used again for a short\ntime.\n"
msgstr "说出混沌真言，迫使附近敌人闪烁离开使用者。受影响者还可能被减速、缠绕或吓退。调用混沌真言并非易事，会降低使用者的部分生命上限，随后短时间内无法再次使用。\n"

#. Terminology correction against reviewed glossary; batch phase3-static-02.
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:will++ status"
msgid "Your willpower is much stronger, protecting against many magical effects.\n"
msgstr "你的意志显著增强，能抵御多种魔法效果。\n"

#. Terminology correction against reviewed glossary; batch phase3-static-02.
msgctxt "textdb:descript/status.txt:regen will++ status"
msgid ""
"Trog's Hand is simultaneously making you regenerate health at an unnaturally\n"
"fast rate and strengthening your willpower to protect you against many magical\n"
"effects.\n"
msgstr "特洛格之手同时使你以异常快的速度恢复生命，并增强意志以抵御多种魔法效果。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:armataur"
msgid ""
"Scaled mammals the size of horses, Armataurs are fast-rolling and tenacious when\n"
"pursuing enemies, but lack dexterity.\n"
msgstr "犰狳人是体型如马、身披鳞甲的哺乳动物。追击敌人时，它们翻滚迅速且锲而不舍，但不够灵巧。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:barachi"
msgid ""
"Barachim are slow-moving, amphibious humanoids who can hop long distances.\n"
"Their extended range of vision also allows them to be seen from further away.\n"
msgstr "蛙人是行动缓慢的两栖类人生物，能够远距离跳跃。它们的视野更广，但也会在更远处被发现。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:coglin"
msgid ""
"Coglins ride enchanted exoskeletons able to wield weapons in both hands,\n"
"wrapping slow-revving metal around their puny goblinoid frames.\n"
msgstr "机甲哥布林驾驶着附魔外骨骼，将运转缓慢的金属装甲裹在瘦弱的哥布林身躯外，能够双手各持一件武器。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:deep elf"
msgid ""
"Deep Elves have a strong affinity for all kinds of magic, but are very fragile.\n"
"They regenerate magical power rapidly.\n"
msgstr "地底精灵对各种魔法都有很强的亲和力，但身体十分脆弱。它们恢复魔力的速度很快。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:demigod"
msgid ""
"Demigods refuse to worship any god, but make up for this with divine attributes\n"
"and high reserves of health and magic.\n"
msgstr "半神拒绝信奉任何神祇，但拥有神一般的属性和充沛的生命与魔力作为补偿。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:demonspawn"
msgid ""
"Demonspawn are half human, half demon. They acquire strong demonic mutations as\n"
"they grow.\n"
msgstr "魔人半人半魔，随着成长会获得强大的恶魔变异。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:djinni"
msgid ""
"Djinn are ever-burning spirits. They learn spells automatically as they grow,\n"
"and cast by drawing down their own fires.\n"
msgstr "灯灵是永燃的精魂。它们随着成长自动习得法术，并消耗自身的火焰施法。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:draconian"
msgid ""
"Draconians are versatile hybrids. They mature when reaching level 7 and develop\n"
"a colour.\n"
msgstr "龙人是多才多艺的混血生物。达到 7 级时，它们会发育成熟，显现出一种颜色。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:formicid"
msgid ""
"Formicids are humanoid ants adept at digging. Their limbs are exceptionally\n"
"strong and they live in a state of permanent stasis.\n"
msgstr "蚁族是擅长挖掘的类人蚂蚁。它们四肢极其强壮，永久处于稳态。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:felid"
msgid "Felids are many-lived sentient cats. They cannot use armour or weapons.\n"
msgstr "猫族是拥有多条性命的智慧猫类。它们无法使用防具或武器。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:gargoyle"
msgid ""
"Made of living stone, Gargoyles have a preternatural affinity for earth magic.\n"
"They have low health, but their stone bodies are incredibly tough.\n"
msgstr "石像鬼由活石构成，对土系魔法有着超自然的亲和力。它们生命值较低，但石质身躯极其坚固。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:gnoll"
msgid ""
"Gnolls are canine-like humanoids. They are unable to specialise in any single\n"
"skill, but instead gradually become proficient in all skills at once.\n"
msgstr "豺狼人是外形似犬的类人生物。它们无法专精某一项技能，而是同时逐渐精通所有技能。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:human"
msgid ""
"Humans are natural explorers. Discovering new places refreshes and invigorates them.\n"
"They are otherwise completely average.\n"
msgstr "人类是天生的探索者。发现新地点会使它们恢复精神、焕发活力。除此之外，它们各方面都很普通。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:tengu"
msgid ""
"Tengu are bird-people who love to fight, both with weapons and spells. They are\n"
"fragile but agile, and eventually learn to fly.\n"
msgstr "天狗是热爱战斗的鸟人，既用武器也用法术。它们脆弱但灵巧，最终能够学会飞行。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:kobold"
msgid ""
"Kobolds are attuned to the shadows and can only see or be seen at a close range.\n"
"They are small and a little fragile, and are talented in most skills.\n"
msgstr "狗头人与阴影相契合，只能在近距离看见其他生物或被其他生物看见。它们体型小、略显脆弱，但大多数技能的天赋都不错。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:merfolk"
msgid ""
"Half fish, half human, Merfolk are citizens of both water and land. They are\n"
"strong combatants, and adept at using magic to assist in battle.\n"
msgstr "人鱼半人半鱼，既能在水中也能在陆地生活。它们擅长战斗，也擅长用魔法辅助作战。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:minotaur"
msgid ""
"Minotaurs are large muscular humans with bovine heads. They excel at all forms\n"
"of close and ranged combat.\n"
msgstr "牛头人是长着牛头、体格高大强壮的类人生物。它们精通各种近战和远程战斗。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:mountain dwarf"
msgid ""
"Mountain Dwarves are strong melee fighters and capable heavy-armoured casters.\n"
"They can use scrolls to enchant even some artefacts.\n"
msgstr "山地矮人是强壮的近战斗士，也是能穿重甲施法的能手。它们甚至能用卷轴强化某些神器。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:mummy"
msgid ""
"Compelled to walk by an ancient curse, Mummies have innate faith and are adept\n"
"at Necromancy, but learn other skills very slowly. They cannot drink potions.\n"
msgstr "木乃伊受古老诅咒驱使而行走，天生虔信，擅长死灵系魔法，但学习其他技能十分缓慢。它们无法饮用药水。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:naga"
msgid ""
"Nagas are hybrids: human from the waist up, with a snake-like tail instead of\n"
"legs. They move very slowly but are naturally resilient.\n"
msgstr "娜迦上半身似人，下半身是蛇尾而非双腿。它们移动十分缓慢，但天生坚韧。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:octopode"
msgid ""
"Octopodes are a species of amphibious cephalopods. They can wear eight rings,\n"
"but almost no armour fits them.\n"
msgstr "章鱼人是一种两栖头足类生物。它们可以佩戴八枚戒指，但几乎没有防具适合它们。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:oni"
msgid ""
"Large, robust, and extremely fond of drinking, Oni make capable brawlers and\n"
"spellcasters and gain extra benefits from healing potions.\n"
msgstr "鬼人体型庞大、身体强健，且极其嗜酒。它们既擅长近身搏斗也擅长施法，还能从治疗药水中获得额外益处。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:poltergeist"
msgid ""
"Formless ghosts who delight in hexing their enemies. They can equip many\n"
"different hats, gloves, boots, or cloaks at once, but cannot wear body armour.\n"
msgstr "骚灵是喜欢用妖术捉弄敌人的无形幽魂。它们可以同时装备多顶帽子、多副手套、多双靴子或多件披风，但无法穿戴躯干防具。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:revenant"
msgid ""
"Revenants are skeletal undead who are strong at melee combat and can empower\n"
"damage-dealing spells by consuming memories they harvest from their victims.\n"
msgstr "还魂者是擅长近战的骸骨亡灵。它们收集受害者的记忆，消耗这些记忆就能强化伤害类法术。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:spriggan"
msgid ""
"Very small, very frail and very fast, Spriggans are highly competent stabbers\n"
"and spellcasters.\n"
msgstr "斯普利根体型极小、身体极弱、速度极快，十分擅长刺杀和施法。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:troll"
msgid ""
"Trolls are monstrous creatures with powerful claws. They regenerate health\n"
"rapidly.\n"
msgstr "巨魔是长着强力利爪的怪物。它们恢复生命的速度很快。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/species.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/species.txt:vine stalker"
msgid ""
"Frail symbionts, Vine Stalkers cannot regain health from potions. Their magical\n"
"reserves absorb damage, and they pack a magic-restoring bite.\n"
msgstr "藤蔓人是脆弱的共生生物，无法靠药水恢复生命。它们的魔力储备可以吸收伤害，撕咬则能恢复魔力。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:berserker"
msgid ""
"Berserkers believe in Trog, the magic-hating god of frenzy. Not much can stop a\n"
"raging berserker early on, apart from hubris.\n"
msgstr "狂战士信奉憎恶魔法的狂怒之神特洛戈。初期几乎没有什么能阻挡暴怒的狂战士，除了狂妄自大。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:brigand"
msgid "Brigands carry poisoned darts and a small number of nasty curare darts.\n"
msgstr "强盗携带毒镖和少量危险的箭毒镖。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:chaos knight"
msgid ""
"Chaos Knights are playthings of the unpredictable Xom, and are subject to the\n"
"god's constantly changing moods.\n"
msgstr "混沌骑士是喜怒无常的佐姆的玩物，始终受这位神祇变幻莫测的心情摆布。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:enchanter"
msgid ""
"Enchanters know a variety of Hexes that can incapacitate their foes, and are\n"
"equipped with an enchanted dagger and potions of invisibility.\n"
msgstr "妖术师掌握多种能让敌人失去行动能力的妖术，并配有附魔匕首和隐形药水。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:fighter"
msgid ""
"Fighters are equipped with armour and shield, as well as a weapon of their\n"
"choice and potions of might.\n"
msgstr "战士起始配有防具、盾牌、自选武器和力量药水。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:gladiator"
msgid ""
"Gladiators are ready for the arena with light armour, a weapon of their choice,\n"
"and a few throwing weapons and nets.\n"
msgstr "角斗士身穿轻甲、手持自选武器，携带少量投掷武器和投网，随时准备进入竞技场。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:hedge wizard"
msgid ""
"Hedge Wizards are magic generalists, good at using a wide variety of tools to\n"
"frustrate their foes and gain an edge in the battlefield.\n"
msgstr "野法师是魔法多面手，擅长用各种手段阻挠敌人、取得战场优势。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:monk"
msgid ""
"Monks start with a simple weapon of their choice, an orb of light, and a potion\n"
"of divine ambrosia, and gain additional piety with the first god they worship.\n"
msgstr "武僧起始携带自选的简单武器、光明宝珠和一瓶神圣琼浆药水，首次信奉神祇时能获得额外虔诚。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/backgrounds.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/backgrounds.txt:shapeshifter"
msgid ""
"Shapeshifters use talismans to shift their form, making them powerful melee\n"
"fighters (especially when unarmed) at the cost of armour.\n"
msgstr "变形者用变形护符改变自身形态，牺牲护甲来换取强大的近战能力，徒手战斗时尤其如此。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:fighting"
msgid ""
"Fighting skill increases your accuracy and damage in physical combat, and\n"
"also increases your maximum health.\n"
msgstr "战斗技能提高物理战斗的命中率和伤害，也提高生命值上限。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:short blades"
msgid ""
"Short Blades are more effective than any other weapon type at stabbing helpless\n"
"foes.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Short Blades will allow you to attack more quickly with all\n"
"weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Short Blades increases your effectiveness with Long Blades,\n"
"and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"短刃比其他任何武器类型都更擅长刺杀无力反抗的敌人。\n"
"\n"
"精通短刃能提高使用此类所有武器时的攻击速度、命中率和伤害。\n"
"\n"
"精通短刃也能提高使用长刃的效能，反之亦然。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:long blades"
msgid ""
"Being skilled with Long Blades will allow you to attack more quickly with all\n"
"weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Long Blades increases your effectiveness with Short Blades,\n"
"and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"精通长刃能提高使用此类所有武器时的攻击速度、命中率和伤害。\n"
"\n"
"精通长刃也能提高使用短刃的效能，反之亦然。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:axes"
msgid ""
"Axes cleave through multiple enemies with a single swing, hitting foes in an\n"
"arc around the wielder.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Axes will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons\n"
"of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Axes increases your effectiveness with Maces & Flails and\n"
"Polearms, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"斧类武器一次挥击能劈砍多个敌人，命中持用者周围弧形范围内的敌人。\n"
"\n"
"精通斧能提高使用此类所有武器时的攻击速度、命中率和伤害。\n"
"\n"
"精通斧也能提高使用锤与连枷、长柄武器的效能，反之亦然。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:maces & flails"
msgid ""
"Being skilled with Maces & Flails will allow you to attack more quickly with\n"
"all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with\n"
"them.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Maces & Flails increases your effectiveness with Axes and\n"
"Staves, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"精通锤与连枷能提高使用此类所有武器时的攻击速度、命中率和伤害。\n"
"\n"
"精通锤与连枷也能提高使用斧、棍杖的效能，反之亦然。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:polearms"
msgid ""
"Polearms can be evoked with ‘v’ to attack enemies from two spaces away.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Polearms will allow you to attack more quickly with all\n"
"weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Polearms increases your effectiveness with Axes and Staves,\n"
"and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"长柄武器可用“v”键发动攻击，命中两格远的敌人。\n"
"\n"
"精通长柄武器能提高使用此类所有武器时的攻击速度、命中率和伤害。\n"
"\n"
"精通长柄武器也能提高使用斧、棍杖的效能，反之亦然。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:staves"
msgid ""
"Staves require a relatively low amount of skill to be used most effectively,\n"
"although they lack the high damage potential of some other weapon classes.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Staves will allow you to attack more quickly with all\n"
"weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled with Staves increases your effectiveness with Maces & Flails and\n"
"Polearms, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"棍杖只需相对较低的技能等级就能发挥最大效能，但伤害潜力不及某些其他武器类型。\n"
"\n"
"精通棍杖能提高使用此类所有武器时的攻击速度、命中率和伤害。\n"
"\n"
"精通棍杖也能提高使用锤与连枷、长柄武器的效能，反之亦然。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:ranged weapons"
msgid ""
"Being skilled with Ranged Weapons will let you attack more quickly with all\n"
"bows, crossbows and slings, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with\n"
"them.\n"
msgstr "精通远程武器能提高使用所有弓、弩和投石索时的攻击速度、命中率和伤害。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:throwing"
msgid ""
"Training Throwing will make thrown weapons (such as javelins) more accurate\n"
"and damaging. It also makes certain magical darts more likely to have an\n"
"effect.\n"
msgstr "训练投掷能提高投掷武器（如标枪）的命中率和伤害，也能让某些魔法飞镖更容易生效。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:armour"
msgid ""
"Armour skill multiplies the AC gained from wearing armour of all kinds, both\n"
"from body armour and cloaks, gloves, etc. It also slightly lessens penalties\n"
"to spellcasting and ranged weapon speed from heavy armour.\n"
msgstr "防具技能按比例提高穿戴各种防具获得的护甲值（AC），既包括躯干防具，也包括披风、手套等。它还会略微减轻重甲对施法和远程武器攻击速度的惩罚。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:stealth"
msgid ""
"By training Stealth, you can make it less likely that monsters will notice you\n"
"if they are asleep or otherwise unalert, and increase your chances of monsters\n"
"losing track of you after you leave their vision. Note that more powerful\n"
"monsters tend to be more suspicious and observant.\n"
"\n"
"Stealth skill, along with the weapon skill for your equipped weapon, also\n"
"governs the likelihood of doing a great amount of damage when attacking a\n"
"distracted or helpless creature, as well as the amount of extra damage dealt.\n"
msgstr ""
"训练潜行能降低熟睡或其他未警觉怪物注意到你的几率，也能提高你离开怪物视野后使其失去踪迹的几率。注意，越强大的怪物通常越多疑、越敏锐。\n"
"\n"
"潜行技能与所持武器的技能共同影响你攻击分心或无力反抗的生物时造成大量伤害的几率，以及额外伤害的大小。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:shields"
msgid ""
"A high Shields skill helps you block melee attacks or projectiles (both magical\n"
"and non-magical) with your equipped shield, and reduces their penalty to your\n"
"evasion, attack speed and spellcasting success.\n"
msgstr "较高的盾牌技能有助于用所装备的盾牌格挡近战攻击或投射物，无论其是否具有魔法性质，也能减轻盾牌对闪避、攻击速度和施法成功率的惩罚。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:unarmed combat"
msgid ""
"Being skilled in Unarmed Combat increases your accuracy, damage and attack\n"
"speed in melee combat when barehanded.\n"
msgstr "精通徒手格斗能提高空手近战时的命中率、伤害和攻击速度。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:conjurations"
msgid ""
"Conjurations are battle oriented spells, which often work by conjuring up a\n"
"chunk of short-lived matter and propelling it towards the victim to deal direct\n"
"damage. Being skilled in Conjurations usually increases the damage and accuracy\n"
"of such spells, and sometimes affects their range or the size of the area\n"
"affected.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Conjurations increases the success rate and spell power of\n"
"spells in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools,\n"
"in which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill\n"
"in these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"塑能系魔法以战斗为主，常通过创造短暂存在的物质并将其射向目标来造成直接伤害。精通塑能系魔法通常会提高此类法术的伤害和命中率，有时也会影响射程或作用范围。\n"
"\n"
"精通塑能系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:summonings"
msgid ""
"Summonings deals with summoning creatures from another plane of reality to\n"
"temporarily aid you. Increasing Summonings skill may grant a number of effects\n"
"depending on the spell, such as longer duration or more powerful allies. Note\n"
"that summoned beings do not leave corpses and give no experience when killed,\n"
"and their equipment is as ephemeral as they are.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Summonings increases the success rate and spell power of\n"
"spells in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools,\n"
"in which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill\n"
"in these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"召唤系魔法从其他现实位面召来生物，暂时为你提供帮助。提高召唤系魔法技能可能产生不同效果，例如延长持续时间或召来更强大的盟友，具体取决于法术。注意，召唤生物死亡时不留下尸体、不提供经验，它们的装备也和它们一样只是暂时存在。\n"
"\n"
"精通召唤系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:forgecraft"
msgid ""
"Forgecraft is the art of shaping tangible objects out of magic. Forgecraft\n"
"spells can construct a wide array of mechanical creatures that will fight\n"
"alongside the caster, as well as create traps and barricades and even turn the\n"
"physical resilience of one's armour into a weapon.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Forgecraft increases the success rate and spell power of\n"
"spells in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools,\n"
"in which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill\n"
"in these schools.\n"
msgstr "锻造术是用魔法塑造实体物件的技艺。此类法术能创造多种机械生物与施法者并肩作战，也能制造陷阱和路障，甚至把防具的物理坚固性化为武器。\n\n精通锻造术能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:necromancy"
msgid ""
"Necromancy is the art of draining and gaining life, although most often\n"
"associated with zombies and other undead. As such, Necromancy spells have a\n"
"wide range of effects, ranging from spells to create or disrupt the undead to\n"
"spells granting unholy healing in various forms.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Necromancy increases the success rate and spell power of\n"
"spells in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools,\n"
"in which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill\n"
"in these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"死灵系魔法是汲取与获取生命的技艺，尽管通常与僵尸及其他亡灵联系在一起。因此，这类法术的效果非常广泛，既能创造或破坏亡灵，也能以各种方式提供邪恶的治疗。\n"
"\n"
"精通死灵系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:translocations"
msgid ""
"Translocations focus on the spatial movement of beings or objects, including\n"
"useful spells to translocate yourself over short distances quickly or to\n"
"transport your enemies away from you.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Translocations increases the success rate and spell power of\n"
"spells in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools,\n"
"in which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill\n"
"in these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"位移系魔法专注于生物或物体在空间中的移动，包含使自己快速移动一小段距离、将敌人传送到远处等实用法术。\n"
"\n"
"精通位移系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:alchemy"
msgid ""
"Alchemy is the art of toxins and transmutation. Spells in this school can twist\n"
"objects and creatures into different shapes, unleash powerful poisons, or even\n"
"unweave the fabric of magic itself.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Alchemy increases the success rate and spell power of\n"
"spells in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools,\n"
"in which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill\n"
"in these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"炼金术是毒素与转化的技艺。这一学派的法术能扭曲物体和生物的形态，释放强力毒素，甚至瓦解魔法本身的结构。\n"
"\n"
"精通炼金术能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:fire magic"
msgid ""
"Fire Magic focuses mainly on dealing fire damage over long distances, with many\n"
"effective Conjurations.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Fire Magic increases the success rate and spell power of\n"
"spells in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools,\n"
"in which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill\n"
"in these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"火系魔法主要用来从远处造成火焰伤害，包含许多强力的塑能法术。\n"
"\n"
"精通火系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:ice magic"
msgid ""
"Ice Magic contains a range of direct damage spells, as well as some defensive\n"
"effects - for example, crafting temporary ice armour.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Ice Magic increases the success rate and spell power of spells\n"
"in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools, in\n"
"which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill in\n"
"these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"冰系魔法包含多种直接伤害法术，也有一些防御效果，例如制造临时冰甲。\n"
"\n"
"精通冰系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:air magic"
msgid ""
"Air Magic provides spells to deal damage directly with the wind, as well as\n"
"noisy but powerful lightning Conjurations. It also provides some utility\n"
"spells, such as a call to the wind to assist your movement or a Hex to prevent\n"
"most use of magic in the area surrounding you.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Air Magic increases the success rate and spell power of spells\n"
"in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools, in\n"
"which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill in\n"
"these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"气系魔法既能直接用风造成伤害，也能施放喧闹而强大的闪电塑能法术。它还包含一些实用法术，例如呼风辅助移动，或用妖术阻止周围区域内的大多数魔法使用。\n"
"\n"
"精通气系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:earth magic"
msgid ""
"Earth Magic contains spells able to deal large amounts of direct physical\n"
"damage, which cannot be resisted like fire, cold and lightning damage can. It\n"
"is also linked with Alchemy, with spells to liquefy the earth around you, or to\n"
"turn your enemies to stone.\n"
"\n"
"Being skilled in Earth Magic increases the success rate and spell power of\n"
"spells in this school. Many spells belong to a combination of several schools,\n"
"in which case spellcasting success and power will depend on the average skill\n"
"in these schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"土系魔法能造成大量直接物理伤害，无法像火焰、寒冷和闪电伤害那样用抗性抵挡。它也与炼金术有关，能使周围土地液化，或将敌人石化。\n"
"\n"
"精通土系魔法能提高该学派法术的成功率和法术强度。许多法术同时属于多个学派，此时施法成功率和法术强度取决于这些学派技能的平均值。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:evocations"
msgid ""
"Evocations skill affects your ability to use magical items like wands and other\n"
"uncommon objects, increasing the power or success rate of such items.\n"
msgstr "唤发技能影响你使用魔杖等魔法物品和其他稀有物件的能力，提高它们的威力或成功率。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:shapeshifting"
msgid ""
"Shapeshifting enables the use of magical talismans to change oneself into other\n"
"forms. Sufficient skill allows one to use more powerful forms without gravely\n"
"damaging one's health. Being skilled in Shapeshifting also makes most forms\n"
"somewhat stronger, in ways which vary between forms.\n"
msgstr "变形术使你能用魔法变形护符变为其他形态。技能足够熟练时，就能使用更强大的形态而不严重损害生命。精通变形术还能使大多数形态更强，具体强化方式因形态而异。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:spellcasting"
msgid ""
"{{\n"
"    if you.race() == \"Djinni\" then\n"
"        return \"Being skilled in Spellcasting increases the success rate and spell \"..\n"
"               \"power of all spells.\"\n"
"    else\n"
"        return \"Being skilled in Spellcasting slightly increases the success \" ..\n"
"                \"rate and spell power of all spells, along with increasing your \" ..\n"
"                \"magical reserves. Training Spellcasting also gives you more spell \" ..\n"
"                \"slots to spend on new spells.\"\n"
"    end\n"
"}}\n"
msgstr ""
"{{\n"
"    if you.race() == \"Djinni\" then\n"
"        return \"精通施法能提高所有法术的成功率和\"..\n"
"               \"法术强度。\"\n"
"    else\n"
"        return \"精通施法能略微提高所有法术的成功率\" ..\n"
"                \"和法术强度，并增加你的\" ..\n"
"                \"魔力储备。训练施法还能增加\" ..\n"
"                \"用于学习新法术的法术槽。\"\n"
"    end\n"
"}}\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/skills.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/skills.txt:invocations"
msgid ""
"Your Invocations skill affects the likelihood that an attempt to use divine\n"
"abilities with certain gods will be successful, and often the power of such\n"
"abilities.\n"
"\n"
"{{\n"
"    if you.race() ~= \"Djinni\" then\n"
"        return \"The Invocations skill also affects your magical reserves, \" ..\n"
"               \"but to a lesser degree than the Spellcasting skill. Only the \" ..\n"
"               \"higher contribution is used.\"\n"
"    end\n"
"}}\n"
msgstr ""
"祈祷技能影响使用某些神祇的神赐能力时的成功率，通常也影响这些能力的威力。\n"
"\n"
"{{\n"
"    if you.race() ~= \"Djinni\" then\n"
"        return \"祈祷技能也会影响魔力储备，\" ..\n"
"               \"但影响小于施法技能。两种加成中，\" ..\n"
"               \"只采用较高的一项。\"\n"
"    end\n"
"}}\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_rest"
msgid "Rest and heal\n"
msgstr "休息并恢复\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_rest verbose"
msgid ""
"Rests while your health and magic regenerate. Resting is interrupted as soon\n"
"as a hostile monster comes into view. If health and magic are both already\n"
"full, resting will wait for 100 turns.\n"
msgstr "休息，等待生命和魔力恢复。敌对怪物一进入视野，休息就会中断。如果生命和魔力都已全满，则等待 100 回合。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_explore"
msgid "Autoexplore the current level\n"
msgstr "自动探索当前楼层\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_explore verbose"
msgid ""
"Automatically explores the current level, collecting items on the way.\n"
"Exploration stops as soon as a hostile monster comes into view, or when you\n"
"encounter new items or features.\n"
msgstr "自动探索当前楼层，沿途拾取物品。一旦敌对怪物进入视野，或遇到新的物品或地形，探索就会停止。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_explore_no_rest"
msgid ""
"Automatically explores the current level, collecting items on the way.\n"
"Exploration stops as soon as a hostile monster comes into view, or when you\n"
"encounter new items or features. Unlike CMD_EXPLORE, will treat\n"
"explore_auto_rest as if it were false and explore_auto_rest_status as if it were\n"
"empty.\n"
msgstr "自动探索当前楼层，沿途拾取物品。一旦敌对怪物进入视野，或遇到新的物品或地形，探索就会停止。与 CMD_EXPLORE 不同，此命令会将 explore_auto_rest 视为 false，将 explore_auto_rest_status 视为空。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_interlevel_travel"
msgid "Travel to distant levels\n"
msgstr "跨层旅行\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_interlevel_travel verbose"
msgid ""
"Automatically travels to a chosen level or branch. Travel is interrupted by\n"
"monsters coming into view.\n"
msgstr "自动前往选定的楼层或分支。怪物进入视野时，旅行就会中断。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_use_ability"
msgid "Use divine, innate or evokable abilities\n"
msgstr "使用神赐、天赋或可发动的能力\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_search_stashes"
msgid "Search for items/features\n"
msgstr "搜索物品或地形\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_search_stashes verbose"
msgid ""
"Searches for items or features seen elsewhere, and allows you to travel to\n"
"their location.\n"
msgstr "搜索曾在其他地方见过的物品或地形，并允许你前往其位置。\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_replay_messages"
msgid "Reread recent messages\n"
msgstr "重读近期消息\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_resists_screen"
msgid "Display character overview\n"
msgstr "显示角色概况\n"

#. Reviewed against 0.34.1 and localization/glossary.csv.
#: crawl-ref/source/dat/descript/commands.txt
msgctxt "textdb:descript/commands.txt:cmd_resists_screen verbose"
msgid ""
"Displays an overview of your current resistances, abilities, equipment and\n"
